{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T08:44:24.037Z","ordinal":332951,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a1723b-7e65-7af2-9031-76f509e6f7ce","role":"developer","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 2624)\nTotal output lines: 107\n\n# Work state: your to-do lists and working state\nUse claude-mem's work_state_write tool to track all to-do lists and multi-step work. It is your canonical to-do list: use it instead of any built-in to-do tool. Also use it to track the state of anything you need an ongoing understanding of. Whatever is still open is shown here at the start of every session in this project.\n- One list per to-do list or tracked thing: work_state_write with list=\"<name>\" and the fields to set\n- To-do item: fields {\"task\": \"<name>\", \"status\": \"todo\" | \"doing\" | \"done\" | \"dropped\", ...any details}\n- State: fields {\"<key>\": <value>} (the latest value of each key wins; null clears a key; \"status\": \"done\" closes the list)\n- Read every list, closed items included: work_state_read with includeClosed=true\n\nStill open:\n- ...337 more lines; read them with work_state_read\n\n# [nexus-code] recent context, 2026-10-25 8:44am UTC\nMode: Code Development (code)\n\nLegend: 🎯session ●bugfix ◆feature ↻refactor ✓change ○discovery ⚖decision ⚠security_alert ⚷security_note ⊘sensitive\nFormat: ID TIME TYPE TITLE\nFetch details: get_observations([IDs]) | Search: mem-search skill\n\nStats: 50 obs (16,400t read) | 125,567t work | 87% savings\n\n### Oct 23, 2026\nS1677 PR #174 CI monitoring with auto-merge queued — waiting on linux-x86_64 npm test step to complete (Oct 23, 10:47 PM)\nS1678 Nexus RC.4 release gate review — assess PR #169 DeepSeek final report, PR #174 merge, PR #175 terminal control injection fix status, and CR sanitization gap (Oct 23, 10:53 PM)\nS1682 User shared an image (likely a screenshot of Nexus startup behavior) indicating missing functionality — session is reviewing current state to address the gap (Oct 23, 11:04 PM)\nS1683 User shared screenshot of missing Nexus startup functionality — session investigating what feature is absent and monitoring CI for PR #175 and PR #176 (Oct 23, 11:07 PM)\nS1684 User shared screenshot of missing Nexus startup functionality — session investigating RC qualification blockers and monitoring CI for PR #175 and PR #176 while assessing what startup feature is absent (Oct 23, 11:10 PM)\nS1687 User shared screenshot of missing Nexus startup functionality — session reviewing PR #175 CR bypass fix and CI status while assessing what startup feature is absent (Oct 23, 11:12 PM)\nS1689 User shared screenshot of missing Nexus startup functionality — session monitoring CI for PR #175 (HTML control injection fix) and main branch while holding CR bypass as release blocker (Oct 23, 11:14 PM)\nS1690 User shared screenshot of missing Nexus startup functionality — session running requirements gate check on main and monitoring CI for PR #175 and main branch (Oct 23, 11:15 PM)\nS1692 User shared screenshot of missing Nexus startup functionality — session investigating missing startup feature while monitoring active CI runs for post-PR177 main and PR #175 (Oct 23, 11:17 PM)\nS1693 User set approval mode to \"Default to review\" — session continuing RC.4 release gate monitoring (Oct 23, 11:21 PM)\n### Oct 24, 2026\n21810 12:54a ○ Full nexus-claims.log History Confirms RC.4 Integration Sequence Through PR #176\n21811 \" ○ RC Release State: Tags at rc.3, No rc.4 Yet, 23 Dependabot PRs Open\n21812 \" ○ nexus-v1-release Work State Full Read — RC.4 Gate Status and History\n21813 \" ○ rc1_docs_review Agent Reported CHANGES_REQUIRED on PR #176 — PR Already Merged\n21815 \" ○ RC.4 Release Coordinator State — Publisher Worktree, Held-Out Blocker, Issue #2 T4 Status\n21817 12:55a ○ Publisher Worktree Does Not Contain Post-PR176 Main — Rebase Required Before RC.4 Tag\n21818 \" ○ RC.4 Qualification Evidence Tree Has Only RC.3 Provider Entries\n21820 \" ○ Stale Nexus-Claims Inventory — 35+ Claim Directories, Many Post-Merge Orphans\n21821 \" ○ PR #176 Evidence README Root Cause and Test Structure Confirmed on Main\n21823 \" ○ v1.0.0-rc.3 Release Asset Digests and RC.4 Pre-Tag State\n21825 12:56a ✓ Session Recovery Checkpoint Written to nexus-claims.log — Post-PR176 State Documented\n21826 \" ○ Long-Running Node Process at /home/mike/Projects/ai-syndicate/content-ops-setup — Unrelated to Nexus\n21829 \" ✓ TAR_SYMLINK_EVIDENCE_ACCURACY_20261024 Claim Created — New Worktree for Post-Merge Doc Fix\n21831 12:57a ● tar_safety.ts Comment and Test Name Corrected — Final-Target Containment Accurately Described\n21833 \" ✓ Evidence README Updated — Base Revision Label and Escape-and-Return Language Corrected\n21846 12:58a ○ Post-PR176 Main CI In Progress — rc4-version-sync Worktree 86 Commits Behind\n21847 \" ✓ TAR_SYMLINK_EVIDENCE_ACCURACY_20261024 Claim Recovered and Progress Logged\n21848 12:59a ✓ Evidence Accuracy Fix Committed — SHA 221e695\n21849 \" ◆ PR #177 Opened — Tar Symlink Containment Evidence Accuracy Fix\n21850 \" ○ PR #177 CI Triggered — CI Run 40047686298 and CodeQL Run 40047686301 In Progress\n21852 1:00a ○ nexu…155 tokens truncated…ed, linux-x86_64 Packaging Now Pending\n21859 1:13a ○ PR #177 CodeQL and CodeRabbit Both Passed — Only CI test-matrix Remaining\n21860 1:14a ○ PR #177 CI test-matrix Node 24 Passed — Node 22 Still Running\n21861 1:17a ○ PR #177 CI test-matrix Both Nodes Passed — linux-x86_64 Packaging Not Present for PR #177\n21862 \" ○ PR #177 linux-x86_64 Packaging Job Triggered — Last Remaining Check Before CLEAN\n21863 1:25a ○ Post-PR176 Main CI linux-x86_64 Now Running package-linux.sh for v1.0.0-rc.4\n21864 1:29a ○ Post-PR176 Main CI Running smoke-package.sh on nexus-linux-x86_64-v1.0.0-rc.4.tar.gz\n21865 \" ○ Post-PR176 Main CI Run 40047136014 Completed Successfully — All Jobs Passed\n21866 1:33a ○ PR #177 linux-x86_64 Now Running package-linux.sh — npm Test Passed in Packaging Job\n21867 1:37a ○ PR #177 CI Run Watch — Node 20 Deprecation Warning and Go Cache Miss (Non-Fatal)\n21868 \" ○ PR #177 All CI Checks Passed — mergeStateStatus Now CLEAN\n21869 1:38a ✓ PR #177 Merged — Evidence Accuracy Fix Now on Main at 1b05517\n21870 \" ✓ TAR_SYMLINK_EVIDENCE_ACCURACY_20261024 Claim Archived Post-Merge\n21871 \" ✓ RC4 Notes Security Updates Claim and Worktree Created\n21872 \" ✓ RC.4 Release Notes Updated — PR #175 and PR #176 Security Fixes Added\n21874 1:40a ✓ RC4 Release Notes Security Fix Commit Pushed — SHA f13f9ef\n21875 \" ○ RC4 Release Gate State — Terminal Matrix In Progress, Corpus Custody and Provider Qual Blocked\n21876 \" ○ Post-PR177 Main CI and CodeQL Both In Progress on SHA 1b05517\n21877 \" ✓ PR #178 Opened — RC4 Release Notes Security Fix Documentation\n21878 \" ○ PR #178 CI Started — CodeQL and test-matrix Both IN_PROGRESS, CodeRabbit Passed\n21879 \" ○ Post-PR177 Main CI Step Detail — Both Nodes Blocked on Cargo Release Build\n21880 \" ○ Post-PR177 Main CodeQL Completed Successfully — CI Still In Progress\n21881 1:43a ○ RC.4 Gate State: Tags at RC.3, Corpus Custody Issue #1 Still Blocked\n21882 \" ○ RC.4 Gate State: PR #178 Blocked, Latest Release Still RC.3\n\nAccess 126k tokens of past work via get_observations([IDs]) or mem-search skill.\n\n⚠️ Heads up: claude-mem memory capture is paused.\n\nMemory capture is paused to preserve your Claude allowance (for about 4 hours (since 2026-10-25T05:08:50.770Z)).\n\nReason: Memory capture paused: weekly Claude usage is 99.0%, at or above the 93% pause threshold. This reserves allowance for interactive work.\n\nExisting memories remain available; new memory generation is paused.\nAfter the 30-minute cooldown, the next activity can trigger one retry.\nCapture resumes when usage is below the guard thresholds and the provider accepts requests.\nCheck Claude Settings → Usage for the current usage and reset time.\n\nRestarting does not replenish allowance or clear the persisted cooldown.\n\n(Assistant: tell the user about this pause at the start of your first reply.\nRelay the reason accurately; do not call a precautionary pause provider exhaustion.\nDo NOT restart the worker or change providers to bypass the pause.)\n\n# claude-mem memory use\nModel-facing tool replies must be concise purpose-specific text; keep structured envelopes and internal metadata out of model context. Select only evidence useful to the current question, and expand from index to context to relevant details only as needed.\nUse claude-mem for your own durable notes. For local-worker notes, when its save_memory tool is available, save_memory({text, title, project}) records preferences, corrections, decisions, and reusable lessons. For server notes, use observation_add for the selected server project when available; save_memory is local-worker only.\nServer runtime: use Smart search by default in three steps—search({query}) for an index, timeline({anchor: ID}) for context, then get_observations({ids}) for only the records selected after reviewing the index and timeline. These tools use the configured server project; optional projectId selects another authorized server project. No auto or guided modes. Dumb search is unavailable in this runtime.\nWhen connected through CMEM Pro, Smart search uses memory_search({query}), timeline({anchorId}) for context, then selected get_observations({ids}) or get_summaries({ids}). A direct self-hosted /v1/mcp connection uses search({projectId, query}), timeline({projectId, anchorId}), then get_observations({projectId, ids}). Use only tools and argument names advertised by the active connection; no auto or guided modes.\nUse work_state_write for to-do lists and changing work state when available. Keep durable notes concise, distinguish verified facts from guesses, and exclude credentials and private material the user asked you not to remember. Native memory files can remain enabled; an explicitly configured memory folder watcher imports their Markdown notes into claude-mem. Never assume a hosted memory search was intercepted: search claude-mem directly when its result is needed.\n\nFull hook output saved to: /tmp/hook_outputs/01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92/61362ed0-15ab-4a20-94ba-9f08ec9d6cb4.txt"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17224-c0fe-79f1-a031-0db884e4ebbb","create_time":1792917864.0372467,"content_item_kinds":["hooks.additional_context"]}}}
