{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T08:58:19.418Z","ordinal":333577,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a1723f-d7c7-7d81-90fc-19d6aade9feb","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016addc4a70c8481a081bb29060d00b7f7","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"**Default to Review** is retained, separate from tool permissions.\n\nThe release campaign advanced on exact `main` `9398ffaf71e8032d0b46f1e55d903305164570e3`. I fixed the evaluator preflight’s missing supervisor control pipe. The full evaluator integrity file then passed **29/29** on the Ubuntu desktop with a temporary bounded workspace mount, and the final candidate `0aca7f5` received independent **ACCEPT**. Requirements enforcement passes on that candidate with the 12 exact-RC deferrals still recorded.\n\nThe candidate remains local and unpushed. The shared suite is still active; its `retention.test.ts` child has been stuck in kernel journal wait for over seven minutes. I recorded a safe-boundary status and handoff request without interrupting it. Main CI is also still running.\n\nThe Ubuntu desktop has all five terminal applications installed and an active GNOME session. The human matrix still awaits an eligible installed RC and operator evidence. Acceptance remains **IN_PROGRESS**; RC4 is still the latest published prerelease, and v1.0.0 is not released."}],"phase":"final_answer"},"started_at_ms":1792918695171,"completed_at_ms":1792918699418}}
