e/B_providers.md:28:| PRV-01 | S2 | config / cloud credentials | cli/src/config.ts:36-39 (cwd `.env` loaded with `override:true`, no key filter) | RUNTIME R2: a project `.env` with `NODE_TLS_REJECT_UNAUTHORIZED=0` turns a self-signed-cert rejection into HTTP 200 with the Authorization header delivered. | Opening an untrusted repo silently disables TLS verification for every later fetch, including cloud API keys/OAuth tokens -> MITM credential theft. Same channel sets LOCAL_LLM_TIMEOUT_MS, recovery policy, provider key vars (credentials.ts:243 reads live env), LOCAL_LLM_FALLBACK_ENDPOINTS. | Fix before v1: allowlist the keys a project `.env` may set (endpoint/model/task-class) or load it into a separate map; never let it set `NODE_*`, `*_PROXY`, `HOME`, credential vars. Add regression test. |\ndocs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/peers.md:19:| **4. Operator control / trust** | Sandbox modes `read-only` / `workspace-write` / `danger-full-access`; macOS Seatbelt, Linux bubblewrap (PATH or bundled helper needing unprivileged userns), WSL2 Linux sandbox, native Windows sandbox; `writable_roots`; `sandbox_workspace_write.network_access`; approvals `on-request`/`never`/granular (`untrusted` retired, `on-failure` deprecated); `approvals_reviewer = auto_review` delegates eligible prompts to a reviewer agent without widening the sandbox [CX-SBX][CX-CFG]. `shell_environment_policy` (inherit all/core/none; KEY/SECRET/TOKEN name exclusion when `ignore_default_excludes=false`); project-local config cannot set provider/notify/otel; command + MCP-tool hooks [CX-CFG]. | Modes default(Manual)/acceptEdits/plan/auto(classifier)/dontAsk/bypassPermissions; auto is the starting mode since v2.1.283; deny rules apply in every mode; critical-path `rm` and protected paths never auto-approved; `blockReadsOutsideWorkingDirectories` [CC-PERM]. Bash sandbox: Seatbelt (macOS), bubblewrap+socat+seccomp (Linux/WSL2), network through local proxy with domain allowlist, built on open-source `