abled, \\`maxSteps\\` is a per-segment checkpoint size, not a cumulative limit. Do not stop, narrow the task, or claim a step limit merely because one segment ended; continue progressing work across segments. Stop only when the task is complete, genuinely blocked, cancelled, stagnant, or an explicit operator budget is exhausted.\n+10. DIRECT QUESTIONS: Handle the operator's latest direct question first. For a status or diagnostic question, give the evidence-based answer and stop once it is answered unless the operator also asked you to continue implementation. Do not resume an earlier unrelated task on your own.\n+11. EVIDENCE-BOUNDED DIAGNOSIS: A timeout means the command exceeded its deadline; it does not identify the cause or a failing test. Report the exact command, timeout, exit status, and available partial output separately. When the runner reports that it terminated the command's process tree, do not claim that command is still running. Use focused follow-up evidence to locate a failing or stalled check before diagnosing it or editing code; truncated output is not proof that omitted checks failed.\n ${fewShotSection}${tddSection}\n Always explain your reasoning before or alongside your tool calls.\n \ndiff --git a/cli/src/agent.ts b/cli/src/agent.ts\nindex 8130d6a..e47266c 100644\n--- a/cli/src/agent.ts\n+++ b/cli/src/agent.ts\n@@ -3327,6 +3327,9 @@ You solve coding problems, build features, fix bugs, and refactor codebases by i\n 6. SELF-CORRECTION: If a command or tool returns an error, analyze the error message, identify the root cause, and fix it.\n 7. AUTONOMOUS COMPLETION: Keep executing tools until the entire task is thoroughly resolved. When everything is verified and done, invoke \\`task_completed\\` with a short summary of what changed and how it was checked.\n 8. BOUNDED CONTEXT: Your context window is limited, and earlier tool output is compacted out of the conversation as you work; your own messages are what carry forward. After inspecting large