ication. Main CI40171717813: Node24 SUCCESS, Node22 running `npm --prefix cli test`; CodeQL40171717805 SUCCESS. PR213 exact head7a5d4dcc3d35c68caf8a93a3bdeb2d7141101153 remains based on 016bbc3; CodeQL and JS/TS SUCCESS, Node22/24 full suites still running; merge state BLOCKED. No refresh/push/merge while exact tests active. Kimi SUITE claim now names branch v1/defect-readonly-mode-admission since 07:16Z; active test process 4034329 and descendants in its dedicated worktree; no competing test started. Issue #1 has no custodian response after coordinator metadata request 6394571756; no protected payload accessed or qualification started. GitHub still lists only RC4 as newest prerelease; tags stop at v1.0.0-rc.4. Folder trust/default approval is already separated in current main and RC5 notes: unset mode defaults to review; no source change needed. Acceptance IN_PROGRESS; RC5 not yet tagged.\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"7c3b7f\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000041758,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1756,\"output\":\"diff --git a/cli/dist/agent.js b/cli/dist/agent.js\\nindex 7b8f35f..6f44b5f 100644\\n--- a/cli/dist/agent.js\\n+++ b/cli/dist/agent.js\\n@@ -3132,6 +3132,9 @@ You solve coding problems, build features, fix bugs, and refactor codebases by i\\n 6. SELF-CORRECTION: If a command or tool returns an error, analyze the error message, identify the root cause, and fix it.\\n 7. AUTONOMOUS COMPLETION: Keep executing tools until the entire task is thoroughly resolved. When everything is verified and done, invoke \\\\`task_completed\\\\` with a short summary of what changed and how it was checked.\\n 8. BOUNDED CONTEXT: Your context window is limited, and earlier tool output is compacted out of the conversation as you work; your own messages are what carry forward. After inspecting large output you will rely on later, state its key findings in a line or two (with file and symbol references) before moving on; do not restate small files or narrate routine steps. Re-read earlier output only when you need a specific detail you did not record or it may have changed.\\n+9. UNBOUNDED PROGRESS: When continuation is enabled, \\\\`maxSteps\\\\` is a per-segment checkpoint size, not a cumulative limit. Do not stop, narrow the task, or claim a step limit merely because one segment ended; continue progressing work across segments. Stop only when the task is complete, genuinely blocked, cancelled, stagnant, or an explicit operator budget is exhausted.\\n+10. DIRECT QUESTIONS: Handle the operator's latest direct question first. For a status or diagnostic question, give the evidence-based answer and stop once it is answered unless the operator also asked you to continue implementation. Do not resume an earlier unrelated task on your own.\\n+11. EVIDENCE-BOUNDED DIAGNOSIS: A timeout means the command exceeded its deadline; it does not identify the cause or a failing test. Report the exact command, timeout, exit status, and available partial output separately. When the runner reports that it terminated the command's process tree, do not claim that command is still running. Use focused follow-up evidence to locate a failing or stalled check before diagnosing it or editing code; truncated output is not proof that omitted checks failed.\\n ${fewShotSection}${tddSection}\\n Always explain your reasoning before or alongside your tool calls.\\n \\ndiff --git a/cli/src/agent.ts b/cli/src/agent.ts\\nindex 8130d6a..e47266c 100644\\n--- a/cli/src/agent.ts\\n+++ b/cli/src/agent.ts\\n@@ -3327,6 +3327,9 @@ You solve coding problems, build features, fix bugs, and refactor codebases by i\\n 6. SELF-CORRECTION: If a command or tool returns an error, analyze the error message, identify the root cause, and fix it.\\n 7. AUTONOMOUS COMPLETION: Keep executing tools until the entire task is thoroughly resolved. When everything is verified and done, invoke \\\\`task_completed\\\\` with a short summary of what changed and how it was checked.\\n 8. BOUNDED CONTEXT: Your context window is limited, and earlier tool output is compacted out of the conversation as you work; your own messages are what carry forward. After inspecting large output you will rely on later, state its key findings in a line or two (with file and symbol references) before moving on; do not restate small files or narrate routine steps. Re-read earlier output only when you need a specific detail you did not record or it may have changed.\\n+9. UNBOUNDED PROGRESS: When continuation is enabled, \\\\`maxSteps\\\\` is a per-segment checkpoint size, not a cumulative limit. Do not stop, narrow the task, or claim a step limit merely because one segment ended; continue progressing work across segments. Stop only when the task is complete, genuinely blocked, cancelled, stagnant, or an explicit operator budget is exhausted.\\n+10. DIRECT QUESTIONS: Handle the operator's latest direct question first. For a status or diagnostic question, give the evidence-based answer and stop once it is answered unless the operator also asked you to continue implementation. Do not resume an earlier unrelated task on your own.\\n+11. EVIDENCE-BOUNDED DIAGNOSIS: A timeout means the command exceeded its deadline; it does not identify the cause or a failing test. Report the exact command, timeout, exit status, and available partial output separately. When the runner reports that it terminated the command's process tree, do not claim that command is still running. Use focused follow-up evidence to locate a failing or stalled check before diagnosing it or editing code; truncated output is not proof that omitted checks failed.\\n ${fewShotSection}${tddSection}\\n Always explain your reasoning before or alongside your tool calls.\\n \\ndiff --git a/cli/src/core/state.ts b/cli/src/core/state.ts\\nindex 93eb632..0d72ea8 100644\\n--- a/cli/src/core/state.ts\\n+++ b/cli/src/core/state.ts\\n@@ -276,6 +276,9 @@ export interface DurableStateManagerOptions {\\n \\n /** Where durable task state is written unless a directory is given. */\\n export function defaultTaskStateDir(): string {\\n+  if (process.env.NEXUS_STATE_DIR) {\\n+    return path.join(process.env.NEXUS_STATE_DIR, \\\"tasks\\\");\\n+  }\\n   return path.join(os.homedir(), \\\".nexus\\\", \\\"tasks\\\");\\n }\\n \\n@@ -289,6 +292,10 @@ export class DurableStateManager {\\n     if (!fs.existsSync(this.baseDir)) {\\n       fs.mkdirSync(this.baseDir, { recursive: true });\\n     }\\n+    // If NEXUS_STATE_DIR is set and no explicit baseDir was given, ensure the env dir exists too.\\n+    if (!options.baseDir && process.env.NEXUS_STATE_DIR) {\\n+      fs.mkdirSync(process.env.NEXUS_STATE_DIR, { recursive: true });\\n+    }\\n   }\\n \\n   public getBaseDir(): string {\\ndiff --git a/cli/test/compaction_continuity.test.ts b/cli/test/compaction_continuity.test.ts\\nindex 504ef5a..25b37c2 100644\\n--- a/cli/test/compaction_continuity.test.ts\\n+++ b/cli/test/compaction_continuity.test.ts\\n@@ -79,14 +79,14 @@ describe(\\\"A. progressing work has no step ceiling\\\", () => {\\n     // A 30k window so the run crosses compaction boundaries on the way.\\n     const agent = quiet(new AutonomousAgent(cfg(gw.url, repo, { contextLimit: 30_000 })));\\n     try {\\n-      const turn = await agent.runTurn(\\\"Write files d/f1.txt through d/f310.txt, one per step.\\\");\\n+      const turn = await agent.runTurn(`Write files d/f1.txt through d/f${STEPS}.txt, one per step.`);\\n       assert.equal(turn.execution, \\\"COMPLETED\\\", JSON.stringify({ reason: turn.reason, detail: turn.detail }));\\n       assert.equal(turn.steps.used, STEPS + 1);\\n       assert.equal(turn.steps.limitReached, false);\\n       assert.ok(fs.existsSync(path.join(repo, \\\"d\\\", `f${STEPS}.txt`)));\\n       for (const body of (gw.requests as any[]).filter((b) => b.tools)) {\\n         const t = allText(body);\\n-        assert.doesNotMatch(t, /steps? remains?|Finish now|step \\\\d+ of \\\\d+|step limit/i, \\\"no step-exhaustion prompt\\\");\\n+        assert.doesNotMatch(t, /steps? remains?|Finish now|step \\\\d+ of \\\\d+|Work left unfinished at the step limit/i, \\\"no step-exhaustion prompt\\\");\\n       }\\n       const tracking = agent.getObjective()!.execution!;\\n       assert.equal(tracking.cumulativeSteps, STEPS + 1);\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Tool execution failed: search: server runtime is selected but configuration is incomplete (missing url, api key, or project id)\"}],\"isError\":true}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17248-8634-7a83-a4b2-aba026a5a971","create_time":1792918825.834758}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
