{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T09:01:56.910Z","ordinal":333782,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a1724a-adb1-7cf0-ad78-c1eaed31db52","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-94933c62-6822-4472-bc80-35e95ad81563","process_id":"32096","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh pr diff 214 && gh pr view 214 --json author,body,files,commits,baseRefOid,headRefOid"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh pr diff 214 && gh pr view 214 --json author,body,files,commits,baseRefOid,headRefOid"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"diff --git a/docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.5.md b/docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.5.md\nindex 0febbf2..4f59a6e 100644\n--- a/docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.5.md\n+++ b/docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.5.md\n@@ -15,6 +15,7 @@ This release packages the Nexus Code Linux x86-64 client: the TypeScript CLI and\n - Upgrades fail closed when `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1` and no trusted GitHub CLI is available. The installer now verifies provenance by default through `/usr/bin/gh` or `/usr/local/bin/gh`; setting `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=0` explicitly skips that check.\n - Corrects SSRF and locality classification for IPv6 NAT64 addresses. The well-known NAT64 prefix is checked against its embedded IPv4 destination, and the local-use NAT64 prefix is rejected.\n - Automated commits never include Nexus-managed `.nexus/` state, even when it was previously staged or ignore rules would expose it, including the first commit in a new repository.\n+- Git-backed candidate identity also excludes `.nexus/` runtime state, so session and checkpoint writes do not appear as source progress or prevent stagnation detection.\n - Protects saved MCP server configuration that may contain credentials: the configuration directory and file use owner-only permissions, writes are atomic, and malformed or invalid existing configuration is preserved instead of being overwritten. Save failures are reported to the user.\n - Bounds `file_info` line counting to 8 MiB while retaining a fixed 1 KiB binary probe. Larger files still return metadata without full line-count scanning.\n - Caps CST symbol and outline reads at 8 MiB; workspace scans skip oversized files, while direct symbol and outline requests return an error. Parsing walks borrowed lines with a bounded nine-line signature lookahead, avoiding millions of per-line allocations on newline-dense files at the size limit.\n{\"author\":{\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\",\"is_bot\":false,\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"Mike Holownych\"},\"baseRefOid\":\"9398ffaf71e8032d0b46f1e55d903305164570e3\",\"body\":\"Updates RC5 notes after PR #213 merged into main. Records that Git-backed candidate identity excludes `.nexus/` runtime state, preventing session and checkpoint writes from appearing as source progress or suppressing stagnation detection. RC5 remains an unqualified prerelease; no qualification or stable-release status is implied.\\n\",\"commits\":[{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-10-25T08:36:41Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"mike@holownych.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\",\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"Mike Holownych\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-10-25T08:36:41Z\",\"messageBody\":\"\",\"messageHeadline\":\"docs(release): note Git candidate state exclusion\",\"oid\":\"1e11423f9d85590ca46d2fe42b0cb5f07cf5e678\"}],\"files\":[{\"path\":\"docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.5.md\",\"additions\":1,\"deletions\":0,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"}],\"headRefOid\":\"1e11423f9d85590ca46d2fe42b0cb5f07cf5e678\"}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":504893153}},"started_at_ms":1792918915405,"completed_at_ms":1792918916910}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T09:01:58.142Z","ordinal":333783,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1724b-93fe-7c40-abde-83137071d7fa","call_id":"call_74bf7e01f73842e29ab833ead5c35391","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.9 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"diff --git a/docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.5.md b/docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.5.md\nindex 0febbf2..4f59a6e 100644\n--- a/docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.5.md\n+++ b/docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.5.md\n@@ -15,6 +15,7 @@ This release packages the Nexus Code Linux x86-64 client: the TypeScript CLI and\n - Upgrades fail closed when `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1` and no trusted GitHub CLI is available. The installer now verifies provenance by default through `/usr/bin/gh` or `/usr/local/bin/gh`; setting `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=0` explicitly skips that check.\n - Corrects SSRF and locality classification for IPv6 NAT64 addresses. The well-known NAT64 prefix is checked against its embedded IPv4 destination, and the local-use NAT64 prefix is rejected.\n - Automated commits never include Nexus-managed `.nexus/` state, even when it was previously staged or ignore rules would expose it, including the first commit in a new repository.\n+- Git-backed candidate identity also excludes `.nexus/` runtime state, so session and checkpoint writes do not appear as source progress or prevent stagnation detection.\n - Protects saved MCP server configuration that may contain credentials: the configuration directory and file use owner-only permissions, writes are atomic, and malformed or invalid existing configuration is preserved instead of being overwritten. Save failures are reported to the user.\n - Bounds `file_info` line counting to 8 MiB while retaining a fixed 1 KiB binary probe. Larger files still return metadata without full line-count scanning.\n - Caps CST symbol and outline reads at 8 MiB; workspace scans skip oversized files, while direct symbol and outline requests return an error. Parsing walks borrowed lines with a bounded nine-line signature lookahead, avoiding millions of per-line allocations on newline-dense files at the size limit.\n{\"author\":{\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\",\"is_bot\":false,\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"Mike Holownych\"},\"baseRefOid\":\"9398ffaf71e8032d0b46f1e55d903305164570e3\",\"body\":\"Updates RC5 notes after PR #213 merged into main. Records that Git-backed candidate identity excludes `.nexus/` runtime state, preventing session and checkpoint writes from appearing as source progress or suppressing stagnation detection. RC5 remains an unqualified prerelease; no qualification or stable-release status is implied.\\n\",\"commits\":[{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-10-25T08:36:41Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"mike@holownych.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\",\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"Mike Holownych\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-10-25T08:36:41Z\",\"messageBody\":\"\",\"messageHeadline\":\"docs(release): note Git candidate state exclusion\",\"oid\":\"1e11423f9d85590ca46d2fe42b0cb5f07cf5e678\"}],\"files\":[{\"path\":\"docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.5.md\",\"additions\":1,\"deletions\":0,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"}],\"headRefOid\":\"1e11423f9d85590ca46d2fe42b0cb5f07cf5e678\"}\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1724a-adb1-7cf0-ad78-c1eaed31db52","create_time":1792918918.1422756}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
