{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T09:02:06.346Z","ordinal":333791,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a1724b-b40a-7ca3-a196-487bb9faf0a7","call_id":"call_2abc5085087645418b03f925389c1f7b","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/current_main_rc_path_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT.** The notes match the merged PRs. PR #207 remains open, and no unmerged #207 change is claimed; the `.nexus/` commit-exclusion behavior is already present on the base through merged PR #198. The notes describe RC5 artifacts as expected workflow outputs and do not claim that RC5 is tagged, published, or accepted.\\n\\nRead-only review; no tests were run.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/pr207_independent_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** — candidate `fb36b03c2ad9a22f4e94139accccee1d2f137ae3` versus current `main` at `016bbc332d694b32072f6346e7f3127fb98b691f`.\\n\\nThe six-file security patch is unchanged. Its diff SHA-256 is `55b0230bcdb125cecc263c83afbb83dc9bc54cab24ca557209a92f57d503de7a`.\\n\\nThe reported 18-file diff against stale base `19b30a4` includes 12 files changed on current `main` since that base; they add no candidate-only changes versus current `main`. Refreshing the PR base to `016bbc3` will make its displayed scope clear. `git diff --check` is clean. I did not run tests.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/t4_runner_independent_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"ACCEPT — the resource probe now supplies fd4 for the supervisor’s control channel while keeping fd3 report handling and all fail-closed resource checks intact. The diff check was clean. No tests or qualification were run.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a1724a-adb1-7cf0-ad78-c1eaed31db52","create_time":1792918926.3466878}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
