ains active; no local tests were started.\\n2026-10-25T08:02:01Z codex-root CLAIM FILE_eval_resources.mjs FILE_eval_cgroup_supervisor.mjs for PLAN-10 T4 SIGTERM/resume orchestration\\n2026-10-25T08:11:59Z codex-root PLAN-10_PR-10c progress: added cgroup-supervisor FD control channel for graceful SIGTERM delivery to every payload pid with bounded forced cleanup; added host fixture proving handler writes its state marker before supervisor cleanup; run-agent signals only after first model response and restarts Nexus with --resume; scorer rejects runner-fault labels lacking runner evidence; task validation accepts sigterm_resume only on T4; corrected memory enforcement fixture to allocate tmpfs-backed pages (instead of output-limited tail). Separate ubuntu-desktop targeted checks: T4 scoring + task validation + graceful signal 3/3 PASS; T4 proxy smoke 2/2 PASS. Broader resource-contract check confirmed memory OOM and process-count enforcement, then failed at workspace-storage assertion because this host uses shared /dev/shm rather than required dedicated size-capped tmpfs; recorded as environment prerequisite, not pass. No held-out tasks/inference. Exact source base 05994a40c6e13bdaad9348fe62751220f7f53099; independent review pending.\\n2026-10-25T09:12:00Z /root PLAN-10_PR-10c_FOLLOWUP_FIXES: Addressed independent T4 review findings in claimed worktree /home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4, branch v1/plan-10-pr10c-t4-qualification, exact base 05994a40c6e13bdaad9348fe62751220f7f53099. Scorer now requires delivered SIGTERM during an active inference turn, first process exit by SIGTERM, resume exit 0, and resulting turn COMPLETED; runner records these observations rather than unconditional resumed=true. Supervisor defers cgroup cleanup/escalation until SIGTERM grace elapses even when main child exits, allowing descendants to flush. Added regressions for missing resume evidence/inactive signal and descendant flush. On ubuntu-desktop isolated snapshot with fresh HOME/XDG: T4 scorer+supervisor focused patterns 2/2 PASS; T4 smoke patterns 2/2 PASS; diff-check PASS. No inference, held-out task, or full suite. Independent read-only re-review requested; no commit/PR until disposition.\\n2026-10-25T09:18:00Z /root PLAN-10_PR-10c_WRAPPER_SIGNAL_FIX: Follow-up independent review identified that child.close observes the systemd-run wrapper, while the contained supervisor reports the actual payload signal. Replaced scorer input with payloadExitSignal sourced from containment.final.signal; recorded supervisorWrapperExitSignal separately for diagnosis. Added regression rejecting wrapper-only SIGTERM. Exact branch base remains 05994a40c6e13bdaad9348fe62751220f7f53099; diff-chec…994 tokens truncated…claimed branch onto refreshed origin/main 9398ffaf71e8032d0b46f1e55d903305164570e3; exact candidate a9b8baad718a607c82c1286d02181d1fad9e377a (two slice commits, no conflicts). Current slice diff 12 files/541 insertions/27 deletions; diff-check clean. `npm exec -- tsc --noEmit` PASS. On ubuntu-desktop 10.0.8.3, reconstructed disposable tree from exact main archive + exact candidate diff, built from source using isolated HOME/XDG, focused eval_integrity T4 cases PASS 2/2. `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` PASS: 123 rows, 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 exact-RC deferrals remain explicitly listed. Fresh independent review ACCEPT exact a9b8baa; reviewer confirms receipts bind to actual agent run_command result, task text cannot forge evidence, and storage exhaustion uses statfs plus configured cap. Limitation retained: containmentCleaned is outer-task cleanup, not per-invocation cleanup. No full suite, inference, held-out access, push, or PR. Kimi SUITE owner still has live make test process; no overlapping tests.\\n2026-10-25T09:00:00Z /root PLAN-10_PR-10c_RESOURCE_PROBE_CONTROL_FD: Full evaluator integrity file initially had 27/29 pass on desktop because its `/dev/shm` was 8.05GB (larger than 256MiB memory cap) and expected dedicated 128MiB workspace mount was absent; corrected test environment by mounting a disposable 128MiB tmpfs at `/home/mike/nexus-t4-validation-work/t4-receipt-a9b8baa/resource-tmpfs` with mode0711 uid1000 and removing it after each run. Resource contract fixture then passed; a reproducible adjacent preflight failure exposed `resourceProbeProblem()` omitting supervisor fd4 control pipe, causing Node EINVAL before report. Fixed eval/resources.mjs to pass fd4 while retaining fd3 report parsing and all resource checks. Final candidate commit 0aca7f51535468e62176cf684d2acb6836d31ec1, base origin/main9398ffaf71e8032d0b46f1e55d903305164570e3. Complete cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts PASS 29/29 on Ubuntu desktop exact candidate tree with isolated HOME/XDG and bounded tmpfs; focused failure test PASS after fix. TypeScript, node syntax, diff-check, requirements enforcement PASS (123 rows; 108 tested,6 partial,2 implemented,7 open; 12 exact-RC deferrals). Independent review ACCEPT exact 0aca7f5; reviewer verified control fd wiring does not weaken fail-closed checks. Kimi SUITE still active; main CI40177240997 active, PR214 Node22/24 passed, Linux package active; no push/PR/full-suite overlap started.\\n2026-10-25T08:57:30Z /root AUDIT_TIMESTAMP_CORRECTION_AND_SUITE_SAFE_BOUNDARY: Correction: the preceding 09:00:00Z PLAN-10 PR-10c progress line was future-dated; its factual content is retained, and this line records the current UTC checkpoint (08:57Z). SUITE owner remains KimiCode-defect-scan with live `make test` PID45708 -> npm PID64644 -> run_tests PID64659 -> serial `node --test` PID64666 in /home/mike/nexus-wt/defect-provider-client-blockers-snapshot/cli. Current file child PID289168 is test/retention.test.ts, state D/jbd2_log_wait_commit for 7m+, CPU 29s, approx 54MiB written, no write-byte increase across repeated samples; child esbuild PID289201 waits. This is process-level stall evidence, not proof owner is inactive. Please provide a safe-boundary update: whether the retention test is expected to recover, exact remaining operation/ETA, or explicit SUITE release/handoff once safe. No signal, kill, claim release, or overlapping full-suite run performed. In parallel, local T4 candidate 0aca7f51535468e62176cf684d2acb6836d31ec1 is source-reviewed ACCEPT and evaluator integrity 29/29 on isolated Ubuntu with the bounded temporary tmpfs; full CI remains queued behind SUITE ownership.\\n2026-10-25T08:59:20Z /root SUITE_PROGRESS_RECHECK: The previously blocked retention.test.ts child PID289168 has exited. Current active serial test child PID316764 is running test/sidecar.test.ts (about 25s elapsed, CPU activity observed); parent Node test runner remains live in the same Kimi worktree. This demonstrates forward progress, so SUITE claim remains protected and is not eligible for takeover; no tests were started here.\\n2026-10-25T09:13:28Z /root CLAIM_RELEASE RC5_NOTES_AFTER_PR213: PR #214 merged at596879597d677a3fc634958cd08741cf4c93f4af after exact CI40177318825 all jobs SUCCESS, CodeQL40177318806 SUCCESS, independent ACCEPT exact notes diff, diff-check PASS. Main now5968795; post-merge CI40179733923 and CodeQL pending/in progress. RC5 notes now accurately mention PR213 candidate identity behavior; no RC tag or qualification inferred.\\n\\n--- claim ---\\n{\\\"agent\\\":\\\"KimiCode-defect-scan\\\",\\\"branch\\\":\\\"v1/defect-objective-continuation-timeout\\\",\\\"since\\\":\\\"2026-10-25T08:08:00Z\\\",\\\"scope\\\":\\\"Short local-mock provider-client blocker reproduction; no live inference.\\\"}\\n\\n--- worktree ---\\n## HEAD (no branch)\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"370c7e\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.002786333,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":32,\"output\":\"    PID    PPID STAT     ELAPSED COMMAND\\n    PID    PPID STAT     ELAPSED COMMAND\\n1072398 1070021 Rl+     11:27:13 kimi-code\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17255-e965-7c11-ad6a-fa374f060967","create_time":1792919