{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T09:14:26.207Z","ordinal":334334,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17255-e965-7c11-ad6a-fa374f060967","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-2e858a3a-75b8-4378-abf6-2374a64605b1","process_id":"69040","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md | rg -n -C 2 'SUITE|handoff|release|stale|owner|PID' | head -120; tail -n 8 /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims.log"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md | rg -n -C 2 'SUITE|handoff|release|stale|owner|PID' | head -120; tail -n 8 /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims.log"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"26-if mkdir \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\" 2>/dev/null; then          # mkdir is atomic: exactly one agent wins\n27-  printf '{\"agent\":\"%s\",\"branch\":\"%s\",\"since\":\"%s\",\"pid\":%s}\\n' \\\n28:    \"$AGENT_NAME\" \"v1/plan-01-pr-1a\" \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ)\" \"$$\" > \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\"\n29-else\n30:  echo \"claimed by: $(cat \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\")\"; exit 1\n31-fi\n32-```\n--\n34-- **Release** the claim by deleting its directory (`rm -r \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\"`) after the slice merges or is abandoned. Write one line about the outcome to `$CLAIMS/../nexus-claims.log`.\n35-- **Hot-file claims** use the same mechanism with the name `FILE_<path with / replaced by _>`, for example `FILE_cli_src_agent.ts`. See §4.\n36:- **Stale claims.** A claim older than 24 h whose PID is gone may be broken, but only by the owner, or by an agent that first records the broken claim in the log.\n37-- If the MCP Agent Mail server is available, its file reservations (`file_reservation_paths`) may be used as well. The git-common-dir claim stays authoritative, because every agent can see it without extra tooling.\n38-\n--\n41-| Resource | Rule |\n42-|---|---|\n43:| Source | One `git worktree` per claimed slice: `git worktree add ../nexus-wt/<slice> -b v1/<plan>-<slice> origin/main`. Never edit `~/nexus-code` itself. It is the owner's checkout, and `/usr/local/bin/nexus` runs from it. |\n44-| Branch | `v1/plan-NN-pr-Nx`. One branch per slice. Never commit to `main` directly. |\n45-| HOME and state | Until PLAN-08 PR-8a lands, every test, build and probe run sets `HOME=$(mktemp -d)` and `XDG_CONFIG_HOME=\"$HOME/.config\"`. After PR-8a, the test setup enforces this, but scripts and probes outside `npm test` must still set it. **Never** run anything that writes to the real `~/.nexus` or `~/.config/nexus`. |\n--\n47-| Builds | Each worktree builds into its own `core/target`, and `cli/dist` is per worktree. To share the Rust build cache, set `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` per worktree, never to one shared directory. |\n48-| Ports | Mock servers bind `127.0.0.1:0` (an ephemeral port) and publish the chosen port to a file. Fixed ports are forbidden. |\n49:| Processes | Kill only PIDs you started, taken from `$!` or `ps -eo pid,args \\| grep -v grep`. **Never `pkill -f` or `killall`.** Long background jobs are stopped through the agent's own task controls. |\n50:| Full test suites | The PTY and provider tests are timing-sensitive. Take the claim `SUITE` before running a full suite (`make test`, or `npm test` over all files). While anyone holds `SUITE`, nobody runs other suites or targeted test files on the same machine. Concurrent load caused a false failure on 2026-10-15: `cloud_providers` saw an extra provider request after a load-induced timeout. Release the claim when the run ends. |\n51-| Inference | There is one inference host (DEC-16). Any run that uses the gateway takes the claim `GATEWAY` first. That includes eval runs, live checks and stripped-proxy runs. One gateway run at a time, which keeps eval timings valid and prevents overload. Small cloud checks (E5) take `CLOUD` to avoid duplicate spend. |\n52-| Credentials | Agents never read or copy `~/.config/nexus/credentials.json`, `config.env` values, or gateway tokens. The stripped proxy reads the token file itself. |\n--\n54-## 4. Hot files: serialise, do not merge blindly\n55-\n56:These files are touched by several plans. An agent editing one must hold its `FILE_` claim for the **shortest** period: edit, test, push, merge, then release.\n57-\n58-| File | Plans that touch it | Rule |\n--\n86-3. Merge order follows the precedence rules in §4 and the ROADMAP milestone order. Within a milestone, the slice with fewer hot-file claims merges first.\n87-4. Rebase onto `origin/main` immediately before merging. Re-run the slice's targeted tests, plus `make test`, on a snapshot of the rebased commit. Merge only if both pass.\n88:5. Pushing, tagging, publishing and changing GitHub state (issues, milestones, releases) are **owner-approved actions** (DECISIONS X-list). Agents prepare them and do not perform them.\n89-6. Preserve unrelated user work: the untracked `nexus-continuity-validation/`, the stashes, and any dirty files you did not create. Never stash, reset, clean or check out over them.\n90-\n--\n94-|---|---|---|\n95-| Claims | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/` | Who owns which slice or file right now |\n96:| Claim log | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims.log` (append-only, one line per event) | Claim, release, broken claim, boundary request |\n97-| Boundary requests and discovered requirements | The PR description, under the heading `Needs from other slices`. Mirrored as one line in the claim log. | So the owning slice's agent can pick it up. Never fixed silently out of scope. |\n98-| Slice evidence | `docs/reviews/evidence/v1/<plan>-<slice>/` (new directory per slice) | No shared evidence files, so agents cannot overwrite each other's evidence |\n2026-10-25T09:20:00Z /root PLAN10_PR10c_BOUNDARY_APPROVED: Approved narrow boundary extension after reviewer showed TaskExecutionResult omits tool messages and text evidence is forgeable; claimed previously free hot files cli/src/agent.ts, cli/src/core/app.ts, cli/src/types.ts. Plan is opt-in eval-only structured run_command receipts bound to actual invocation and runner output; no user-facing/default behavior change, thresholds or held-out access. Existing prototype remains untrusted until replaced and reviewed.\n2026-10-25T08:37:43Z /root CLAIM_RELEASE PR213: PR #213 merged at9398ffaf after exact-head CI40174568839 all jobs SUCCESS, CodeQL40174568856 SUCCESS, independent ACCEPT exact diff, requirement enforcement PASS, and diff-check PASS. Release slice and hot-file claims removed. Coordination note: candidate.test.ts was edited as part of the reviewed remediation without a separate hot-file claim; no competing claim existed, and it is now merged.\n2026-10-25T08:37:43Z /root PR214_NOTES_PENDING: RC5 notes now include candidate identity state behavior after PR213; exact head1e11423 against main9398ffa, one-file/one-line diff, diff-check PASS. PR214 exact CI40177318825 and CodeQL40177318806 active; independent review requested. Main post-merge CI40177240997 and CodeQL40177241010 active.\n2026-10-25T08:47:30Z /root PLAN-10_PR-10c_REBASED_EXACT_CANDIDATE: Rebased claimed branch onto refreshed origin/main 9398ffaf71e8032d0b46f1e55d903305164570e3; exact candidate a9b8baad718a607c82c1286d02181d1fad9e377a (two slice commits, no conflicts). Current slice diff 12 files/541 insertions/27 deletions; diff-check clean. `npm exec -- tsc --noEmit` PASS. On ubuntu-desktop 10.0.8.3, reconstructed disposable tree from exact main archive + exact candidate diff, built from source using isolated HOME/XDG, focused eval_integrity T4 cases PASS 2/2. `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` PASS: 123 rows, 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 exact-RC deferrals remain explicitly listed. Fresh independent review ACCEPT exact a9b8baa; reviewer confirms receipts bind to actual agent run_command result, task text cannot forge evidence, and storage exhaustion uses statfs plus configured cap. Limitation retained: containmentCleaned is outer-task cleanup, not per-invocation cleanup. No full suite, inference, held-out access, push, or PR. Kimi SUITE owner still has live make test process; no overlapping tests.\n2026-10-25T09:00:00Z /root PLAN-10_PR-10c_RESOURCE_PROBE_CONTROL_FD: Full evaluator integrity file initially had 27/29 pass on desktop because its `/dev/shm` was 8.05GB (larger than 256MiB memory cap) and expected dedicated 128MiB workspace mount was absent; corrected test environment by mounting a disposable 128MiB tmpfs at `/home/mike/nexus-t4-validation-work/t4-receipt-a9b8baa/resource-tmpfs` with mode0711 uid1000 and removing it after each run. Resource contract fixture then passed; a reproducible adjacent preflight failure exposed `resourceProbeProblem()` omitting supervisor fd4 control pipe, causing Node EINVAL before report. Fixed eval/resources.mjs to pass fd4 while retaining fd3 report parsing and all resource checks. Final candidate commit 0aca7f51535468e62176cf684d2acb6836d31ec1, base origin/main9398ffaf71e8032d0b46f1e55d903305164570e3. Complete cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts PASS 29/29 on Ubuntu desktop exact candidate tree with isolated HOME/XDG and bounded tmpfs; focused failure test PASS after fix. TypeScript, node syntax, diff-check, requirements enforcement PASS (123 rows; 108 tested,6 partial,2 implemented,7 open; 12 exact-RC deferrals). Independent review ACCEPT exact 0aca7f5; reviewer verified control fd wiring does not weaken fail-closed checks. Kimi SUITE still active; main CI40177240997 active, PR214 Node22/24 passed, Linux package active; no push/PR/full-suite overlap started.\n2026-10-25T08:57:30Z /root AUDIT_TIMESTAMP_CORRECTION_AND_SUITE_SAFE_BOUNDARY: Correction: the preceding 09:00:00Z PLAN-10 PR-10c progress line was future-dated; its factual content is retained, and this line records the current UTC checkpoint (08:57Z). SUITE owner remains KimiCode-defect-scan with live `make test` PID45708 -> npm PID64644 -> run_tests PID64659 -> serial `node --test` PID64666 in /home/mike/nexus-wt/defect-provider-client-blockers-snapshot/cli. Current file child PID289168 is test/retention.test.ts, state D/jbd2_log_wait_commit for 7m+, CPU 29s, approx 54MiB written, no write-byte increase across repeated samples; child esbuild PID289201 waits. This is process-level stall evidence, not proof owner is inactive. Please provide a safe-boundary update: whether the retention test is expected to recover, exact remaining operation/ETA, or explicit SUITE release/handoff once safe. No signal, kill, claim release, or overlapping full-suite run performed. In parallel, local T4 candidate 0aca7f51535468e62176cf684d2acb6836d31ec1 is source-reviewed ACCEPT and evaluator integrity 29/29 on isolated Ubuntu with the bounded temporary tmpfs; full CI remains queued behind SUITE ownership.\n2026-10-25T08:59:20Z /root SUITE_PROGRESS_RECHECK: The previously blocked retention.test.ts child PID289168 has exited. Current active serial test child PID316764 is running test/sidecar.test.ts (about 25s elapsed, CPU activity observed); parent Node test runner remains live in the same Kimi worktree. This demonstrates forward progress, so SUITE claim remains protected and is not eligible for takeover; no tests were started here.\n2026-10-25T09:13:28Z /root CLAIM_RELEASE RC5_NOTES_AFTER_PR213: PR #214 merged at596879597d677a3fc634958cd08741cf4c93f4af after exact CI40177318825 all jobs SUCCESS, CodeQL40177318806 SUCCESS, independent ACCEPT exact notes diff, diff-check PASS. Main now5968795; post-merge CI40179733923 and CodeQL pending/in progress. RC5 notes now accurately mention PR213 candidate identity behavior; no RC tag or qualification inferred.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":27453}},"started_at_ms":1792919666206,"completed_at_ms":1792919666206}}
