{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T09:18:42.646Z","ordinal":334579,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_060b64278a9dfb15016addc971e78481a0b598f6397915f4b7","status":"completed","call_id":"call_859b9f22641f417cb776c7c0f9d00a8c","name":"exec","input":"const r=await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | sed -n '190,230p'; git show origin/v1/qual108-terminal-worksheet:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/QUAL108_TERMINAL_MATRIX.md 2>/dev/null | sed -n '1,100p' || true\",workdir:\"/home/mike/nexus-code\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:1800});text(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17255-e965-7c11-ad6a-fa374f060967","create_time":1792919921.9096928}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T09:18:43.217Z","ordinal":334580,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17255-e965-7c11-ad6a-fa374f060967","session_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","root_turn_id":"01a17255-e965-7c11-ad6a-fa374f060967","response_id":"resp_060b64278a9dfb15016addc9714e3c81a0b38ce51809c676cd","usage":{"input_tokens":116325,"cached_input_tokens":114560,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":131,"reasoning_output_tokens":7,"total_tokens":116456},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":4960752,"cached_input_tokens":4884864,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":19674,"reasoning_output_tokens":10121,"total_tokens":4980426},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":6101168601,"cached_input_tokens":6035621504,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":17401160,"reasoning_output_tokens":10038816,"total_tokens":6118569761}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T09:18:43.690Z","ordinal":334581,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17255-e965-7c11-ad6a-fa374f060967","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-c93eec20-cb79-4aa3-b9bd-07f40ad75b62","process_id":"72470","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | sed -n '190,230p'; git show origin/v1/qual108-terminal-worksheet:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/QUAL108_TERMINAL_MATRIX.md 2>/dev/null | sed -n '1,100p' || true"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | sed -n '190,230p'; git show origin/v1/qual108-terminal-worksheet:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/QUAL108_TERMINAL_MATRIX.md 2>/dev/null | sed -n '1,100p' || true"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"### 5.3 Manual real-terminal matrix (E3)\n\nTerminals: xterm, kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on), tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code integrated terminal, GNOME Terminal. Sizes: 80×24, 40×14, 200×60.\n\nFor each terminal × size, check:\n\n1. Launch `nexus` (the TUI appears).\n2. Approval panel. Type continuously across it. Paste 3 lines. Approve with a deliberate key.\n3. Shift+Enter or Alt+Enter multiline.\n4. Resize during streaming.\n5. Esc during `sleep 30` (no survivors).\n6. Ctrl-C twice (clean terminal restore: echo on, no stray escape codes).\n7. NO_COLOR.\n\nRecord PASS/FAIL per cell, with a screenshot of the approval panel and the post-exit terminal state.\n\n**Gate:** zero FAIL on checks 2, 5 and 6, which are safety checks. Other FAILs need a written disposition (fix, or a documented known limitation).\n\n## 6. Task-quality qualification (REQ-QUAL-101 to REQ-QUAL-106, REQ-QUAL-109)\n\nEnvironment: E4 (gateway direct), serial runs, with matched model fingerprint, budgets and env (REQ-QUAL-102).\n\n### 6.1 T2 held-out (ACC-QUAL-T2)\n\n- 40 sealed tasks. The manifest is committed before RC1, and authorship is recorded (agent-authored, DEC-05).\n- 5 runs × {Nexus RC, Goose, OpenCode}.\n- Before execution, freeze three qualification configs at `eval/configs/v1-t2-nexus.json`, `eval/configs/v1-t2-goose.json`, and `eval/configs/v1-t2-opencode.json`. Each must set `qualification: true`, identify the same model fingerprint and sampling settings, and record equal context/output and task budgets; the Nexus config must identify the installed RC and its package digest. Do not derive these files from the pilot configs by silently inheriting or changing settings.\n- Set `T2_TASKS` to the custodian-approved, sealed task directory and `T2_OUT` to a new, empty, run-specific output directory. Do not use the disclosed `eval/tasks` development set as held-out evidence. Preserve all three outputs and their manifests; never reuse an output directory for a retry.\n- Run each config serially, with identical task selection and five runs per task:\n\n  ```bash\n  set -euo pipefail\n  : \"${T2_TASKS:?set the sealed task directory}\"\n  : \"${T2_OUT:?set a new unique output directory}\"\n  test ! -e \"$T2_OUT\"\n  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-nexus.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/nexus\" --runs 5\n  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-goose.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/goose\" --runs 5\n  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-opencode.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/opencode\" --runs 5\n  node eval/score.mjs --pairs \"$T2_OUT/nexus/results.jsonl\" \"$T2_OUT/goose/results.jsonl\" \"$T2_OUT/opencode/results.jsonl\"\n  ```\n\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":37613}},"started_at_ms":1792919923690,"completed_at_ms":1792919923690}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T09:18:44.980Z","ordinal":334582,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1725a-f0f4-7793-a1ef-bcc3baeca9ab","call_id":"call_859b9f22641f417cb776c7c0f9d00a8c","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.3 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"### 5.3 Manual real-terminal matrix (E3)\n\nTerminals: xterm, kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on), tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code integrated terminal, GNOME Terminal. Sizes: 80×24, 40×14, 200×60.\n\nFor each terminal × size, check:\n\n1. Launch `nexus` (the TUI appears).\n2. Approval panel. Type continuously across it. Paste 3 lines. Approve with a deliberate key.\n3. Shift+Enter or Alt+Enter multiline.\n4. Resize during streaming.\n5. Esc during `sleep 30` (no survivors).\n6. Ctrl-C twice (clean terminal restore: echo on, no stray escape codes).\n7. NO_COLOR.\n\nRecord PASS/FAIL per cell, with a screenshot of the approval panel and the post-exit terminal state.\n\n**Gate:** zero FAIL on checks 2, 5 and 6, which are safety checks. Other FAILs need a written disposition (fix, or a documented known limitation).\n\n## 6. Task-quality qualification (REQ-QUAL-101 to REQ-QUAL-106, REQ-QUAL-109)\n\nEnvironment: E4 (gateway direct), serial runs, with matched model fingerprint, budgets and env (REQ-QUAL-102).\n\n### 6.1 T2 held-out (ACC-QUAL-T2)\n\n- 40 sealed tasks. The manifest is committed before RC1, and authorship is recorded (agent-authored, DEC-05).\n- 5 runs × {Nexus RC, Goose, OpenCode}.\n- Before execution, freeze three qualification configs at `eval/configs/v1-t2-nexus.json`, `eval/configs/v1-t2-goose.json`, and `eval/configs/v1-t2-opencode.json`. Each must set `qualification: true`, identify the same model fingerprint and sampling settings, and record equal context/output and task budgets; the Nexus config must identify the installed RC and its package digest. Do not derive these files from the pilot configs by silently inheriting or changing settings.\n- Set `T2_TASKS` to the custodian-approved, sealed task directory and `T2_OUT` to a new, empty, run-specific output directory. Do not use the disclosed `eval/tasks` development set as held-out evidence. Preserve all three outputs and their manifests; never reuse an output directory for a retry.\n- Run each config serially, with identical task selection and five runs per task:\n\n  ```bash\n  set -euo pipefail\n  : \"${T2_TASKS:?set the sealed task directory}\"\n  : \"${T2_OUT:?set a new unique output directory}\"\n  test ! -e \"$T2_OUT\"\n  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-nexus.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/nexus\" --runs 5\n  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-goose.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/goose\" --runs 5\n  node eval/run.mjs --config eval/configs/v1-t2-opencode.json --tasks \"$T2_TASKS\" --out \"$T2_OUT/opencode\" --runs 5\n  node eval/score.mjs --pairs \"$T2_OUT/nexus/results.jsonl\" \"$T2_OUT/goose/results.jsonl\" \"$T2_OUT/opencode/results.jsonl\"\n  ```\n\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17255-e965-7c11-ad6a-fa374f060967","create_time":1792919924.9801743}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
