{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T09:33:58.698Z","ordinal":335090,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17267-b4a8-7073-9d2a-32da76e0ee35","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-e6c16c07-472f-47b0-a743-fd7b31c8e56d","process_id":"36820","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/defect-eval-resource-assertion status --short --branch; sed -n '1,180p' /home/mike/nexus-wt/defect-eval-resource-assertion/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/defect-eval-resource-assertion/README.md; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/defect-eval-resource-assertion show -1 --format='%H %cI %s' --stat; tail -n 10 .git/nexus-claims.log"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/defect-eval-resource-assertion status --short --branch; sed -n '1,180p' /home/mike/nexus-wt/defect-eval-resource-assertion/docs/reviews/evidence/v1/defect-eval-resource-assertion/README.md; git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/defect-eval-resource-assertion show -1 --format='%H %cI %s' --stat; tail -n 10 .git/nexus-claims.log"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"## v1/defect-eval-resource-assertion...origin/main [ahead 3]\n# Evaluator resource-order fixture correction\n\n## Scope and identity\n\n- Source base: `29eab4c`.\n- Reviewed source commit: `36b702f` (`test(eval): assert resource failures from actual limits`).\n- Branch: `v1/defect-eval-resource-assertion`.\n- Change type: test fixture correction only; no evaluator production code changed.\n\n## Investigation and defect\n\nRepeated full suites failed the resource contract with `oomKills=3` where zero was asserted. Independent root-cause investigation and a synthetic `runIsolated` probe established that the local fallback uses `/dev/shm` (about 24 GiB on this host), so the 512 MiB write reaches the 256 MiB memory cgroup before filesystem capacity. The CI/release workflows instead provide a dedicated 128 MiB tmpfs, which correctly reaches `ENOSPC` before memory exhaustion.\n\nThe test therefore encoded an invalid environment-independent ordering assumption. It was not evidence of an evaluator containment defect. The supervisor's OOM statistics and final process reaping were working.\n\n## Fix and validation\n\nThe test now:\n\n- requires a configured CI workspace to be smaller than `memoryBytes`, preserving the original strict storage-first assertion;\n- expects `oomKills === 0` for storage-first runs and `oomKills >= 1` for memory-first runs;\n- preserves all nonzero-exit, cleanup, process, CPU, storage-bound, and containment assertions.\n\nAll commands used isolated `HOME` and `XDG_CONFIG_HOME` directories; no held-out payload, live inference, or credentials were used.\n\n- Before the correction, the resource-contract assertion failed repeatedly with `3 !== 0`.\n- After the correction, `node scripts/run_tests.mjs test/eval_integrity.test.ts` passed 26/26 following the required CLI build. An initial run had one unrelated missing-`dist` failure and was not counted as a product result.\n- `npm run build` and `tsc --noEmit` passed.\n- `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed: 123 rows; 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open; 12 exact-RC qualification deferrals. This is a source gate, not installed-RC qualification.\n- Full-suite snapshot `23f0b05` completed `make build && make test` with 1,663 tests: 1,661 passed and 2 failed. The corrected resource-contract test passed in the full suite. The remaining failures were the CI-only capped-storage prerequisite and the intermittent TUI upgrade path; focused upgrade tests previously passed 77/77. This was not a clean suite.\n\n## Independent review and integration\n\nThe investigator independently reviewed the final diff and returned **ACCEPT**, confirming CI requirement fidelity, correct local OOM expectations, unchanged containment checks, and single-file scope. Review was read-only and did not rerun tests.\n\nNo push, pull-request integration, release qualification, or installed-candidate acceptance is claimed.\n5918ba490f7f2e379648f2bd84cc04a696b70ea2 2026-10-25T09:31:44+00:00 docs: record evaluator fixture suite result\n\n docs/reviews/evidence/v1/defect-eval-resource-assertion/README.md | 2 +-\n 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)\n2026-10-25T09:00:00Z /root PLAN-10_PR-10c_RESOURCE_PROBE_CONTROL_FD: Full evaluator integrity file initially had 27/29 pass on desktop because its `/dev/shm` was 8.05GB (larger than 256MiB memory cap) and expected dedicated 128MiB workspace mount was absent; corrected test environment by mounting a disposable 128MiB tmpfs at `/home/mike/nexus-t4-validation-work/t4-receipt-a9b8baa/resource-tmpfs` with mode0711 uid1000 and removing it after each run. Resource contract fixture then passed; a reproducible adjacent preflight failure exposed `resourceProbeProblem()` omitting supervisor fd4 control pipe, causing Node EINVAL before report. Fixed eval/resources.mjs to pass fd4 while retaining fd3 report parsing and all resource checks. Final candidate commit 0aca7f51535468e62176cf684d2acb6836d31ec1, base origin/main9398ffaf71e8032d0b46f1e55d903305164570e3. Complete cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts PASS 29/29 on Ubuntu desktop exact candidate tree with isolated HOME/XDG and bounded tmpfs; focused failure test PASS after fix. TypeScript, node syntax, diff-check, requirements enforcement PASS (123 rows; 108 tested,6 partial,2 implemented,7 open; 12 exact-RC deferrals). Independent review ACCEPT exact 0aca7f5; reviewer verified control fd wiring does not weaken fail-closed checks. Kimi SUITE still active; main CI40177240997 active, PR214 Node22/24 passed, Linux package active; no push/PR/full-suite overlap started.\n2026-10-25T08:57:30Z /root AUDIT_TIMESTAMP_CORRECTION_AND_SUITE_SAFE_BOUNDARY: Correction: the preceding 09:00:00Z PLAN-10 PR-10c progress line was future-dated; its factual content is retained, and this line records the current UTC checkpoint (08:57Z). SUITE owner remains KimiCode-defect-scan with live `make test` PID45708 -> npm PID64644 -> run_tests PID64659 -> serial `node --test` PID64666 in /home/mike/nexus-wt/defect-provider-client-blockers-snapshot/cli. Current file child PID289168 is test/retention.test.ts, state D/jbd2_log_wait_commit for 7m+, CPU 29s, approx 54MiB written, no write-byte increase across repeated samples; child esbuild PID289201 waits. This is process-level stall evidence, not proof owner is inactive. Please provide a safe-boundary update: whether the retention test is expected to recover, exact remaining operation/ETA, or explicit SUITE release/handoff once safe. No signal, kill, claim release, or overlapping full-suite run performed. In parallel, local T4 candidate 0aca7f51535468e62176cf684d2acb6836d31ec1 is source-reviewed ACCEPT and evaluator integrity 29/29 on isolated Ubuntu with the bounded temporary tmpfs; full CI remains queued behind SUITE ownership.\n2026-10-25T08:59:20Z /root SUITE_PROGRESS_RECHECK: The previously blocked retention.test.ts child PID289168 has exited. Current active serial test child PID316764 is running test/sidecar.test.ts (about 25s elapsed, CPU activity observed); parent Node test runner remains live in the same Kimi worktree. This demonstrates forward progress, so SUITE claim remains protected and is not eligible for takeover; no tests were started here.\n2026-10-25T09:13:28Z /root CLAIM_RELEASE RC5_NOTES_AFTER_PR213: PR #214 merged at596879597d677a3fc634958cd08741cf4c93f4af after exact CI40177318825 all jobs SUCCESS, CodeQL40177318806 SUCCESS, independent ACCEPT exact notes diff, diff-check PASS. Main now5968795; post-merge CI40179733923 and CodeQL pending/in progress. RC5 notes now accurately mention PR213 candidate identity behavior; no RC tag or qualification inferred.\n2026-10-25T09:14:29Z /root SUITE_SAFE_BOUNDARY_HANDOFF_REQUEST: Rechecked SUITE owner KimiCode-defect-scan (claim since 08:08Z; owner process 1072398 still live, but claim scope now states short local-mock provider-client reproduction). The previously observed make/npm/run_tests/node-test process tree PIDs 45708/64644/64659/64666/64677 are absent; no suite result or claim release is recorded after the 08:59Z progress entry. Requested via shared coordination record: report terminal suite result/log location and release SUITE, or explicitly transfer it at a safe boundary. Claim remains protected; no local suite started and no ownership change made.\n2026-10-25T09:16:00Z /root PLAN-10_PR-10c_REBASE_EVIDENCE_REFRESH: Candidate rebased onto origin/main 596879597d677a3fc634958cd08741cf4c93f4af at 1b43e5ac4d91551162d3550e77a9ccf9e330f1fd (3 commits ahead; 12 files; diff-check clean). Fresh requirements enforcement PASS: 123 rows (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open); 12 qualification rows remain explicitly deferred. Independent reviewer ACCEPT exact head. Main CI40179733923 and CodeQL40179733832 remain in progress; SUITE claim directory absent, no local test process observed.\n2026-10-25T09:18:00Z /root SUITE_SAFE_BOUNDARY_STATUS_REQUEST: SUITE claim now names KimiCode-defect-scan on v1/defect-provider-client-blockers for serial focused validation after main advanced to 5968795. The previous claim had no owner.json while its directory existed, so no takeover or local tests occurred. Please confirm exact command/worktree, whether the validation is active, expected safe-boundary completion, and release/handoff when finished. PR #215 exact-head CI is running remotely; this request does not interrupt or reassign the claim.\n2026-10-25T09:22:30Z /root CLAIM_RELEASE QUAL108_TERMINAL_MATRIX_WORKSHEET: No edits made. Found an existing protected FILE_docs_v1.0.0_TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md claim on the parallel v1/terminal-matrix-rc4-worksheet lane; its owner status is awaiting a next eligible RC, so this duplicate worksheet lane was released without taking or modifying the file claim.\n2026-10-25T09:23:00Z /root PLAN-