{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T09:47:01.119Z","ordinal":335656,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17267-b4a8-7073-9d2a-32da76e0ee35","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_060b64278a9dfb15016addd01453d481a08a8784e3327ff30e","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"I found a likely lifecycle bug: after a contained version-probe child has already exited, `runIsolatedProcess` still invokes its emergency-kill path. That path starts a repeating cgroup cleanup timer that is normally cleared by the child’s `close` event—but the `close` listener has already run, so the timer can keep the evaluator alive. I’m testing that hypothesis against the isolated failure before making a source change."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1792921620348,"completed_at_ms":1792921621119}}
