{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T11:07:13.280Z","ordinal":336962,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17267-b4a8-7073-9d2a-32da76e0ee35","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-1a0b564d-c9aa-4380-9a6b-6d710d12d79d","process_id":"49475","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git fetch origin main >/dev/null 2>&1; git rev-parse origin/main; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | sed -n '1,110p'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md | rg -n -i -C 3 'rc|pre-release|pre-rc|release candidate|enforce|t2|custod|t4|terminal'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md | rg -n 'open|partial|implemented|tested|REQ-QUAL|REQ-REL|REQ-AGT-010|REQ-AGT-118' | tail -n 60"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git fetch origin main >/dev/null 2>&1; git rev-parse origin/main; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | sed -n '1,110p'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md | rg -n -i -C 3 'rc|pre-release|pre-rc|release candidate|enforce|t2|custod|t4|terminal'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md | rg -n 'open|partial|implemented|tested|REQ-QUAL|REQ-REL|REQ-AGT-010|REQ-AGT-118' | tail -n 60"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"ae69fe03b935006ccda12b7a28f49f610d064617\n# Nexus Code v1.0.0: release qualification procedure\n\nThis is the procedure that decides whether a release candidate (RC) may become v1.0.0. It defines:\n\n- the environments;\n- the workflow matrix;\n- the evidence each step must produce;\n- explicit pass/fail gates.\n\nThree separate questions are judged and recorded separately:\n\n| Question | Who answers it |\n|---|---|\n| **Implementation self-assessment** | Did the implementer's tests pass? |\n| **Product qualification** | Did the RC meet these gates on real workflows? |\n| **Independent acceptance** | Did a reviewer other than the implementer agree? |\n\nA gate passes only on archived evidence bound to the source commit or installed RC artifact that the gate evaluates. Source-level evidence names the exact source commit; installed-RC evidence names both that commit and the installed package digest. A green test suite alone never qualifies the product.\n\n## 1.1 Release-candidate lifecycle and evidence identity\n\nThe release sequence has five distinct stages. Passing an earlier stage is a prerequisite for the next stage, not a substitute for it. Every G0–G4 acceptance ID remains mandatory; the stage determines which exact input and evidence it evaluates, not whether the check applies.\n\n1. **Pre-RC source gates.** Before creating an RC tag, run required source CI and every G0–G4 check whose acceptance method evaluates source, a source-built test binary, or an environment without requiring a published RC. Record the full commit ID and check results. Source checks do not establish behavior of the installed package.\n2. **RC artifact construction.** After the required owner authorization, create the version-matched RC tag on that exact source commit and use the repository release workflow to build and publish the RC artifacts. Record the workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and provenance. The workflow-produced artifacts are the candidates for qualification; a local build or a different commit is not interchangeable. RC artifact publication is not product qualification or final release acceptance.\n3. **RC artifact gates.** Before installed-RC product qualification, run every G0–G4 check whose acceptance method requires the RC archive, RC attestation/release, or workflow-produced artifact. This includes ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08. ACC-PKG checks that explicitly require an installed package run against this RC as specified by their test method. Record the RC tag commit, workflow run, artifact digests, and each check result. A source-level analogue does not replace an artifact-bound check.\n4. **Installed-RC qualification.** Install the workflow-produced RC package using the documented procedure and run the applicable product, provider, task-quality, terminal, installation, and independent-acceptance gates in §§4–8. Bind each result to both the RC source commit and installed package digest. If a source change or rebuilt artifact changes either identity, rerun every affected gate against the new candidate and retain prior results as historical evidence.\n5. **Stable promotion and publication.** After exact-RC acceptance and G6 pass, create a stable-version commit directly on the accepted RC commit, changing only the synchronized version metadata required for v1.0.0. Record both commits and the version-only diff. Run required source CI and all applicable source G0–G4 checks on this exact stable-version commit before tagging. If any other source changes, restart RC construction and qualification. Then create the `v1.0.0` tag on that checked commit and build a draft release. Keep its assets unpublished while verifying the stable artifact identity, provenance, package contents, installation, and publication metadata. Compare the stable package contents with the accepted RC; if packaged behavior or content differs beyond version-specific metadata, rerun affected installed-RC qualification gates and obtain independent acceptance for the stable artifact. Publish the draft only after these checks pass and the signed acceptance disposition is recorded. Record the published digests and provenance.\n\nThe final G6 decision in §10 applies to promoting the accepted RC toward a stable release. It requires the applicable gates to pass for the accepted RC and authorizes the version-only stable commit and its source checks, followed by the stable tag and draft build; it does not waive source CI, artifact identity, installed-RC qualification, or any threshold. Public publication is a separate post-build gate in stage 5 above. The release workflow must keep stable assets in draft state until stable artifact checks pass. Source verification at integration 6a16cb6 confirms the tag-triggered release workflow now supports published RC prereleases and draft stable releases. The earlier immediate-stable-publication source blocker is resolved; an actual stable draft build, artifact verification, signed acceptance, and deliberate publication are still required and remain unproven until their run evidence is recorded.\n\nExact-RC requirements records identify at least one implementer and an independent reviewer. For a blocking requirement recorded as `tested` instead of `product-qualified`, the cited decision must be explicitly allowlisted for that requirement in the approved qualification-exceptions table below, and its `DECISIONS.md` section must contain a matching requirement-specific line of the form `Qualification applicability: REQ-... = NOT REQUIRED ...`. A record-supplied or unrelated decision cannot authorize an exception. The record must include digest-bound evidence for every `ACC-*` criterion in that requirement's ledger Acceptance column.\n\nThe post-RC closure requirements listed below may remain `open`, `partial`, or `implemented` in the source ledger at the RC commit because their remaining acceptance is completed during G6 or installed-RC qualification. The bare `--enforce` invocation is the pre-RC source gate: it checks every other B/RR row against the source threshold and reports mapped rows as deferred, not accepted. At G6, the exact-RC invocation must provide a record meeting the normal B/RR status threshold and digest-bound evidence for every criterion in this table. The table also supplies the criterion mapping for rows whose ledger points to an ACCEPTANCE section instead of naming ACC IDs. The source ledger is never rewritten by the record. Any below-tested required row omitted from this table still fails.\n\n<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:START -->\n### Qualification-only requirements for exact-RC enforcement\n\n| Requirement | Acceptance criteria required in the exact-RC record | Remaining stage |\n|---|---|---|\n| REQ-REL-003 | ACC-PLAT | Installed-RC platform and Node-version matrix |\n| REQ-AGT-002 | ACC-VER-03, ACC-VER-04, ACC-VER-09, ACC-QUAL-T2, ACC-QUAL-T3, ACC-QUAL-T4 | Installed-RC T2/T3/T4 outcome thresholds |\n| REQ-AGT-010 | ACC-TRUST-04 | Independent acceptance of the DEC-04 v1 subset |\n| REQ-PRV-003 | ACC-INF-10 | Installed-RC standalone and absent-gateway behavior |\n| REQ-REL-005 | ACC-SUP-04, ACC-SUP-05 | Exact-RC security and dependency artifact checks |\n| REQ-AGT-110 | ACC-CONT-10, ACC-GOV-06 | Installed-RC continuity and independent acceptance |\n| REQ-PRV-111 | ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC provider verification |\n| REQ-REL-114 | ACC-SUP-08 | Exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility |\n| REQ-QUAL-101 | ACC-QUAL-T2 | Installed-RC held-out T2 qualification |\n| REQ-QUAL-107 | ACC-PRV-STANDALONE, ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC standalone and provider matrix |\n| REQ-QUAL-108 | ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y, ACC-TUI-MANUAL | CI PTY checks and installed-RC real-terminal matrix |\n| REQ-QUAL-109 | ACC-QUAL-T3 | Installed-RC T3 long-task qualification |\n<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:END -->\n\n<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:START -->\n### Approved exact-RC qualification exceptions\n\n| Requirement | Approved decision | Scope |\n|---|---|---|\n<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:END -->\n\n## 1. Rules\n\n1. The RC is built and published by the release workflow from a clean tag. Its version is identical across all components (REQ-REL-103).\n2. All qualification runs use the **installed RC package**, installed with the documented one-line command. They never use a checkout build. The only exception is CI unit and PTY suites, which run from source at the same commit.\n3. Thresholds (DEC-05) are frozen before the first M5 run. A failing gate is fixed in code and the run is repeated as `rc.N+1`. A threshold is never relaxed after results are known.\n4. Evidence goes to `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/`. The directory contains:\n   - `manifest.json`: commit, package sha256, environment, model fingerprint, dates;\n   - raw outputs;\n   - a `SHA256SUMS` file.\n\n   Secrets are redacted before commit.\n5. Any step that cannot run in the available environment is recorded as **NOT RUN** with its reason. A NOT RUN on a blocker gate fails the gate.\n\n## 2. Environments\n\n| ID | Environment | Used for |\n|---|---|---|\n| E1 | GitHub Actions: ubuntu-22.04 and ubuntu-24.04; Node 22 and 24; pinned Rust | Unit, integration and PTY suites; packaging; reproducibility |\n| E2 | Docker clean images: ubuntu:22.04, ubuntu:24.04, debian:12, fedora:40. Each with no Node, then with Node 20, Node 22 and Node 24. Non-root user. | Installer, upgrade, rollback, uninstall, platform failure messages |\n| E3 | Operator dev box: Linux x86-64, real terminals (xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal) | Terminal matrix, live sessions |\n| E4 | Homelab-ai gateway, the **only** inference path (DEC-16): direct, and through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` | Task-quality runs, standalone qualification, T3/T4 |\n| E5 | Cloud, small spend: ChatGPT sign-in (experimental tier) and OpenRouter with a pinned model; OpenAI and Anthropic keys if added | Provider verify; one live task per supported cloud provider |\n\n## 3. Gate checklist (G0–G4: automated acceptance IDs)\n\nEvery ACC ID below is defined in the linked spec. The plan for each spec names the test that implements it. Run each check at the lifecycle stage dictated by its acceptance method in §1.1: source-applicable checks before the RC tag; checks requiring the RC archive, attestation, release, or installed package after RC construction; environment-specific checks in their declared environment. Bind every result to the exact source commit and, when artifact-dependent, the RC package digest. A source test or local build does not replace an artifact-bound check, and no G0–G4 ID is complete until all of its applicable checks pass.\n\n| Gate | Acceptance IDs | Spec |\n|---|---|---|\n| Safety | ACC-SAFE-01 to ACC-SAFE-10 | SPEC-01 |\n| Process ownership | ACC-PROC-01 to ACC-PROC-08 (ACC-PROC-07 is the load test, run in E3) | SPEC-02 |\n| Untrusted inputs | ACC-TRUST-01 to ACC-TRUST-09 | SPEC-03 |\n| Continuity | ACC-CONT-01 to ACC-CONT-09 (ACC-CONT-10 is in §8) | SPEC-04 |\n| Inference | ACC-INF-01 to ACC-INF-09 (ACC-INF-10 is in §4) | SPEC-05 |\n| Packaging | ACC-PKG-01 to ACC-PKG-09 | SPEC-06 |\n| Supply chain | ACC-SUP-01 to ACC-SUP-08 (artifact-bound ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08 after RC construction) | SPEC-07 |\n| Persistence | ACC-PER-01 to ACC-PER-07 | SPEC-08 |\n| Governance | ACC-GOV-01 to ACC-GOV-06 | SPEC-09 |\n| Verification | ACC-VER-01 to ACC-VER-09 | SPEC-11 |\n| Upgrade | ACC-UPG-01 to ACC-UPG-14 | SPEC-12 |\n\n\n### 3.1 Acceptance IDs defined in this file\n\nThese are retained commitments from REQUIREMENTS §2 and cross-cutting checks.\n\n| ID | Check | Pass condition |\n|---|---|---|\n| ACC-TUI-STEER | PTY: submit a task; while a tool runs, type steering text and press Enter; also queue a steer before a cancel | Steering is applied at the next step boundary. Unapplied steering is returned to the composer. Nothing is dropped silently (existing `sidecar_steering_diff` plus PTY s6). |\n12-## Milestones\n13-\n14-```\n15:M0 Foundation ──► M1 Safety floor ──────────────► M3 Continuity & inference ──► RC1 ──► M5 Qualification ──► M6 Release\n16-        │               │                                ▲                                  ▲\n17-        │               └──► M2 Product parity & supply chain (parallel) ──────────────────┤\n18-        │                                                                                   │\n--\n22-\n23-| Milestone | Scope (plans) | Deliverables | Exit gate | Effort |\n24-|---|---|---|---|---|\n25:| **M0 Foundation** | PLAN-08 task 1 (test HOME isolation); PLAN-06 task 3 (version sync). Owner action X1 (stale local tags deleted) is already done.; PLAN-09 tasks 1, 2, 5 (ledger checker in report mode, historical banners, cheap doc truth fixes) | Tests never touch the real HOME. One version identity. The ledger is enforced in CI. | **G0**: ACC-PER-03, ACC-PKG-03, ACC-GOV-01/03 | 2–4 ed |\n26-| **M1 Safety floor** (critical path) | PLAN-01 (effect classes, DEC-01 posture, verifier gating, REPL approvals, read-only masking, argv sandbox, tripwire); PLAN-02 (process registry, cancel and shutdown sweep, bounds); PLAN-03 (project `.env` allowlist, CIDR locality, SSRF-safe fetch, skills/knowledge trust, plugin directories, EXT-004); PLAN-11 PR-11a/11b (parser, binding) | Untrusted input cannot cause unapproved exec, egress or configuration changes. Stop means stopped. No false VERIFIED from a filename coincidence. | **G1**: all ACC-SAFE, ACC-PROC, ACC-TRUST, ACC-VER-01..04 | 15–25 ed |\n27-| **M2 Product parity and supply chain** (parallel with M1 after PLAN-01 PR-1b) | PLAN-06 (unified launcher with the TUI as the packaged default, doc commands, doctor, installer); PLAN-07 (notices, SBOM, provenance, CI matrix, `cli/dist` untracked, SECURITY.md, CHANGELOG); PLAN-12 (CLI and TUI upgrade engine) | The installed product equals the tested product. Compliant release assets. In-place upgrade safely verifies and swaps releases. | **G2**: ACC-PKG-01..09, ACC-SUP-01..07, ACC-UPG-01..06 | 8–14 ed |\n28-| **M3 Continuity and inference** | PLAN-04 (resume, durable work units, accounting, error path, stagnation, team semantics); PLAN-05 code tasks (server-kind discovery, compact-and-retry, error bounds, timeouts, parser robustness, receipts, startup probe, decoupling, CA); PLAN-11 PR-11c..e; PLAN-10 harness tasks 1–7, 9, 10, 13 | Resume and compaction never lose state. Standalone sizing works. Eval harness ready. | **G3**: ACC-CONT-01..09, ACC-INF-01..09, ACC-VER-05..09, eval self-tests | 15–25 ed |\n29-| **M4 Persistence hygiene** (parallel with M2/M3) | PLAN-08 tasks 2–10 | Private state permissions, retention/GC, corruption reporting, schema policy | **G4**: ACC-PER-01..07 | 5–8 ed |\n30:| **RC1** | After PLAN-09 task 7's pre-RC source-ledger reconciliation and enforce gate, tag `v1.0.0-rc.1` (owner approves publishing a prerelease; X7) | RC build installed through the documented command | G0–G4 green on the exact RC source; pre-RC requirements enforcement passed | <1 ed |\n31:| **M5 Qualification** | PLAN-10 task 11 (T2 held-out 5×, T3, T4, standalone stripped-proxy profiles, provider verify); task 12 (terminal matrix); ACC-SUP-08 cross-runner reproducibility; independent acceptance (X5) of continuity and of the RC | Qualification evidence archive, scorer verdict table, independent reports | **G5**: ACCEPTANCE §4–§8 all PASS | 10–20 calendar days. About 84 h of serial inference for T2, plus T3/T4/standalone. Excludes fix loops. |\n32:| **Fix loop(s)** | Defects found in M5, landed as `rc.N` | Re-run the failed gate subsets, plus regression subsets | G5 | 0–15 ed per loop (unknown) |\n33:| **M6 Release** | PLAN-09 task 7 (verify the pre-RC source-ledger reconciliation and enforcement evidence; record exact-RC dispositions in the acceptance record without mutating the accepted RC source); docs sign-off; release notes; tag `v1.0.0` (X7) | Published v1.0.0 with notices, SBOM and attestation | **G6**: ACCEPTANCE §10 checklist | 2–4 ed |\n34-\n35-**Total implementation:** about 46–78 ed (the sum of M0–M4 and M6). **Qualification:** 2–4 calendar weeks. **Fix loops:** unknown. A plausible range is 0–2 loops.\n36-\n--\n38-\n39-The longest dependency chain is:\n40-\n41:**M0 → M1 → M3 → RC1 → M5 (T2 held-out runs) → M6**\n42-\n43-- M1 comes first because the posture change (DEC-01) alters behaviour that every later test, eval and acceptance run depends on. Qualifying before it would have to be redone.\n44:- M3 is on the path because resume (AGT-01), work-unit durability (AGT-02a) and standalone sizing (PRV-06) are blockers, and the T4 class 9 test (SIGTERM, then resume) needs them.\n45-- M5 is bounded by serial inference on the single gateway host.\n46-\n47-When several agents work at once, the parallel lanes, hot-file serialisation and the single-`GATEWAY` lock in [CONCURRENCY.md](CONCURRENCY.md) govern the order in which work merges.\n48-\n49:Off the critical path, but must finish before RC1:\n50-\n51-- M2, M4;\n52:- the 40 held-out T2 tasks and 8 T3 tasks (agent-authored), with their manifest sealed **before** RC1;\n53-- the stripping proxy and the conformance fixtures.\n54-\n55-## Release gates\n--\n59-| G0 | End of M0 | Foundation acceptance IDs pass. `make test` passes on a clean clone and leaves the real HOME untouched. |\n60-| G1 | End of M1 | All safety acceptance IDs pass in CI. Existing PTY suites stay green. No new skipped tests. |\n61-| G2 | End of M2 | A package smoke run in a PTY shows the TUI. The doc-command test passes. Release dry-run assets are complete. |\n62:| G3 | End of M3 | Continuity, inference and verification acceptance IDs pass. The eval harness self-tests pass, including the T4 smoke. |\n63-| G4 | End of M4 | Persistence acceptance IDs pass. |\n64:| G5 | After the RC | ACCEPTANCE §4–§8 pass. The DEC-05 thresholds are met. Independent reports are filed. |\n65:| G6 | Release | The ledger checker passes in enforce mode, so every B/RR row is ≥ tested and B rows are product-qualified where ACCEPTANCE requires it. Docs are signed off. Owner approval X7 is given. |\n66-\n67-## Classification of the work\n68-\n--\n78-| Risk | Effect | Mitigation |\n79-|---|---|---|\n80-| The DEC-01 default change breaks many test fixtures | M1 takes longer | PR-1a lands the classes behind a constant; PR-1b flips the default with mechanical fixture updates |\n81:| The gateway host is unavailable or thermally limited during M5 | M5 is delayed | Serial runs with resumable runner; schedule against the thermal-soak findings; T2 runs are resumable per task |\n82-| Held-out results miss the thresholds | Fix loops | Thresholds are pre-registered, so they are not moved after the fact. The fix is a code change, and the affected run classes are re-run. |\n83:| Parser restriction (PLAN-11) lowers the tool-call rate on text-only models | Task quality falls | Recorded fixtures; one-RC escape hatch; the qualification measures it |\n84-| Independent reviewer is unavailable (X5) | G5 cannot be met honestly | The owner must supply a reviewer. The audit does not substitute self-assessment for it. |\n85-\n86-## What must be re-run after implementation\n87-\n88:Everything marked RT or MEAS in AUDIT §5 must be re-run on the RC:\n89-\n90-- the PTY scripts in `evidence/D_pty`;\n91-- the probes in `evidence/prv`, `evidence/a2probe`, `evidence/probes` and `evidence/repro`;\n92-- the installer and doctor runs;\n93-- the memory measurements.\n94-\n95:The baseline suite (905 CLI + 266 Rust tests) must be re-run at every gate. The two live provider verifications and the live end-to-end run (EVIDENCE §3) must be repeated on the RC with pinned models.\n162:| REQ-AGT-108 | Audit | No false stagnation when state identity is unknown. | workflow | `execution_tracking.ts` | TEST (ACC-CONT-09; test:cli/test/execution_tracking.test.ts) | tested | ACC-CONT-09 | RR | AGT-09 | SPEC-04 / PLAN-04 |\n163:| REQ-AGT-110 | HIST-09 | Independent acceptance of continuity, compaction and truncation recovery. | qualification | — | DOC (\"pending\") | open | ACC-CONT-10, ACC-GOV-06 | RR | HIST-09 | SPEC-04 / PLAN-09 |\n164:| REQ-AGT-111 | EXECUTION_CONVERGENCE §10 | A single step implementation for the main and subagent loops. | maintainability | `agent.ts:5298-5431` | SRC (AGT-05) | open | — | P (v1: document and add `measureAdmission`) | AGT-05 | SPEC-04 / PLAN-04 |\n170:| REQ-PRV-101 | Standalone commitment | Context discovery for vLLM, llama.cpp, LM Studio and Ollama, with the source labelled. | standalone workflow | `provider_capabilities.ts` | TEST (PRV-06; test:cli/test/server_context_discovery.test.ts::\"discovery against a local server\") | tested | ACC-INF-01 | **B** | PRV-06 | SPEC-05 / PLAN-05 |\n171:| REQ-PRV-102 | TOP_TIER I-05 (carried) | A capacity rejection leads to one compact-and-retry, then an actionable error. llama.cpp, LM Studio and Ollama bodies are classified. | standalone / failure | `provider_recovery.ts:82,106`; `agent.ts:5072` | TEST (PRV-07; test:cli/test/provider_recovery_agent.test.ts::\"capacity rejection handling (ACC-INF-02)\") | tested | ACC-INF-02 | **B** | PRV-06, PRV-07 | SPEC-05 / PLAN-05 |\n172:| REQ-PRV-103 | CRED-003 (carried) | Error text is bounded and redacted on every path. | safety | `client.ts:903,1636,1689`, `oauth.ts` | TEST (PRV-03; test:cli/test/provider_robustness.test.ts::\"listModels and generateEmbedding huge error bodies are bounded and redacted (ACC-INF-03)\") | tested | ACC-INF-03 | RR | PRV-03 | SPEC-05 / PLAN-05 |\n173:| REQ-PRV-104 | Audit | Timeouts and cancel on every network call. First-byte, idle and total timeouts. Bounded replays. | failure | `client.ts`, `embeddings.ts`, `model_catalog.ts` | TEST (PRV-05, PRV-10; test:cli/test/provider_robustness.test.ts::\"watchdog first-byte and idle timeouts reject when server hangs or stalls (ACC-INF-04)\") | tested | ACC-INF-04 | RR | PRV-05, PRV-10 | SPEC-05 / PLAN-05 |\n174:| REQ-PRV-105 | Audit | Stream parser robustness, with recorded real-server fixtures. | compatibility | `client.ts:1326-1483` | TEST (PRV-04; test:cli/test/provider_fixes.test.ts::\"stream parser handles tool name chunks, repeated tool names, and object arguments (PRV-04 / REQ-PRV-105)\", test:cli/test/provider_robustness.test.ts::\"empty stream re-request records executions: 2 in receipt (ACC-INF-06)\") | tested | ACC-INF-05, ACC-INF-06 | RR | PRV-04 | SPEC-05 / PLAN-05 |\n175:| REQ-PRV-106 | Standalone commitment; HIST-08; DEC-16 | Standalone qualification: (a) live runs through the gateway-stripping proxy, in plain and emulated-server profiles; (b) server-kind conformance fixtures. | standalone (product principle) | `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` | TEST (test:cli/test/standalone_profiles.test.ts); eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs; **RT 2026-10-17 @a2abdf7:** live dry run through the gateway, llama.cpp profile, 1 development task VERIFIED with hidden and regression tests passing (`evidence/live/standalone_dryrun_2026-10-17/`). Gap: `eval/run.mjs` always passes `--context-limit`, so the discovered context is never the source in profile runs (boundary request logged). Product-qualified needs the ACCEPTANCE §4.2 matrix on the RC. | tested | ACC-INF-10, ACCEPTANCE §4.2 | **B** | HIST-08 | SPEC-05 / PLAN-05, PLAN-10 |\n176:| REQ-PRV-107 | TOP_TIER I-07 | Local receipts (opt-out). | evidence | `client.ts:561-569`, `usage.ts` | TEST (B §6 G1; test:cli/test/provider_robustness.test.ts::\"local receipts are recorded with origin_class: local and opt out with NEXUS_RECEIPTS=0 (REQ-PRV-107)\") | tested | ACC-INF-06 | RR | B §6 G1 | SPEC-05 / PLAN-05 |\n177:| REQ-PRV-109 | Standalone commitment | No homelab identifiers in code or docs. The gateway token path is configurable. | standalone / honesty | `client.ts:66-79,751-764`, `docs/LOCAL_SERVERS.md` | TEST (PRV-11, PRV-17; test:cli/test/task_class.test.ts::\"ACC-INF-08: code and docs carry no homelab-specific identifiers (t5820, engineering/b0, A770, 18010)\") | tested | ACC-INF-08 | RR | PRV-11, PRV-17 | SPEC-05 / PLAN-05 |\n178:| REQ-PRV-110 | Audit | Custom CA is documented and validated by doctor. | safety (prevents an insecure workaround) | launcher, `doctor.ts` | TEST (PRV-18; test:cli/test/inference_transport.test.ts::\"ACC-INF-09: doctor validates NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS in ~/.config/nexus/config.env\") | tested | ACC-INF-09 | RR | PRV-18 | SPEC-05 / PLAN-05 |\n179:| REQ-PRV-111 | DEC-06 | Live `providers verify` for each provider listed as supported. The others are labelled experimental. | compatibility claims | `provider_cli.ts` | **RT 2026-10-14 @db1ca55:** chatgpt (gpt-6-luna) PASS, openrouter (openrouter/free) PASS. **RT 2026-10-16 @6151a23+4d82578, pinned models:** open