\n199:| REQ-REL-110 | SCAN-003 (carried) | The vulnerability gate fails closed. | security gate honesty | `security_gates.sh` | TEST (ACC-SUP-04; test:cli/test/security_gates.test.ts, scripts/security_gates.sh) | tested | ACC-SUP-04 | RR | REL-07 | SPEC-07 / PLAN-07 |\n200:| REQ-REL-111 | Audit; DEC-12 | CI matrix for Node 22/24; release, reproducibility and evaluator builds use Node 22; pinned toolchain and MSRV, engines field, dist freshness (untracked). | compatibility | `ci.yml`, `release.yml`, `repro.yml` | At exact candidate `7c46a6d52095588f48579d9a96c5b2d526bdb3d9`, PR #150 CI run `39866110578` passed both required matrix jobs (Node 22 job `120128589470`; Node 24 job `120128589221`). The same revision declares Node `>=22` in both package manifests, uses pinned Rust/MSRV, sets release and reproducibility packaging to Node 22, and runs the `cli/dist` freshness check in the matrix and package workflows. Exact-candidate Linux packaging remains a separate active source gate; this row covers ACC-SUP-05 only. | tested | ACC-SUP-05 | RR | REL-13, MNT-01 | SPEC-07 / PLAN-07 |\n201:| REQ-REL-112 | REL-004 (carried) | SECURITY.md, CHANGELOG.md, release body taken from release notes. | supportability | root, `release.yml` | TEST (ACC-SUP-06; test:SECURITY.md, CHANGELOG.md, release.yml) | tested | ACC-SUP-06 | RR | HIST-07, MNT-05 | SPEC-07 / PLAN-07 |\n202:| REQ-REL-113 | Audit | Remove dead CI and tracked bytecode. | maintainability | `.gitlab-ci.yml`, `*.pyc` | TEST (ACC-SUP-07) | tested | ACC-SUP-07 | RR | MNT-02, EVL-007 | SPEC-07 / PLAN-07 |\n203:| REQ-REL-114 | REL-001 (carried) | Cross-runner reproducibility, demonstrated once for the RC. | supply chain | `repro.yml` | UNV | open | ACC-SUP-08 | RR | E §6 | SPEC-07 / PLAN-07 |\n204:| REQ-REL-115 | Scope addition | CLI (`nexus upgrade`) and TUI (`/upgrade`) compare installed version with releases and safely upgrade to latest stable or pinned version. | user maintenance / lifecycle | `cli/src/upgrade.ts`, `cli/src/s