§2.2 | DOC (§2.2); test:cli/test/check_requirements.test.ts::\"the ledger checker rejects a blocker without spec, plan or acceptance\" | tested | ACC-GOV-02 | **B** | HIST-01, HIST-11 | SPEC-09 / PLAN-09 |\n227:| REQ-DX-105 | Audit | User docs make no claim contradicted by source, contain no homelab IDs, and make no parity claims. | honesty | docs | ACC-GOV-04 (scripts/security_gates.sh) | tested | ACC-GOV-04 | RR | as listed | SPEC-09 / PLAN-09 |\n228:| REQ-DX-106 | HIST-10 | Open v1 work is tracked as GitHub issues under a milestone. | process | GitHub | RT 2026-10-17: [v1.0.0 milestone](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/milestone/1), 7 open plan-group issues ([#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1)–[#7](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/7)); issue bodies link affected plan tasks and ledger IDs. | tested | ACC-GOV-05 | RR | HIST-10 | SPEC-09 / PLAN-09 |\n234:| REQ-QUAL-101 | TOP_TIER Q1; DEC-05 | Held-out T2 evaluation: 40 tasks, ≥ 50% external, sealed manifest. | product maturity | `eval/` | HIST (6 tuned tasks) | open | ACCEPTANCE §6.1 | **B** | EVL-001 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\n235:| REQ-QUAL-102 | DEC-05 | Matched conditions with a model fingerprint. | validity | `eval/run.mjs`, `eval/validate.mjs` | TEST (EVL-004; test:cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts::\"a qualification run is refused without a model fingerprint\") | tested | ACC-QUAL-T2 (ACCEPTANCE §6.1) | **B** | EVL-004 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\n236:| REQ-QUAL-103 | DEC-05 | 5 runs per task and configuration; Goose and OpenCode as peers. | statistics | `eval/run.mjs`, `eval/score.mjs` | TEST (`eval_harness.test.ts`: peer version/budget forwarding, installed RC/version/package pin, Nexus/provider-limit parity, paired fingerprint/limit/sampling/budget/version and 5-run checks; commits `ef2d040`, `b27ae04`; [validation record](../reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-10_PR-10d/validation.md)); UNV (live M5 runs) | tested | ACC-QUAL-T2 (ACCEPTANCE §6.1) | **B** | EVL-001 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\n237:| REQ-QUAL-104 | DEC-05 | Separately reported metrics, including false VERIFIED = 0. | honesty | `eval/score.mjs` | TEST (EVL-005; test:cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts, test:cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts) | tested | ACC-QUAL-T2 (ACCEPTANCE §6.1) | **B** | EVL-005 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\n238:| REQ-QUAL-105 | TOP_TIER Q6; DEC-05 | T4 fault injection: 9 classes × 5 runs (DEC-05 amendment 2026-10-17: union of the nine distinct scenarios retained), 100% truthful outcomes. | failure / recovery | `eval/model_proxy.mjs`, `eval/score.mjs` | TEST (EVL-001; test:cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts::\"the model proxy injects each scheduled fault\", test:cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts::\"T4 smoke\") | tested | ACC-QUAL-T4 (ACCEPTANCE §6.2) | **B** | EVL-001 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\n239:| REQ-QUAL-106 | Audit | Scoring integrity (symmetric infra handling, contamination, hidden tests). | validity | `eval/infra.mjs`, `eval/score.mjs`, `eval/run.mjs` | TEST (EVL-002, EVL-003; test:cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts::\"contaminated runs leave the pass rate\", test:cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts::\"infrastructure reruns use one rule\") | tested | ACC-QUAL-T2 (ACCEPTANCE §6.1) | **B** | EVL-002, EVL-003, VER-07 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\n240:| REQ-QUAL-107 | Standalone; DEC-06 | Standalone and provider live matrix. | standalone | — | HIST | open | ACCEPTANCE §4.2, §4.3 | **B** | HIST-08 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\n241:| REQ-QUAL-108 | Audit | PTY CI plus a manual real-terminal matrix. | terminal acceptance | `cli/test/tui_*`; ACCEPTANCE §5.3 | TEST (PTY suites in CI); UNV (real terminals) | partial | ACCEPTANCE §5 | RR | D §6 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\n242:| REQ-QUAL-109 | eval/README T3 | T3 long tasks: 8 × 5. | long-task workflow | `eval/` | — | open | ACCEPTANCE §6.3 | RR | EVL-001 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\n243:| REQ-QUAL-110 | Audit | T1 self-test and a T4 smoke run in `make test`. | regression | `eval_harness.test.ts` | TEST (test:cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts::\"T4 smoke: an overloaded endpoint is waited out\") | tested | ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | RR | — | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\n247:These are REQ-CON-101 to REQ-CON-107, specified in [SPEC-C1](specs/SPEC-C1-contest-submission-track.md). The submission was **completed** (2026-10-14), judging has concluded, and no contest freeze applies (DEC-13 status amendment). Every row remains post-contest hardening with status `open`; no evidence status is promoted by this clarification. The evidence is `evidence/G_contest_eval.md` (CON-001 to CON-014).\n263:- REQ-REL-106 (self uninstall).\n276:| New v1 rows (§3) | 92 | **31 B**, 58 RR, 3 P. 79 open, 9 partial (REQ-SEC-118, REQ-PRV-101, REQ-PRV-103, REQ-PRV-105, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-PER-106, REQ-OPS-101, REQ-QUAL-108, REQ-QUAL-110), 1 implemented (REQ-OPS-103), 4 tested (REQ-SEC-103, REQ-SEC-119, REQ-PER-101, REQ-PER-102). |\n277:| Carried rows (§2.1) | 29 | 14 tested and unchanged (Keep). 1 visually-accepted (REQ-TUI-001). The rest are partial, or have open items mapped to §3. |\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":277723141}},"started_at_ms":1792926433001,"completed_at_ms":1792926433280}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T11:07:14.286Z","ordinal":336963,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a172be-43ee-7a21-b9b0-e4892b9aae13","call_id":"call_664d9cd0b41c4b188fc96ca831b3c565","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.4 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 9901)\nTotal output lines: 243\n\nae69fe03b935006ccda12b7a28f49f610d064617\n# Nexus Code v1.0.0: release qualification procedure\n\nThis is the procedure that decides whether a release candidate (RC) may become v1.0.0. It defines:\n\n- the environments;\n- the workflow matrix;\n- the evidence each step must produce;\n- explicit pass/fail gates.\n\nThree separate questions are judged and recorded separately:\n\n| Question | Who answers it |\n|---|---|\n| **Implementation self-assessment** | Did the implementer's tests pass? |\n| **Product qualification** | Did the RC meet these gates on real workflows? |\n| **Independent acceptance** | Did a reviewer other than the implementer agree? |\n\nA gate passes only on archived evidence bound to the source commit or installed RC artifact that the gate evaluates. Source-level evidence names the exact source commit; installed-RC evidence names both that commit and the installed package digest. A green test suite alone never qualifies the product.\n\n## 1.1 Release-candidate lifecycle and evidence identity\n\nThe release sequence has five distinct stages. Passing an earlier stage is a prerequisite for the next stage, not a substitute for it. Every G0–G4 acceptance ID remains mandatory; the stage determines which exact input and evidence it evaluates, not whether the check applies.\n\n1. **Pre-RC source gates.** Before creating an RC tag, run required source CI and every G0–G4 check whose acceptance method evaluates source, a source-built test binary, or an environment without requiring a published RC. Record the full commit ID and check results. Source checks do not establish behavior of the installed package.\n2. **RC artifact construction.** After the required owner authorization, create the version-matched RC tag on that exact source commit and use the repository release workflow to build and publish the RC artifacts. Record the workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and provenance. The workflow-produced artifacts are the candidates for qualification; a local build or a different commit is not interchangeable. RC artifact publication is not product qualification or final release acceptance.\n3. **RC artifact gates.** Before installed-RC product qualification, run every G0–G4 check whose acceptance method requires the RC archive, RC attestation/release, or workflow-produced artifact. This includes ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08. ACC-PKG checks that explicitly require an installed package run against this RC as specified by their test method. Record the RC tag commit, workflow run, artifact digests, and each check result. A source-level analogue does not replace an artifact-bound check.\n4. **Installed-RC qualification.** Install the workflow-produced RC package using the documented procedure and run the applicable product, provider, task-quality, terminal, installation, and independent-acceptance gates in §§4–8. Bind each result to both the RC source commit and installed package digest. If a source change or rebuilt artifact changes either identity, rerun every affected gate against the new candidate and retain prior results as historical evidence.\n5. **Stable promotion and publication.** After exact-RC acceptance and G6 pass, create a stable-version commit directly on the accepted RC commit, changing only the synchronized version metadata required for v1.0.0. Record both commits and the version-only diff. Run required source CI and all applicable source G0–G4 checks on this exact stable-version commit before tagging. If any other source changes, restart RC construction and qualification. Then create the `v1.0.0` tag on that checked commit and build a draft release. Keep its assets unpublished while verifying the stable artifact identity, provenance, package contents, installation, and publication metadata. Compare the stable package contents with the accepted RC; if packaged behavior or content differs beyond version-specific metadata, rerun affected installed-RC qualification gates and obtain independent acceptance for the stable artifact. Publish the draft only after these checks pass and the signed acceptance disposition is recorded. Record the published digests and provenance.\n\nThe final G6 decision in §10 applies to promoting the accepted RC toward a stable release. It requires the applicable gates to pass for the accepted RC and authorizes the version-only stable commit and its source checks, followed by the stable tag and draft build; it does not waive source CI, artifact identity, installed-RC qualification, or any threshold. Public publication is a separate post-build gate in stage 5 above. The release workflow must keep stable assets in draft state until stable artifact checks pass. Source verification at integration 6a16cb6 confirms the tag-triggered release workflow now supports published RC prereleases and draft stable releases. The earlier immediate-stable-publication source blocker is resolved; an actual stable draft build, artifact verification, signed acceptance, and deliberate publication are still required and remain unproven until their run evidence is recorded.\n\nExact-RC requirements records identify at least one implementer and an independent reviewer. For a blocking requirement recorded as `tested` instead of `product-qualified`, the cited decision must be explicitly allowlisted for that requirement in the approved qualification-exceptions table below, and its `DECISIONS.md` section must contain a matching requirement-specific line of the form `Qualification applicability: REQ-... = NOT REQUIRED ...`. A record-supplied or unrelated decision cannot authorize an exception. The record must include digest-bound evidence for every `ACC-*` criterion in that requirement's ledger Acceptance column.\n\nThe post-RC closure requirements listed below may remain `open`, `partial`, or `implemented` in the source ledger at the RC commit because their remaining acceptance is completed during G6 or installed-RC qualification. The bare `--enforce` invocation is the pre-RC source gate: it checks every other B/RR row against the source threshold and reports mapped rows as deferred, not accepted. At G6, the exact-RC invocation must provide a record meeting the normal B/RR status threshold and digest-bound evidence for every criterion in this table. The table also supplies the criterion mapping for rows whose ledger points to an ACCEPTANCE section instead of naming ACC IDs. The source ledger is never rewritten by the record. Any below-tested required row omitted from this table still fails.\n\n<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:START -->\n### Qualification-only requirements for exact-RC enforcement\n\n| Requirement | Acceptance criteria required in the exact-RC record | Remaining stage |\n|---|---|---|\n| REQ-REL-003 | ACC-PLAT | Installed-RC platform and Node-version matrix |\n| REQ-AGT-002 | ACC-VER-03, ACC-VER-04, ACC-VER-09, ACC-QUAL-T2, ACC-QUAL-T3, ACC-QUAL-T4 | Installed-RC T2/T3/T4 outcome thresholds |\n| REQ-AGT-010 | ACC-TRUST-04 | Independent acceptance of the DEC-04 v1 subset |\n| REQ-PRV-003 | ACC-INF-10 | Installed-RC standalone and absent-gateway behavior |\n| REQ-REL-005 | ACC-SUP-04, ACC-SUP-05 | Exact-RC security and dependency artifact checks |\n| REQ-AGT-110 | ACC-CONT-10, ACC-GOV-06 | Installed-RC continuity and independent acceptance |\n| REQ-PRV-111 | ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC provider verification |\n| REQ-REL-114 | ACC-SUP-08 | Exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility |\n| REQ-QUAL-101 | ACC-QUAL-T2 | Installed-RC held-out T2 qualification |\n| REQ-QUAL-107 | ACC-PRV-STANDALONE, ACC-PRV-LIVE | Installed-RC standalone and provider matrix |\n| REQ-QUAL-108 | ACC-TUI-STEER, ACC-TUI-A11Y, ACC-TUI-MANUAL | CI PTY checks and installed-RC real-terminal matrix |\n| REQ-QUAL-109 | ACC-QUAL-T3 | Installed-RC T3 long-task qualification |\n<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-ONLY:END -->\n\n<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:START -->\n### Approved exact-RC qualification exceptions\n\n| Requirement | Approved decision | Scope |\n|---|---|---|\n<!-- RC-QUALIFICATION-EXCEPTIONS:END -->\n\n## 1. Rules\n\n1. The RC is built and published by the release workflow from a clean tag. Its version is identical across all components (REQ-REL-103).\n2. All qualification runs use the **installed RC package**, installed with the documented one-line command. They never use a checkout build. The only exception is CI unit and PTY suites, which run from source at the same commit.\n3. Thresholds (DEC-05) are frozen before the first M5 run. A failing gate is fixed in code and the run is repeated as `rc.N+1`. A threshold is never relaxed after results are known.\n4. Evidence goes to `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/`. The directory contains:\n   - `manifest.json`: commit, package sha256, environment, model fingerprint, dates;\n   - raw outputs;\n   - a `SHA256SUMS` file.\n\n   Secrets are redacted before commit.\n5. Any step that cannot run in the available environment is recorded as **NOT RUN** with its reason. A NOT RUN on a blocker gate fails the gate.\n\n## 2. Environments\n\n| ID | Environment | Used for |\n|---|---|---|\n| E1 | GitHub Actions: ubuntu-22.04 and ubuntu-24.04; Node 22 and 24; pinned Rust | Unit, integration and PTY suites; packaging; reproducibility |\n| E2 | Docker clean images: ubuntu:22.04, ubuntu:24.04, debian:12, fedora:40. Each with no Node, then with Node 20, Node 22 and Node 24. Non-root user. | Installer, upgrade, rollback, uninstall, platform failure messages |\n| E3 | Operator dev box: Linux x86-64, real terminals (xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal) | Terminal matrix, live sessions |\n| E4 | Homelab-ai gateway, the **only** inference path (DEC-16): direct, and through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` | Task-quality runs, standalone qualification, T3/T4 |\n| E5 | Cloud, small spend: ChatGPT sign-in (experimental tier) and OpenRouter with a pinned model; OpenAI and Anthropic keys if added | Provider verify; one live task per supported cloud provider |\n\n## 3. Gate checklist (G0–G4: automated acceptance IDs)\n\nEvery ACC ID below is defined in…4901 tokens truncated…remains a separate active source gate; this row covers ACC-SUP-05 only. | tested | ACC-SUP-05 | RR | REL-13, MNT-01 | SPEC-07 / PLAN-07 |\n201:| REQ-REL-112 | REL-004 (carried) | SECURITY.md, CHANGELOG.md, release body taken from release notes. | supportability | root, `release.yml` | TEST (ACC-SUP-06; test:SECURITY.md, CHANGELOG.md, release.yml) | tested | ACC-SUP-06 | RR | HIST-07, MNT-05 | SPEC-07 / PLAN-07 |\n202:| REQ-REL-113 | Audit | Remove dead CI and tracked bytecode. | maintainability | `.gitlab-ci.yml`, `*.pyc` | TEST (ACC-SUP-07) | tested | ACC-SUP-07 | RR | MNT-02, EVL-007 | SPEC-07 / PLAN-07 |\n203:| REQ-REL-114 | REL-001 (carried) | Cross-runner reproducibility, demonstrated once for the RC. | supply chain | `repro.yml` | UNV | open | ACC-SUP-08 | RR | E §6 | SPEC-07 / PLAN-07 |\n204:| REQ-REL-115 | Scope addition | CLI (`nexus upgrade`) and TUI (`/upgrade`) compare installed version with releases and safely upgrade to latest stable or pinned version. | user maintenance / lifecycle | `cli/src/upgrade.ts`, `cli/src/slash/session_commands.ts` | TEST (ACC-UPG-01 to ACC-UPG-06; test:cli/test/upgrade.test.ts::\"successfully performs an end-to-end upgrade with atomic symlink swap and verification\", test:cli/test/upgrade_cli.test.ts::\"returns exit code 1 when update is available in --check mode\", test:cli/test/upgrade_tui.test.ts::\"exercises deliberate approval interaction when executing /upgrade in TUI\") | tested | ACC-UPG-01 to ACC-UPG-06 | **B** | REL-14 | SPEC-12 / PLAN-12 |\n205:| REQ-REL-116 | Scope addition | Machine-readable compatibility metadata, download origin & archive extraction safety, pre-migration backups, downgrade state protection, durable provenance, crash recovery, and runtime verification. | installation integrity & lifecycle | `cli/src/upgrade.ts`, `cli/src/compatibility.ts`, `cli/src/tar_safety.ts`, `cli/src/upgrade_journal.ts`, `docs/UPGRADE_SECURITY.md` | TEST (ACC-UPG-07 to ACC-UPG-14; test:cli/test/upgrade_safety.test.ts::\"rejects malicious tar archive with path traversal\", test:cli/test/upgrade_safety.test.ts::\"creates protected config and state backups with 0600 file and 0700 dir permissions\", test:cli/test/upgrade_acceptance.test.ts::\"upgrades from previous release v0.1.0-alpha.2 to v1.0.0 preserving state, configuration and permissions\", test:cli/test/upgrade_acceptance.test.ts::\"refuses downgrade when target release has incompatible state schema version\") | tested | ACC-UPG-07 to ACC-UPG-14 | **B** | REL-15 | SPEC-12 / PLAN-12 |\n212:| REQ-PER-101 | PERS-002 (carried) | `~/.nexus` is 0700 and files are 0600. Doctor repairs both. | privacy on multi-user hosts | `checkpoint.ts`, `flight.ts`, `session.ts`, etc. | MEAS (PER-01) | tested | ACC-PER-01 | RR | PER-01 | SPEC-08 / PLAN-08 |\n213:| REQ-PER-102 | Audit; DEC-11 | Retention and GC; audit log rotation; indexed session listing. | resource / failure | new `retention.ts` | MEAS (PER-02: 916 MB) | tested | ACC-PER-02, ACC-PER-06 | RR | PER-02 | SPEC-08 / PLAN-08 |\n214:| REQ-PER-103 | Audit | The test suite never writes to the real HOME. | hygiene; prerequisite | `state.ts:278-288`; test setup | TEST (ACC-PER-03; test:cli/test/home_isolation.test.ts; docs/reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-08_PR-8a/verification.md) | tested | ACC-PER-03 | RR (M0 prerequisite) | PER-03 | SPEC-08 / PLAN-08 |\n215:| REQ-PER-104 | TOP_TIER P2–P6 | Corrupt and future-schema state is reported and quarantined. Resume ids are unambiguous. | failure | `session.ts:113-239` | TEST (ACC-PER-04; test:cli/test/state_migration.test.ts, cli/test/state.test.ts) | tested | ACC-PER-04 | RR | PER-05 | SPEC-08 / PLAN-08 |\n216:| REQ-PER-105 | Audit | Telemetry is never committable by default. | privacy | `flight.ts:55-59` | TEST (ACC-PER-05; test:cli/test/flight_exclude.test.ts) | tested | ACC-PER-05 | RR | PER-06 | SPEC-08 / PLAN-08 |\n217:| REQ-PER-106 | MATURITY_REVIEW (migration policy) | Documented schema and migration policy with tests. | compatibility | docs, `state.ts` | TEST (ACC-PER-07; test:cli/test/state_migration.test.ts, docs/STATE_COMPATIBILITY.md) | tested | ACC-PER-07 | RR | — | SPEC-08 / PLAN-08 |\n218:| REQ-PER-107 | Audit | Rust atomic write fsyncs the parent directory. | durability | `file_ops.rs:156-182` | SRC (PER-04; core/src/file_ops.rs:188-194) | implemented | — | P | PER-04 | SPEC-08 / PLAN-08 |\n224:| REQ-OPS-101 | HIST-02 | This ledger is authoritative. The historical matrices carry banners. | governance | this file; docs banners | DOC (docs/HISTORICAL.md; reviews banners) | tested | ACC-GOV-02, ACC-GOV-03 | **B** | HIST-02 | SPEC-09 / PLAN-09 |\n225:| REQ-OPS-102 | HIST-02 | A CI checker binds rows to tests and acceptance IDs. | governance | `scripts/check_requirements.mjs` | test:cli/test/check_requirements.test.ts::\"the ledger checker passes the repository ledger in report mode\" | tested | ACC-GOV-01 | RR | HIST-02 | SPEC-09 / PLAN-09 |\n226:| REQ-OPS-103 | HIST-01, HIST-11 | Written dispositions for the Issue #12 open blockers and superseded items. | governance | §2.2 | DOC (§2.2); test:cli/test/check_requirements.test.ts::\"the ledger checker rejects a blocker without spec, plan or acceptance\" | tested | ACC-GOV-02 | **B** | HIST-01, HIST-11 | SPEC-09 / PLAN-09 |\n227:| REQ-DX-105 | Audit | User docs make no claim contradicted by source, contain no homelab IDs, and make no parity claims. | honesty | docs | ACC-GOV-04 (scripts/security_gates.sh) | tested | ACC-GOV-04 | RR | as listed | SPEC-09 / PLAN-09 |\n228:| REQ-DX-106 | HIST-10 | Open v1 work is tracked as GitHub issues under a milestone. | process | GitHub | RT 2026-10-17: [v1.0.0 milestone](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/milestone/1), 7 open plan-group issues ([#1](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1)–[#7](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/7)); issue bodies link affected plan tasks and ledger IDs. | tested | ACC-GOV-05 | RR | HIST-10 | SPEC-09 / PLAN-09 |\n234:| REQ-QUAL-101 | TOP_TIER Q1; DEC-05 | Held-out T2 evaluation: 40 tasks, ≥ 50% external, sealed manifest. | product maturity | `eval/` | HIST (6 tuned tasks) | open | ACCEPTANCE §6.1 | **B** | EVL-001 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\n235:| REQ-QUAL-102 | DEC-05 | Matched conditions with a model fingerprint. | validity | `eval/run.mjs`, `eval/validate.mjs` | TEST (EVL-004; test:cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts::\"a qualification run is refused without a model fingerprint\") | tested | ACC-QUAL-T2 (ACCEPTANCE §6.1) | **B** | EVL-004 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\n236:| REQ-QUAL-103 | DEC-05 | 5 runs per task and configuration; Goose and OpenCode as peers. | statistics | `eval/run.mjs`, `eval/score.mjs` | TEST (`eval_harness.test.ts`: peer version/budget forwarding, installed RC/version/package pin, Nexus/provider-limit parity, paired fingerprint/limit/sampling/budget/version and 5-run checks; commits `ef2d040`, `b27ae04`; [validation record](../reviews/evidence/v1/PLAN-10_PR-10d/validation.md)); UNV (live M5 runs) | tested | ACC-QUAL-T2 (ACCEPTANCE §6.1) | **B** | EVL-001 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\n237:| REQ-QUAL-104 | DEC-05 | Separately reported metrics, including false VERIFIED = 0. | honesty | `eval/score.mjs` | TEST (EVL-005; test:cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts, test:cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts) | tested | ACC-QUAL-T2 (ACCEPTANCE §6.1) | **B** | EVL-005 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\n238:| REQ-QUAL-105 | TOP_TIER Q6; DEC-05 | T4 fault injection: 9 classes × 5 runs (DEC-05 amendment 2026-10-17: union of the nine distinct scenarios retained), 100% truthful outcomes. | failure / recovery | `eval/model_proxy.mjs`, `eval/score.mjs` | TEST (EVL-001; test:cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts::\"the model proxy injects each scheduled fault\", test:cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts::\"T4 smoke\") | tested | ACC-QUAL-T4 (ACCEPTANCE §6.2) | **B** | EVL-001 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\n239:| REQ-QUAL-106 | Audit | Scoring integrity (symmetric infra handling, contamination, hidden tests). | validity | `eval/infra.mjs`, `eval/score.mjs`, `eval/run.mjs` | TEST (EVL-002, EVL-003; test:cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts::\"contaminated runs leave the pass rate\", test:cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts::\"infrastructure reruns use one rule\") | tested | ACC-QUAL-T2 (ACCEPTANCE §6.1) | **B** | EVL-002, EVL-003, VER-07 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\n240:| REQ-QUAL-107 | Standalone; DEC-06 | Standalone and provider live matrix. | standalone | — | HIST | open | ACCEPTANCE §4.2, §4.3 | **B** | HIST-08 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\n241:| REQ-QUAL-108 | Audit | PTY CI plus a manual real-terminal matrix. | terminal acceptance | `cli/test/tui_*`; ACCEPTANCE §5.3 | TEST (PTY suites in CI); UNV (real terminals) | partial | ACCEPTANCE §5 | RR | D §6 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\n242:| REQ-QUAL-109 | eval/README T3 | T3 long tasks: 8 × 5. | long-task workflow | `eval/` | — | open | ACCEPTANCE §6.3 | RR | EVL-001 | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\n243:| REQ-QUAL-110 | Audit | T1 self-test and a T4 smoke run in `make test`. | regression | `eval_harness.test.ts` | TEST (test:cli/test/eval_harness.test.ts::\"T4 smoke: an overloaded endpoint is waited out\") | tested | ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | RR | — | SPEC-10 / PLAN-10 |\n247:These are REQ-CON-101 to REQ-CON-107, specified in [SPEC-C1](specs/SPEC-C1-contest-submission-track.md). The submission was **completed** (2026-10-14), judging has concluded, and no contest freeze applies (DEC-13 status amendment). Every row remains post-contest hardening with status `open`; no evidence status is promoted by this clarification. The evidence is `evidence/G_contest_eval.md` (CON-001 to CON-014).\n263:- REQ-REL-106 (self uninstall).\n276:| New v1 rows (§3) | 92 | **31 B**, 58 RR, 3 P. 79 open, 9 partial (REQ-SEC-118, REQ-PRV-101, REQ-PRV-103, REQ-PRV-105, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-PER-106, REQ-OPS-101, REQ-QUAL-108, REQ-QUAL-110), 1 implemented (REQ-OPS-103), 4 tested (REQ-SEC-103, REQ-SEC-119, REQ-PER-101, REQ-PER-102). |\n277:| Carried rows (§2.1) | 29 | 14 tested and unchanged (Keep). 1 visually-accepted (REQ-TUI-001). The rest are partial, or have open items mapped to §3. |\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17267-b4a8-7073-9d2a-32da76e0ee35","create_time":1792926434.2867086}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
