-invocation micro-approvals. | **SUBP-002, CRED-002** | ACCEPTED. Ambient credentials scrubbed by default in bounded domains, but execution domain policy MAY explicitly authorize inherited credential sets in broad/full-access domains without per-invocation approval. |\ndocs/PHASE2_RECONCILED_REQUIREMENTS.md:848:    - `SUBP-002` & `CRED-002`: Scrubbed ambient credentials by default in bounded domains, while permitting execution domain policy to authorize inherited credential sets in broad domains without per-invocation micro-approvals.\ndocs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-04-nexus-ratatui-live-default-design.md:119:3. **Composer and default entry.** Multi-line composer, approval modal, Ctrl-C cancel, slash commands. `harness` opens the TUI; `--repl` is the escape hatch.\ndocs/v1.0.0/README.md:24:| 01 | Safe execution defaults and approval integrity | [SPEC-01](specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md) | [PLAN-01](plans/PLAN-01-safe-execution-defaults.md) | M1 | SEC-101, 102, 103, 119 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:1:# PLAN-01: Safe execution defaults and approval integrity\ndocs/reviews/2026-10-13-compaction-continuity-acceptance.md:96:| Same guarantees for default and `--llm` | both through `compactNow` → `commitCompaction` | approval test runs `--llm` queued | Met (scripted) | `--llm` summary quality with a live model not evaluated |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_terminal.md:46:- Approval default: both sidecar and REPL default to `auto` (no approvals) unless `--approve` (sidecar.ts:935,\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_terminal.md:63:| TUI-07 | S2 | Default safety posture | sidecar.ts:935; repl.ts:69; quickstart.md:55 | SOURCE + DOC-CLAIM: default mode is `auto` (no approvals) for both surfaces; quickstart says \"Enter a small task, review requested actions\" | New users unknowingly grant the model unprompted write/shell authority | Decide v1 default (recommend review on first run / untrusted workspace); fix quickstart wording |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:1:# SPEC-01: Safe execution defaults and approval integrity\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-01-safe-execution-defaults.md:140:- Persisted sessions do **not** persist an approval mode. Resume uses the current launch posture. This avoids resurrecting authority, per PERS-004.\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/C_tools_security_persistence.md:132:| R-SEC-1 | By default, run_command and network egress need approval OR run in an enforced sandbox. The startup banner states the mode. | safety | BLOCKER | A fresh `nexus repl` with no flags gets a prompt/denial for run_command `echo x > /tmp/y` and for fetch_web. |\ndocs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-04-nexus-tui-phase3b-slash-commands.md:3395:- Spec coverage for phase 3: slash commands (Tasks 1–8), default entry with `--repl` escape hatch (Task 9). Together with 3A: multi-line composer, approval modal, Ctrl-C cancel. Detail and receipt overlays are plan 3C.\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_TUI_SURFACE_2026-10-12.md:70:| F1 typing that continues across the panel's appearance approves (`a` of \"add\" approved all later actions) | A decision key counts only after the grace period **and** 600 ms without typing (`APPROVAL_QUIET`); no default focus (Enter alone decides nothing); `a` only selects \"approve all later actions\", Enter confirms | unit `typing_that_continues_across_the_approval_panel_never_decides`; PTY step 5 of `tui_approval_input_e2e` types a sentence at 100 ms/key across the third approval: no decision, `third.txt` not written, then a deliberate `n` after a pause denies |\ndocs/reviews/NEXUS_TOP_TIER_QUALIFICATION_ASSESSMENT_2026-10-12.md:262:| B7 | **Approval input**: a decision requires deliberate input — no decision keys within N ms of composer typing, default focus none (or Deny), Enter only after explicit focus; approvals queue behind open panels with a visible notice; never mark shown when not rendered | F1–F3 | PTY: typing \"please add tests\" continuously across the panel → no decision; approval during help/diff review/connect → queued, panel state preserved; 39×9 terminal → no decision possible |\ndocs/reviews/evidence/qualification_2026-10-12/peers.md:19:| **4. Operator control / trust** | Sandbox modes `read-only` / `workspace-write` / `danger-full-access`; macOS Seatbelt, Linux bubblewrap (PATH or bundled helper needing unprivileged userns), WSL2 Linux sandbox, native Windows sandbox; `writable_roots`; `sandbox_workspace_write.network_access`; approvals `on-request`/`never`/granular (`untrusted` retired, `on-failure` deprecated); `approvals_reviewer = auto_review` delegates eligible prompts to a reviewer agent without widening the sandbox [CX-SBX][CX-CFG]. `shell_environment_policy` (inherit all/core/none; KEY/SECRET/TOKEN name exclusion when `ignore_default_excludes=false`); project-local config cannot set provider/notify/otel; command + MCP-tool hooks [CX-CFG]. | Modes default(Manual)/acceptEdits/plan/auto(classifier)/dontAsk/bypassPermissions; auto is the starting mode since v2.1.283; deny rules apply in every mode; critical-path `rm` and protected paths never auto-approved; `blockReadsOutsideWorkingDirectories` [CC-PERM]. Bash sandbox: Seatbelt (macOS), bubblewrap+socat+seccomp (Linux/WSL2), network through local proxy with domain allowlist, built on open-source `@anthropic-ai/sandbox-runtime`; file tools, MCP and hooks run outside it; native Windows unsandboxed; unsandboxed retry needs approval [CC-SBX]. Hooks incl. `onFailure:\"block\"` (2.1.295) [CC-CHG]; managed settings, `allowedProviders` pin [CC-GW]. | Per-tool `allow/ask/deny` with glob patterns, last match wins; `external_directory` and `doom_loop` (3 identical calls) default `ask`; `*.env` reads denied by default; `--auto` keeps explicit denies [OC-PERM]. No OS sandbox documented [OC-PERM]. | Modes auto (default per docs) / approve / smart_approve (risk-based) / chat; per-tool Always/Ask/Never in approve & smart modes; first-run mode prompt (v1.54.0); adversary-mode reviewer; prompt-injection detection mentioned [GS-PERM][GS-REL][GS-HOME]. OS sandbox not verified. | No approval/sandbox model documented on pages read; safety relies on git commits + `/undo` [AI-GIT]. |\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":963826797}},"started_at_ms":1792927663797,"completed_at_ms":1792927664761}}
