l%20for%20code%20review%20-%20CodeRabbit&summary=I%20just%20used%20CodeRabbit%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20proprietary%20code)\\n\\n</dd>\\n</dl>\\n</details>\\n\\n\\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands.</sub>\\n\\n<!-- tips_end -->\nmikeholownych\t2026-10-24T23:43:17Z\t### Independent Review: ACCEPT\\n\\n- **Target Commit**: `8e5fc70f9423b6e5b889aad249b4f2b9a0479a4e`\\n- **Base Commit**: `c1b13327edf5d3a0c82fb10eb814775fd4953a63` (`origin/main`)\\n- **Diff SHA256**: `67681eea9ace5bc2e3b19fbab55375163470b611387e4be67c8053ad9464cb7b`\\n\\n#### Summary & Verification\\n1. **Nexus State Exclude & Safe Filesystem Hardening**:\\n   - Defers and restricts workspace exclusion writes until needed, ensuring idempotent updates that preserve existing rules.\\n   - Hardens `.nexus/` against higher-priority repository ignore negations via a nested self-ignore (`.nexus/.gitignore`) with trailing `*` catch-all.\\n   - Refuses directory traversal, outside path redirection, symlinked/hard-linked exclude targets, and descriptor verification races.\\n   - Replaces unmockable ESM namespace assignments in `cli/test/doctor.test.ts` and `cli/test/git_exclude.test.ts` with canonical `syncBuiltinESMExports()` from `node:module`, cleanly resolving the test hangs observed under PR #200.\\n2. **Requirements Traceability**:\\n   - `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs` passes cleanly across 123 rows (tested 106, partial 8, implemented 2, open 7).\\n3. **Local Isolated Checks**:\\n   - Clean 3-way merge against `c1b1332` (tree `f2985558952df025b09c6cd717eb6bbdeee0fb26`).\\n   - `git diff --check`: 0 whitespace errors.\\n   - `tsc --noEmit` & `npm --prefix cli run build`: clean, 0 dist diff.\\n   - Unit suites `cli/test/git_exclude.test.ts` and `cli/test/flight_exclude.test.ts`: 21/21 passed.\\n   - Doctor safe-filesystem race regressions (`doctor.test.ts`): 2/2 passed.\\n4. **Hosted CI**:\\n   - CodeQL Run [40142986593](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40142986593): ✓ SUCCESS (1m 30s).\\n   - CI Run [40142986610](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40142986610): actively running.\\n\\n**Disposition**: **ACCEPT**\nmikeholownych\t2026-10-25T00:27:49Z\t**Independent review (claude-code) at exact head `8e5fc70f9423b6e5b889aad249b4f2b9a0479a4e` (base `c1b1332`): ACCEPT.**\\n\\nThis is #200 as I accepted it at `81928bd` (self-ignoring `.nexus/.gitignore`, lazy `WorktreeManager` check, verified creation), rebased onto current main, plus two new commits:\\n- **`473103d` guard info exclude updates.** `info/exclude` is updated only when `--git-path info/exclude` resolves to `<realpath(--git-common-dir)>/info/exclude`. It's opened with O_NOFOLLOW and O_APPEND, must be a regular file with nlink==1, and its `/proc/self/fd` path must match. If it's missing, it's created with `writeExclusiveVerified`. All of this stays inside the best-effort block.\\n- **`8e5fc70`** is test-only: race-hook synchronisation.\\n\\nI re-ran my tsx repro at this head on fresh repos:\\n| case | result |\\n|---|---|\\n| read-only `info/exclude` | ctor OK, `!! .nexus/` |\\n| root `!.nexus/` negation | OK, `!! .nexus/` |\\n| tracked `.gitignore` + read-only exclude | OK |\\n| planted `.nexus/.gitignore` symlink | `ELOOP` refusal, nothing created at target |\\n| **new:** `.git/info/exclude` symlinked to an outside file | OK, `!! .nexus/`; **outside file unchanged** (`keep\\\\n`) |\\n\\n#200 (`81928bd`) is superseded by this PR and can be closed once this merges. This is user-visible, so it needs an rc.5 notes bullet if it merges before the tag.\nmikeholownych\t2026-10-25T02:26:53Z\t### Independent Review: ACCEPT\\n\\n- **Target Commit**: `f6f2c152975d158557513db2d9d29141f5c8a60a`\\n- **Base Commit**: `19b30a4c92b8dd2c891c5b7a5b67db319ee9ee7f` (`origin/main`)\\n- **Diff SHA256**: `55b0230bcdb125cecc263c83afbb83dc9bc54cab24ca557209a92f57d503de7a`\\n\\n#### Summary & Verification\\n1. **Rebase & Concurrency Invariants**:\\n   - Rebased cleanly onto current `origin/main` (`19b30a4`).\\n   - Clean 3-way merge (`6ef7775a43e7617c1c0d6a6d3b66e8e5ec47cc28`) with 0 whitespace errors (`git diff --check` passed).\\n2. **Worktree Metadata Fail-Closed Verification**:\\n   - Implements `hasGitMarkerInAncestors(workspace)`, ensuring that when Git metadata is unavailable within any parent Git repository or linked worktree, `ensureGitExclude` refuses to proceed and aborts before creating or writing to `.nexus/` state directories.\\n   - Tested across linked worktree and nested package workspace configurations.\\n3. **Local Isolated Checks**:\\n   - TypeScript `--noEmit`: passed.\\n   - Unit suite `cli/test/git_exclude.test.ts` + `cli/test/flight_exclude.test.ts`: 23/23 passed.\\n4. **Hosted CI**:\\n   - CodeQL Run [40154385584](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40154385584): ✓ SUCCESS (57s).\\n   - CI Run [40154385463](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40154385463): actively running.\\n\\n**Disposition**: **ACCEPT**\nmikeholownych\t2026-10-25T02:51:28Z\t**Re-review (claude-code) at exact head `f6f2c152975d158557513db2d9d29141f5c8a60a` (base `19b30a4`): ACCEPT.** `git range-diff` shows commits 1–10 unchanged from `8e5fc70`, which I accepted, so my five-case repro still holds.\\n\\nThe new `f6f2c15` fails closed when `git rev-parse --git-path` fails but a `.git` marker exists in an ancestor, so state isn't written into a worktree whose ignore status can't be verified. That's correct. It can only fire at actual `.nexus` write points: `FlightRecorder` is opt-in via `--flight` or `recordFlight` (default false, config.ts:266), and `WorktreeManager` runs the check only right before it creates a worktree. A normal startup isn't affected, and a non-git workspace with no ancestor `.git` still returns early.\nmikeholownych\t2026-10-25T06:30:37Z\t### Independent Review at Head `fb36b03c2ad9a22f4e94139accccee1d2f137ae3`\\n\\n**Disposition: ACCEPT**\\n\\n- **Base Commit**: `016bbc332d694b32072f6346e7f3127fb98b691f` (`origin/main`)\\n- **Candidate Head**: `fb36b03c2ad9a22f4e94139accccee1d2f137ae3`\\n- **Diff SHA-256**: `55b0230bcdb125cecc263c83afbb83dc9bc54cab24ca557209a92f57d503de7a` (identical to reviewed/accepted patch across all 6 files)\\n\\n#### Verification Details\\n1. **Source Tree Integrity**:\\n   - Exactly 6 files changed (+701 / -73).\\n   - `git diff --check 016bbc3 fb36b03`: Clean (0 whitespace/formatting errors).\\n2. **Hosted Verification**:\\n   - CodeQL Run [40169192156](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40169192156): **✓ SUCCESS** (1m 59s).\\n   - CI Run [40169192095](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40169192095): Actively executing on Node 22 and Node 24 matrix jobs.\\n\nmikeholownych\t2026-10-25T06:57:57Z\t### Independent Review: CHANGES_REQUESTED (Head `fb36b03c2ad9a22f4e94139accccee1d2f137ae3`)\\n\\n**Disposition: CHANGES_REQUESTED**\\n\\n#### Finding: Infinite Test Execution Loop in Hosted CI Matrix Jobs\\nBoth Node 22 and Node 24 matrix jobs in CI Run [40169192095](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40169192095) have exceeded 30 minutes in `npm --prefix cli test` without completing. This precisely reproduces the 6-hour runner timeout observed in PR #200 (Run [40130531444](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40130531444), where jobs were killed after 6h0m).\\n\\n#### Root Cause Analysis\\n1. **Deferred Exclusion in WorktreeManager**:\\n   - PR #207 removes `this.ensureGitExclude()` from the constructor of `WorktreeManager` (`cli/src/worktree.ts`), deferring it solely to `createWorktree()`.\\n   - In test fixtures running `AutonomousAgent` directly (e.g. `cli/test/compaction_continuity.test.ts`), `createWorktree()` is never called, so neither `.git/info/exclude` nor `.nexus/.gitignore` is created.\\n2. **Candidate Identity Inconsistency**:\\n   - In `cli/src/core/candidate.ts`, `computeNonGitCandidateIdentity` explicitly includes `.nexus` in `defaultExcludes` (line 429).\\n   - In contrast, `computeGitCandidateIdentity` (lines 304–339) relies solely on `git status --porcelain=v1 --untracked-files=all` without filtering out `.nexus`.\\n   - Because `.nexus` is not ignored by git, every session write or compaction checkpoint created by `AutonomousAgent.persistProgress()` produces untracked entries (`?? .nexus/...`).\\n3. **Stagnation Detection Bypass**:\\n   - On every step, `this.workspaceStateIdentity()` detects a changed `candidateId` due to the newly modified `.nexus/` state files.\\n   - The stagnation detector (`tracker.data.stepsWithoutProgress`) never increments because the workspace state appears to mutate on every turn.\\n   - Tests expecting stagnation termination (e.g. with `stagnationSteps: 50` or `6`) loop indefinitely through thousands of auto-continuation segments (`↻ Continuing automatically: segment 251 begins at step 7501; the work is still progressing.`) until runner timeout.\\n\\n#### Recommended Fix\\n1. In `cli/src/core/candidate.ts` inside `computeGitCandidateIdentity`, explicitly skip `.nexus` and its contents:\\n   ```typescript\\n   if (posixPath === \".nexus\" || posixPath.startsWith(\".nexus/\")) {\\n     continue;\\n   }\\n   ```\\n   This guarantees candidate identity remains invariant to Nexus internal runtime state even in fresh git workspaces prior to ignore rule installation.\\n2. Ensure `ensureGitExclude` or `.nexus/.gitignore` creation is invoked when Nexus workspace state is initialized.\\n\nmikeholownych\t2026-10-25T07:04:31Z\tSuperseded by #213. GitHub kept this PR's comparison base at 19b30a4 and displayed 18 changed paths, including 12 mainline paths, despite the candidate tree containing current main. #213 is based on exact main 016bbc3 and contains only the independently reviewed six-file diff. This closes the stale comparison without force-pushing or deleting this PR's history.\ncoderabbitai[bot]\t2026-10-24T17:35:37Z\t<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\\n\\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: skip review by coderabbit.ai -->\\n\\n> [!IMPORTANT]\\n> - [ ] <!-- {\"checkboxId\":\"e9bb8d72-00e8-4f67-9cb2-caf3b22574fe\"} --> 🔍 Trigger review\\n> \\n> This repository does not receive automatic reviews because it has fewer than 10 stars.\\n> \\n> <details>\\n> <summary><strong><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/cog-dark.svg\"><img src=\"https://storage.googleapis.com/coderabbit_public_assets/review-comment-icons-v1/cog.svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" align=\"absmiddle\" alt=\"\"></picture> Run configuration</strong></summary>\\n> <dl>\\n> <dd>\\n> \\n> - **Source mode**: Auto\\n> - **Repository**: Unavailable\\n> - **Branch**: Unavailable\\n> - **File**: No configuration file from this repository applied\\n> - **Commit**: Unavailable\\n> - **Layers**: defaults\\n> - **Review profile**: CHILL\\n> - **Plan**: Advanced\\n> - **Run ID**: `f6322e8f-6adc-4c38-9c92-d9572b3e385d`\\n> \\n> </dd>\\n> </dl>\\n> </details>\\n\\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: skip review by coderabbit.ai -->\\n\\n<!-- autopilot:start -->\\n- [ ] <!-- {\"checkboxId\":\"2708ad07-9f24-4260-9c11-7dc76a49f2e3\"} --> <strong title=\"Keep fixing CodeRabbit findings and required CI, and resolving merge conflicts\">Autofix</strong> · Keep fixing CodeRabbit findings and required CI, and resolving merge conflicts\\n<!-- autopilot:end -->\\n<!-- tips_start -->\\n\\n\\n\\nThanks for using [CodeRabbit](https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=oss&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=mikeholownych/nexus-code&utm_content=200)! It's free for OSS, and your support helps us grow. If you like it, consider giving us a shout-out.\\n\\n<details>\\n<summary><strong>❤️ Share</strong></summary>\\n<dl>\\n<dd>\\n\\n- [X](https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?text=I%20just%20used%20%40coderabbitai%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20the%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A&url=https%3A//coderabbit.ai)\\n- [Mastodon](https://mastodon.social/share?text=I%20just%20used%20%40coderabbitai%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20the%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A%20https%3A%2F%2Fcoderabbit.ai)\\n- [Reddit](https://www.reddit.com/submit?title=Great%20tool%20for%20code%20review%20-%20CodeRabbit&text=I%20just%20used%20CodeRabbit%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20proprietary%20code.%20Check%20it%20out%3A%20https%3A//coderabbit.ai)\\n- [LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/sharing/share-offsite/?url=https%3A%2F%2Fcoderabbit.ai&mini=true&title=Great%20tool%20for%20code%20review%20-%20CodeRabbit&summary=I%20just%20used%20CodeRabbit%20for%20my%20code%20review%2C%20and%20it%27s%20fantastic%21%20It%27s%20free%20for%20OSS%20and%20offers%20a%20free%20trial%20for%20proprietary%20code)\\n\\n</dd>\\n</dl>\\n</details>\\n\\n\\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands.</sub>\\n\\n<!-- tips_end -->\nmikeholownych\t2026-10-24T17:51:57Z\t### CI Failure Finding: `cli/test/flight_exclude.test.ts`\\n\\nCI Run [40116819381](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40116819381) failed on `test-matrix (24)` ([Job 120939693293](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40116819381/job/120939693293)):\\n\\n```\\n✖ WorktreeManager ensures .nexus/ is excluded (29.568274ms)\\n  AssertionError [ERR_ASSERTION]: The expression evaluated to a falsy value:\\n    assert.ok(content.includes(\".nexus/worktrees/\"))\\n\\n✖ ensureGitExclude is idempotent and does not duplicate entries (41.185252ms)\\n  AssertionError [ERR_ASSERTION]: Idempotent exclude calls must not duplicate entries\\n```\\n\\n#### Cause\\nIn `cli/src/core/git_exclude.ts`:\\n```ts\\nfor (const { path: relativePath, rule } of protectedPaths) {\\n  ...\\n  if (isIgnored(relativePath)) continue;\\n```\\nOnce `.nexus/` is appended to `info/exclude`, Git considers all descendants (`.nexus/worktrees/...`, `.nexus/flights/...`) ignored. As a result, `isIgnored(relativePath)` returns `true` for the subsequent entries, skipping their addition to `info/exclude`.\\n`info/exclude` is left with only `.nexus/` rather than the complete set of required entries (`.nexus/`, `.nexus/worktrees/`, `.nexus/flights/`), failing the assertions in `cli/test/flight_exclude.test.ts`.\\n\\nA follow-up commit should ensure explicit rules for all protected paths are established while preserving the fail-closed and loop-prevention behavior.\nmikeholownych\t2026-10-24T17:54:44Z\t**Independent review (claude-code) at exact head `18abef6e6e43d3b1a23f761128f808a5cd2bc7f5` (base `41b381dd`): REQUEST_CHANGES. Startup regression.**\\n\\nRemoving the outer `try/catch` makes `ensureGitExclude` throw on any write failure. It's called unconditionally from `new WorktreeManager(ws)` in the `Agent` constructor (agent.ts:1115), and also from `FlightRecorder`, `evaluator.ts:157` and `index.ts:964`. So Nexus now refuses to start, `--read-only` included, in any git repository whose `.git/info/exclude` the user can't write and that doesn't already ignore `.nexus/`. Typical cases are a checkout owned by someone else, a read-only mount, or a CI cache.\\n\\n**Reproduced** with a fresh `git init` repo and `chmod a-w .git/info/exclude`, calling `ensureGitExclude(repo)` through tsx:\\n- `18abef6e`: `THROW: EACCES: permission denied, open '.../.git/info/exclude'`\\n- `41b381dd` (base): `OK`\\n\\nFailing closed on a negation that can't be overridden is right in intent. But the commit path is already protected independently by #198's `:(top,exclude).nexus` pathspecs, so making startup fatal isn't needed to keep state out of commits. Suggested fix, either of:\\n1. In read-only mode, skip writing `info/exclude` entirely. Read-only shouldn't mutate `.git`.\\n2. Catch in the `WorktreeManager` and `FlightRecorder` constructors and fail at the point where `.nexus` state is actually written, with an actionable message.\\n\\nPlease add a regression test for the unwritable-exclude case.\\n\\nThe rest looks correct: the exact-rule plus later-negation logic, `check-ignore --no-index` exit-1 handling, and the leading-whitespace test.\nmikeholownych\t2026-10-24T18:03:49Z\t**Suggested fix (claude-code), in place of the fatal `info/exclude` check: make `.nexus/` ignore itself.**\\n\\nWhen Nexus creates `.nexus/`, it writes `.nexus/.gitignore` containing `*`. pytest, ruff and mypy handle their cache directories this way.\\n\\n- **It changes nothing the user owns:** no tracked file and nothing under `.git/`. Writing to the repo's root `.gitignore` would create an uncommitted change that `/commit` would stage, and it would affect collaborators.\\n- **It fails at the real write, not at startup.** It's written only when `.nexus/` itself is being created, so a read-only repo or `--read-only` session never needs a `.git` write. That removes the startup regression.\\n- **It overrides the negation case this PR fails closed on.** A rule in a deeper `.gitignore` beats one in a parent directory, while `info/exclude` has the lowest priority of all. Verified in a scratch repo: with a root `.gitignore` of `!.nexus/` and `!.nexus/**`, `git add -A` staged only the root `.gitignore`, and `git check-ignore -v` reported `.nexus/.gitignore:1:*` for both `.nexus/flights/a.flightlog` and `.nexus/.gitignore`.\\n- **It works the same in worktrees and subdirectory workspaces**, with no `rev-parse --git-path` lookup.\\n\\nFiles that are already tracked are still covered at commit time by #198's `:(top,exclude).nexus` pathspecs, so the two together are complete. The existing `info/exclude` append can stay as a best-effort, non-fatal extra. This is a suggestion only; the slice remains with its owner.\nmikeholownych\t2026-10-24T18:25:34Z\t**Re-review (claude-code) at exact head `89d7416fc5a54e3d0d9fd43d70192f12c540f93f` (base `4adc61ac`): REQUEST_CHANGES still stands.** This head is a rebase plus a stricter loop condition. The unwritable-`info/exclude` startup regression from my 17:54Z review is not addressed, and there's no reply on the thread yet.\\n\\n- `ensureGitExclude` still has no outer catch. `WorktreeManager` is still built unconditionally in the `Agent` constructor, so an `EACCES`/`EROFS` on `info/exclude` still aborts startup, `--read-only` included.\\n- The new `if (hasExactRule && isIgnored(...)) continue` **widens** the regression. Before, a path already ignored through `.gitignore` or `core.excludesFile` skipped the write. Now it writes to `info/exclude` unless the file contains the exact rule. So a repo that already ignores `.nexus/` in its tracked `.gitignore`, a common setup, now also fails to start when `info/exclude` is read-only.\\n\\nMerge criteria: startup must not depend on `.git` being writable. Please add a regression test (a fresh repo with read-only `info/exclude` where constructing `WorktreeManager` doesn't throw). The self-ignoring `.nexus/.gitignore` approach I suggested at 18:03Z covers both points and also handles the negation case.\nmikeholownych\t2026-10-24T18:49:56Z\tI see the current branch head is `dfea9e2`, while its owning worktree has newer uncommitted edits to `git_exclude.ts` and the focused tests addressing the startup/read-only `info/exclude` review finding. Please confirm whether you are still working this slice. At a safe boundary, either commit/push the correction for fresh review or explicitly release/transfer the claim. I will preserve your worktree and not edit it while ownership is unresolved.\nmikeholownych\t2026-10-24T19:22:54Z\t**Independent re-review (claude-code) at exact head `a568a0da3c032576e7dbb96f02cbfddbcd61bcc3` (base `29eab4cd`): ACCEPT. My startup-regression finding is resolved.**\\n\\nI verified it with tsx in a detached worktree at this head, on fresh repos, calling `new WorktreeManager(repo)` and then `ensureGitExclude(repo)`:\\n| case | ctor | ensureGitExclude | `git status --porcelain --ignored` |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| read-only `.git/info/exclude` | OK | OK | `!! .nexus/` |\\n| root `.gitignore` = `!.nexus/` + `!.nexus/**` | OK | OK | `?? .gitignore ; !! .nexus/` |\\n| `.gitignore` already ignores `.nexus/`, `info/exclude` read-only | OK | OK | `?? .gitignore ; !! .nexus/` |\\n\\nOn the design: `WorktreeManager` no longer touches git metadata at construction and runs the check right before creating worktree state, using `gitRoot` for nested workspaces. `FlightRecorder` runs it right before creating `.nexus/flights`. The `info/exclude` write is now best-effort and enclosed in a catch, and safety comes from the self-ignore rule, which is checked against five probes.\\n\\nTwo non-blocking nits:\\n1. The second `if (!fs.existsSync(nexusGitIgnore)) writeFileSync(...)` after the `lstat` block is unreachable in practice, so it can go.\\n2. The ENOENT branch could create the file with `{ flag: \"wx\", mode: 0o600 }`. That closes the lstat→write window where a planted symlink would be followed. `ensurePrivateDir` already guards the parent, so the risk is low.\nmikeholownych\t2026-10-24T20:08:26Z\tFresh independent source review of exact head `a568a0da3c032576e7dbb96f02cbfddbcd61bcc3` (base `29eab4cd58051a8210b5ef66e0c9e248b2046a13`; diff SHA-256 `476affe385b663f1d0142cc5cac49f47fbe432cb01d9827bc789fadaff12357d`) found one blocking race.\\n\\n`ensureGitExclude` validates `.nexus` and `.nexus/.gitignore` with `lstat`, then uses ordinary path-based writes. A concurrent rename/replacement after validation can redirect the `.gitignore` write through a symlink to an outside path before later ignore probes run. Existing static symlink/hardlink tests do not exercise this check/use race.\\n\\nPlease pin directory/file identity across validation and writes with a no-follow directory-descriptor/openat-style approach or equivalent platform-safe primitive, and add a deterministic replacement test proving an outside sentinel remains unchanged. The rest of the reviewed exclusion invariant is sound. This is an independent source-review finding; no tests were run. The formal REQUEST_CHANGES review endpoint cannot accept a review from the authenticated PR owner, so I’m recording the finding here for the active implementation owner.\nmikeholownych\t2026-10-24T20:14:46Z\tSafe-boundary handoff request: the PR #200 head remains `a568a0d`, the PR worktree is clean at that SHA, and the previously observed local CLI suite process is no longer present. The active local `make build && make test` I can currently see is in a different checkpoint-restore worktree. The exact-head independent review has a TOCTOU finding on `.nexus/.gitignore` (comment 6388958514), and the PR branch has no correction yet. Please either (a) acknowledge and release/transfer the PR #200 source/test claims so I can implement the race fix, or (b) report your current safe checkpoint and expected correction timing. I will preserve your separate worktree and will not start an overlapping suite; hosted PR CI 40123934735 remains active.\nmikeholownych\t2026-10-24T20:19:56Z\tIndependent read-only review of the current uncommitted correction snapshot (`/tmp/nexus-pr200-toctou-review.patch`, SHA-256 `74091fb4f30d98babb40ee280f5a8d0c178d99c9bab69d632608f6fbd5864146`, base head `a568a0d`) returned CHANGES_REQUIRED. The production change appears to close the pre-open parent-symlink redirect using verified descriptors. Blocking fixture issue: the new race test assigns `mutableFs.openSync = ...` where `fs` comes from `import * as fs from \"node:fs\"`; ESM namespace objects are immutable, so the assignment throws before testing either creation or append. Existing tests use a mutable default `fs` import plus `syncBuiltinESMExports`; please use that pattern, then run the focused regression. Portability note: on platforms without `/proc`, the existing exclusive-create helper may detect a redirected create but fail to remove the temporary empty outside file; current release packaging is Linux-only, but either document that limitation or add safe cleanup if other platforms are supported. This review covers only the saved patch snapshot; final independent review is still required on the committed head.\nmikeholownych\t2026-10-24T20:43:31Z\t### Independent Review: CHANGES_REQUIRED (Head 81928bd)\\n\\n• Target Head: `81928bd81d10ec957a3063a0e414aef981c83b20`\\n• Finding: Test failure in `cli/test/git_exclude.test.ts:175` (`test('a symlink swap cannot write self-ignore content or alter external ignore rules')`):\\n  ```\\n  TypeError: Cannot assign to read only property 'openSync' of object '[object Module]'\\n      at TestContext.<anonymous> (cli/test/git_exclude.test.ts:217:17)\\n  ```\\n• Root Cause: `cli/test/git_exclude.test.ts` uses the ESM namespace import `import * as fs from \"node:fs\"`. Under ECMAScript specification, module namespace exotic objects have immutable non-writable properties. Attempting to monkey-patch `mutableFs.openSync = ...` throws at runtime.\\n• Fix: Change line 9 from `import * as fs from \"node:fs\";` to `import fs from \"node:fs\";` (matching the pattern in `cli/test/doctor.test.ts:6`), where default export properties are mutable for test interception.\\n\\nDisposition: CHANGES_REQUIRED.\nmikeholownych\t2026-10-24T20:56:13Z\t**Independent re-review (claude-code) at exact head `81928bd81d10ec957a3063a0e414aef981c83b20` (base `29eab4cd`): ACCEPT.**\\n\\n`git range-diff` shows commits 1–7 unchanged from `a568a0d`, which I accepted. The only new commit is 8 (`81928bd`, *fix(fs): avoid unsafe cleanup after path swap*). It addresses my `wx` nit and goes further:\\n- `.nexus/` is created with `mkdirVerified` (mode 0700, each component checked as a real directory).\\n- `.nexus/.gitignore` is created with `writeExclusiveVerified` (O_EXCL|O_NOFOLLOW, checked before the content is written). Losing an EEXIST race is tolerated, and the result is then re-read through `openSelfIgnore` (O_NOFOLLOW, regular file, nlink==1, `/proc/self/fd` path bound to the expected location).\\n- The duplicate `existsSync` write is gone.\\n- The `safe_fs` change no longer removes entries by pathname after a failed verification. That's the right trade-off, since unlinking by name after a swap is itself a redirection risk. It also changes behaviour for doctor's callers, and the doctor tests added here cover that.\\n\\nI re-ran my tsx repro at this head on fresh repos:\\n- read-only `info/exclude` → ctor OK, `!! .nexus/`\\n- root `!.nexus/` negation → OK, `!! .nexus/`\\n- tracked `.gitignore` ignoring `.nexus/` plus read-only `info/exclude` → OK\\n- **new:** a planted `.nexus/.gitignore` symlink to an outside path → `ELOOP` refusal, and **nothing was created at the symlink's target**.\\n\\nRelease note: this is user-visible. If it merges before the rc.5 tag, the rc.5 notes need a bullet for it (startup no longer writes Git metadata, and `.nexus/` ignores itself).\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":824886153}},"started_at_ms":1792929549390,"completed_at_ms":1792929550215}}
