{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T13:00:09.497Z","ordinal":338817,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17267-b4a8-7073-9d2a-32da76e0ee35","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-c3e6e9be-3aaa-4cc6-bab6-71e36204fa9e","process_id":"56861","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh attestation verify --help | rg -n -C 2 'signer-workflow|cert-identity|verify|owner|repo|verbose|format' && gh --version"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh attestation verify --help | rg -n -C 2 'signer-workflow|cert-identity|verify|owner|repo|verbose|format' && gh --version"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"1:Verify the integrity and provenance of an artifact using its associated\n2-cryptographically signed attestations.\n3-\n--\n7-(i.e. a GitHub Actions workflow) regarding a subject (i.e. an artifact).\n8-\n9:In order to verify an attestation, you must provide an artifact and validate:\n10-* the identity of the actor that produced the attestation\n11-* the expected attestation predicate type (the nature of the claim)\n12-\n13-By default, this command enforces the `https://slsa.dev/provenance/v1`\n14:predicate type. To verify other attestation predicate types use the\n15-`--predicate-type` flag.\n16-\n17-The \"actor identity\" consists of:\n18:* the repository or the repository owner the artifact is linked with\n19-* the Actions workflow that produced the attestation (a.k.a the\n20-  signer workflow)\n21-\n22-This identity is then validated against the attestation's certificate's\n23:SourceRepository, SourceRepositoryOwner, and SubjectAlternativeName\n24-(SAN) fields, among others.\n25-\n--\n27-\n28-At a minimum, this command requires either:\n29:* the `--owner` flag (e.g. --owner github), or\n30:* the `--repo` flag (e.g. --repo github/example)\n31-\n32-The more precisely you specify the identity, the more control you will\n--\n34-\n35-Ideally, the path of the signer workflow is also validated using the\n36:`--signer-workflow` or `--cert-identity` flags.\n37-\n38-Please note: if your attestation was generated via a reusable workflow then\n39-that reusable workflow is the signer whose identity needs to be validated.\n40:In this situation, you must use either the `--signer-workflow` or\n41:the `--signer-repo` flag.\n42-\n43-For more options, see the other available flags.\n--\n52-\n53-By default, this command will attempt to fetch relevant attestations via the\n54:GitHub API using the values provided to `--owner` or  `--repo`.\n55-\n56-To instead fetch attestations from your artifact's OCI registry, use the\n--\n62-## Additional Policy Enforcement\n63-\n64:Given the `--format=json` flag, upon successful verification this\n65-command will output a JSON array containing one entry per verified attestation.\n66-\n--\n101-whose execution cannot be influenced by input provided through the caller workflow.\n102-\n103:See above re: `--signer-workflow`.\n104-\n105:For more information about output formatting flags, see `gh help formatting`.\n106-\n107-USAGE\n108:  gh attestation verify [<file-path> | oci://<image-uri>] [--owner | --repo] [flags]\n109-\n110-FLAGS\n111-  -b, --bundle string                Path to bundle on disk, either a single bundle in a JSON file or a JSON lines file with multiple bundles\n112:      --bundle-from-oci              When verifying an OCI image, fetch the attestation bundle from the OCI registry instead of from GitHub\n113:      --cert-identity string         Enforce that the certificate's SubjectAlternativeName matches the provided value exactly\n114:  -i, --cert-identity-regex string   Enforce that the certificate's SubjectAlternativeName matches the provided regex\n115-      --cert-oidc-issuer string      Enforce that the issuer of the OIDC token matches the provided value (default \"https://token.actions.githubusercontent.com\")\n116-      --custom-trusted-root string   Path to a trusted_root.jsonl file; likely for offline verification\n117-      --deny-self-hosted-runners     Fail verification for attestations generated on self-hosted runners\n118-  -d, --digest-alg string            The algorithm used to compute a digest of the artifact: {sha256|sha512} (default \"sha256\")\n119:      --format string                Output format: {json}\n120-      --hostname string              Configure host to use\n121-  -q, --jq expression                Filter JSON output using a jq expression\n122-  -L, --limit int                    Maximum number of attestations to fetch (default 30)\n123:      --no-public-good               Do not verify attestations signed with Sigstore public good instance\n124:  -o, --owner string                 GitHub organization to scope attestation lookup by\n125-      --predicate-type string        Enforce that verified attestations' predicate type matches the provided value (default \"https://slsa.dev/provenance/v1\")\n126:  -R, --repo string                  Repository name in the format <owner>/<repo>\n127-      --signer-digest string         Enforce that the digest associated with the signer workflow matches the provided value\n128:      --signer-repo string           Enforce that the workflow that signed the attestation's repository matches the provided value (<owner>/<repo>)\n129:      --signer-workflow string       Enforce that the workflow that signed the attestation matches the provided value ([host/]<owner>/<repo>/<path>/<to>/<workflow>)\n130:      --source-digest string         Enforce that the digest associated with the source repository matches the provided value\n131:      --source-ref string            Enforce that the git ref associated with the source repository matches the provided value\n132:  -t, --template string              Format JSON output using a Go template; see \"gh help formatting\"\n133-\n134-INHERITED FLAGS\n--\n136-\n137-EXAMPLES\n138:  # Verify an artifact linked with a repository\n139:  $ gh attestation verify example.bin --repo github/example\n140-  \n141:  # Verify an artifact linked with an organization\n142:  $ gh attestation verify example.bin --owner github\n143-  \n144:  # Verify an artifact and output the full verification result\n145:  $ gh attestation verify example.bin --owner github --format json\n146-  \n147:  # Verify an OCI image using attestations stored on disk\n148:  $ gh attestation verify oci://<image-uri> --owner github --bundle sha256:foo.jsonl\n149-  \n150:  # Verify an artifact signed with a reusable workflow\n151:  $ gh attestation verify example.bin --owner github --signer-repo actions/example\n152-\n153-LEARN MORE\n154:  Use `gh <command> <subcommand> --help` for more information about a command.\n155-  Read the manual at https://cli.github.com/manual\n156-  Learn about exit codes using `gh help exit-codes`\ngh version 2.100.0 (2026-09-03)\nhttps://github.com/cli/cli/releases/tag/v2.100.0\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":148853047}},"started_at_ms":1792933209348,"completed_at_ms":1792933209497}}
