{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T13:04:09.950Z","ordinal":339046,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17267-b4a8-7073-9d2a-32da76e0ee35","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-f754b0c7-38a0-4707-85bf-377b3e07c8cc","process_id":"5938","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | rg -n -C 4 'M5|T4|fault' | head -100 && gh issue view 2 --json body,comments --jq '{body,comments:[.comments[-4:][]|{author:.author.login,createdAt,body}]}'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | rg -n -C 4 'M5|T4|fault' | head -100 && gh issue view 2 --json body,comments --jq '{body,comments:[.comments[-4:][]|{author:.author.login,createdAt,body}]}'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"38-\n39-| Requirement | Acceptance criteria required in the exact-RC record | Remaining stage |\n40-|---|---|---|\n41-| REQ-REL-003 | ACC-PLAT | Installed-RC platform and Node-version matrix |\n42:| REQ-AGT-002 | ACC-VER-03, ACC-VER-04, ACC-VER-09, ACC-QUAL-T2, ACC-QUAL-T3, ACC-QUAL-T4 | Installed-RC T2/T3/T4 outcome thresholds |\n43-| REQ-AGT-010 | ACC-TRUST-04 | Independent acceptance of the DEC-04 v1 subset |\n44-| REQ-PRV-003 | ACC-INF-10 | Installed-RC standalone and absent-gateway behavior |\n45-| REQ-REL-005 | ACC-SUP-04, ACC-SUP-05 | Exact-RC security and dependency artifact checks |\n46-| REQ-AGT-110 | ACC-CONT-10, ACC-GOV-06 | Installed-RC continuity and independent acceptance |\n--\n62-## 1. Rules\n63-\n64-1. The RC is built and published by the release workflow from a clean tag. Its version is identical across all components (REQ-REL-103).\n65-2. All qualification runs use the **installed RC package**, installed with the documented one-line command. They never use a checkout build. The only exception is CI unit and PTY suites, which run from source at the same commit.\n66:3. Thresholds (DEC-05) are frozen before the first M5 run. A failing gate is fixed in code and the run is repeated as `rc.N+1`. A threshold is never relaxed after results are known.\n67-4. Evidence goes to `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/`. The directory contains:\n68-   - `manifest.json`: commit, package sha256, environment, model fingerprint, dates;\n69-   - raw outputs;\n70-   - a `SHA256SUMS` file.\n--\n78-|---|---|---|\n79-| E1 | GitHub Actions: ubuntu-22.04 and ubuntu-24.04; Node 22 and 24; pinned Rust | Unit, integration and PTY suites; packaging; reproducibility |\n80-| E2 | Docker clean images: ubuntu:22.04, ubuntu:24.04, debian:12, fedora:40. Each with no Node, then with Node 20, Node 22 and Node 24. Non-root user. | Installer, upgrade, rollback, uninstall, platform failure messages |\n81-| E3 | Operator dev box: Linux x86-64, real terminals (xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal) | Terminal matrix, live sessions |\n82:| E4 | Homelab-ai gateway, the **only** inference path (DEC-16): direct, and through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` | Task-quality runs, standalone qualification, T3/T4 |\n83-| E5 | Cloud, small spend: ChatGPT sign-in (experimental tier) and OpenRouter with a pinned model; OpenAI and Anthropic keys if added | Provider verify; one live task per supported cloud provider |\n84-\n85-## 3. Gate checklist (G0–G4: automated acceptance IDs)\n86-\n--\n115-| ACC-PRV-STANDALONE | §4.2 on the installed RC through the approved stripped proxy, with gateway credentials absent from the child environment | Every required profile completes through the proxy and the absent-gateway boundary holds; receipts archived. |\n116-| ACC-PLAT | E2 matrix, §7 | All rows pass. |\n117-| ACC-QUAL-T2 | §6.1 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n118-| ACC-QUAL-T3 | §6.3 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n119:| ACC-QUAL-T4 | §6.2 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n120:| ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | `make test` includes the T1 self-test and the T4 smoke | Present and passing. |\n121-| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five required terminal environments and three required sizes | Every cell passes; screenshots and per-cell verdicts are archived. |\n122-\n123-## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\n124-\n--\n138-### 4.2 Standalone matrix\n139-\n140-| Profile | What Nexus sees | Runs | Pass condition |\n141-|---|---|---|---|\n142:| P-plain | Bare OpenAI-compatible `/models` and chat. No tokenize, no capacity headers. | Standalone T2 subset (≥ 10 held-out tasks) × 3 runs; T4 classes 1, 3, 4, 7 × 3 | T2 correctness ≥ (gateway-direct T2 correctness on the same tasks − 10 pts). False VERIFIED = 0. T4 truthful = 100%. Context source reported as `client_default` or an operator override, with no error. |\n143-| P-llamacpp | Emulated llama.cpp `/props` and overflow body | Same tasks × 1 run; plus the forced-overflow case (context limit set to 8k) | Context discovered from `/props`. Overflow gives one compact-and-retry, then success or an actionable error. |\n144-| P-vllm | Emulated `max_model_len` and vLLM overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `max_model_len` |\n145-| P-ollama | Emulated `/api/show` and Ollama overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `ollama_show` |\n146-| Conformance | CI fixtures for llama.cpp, vLLM, LM Studio and Ollama shapes | CI | All pass (ACC-INF-01, -02, -05) |\n--\n229-  ```\n230-\n231-  Record the resolved `T2_TASKS`, unique `T2_OUT`, config digests, installed RC identity, model fingerprint, and exact commands in the frozen run record before starting. A failed or interrupted invocation remains evidence; any permitted infrastructure rerun uses the accepted rerun procedure and is retained separately. Do not score until all required runs and manifests exist. The scorer accepts exactly the Nexus, Goose and OpenCode result files.\n232-\n233:### 6.2 T4 fault injection (ACC-QUAL-T4)\n234-\n235:9 fault classes × 5 runs on the Nexus RC. The configured faults run through `eval/run.mjs` and `eval/model_proxy.mjs`; the hanging-command and full-disk cases use task fixtures, and SIGTERM-then-resume uses the runner case (DEC-05 amendment, 2026-10-17: the union of the distinct scenarios below):\n236-\n237-1. refused connection mid-turn\n238-2. 5xx / overloaded\n239-3. stream cut mid-tool-call\n--\n251-### 6.4 Thresholds (DEC-05; all must hold)\n252-\n253-| Metric | Gate |\n254-|---|---|\n255:| False VERIFIED (T2 + T3 + T4) | **= 0** |\n256-| T2 pooled hidden-test correctness | ≥ 60% and ≥ best matched peer − 10 pts |\n257-| T2 per class (bugfix, feature, refactor, debug) | ≥ 40% |\n258-| Crash rate (all Nexus runs) | ≤ 2% |\n259-| Regression rate | ≤ 5% |\n260:| T4 truthful outcome | = 100% |\n261:| T4 hang beyond budget + 5 min | = 0 |\n262-| T3 false-absence | = 0 |\n263-| T3 false-presence | = 0 |\n264-| T3 steering honoured | ≥ 95% |\n265-| Operator interventions in `run` mode | = 0 |\n--\n304-   - ACC-CONT-01, 03;\n305-   - ACC-VER-01, 03;\n306-   - ACC-PKG-01;\n307-   - 5 random T2 tasks;\n308:   - 2 T4 classes.\n309-2. One live long task (≥ 60 steps, ≥ 2 compactions) on the RC through the gateway, including one kill and resume.\n310-3. A review of the scorer verdict and of contamination handling.\n311-\n312-**Output:** `docs/reviews/<date>-v1-rc-independent-acceptance.md` with an ACCEPT, ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS, or REJECT verdict per area. \"Accept with defects\" needs an owner disposition for every defect, and for a blocker area the only acceptable disposition is a fix.\n{\"body\":\"## Scope\\nRun M5 only against an exact accepted RC after all prerequisites and explicit operation-specific authorizations are satisfied. This is not authorized by issue creation or by synthetic results.\\n\\n## Linked requirements\\nREQ-AGT-002; REQ-QUAL-101, REQ-QUAL-103, REQ-QUAL-104, REQ-QUAL-105, REQ-QUAL-107, REQ-QUAL-109; REQ-PRV-111. The terminal matrix (REQ-QUAL-108) is tracked separately in issue #3, and independent continuity acceptance (REQ-AGT-110) is tracked separately in issue #6.\\n\\n## Acceptance\\n- Freeze run population, scoring, identities, configs, budgets, and unique output directories before execution.\\n- Complete T2 (5 runs per task/configuration), T3 (8×5), T4 (accepted fault matrix), standalone proxy profiles, and required provider verification.\\n- Preserve original failures, retries, manifests, and hashes; no post-result exclusions or tuning on held-out data.\\n- Apply unchanged thresholds and obtain independent acceptance under ACCEPTANCE.md.\\n- Update relevant ledger evidence only after exact-RC gates pass.\\n\\nReferences: `docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md` task 11; `docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md` §§4, 6–8.\",\"comments\":[{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Acceptance reconciliation required before T4 execution: ACCEPTANCE.md §6.2 says “8 fault classes × 5 runs” but enumerates nine fault classes (items 1–9). PLAN-10 task 11 also says T4 (8×5), while PLAN-10 task 5 and eval/README.md describe class 9 (SIGTERM then resume). No class has been removed and no threshold has been selected here. The release owner/spec owner must resolve the denominator and run matrix without post-result relaxation; until then T4 execution is blocked.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-17T02:25:37Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Status check at `6a16cb6` (claude-code).\\n\\n- **T4 denominator (prior comment):** resolved in ACCEPTANCE.md §6.2. The DEC-05 amendment (PRs #11/#13) keeps **9 fault classes × 5 runs**, including SIGTERM + resume. **Remaining inconsistency:** `docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md` line 34 (task 11) still says \\\"T4 (8×5)\\\". A boundary request to the plan owner is in the claim log; ACCEPTANCE §6.2 is authoritative.\\n- **Prerequisites not yet met:** no RC exists (package `0.1.0-alpha.2`). PR #33 (evaluator confidentiality and hardened-legacy checks) is open with CHANGES-REQUIRED, and held-out runs are prohibited until it is accepted. The qualification host is provisioned and validated on PR #33's branch, but that has not been accepted on integration.\\n- Requirements `--enforce` still fails at `6a16cb6`: 11 rows below threshold, including all of this issue's QUAL rows plus REQ-AGT-002 and REQ-PRV-111.\\n\\nNo M5 run has started.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-18T17:34:27Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"T4 denominator reconciliation (2026-10-22, source check at `main@a4a7edd9a17a0015abdf8135ecf3c1caac05560c`): the inconsistency described in the October 18 note is no longer present in current main. `ACCEPTANCE.md` §6.2 specifies nine fault classes × five runs, including SIGTERM/resume, and PLAN-10 task 11 now says `T4 (9×5)`. The separate run-wall-time table still contains the old `8×5` estimate, but explicitly labels it historical and says it predates the nine-class correction; it is not an execution denominator.\\n\\nThis resolves the planning-text discrepancy only. T4 qualification has not run and remains gated on an accepted installed RC, frozen workload, provider/standalone prerequisites, and the other stated qualification dependencies. No threshold or denominator was changed.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-22T22:47:41Z\"}]}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":536090877}},"started_at_ms":1792933449413,"completed_at_ms":1792933449950}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T13:04:11.002Z","ordinal":339047,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a17329-54f9-7bd3-bd3f-feeb09ad9e78","call_id":"call_e3ce8425cb11444690cf007c8096a984","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.7 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 2573)\nTotal output lines: 89\n\n38-\n39-| Requirement | Acceptance criteria required in the exact-RC record | Remaining stage |\n40-|---|---|---|\n41-| REQ-REL-003 | ACC-PLAT | Installed-RC platform and Node-version matrix |\n42:| REQ-AGT-002 | ACC-VER-03, ACC-VER-04, ACC-VER-09, ACC-QUAL-T2, ACC-QUAL-T3, ACC-QUAL-T4 | Installed-RC T2/T3/T4 outcome thresholds |\n43-| REQ-AGT-010 | ACC-TRUST-04 | Independent acceptance of the DEC-04 v1 subset |\n44-| REQ-PRV-003 | ACC-INF-10 | Installed-RC standalone and absent-gateway behavior |\n45-| REQ-REL-005 | ACC-SUP-04, ACC-SUP-05 | Exact-RC security and dependency artifact checks |\n46-| REQ-AGT-110 | ACC-CONT-10, ACC-GOV-06 | Installed-RC continuity and independent acceptance |\n--\n62-## 1. Rules\n63-\n64-1. The RC is built and published by the release workflow from a clean tag. Its version is identical across all components (REQ-REL-103).\n65-2. All qualification runs use the **installed RC package**, installed with the documented one-line command. They never use a checkout build. The only exception is CI unit and PTY suites, which run from source at the same commit.\n66:3. Thresholds (DEC-05) are frozen before the first M5 run. A failing gate is fixed in code and the run is repeated as `rc.N+1`. A threshold is never relaxed after results are known.\n67-4. Evidence goes to `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/`. The directory contains:\n68-   - `manifest.json`: commit, package sha256, environment, model fingerprint, dates;\n69-   - raw outputs;\n70-   - a `SHA256SUMS` file.\n--\n78-|---|---|---|\n79-| E1 | GitHub Actions: ubuntu-22.04 and ubuntu-24.04; Node 22 and 24; pinned Rust | Unit, integration and PTY suites; packaging; reproducibility |\n80-| E2 | Docker clean images: ubuntu:22.04, ubuntu:24.04, debian:12, fedora:40. Each with no Node, then with Node 20, Node 22 and Node 24. Non-root user. | Installer, upgrade, rollback, uninstall, platform failure messages |\n81-| E3 | Operator dev box: Linux x86-64, real terminals (xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal) | Terminal matrix, live sessions |\n82:| E4 | Homelab-ai gateway, the **only** inference path (DEC-16): direct, and through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` | Task-quality runs, standalone qualification, T3/T4 |\n83-| E5 | Cloud, small spend: ChatGPT sign-in (experimental tier) and OpenRouter with a pinned model; OpenAI and Anthropic keys if added | Provider verify; one live task per supported cloud provider |\n84-\n85-## 3. Gate checklist (G0–G4: automated acceptance IDs)\n86-\n--\n115-| ACC-PRV-STANDALONE | §4.2 on the installed RC through the approved stripped proxy, with gateway credentials absent from the child environment | Every required profile completes through the proxy and the absent-gateway boundary holds; receipts archived. |\n116-| ACC-PLAT | E2 matrix, §7 | All rows pass. |\n117-| ACC-QUAL-T2 | §6.1 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n118-| ACC-QUAL-T3 | §6.3 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n119:| ACC-QUAL-T4 | §6.2 + §6.4 | Thresholds met. |\n120:| ACC-QUAL-SMOKE | `make test` includes the T1 self-test and the T4 smoke | Present and passing. |\n121-| ACC-TUI-MANUAL | §5.3 on the installed RC across five required terminal environments and three required sizes | Every cell passes; screenshots and per-cell verdicts are archived. |\n122-\n123-## 4. Standalone and provider qualification (REQ-PRV-106, REQ-PRV-111, REQ-QUAL-107)\n124-\n--\n138-### 4.2 Standalone matrix\n139-\n140-| Profile | What Nexus sees | Runs | Pass condition |\n141-|---|---|---|---|\n142:| P-plain | Bare OpenAI-compatible `/models` and chat. No tokenize, no capacity headers. | Standalone T2 subset (≥ 10 held-out tasks) × 3 runs; T4 classes 1, 3, 4, 7 × 3 | T2 correctness ≥ (gateway-direct T2 correctness on the same tasks − 10 pts). False VERIFIED = 0. T4 truthful = 100%. Context source reported as `client_default` or an operator override, with no error. |\n143-| P-llamacpp | Emulated llama.cpp `/props` and overflow body | Same tasks × 1 run; plus the forced-overflow case (context limit set to 8k) | Context discovered from `/props`. Overflow gives one compact-and-retry, then success or an actionable error. |\n144-| P-vllm | Emulated `max_model_len` and vLLM overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `max_model_len` |\n145-| P-ollama | Emulated `/api/show` and Ollama overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `ollama_show` |\n146-| Conform…373 tokens truncated…2-| T3 false-absence | = 0 |\n263-| T3 false-presence | = 0 |\n264-| T3 steering honoured | ≥ 95% |\n265-| Operator interventions in `run` mode | = 0 |\n--\n304-   - ACC-CONT-01, 03;\n305-   - ACC-VER-01, 03;\n306-   - ACC-PKG-01;\n307-   - 5 random T2 tasks;\n308:   - 2 T4 classes.\n309-2. One live long task (≥ 60 steps, ≥ 2 compactions) on the RC through the gateway, including one kill and resume.\n310-3. A review of the scorer verdict and of contamination handling.\n311-\n312-**Output:** `docs/reviews/<date>-v1-rc-independent-acceptance.md` with an ACCEPT, ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS, or REJECT verdict per area. \"Accept with defects\" needs an owner disposition for every defect, and for a blocker area the only acceptable disposition is a fix.\n{\"body\":\"## Scope\\nRun M5 only against an exact accepted RC after all prerequisites and explicit operation-specific authorizations are satisfied. This is not authorized by issue creation or by synthetic results.\\n\\n## Linked requirements\\nREQ-AGT-002; REQ-QUAL-101, REQ-QUAL-103, REQ-QUAL-104, REQ-QUAL-105, REQ-QUAL-107, REQ-QUAL-109; REQ-PRV-111. The terminal matrix (REQ-QUAL-108) is tracked separately in issue #3, and independent continuity acceptance (REQ-AGT-110) is tracked separately in issue #6.\\n\\n## Acceptance\\n- Freeze run population, scoring, identities, configs, budgets, and unique output directories before execution.\\n- Complete T2 (5 runs per task/configuration), T3 (8×5), T4 (accepted fault matrix), standalone proxy profiles, and required provider verification.\\n- Preserve original failures, retries, manifests, and hashes; no post-result exclusions or tuning on held-out data.\\n- Apply unchanged thresholds and obtain independent acceptance under ACCEPTANCE.md.\\n- Update relevant ledger evidence only after exact-RC gates pass.\\n\\nReferences: `docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md` task 11; `docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md` §§4, 6–8.\",\"comments\":[{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Acceptance reconciliation required before T4 execution: ACCEPTANCE.md §6.2 says “8 fault classes × 5 runs” but enumerates nine fault classes (items 1–9). PLAN-10 task 11 also says T4 (8×5), while PLAN-10 task 5 and eval/README.md describe class 9 (SIGTERM then resume). No class has been removed and no threshold has been selected here. The release owner/spec owner must resolve the denominator and run matrix without post-result relaxation; until then T4 execution is blocked.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-17T02:25:37Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Status check at `6a16cb6` (claude-code).\\n\\n- **T4 denominator (prior comment):** resolved in ACCEPTANCE.md §6.2. The DEC-05 amendment (PRs #11/#13) keeps **9 fault classes × 5 runs**, including SIGTERM + resume. **Remaining inconsistency:** `docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md` line 34 (task 11) still says \\\"T4 (8×5)\\\". A boundary request to the plan owner is in the claim log; ACCEPTANCE §6.2 is authoritative.\\n- **Prerequisites not yet met:** no RC exists (package `0.1.0-alpha.2`). PR #33 (evaluator confidentiality and hardened-legacy checks) is open with CHANGES-REQUIRED, and held-out runs are prohibited until it is accepted. The qualification host is provisioned and validated on PR #33's branch, but that has not been accepted on integration.\\n- Requirements `--enforce` still fails at `6a16cb6`: 11 rows below threshold, including all of this issue's QUAL rows plus REQ-AGT-002 and REQ-PRV-111.\\n\\nNo M5 run has started.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-18T17:34:27Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"T4 denominator reconciliation (2026-10-22, source check at `main@a4a7edd9a17a0015abdf8135ecf3c1caac05560c`): the inconsistency described in the October 18 note is no longer present in current main. `ACCEPTANCE.md` §6.2 specifies nine fault classes × five runs, including SIGTERM/resume, and PLAN-10 task 11 now says `T4 (9×5)`. The separate run-wall-time table still contains the old `8×5` estimate, but explicitly labels it historical and says it predates the nine-class correction; it is not an execution denominator.\\n\\nThis resolves the planning-text discrepancy only. T4 qualification has not run and remains gated on an accepted installed RC, frozen workload, provider/standalone prerequisites, and the other stated qualification dependencies. No threshold or denominator was changed.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-22T22:47:41Z\"}]}\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17267-b4a8-7073-9d2a-32da76e0ee35","create_time":1792933451.0019195}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
