{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T13:04:55.320Z","ordinal":339085,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17267-b4a8-7073-9d2a-32da76e0ee35","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-22386e1c-3b46-4171-abec-b63ef73d323c","process_id":"45813","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/readiness-rc4-refresh diff --stat && git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/readiness-rc4-refresh diff -- docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md | sed -n '1,140p' && git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/readiness-rc4-refresh log -1 --format='%H %cs %s'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/readiness-rc4-refresh diff --stat && git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/readiness-rc4-refresh diff -- docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md | sed -n '1,140p' && git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/readiness-rc4-refresh log -1 --format='%H %cs %s'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":" docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md | 36 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n 1 file changed, 36 insertions(+)\ndiff --git a/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md b/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\nindex bf5f5de..c957507 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\n+++ b/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\n@@ -1,3 +1,39 @@\n+## Current release convergence status (observed 2026-10-24 20:57 UTC at `29eab4c`)\n+\n+**Authoritative source and source gates:** `origin/main` is `29eab4cd58051a8210b5ef66e0c9e248b2046a13`; `origin/v1/integration` is `7d6673f108316dda015b858c85b2abe20f3a4f78` and is not the release source. Exact-main CI [40123199081](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40123199081) completed successfully on `29eab4c`: Node 22, Node 24, and Linux x86-64 passed the CLI suite, security gates, package build, reproducibility checks, SBOM validation, package smoke, and installer smoke. Exact-main CodeQL [40123199130](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40123199130) also passed. In a clean detached checkout with isolated HOME/XDG, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed on this exact SHA: 123 rows (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open), with 12 requirements explicitly deferred to exact-RC qualification. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` passed and reports all components at `1.0.0-rc.4`. These are source-gate results, not acceptance of an installed candidate.\n+\n+**Release candidate identity:** The latest public prerelease remains [v1.0.0-rc.4](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.4), tag object `79b2f4fab6b9584c4e4e3245a5359f009889b7e2`, peeling to source `57b9285c6cead27b2260bf3113b3fc0b847f8169`. Current main descends from that source but contains later changes, including the merged reproducibility fixes in PRs #194 and #196. RC.4 is immutable and does not contain those later changes. A new versioned candidate (next sequence: RC.5) is needed after the remaining source PRs integrate and pass exact-head checks. No stable v1.0.0 release exists; GitHub installer/archive is the approved distribution, and npm publication is inapplicable.\n+\n+**Open source convergence:** PR #200 head `81928bd81d10ec957a3063a0e414aef981c83b20` has independent review ACCEPT; CodeQL passed and Node 22/24 CI was running at the latest check. PR #203 head `ef404986e60a9f53b2d5ea3fca55cf08dada60b3` also has independent review ACCEPT; Node 22/24 checks passed, CodeQL passed, and Linux x86-64 packaging checks were still running. A reviewer identified a read-only status-display inconsistency in REPL/sidecar as a user-visible follow-up. The local folder-trust/permission decoupling change is on an unintegrated local branch at `e9486c6`; it is not independently acceptable yet because the separately claimed `agent.ts` fallback still maps a trusted workspace with missing mode to `auto`, and two headless errors suggest `nexus trust .` changes approvals. No edit or takeover of that active claim is recorded.\n+\n+**Held-out and provider qualification:** Issue #1 has no new custodian acceptance in the public status thread; the latest request is comment `6378649211`. No private payload was accessed and no held-out task was run. The public 40-task manifest alone does not prove private custody, independent validation, or a compatible evaluator path. RC.4-bound provider, standalone, T2/T3/T4, long-task and fault-injection qualification, and independent RC acceptance remain unproven. The source evaluator resource and Git-isolation fixtures are not held-out qualification evidence.\n+\n+**Cross-runner reproducibility:** The exact-RC workflow fixes merged through PRs #194 and #196, and current main CI proves same-runner deterministic packaging. The cross-runner workflow has not yet produced accepted evidence for a current candidate: RC.4's earlier run failed before comparison, and it cannot include the archive-normalization source changes now on main. Run the accepted Ubuntu 22.04/24.04 workflow only after publishing the new exact candidate, and bind its comparison to the tag, source, workflow revision, and published artifact digests.\n+\n+**Human terminal matrix:** A connected Ubuntu 26.04 GNOME desktop has an active local GNOME/Wayland session. Preflight found xterm `XTerm(407)`, kitty `0.45.0`, GNOME Terminal `3.58.0`, tmux `3.6`, and VS Code `1.143.1` installed. The `nexus` command is not installed there. Issue #3 comment `6389426338` records this setup-only result. The human matrix remains **0/15**; every cell requires the §5.3 interactive checks and screenshots of both the approval panel and restored post-exit terminal. Automated PTY results do not count. Install the exact selected candidate before running any cell.\n+\n+**Disposition:** `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance `IN_PROGRESS`. Publication authorization remains granted and gated. The next source actions are to finish and integrate PRs #200 and #203 through their checks, resolve the trust/approval fallback and read-only status-display defects under their claims, and requalify the resulting exact main revision. Then construct RC.5 through the accepted workflow and continue installed-candidate qualification. No accepted RC or stable release is claimed.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Current release convergence status (observed 2026-10-24 14:12 UTC at `be2cd2f`)\n+\n+**Authoritative source and source gates:** `origin/main` is `be2cd2f255414f554572c86baa884d9271ff5ea1`. Exact-head CI [40098339766](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40098339766) completed successfully on this SHA: Node 22, Node 24, and Linux x86-64 package/reproducibility/SBOM/package-smoke/installer-smoke jobs passed. Exact-head CodeQL [40098339763](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40098339763) passed. The requirements enforcement record for this revision reports 123 requirements: 108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, and 7 open; 12 rows remain explicitly deferred to exact-RC qualification. These results establish source gates only.\n+\n+**Distribution and release candidate:** The supported distribution target is the GitHub installer/archive; npm publication is inapplicable. The published GitHub prerelease [v1.0.0-rc.4](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/releases/tag/v1.0.0-rc.4) is bound to tag object `79b2f4fab6b9584c4e4e3245a5359f009889b7e2`, peeling to source `57b9285c6cead27b2260bf3113b3fc0b847f8169`. Its Linux archive is `nexus-linux-x86_64-v1.0.0-rc.4.tar.gz`, with GitHub SHA-256 `07867e26077e5eec6f2cb665c4c34045a116669cacbe7f81f62f40b6fac8b806`. RC4 is a published qualification candidate, not an accepted RC; it predates the current main source and is not changed by CI on `be2cd2f`.\n+\n+**Known RC4 user-facing behavior:** The reported `Sensitive content prevents durable persistence to checkpoint` startup failure was reproduced as a limitation of immutable RC1. The choice flow is integrated in later source: read-only, continue without a rollback checkpoint, create the checkpoint with the sensitivity risk acknowledged, cancel, or enter a different instruction. Source integration does not establish this flow on an installed candidate; it must be exercised against the exact candidate. The folder-trust chooser matching the requested startup behavior is also present in current main and RC4 source.\n+\n+**Reproducibility remediation:** RC4 cross-runner workflow [40092008160](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40092008160) built the tagged source on Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04 but failed before comparison because the workflow used an invalid `actions/download-artifact` SHA. PR [#194](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/194) pins the correct download action on head `6b84a97a092dbc9a04bb056ac7fba504bfd65685`, based on this exact main revision. At this checkpoint, its Node 22 and Node 24 checks are running; TypeScript, CodeQL, actionlint, and diff checks pass, and independent source review accepted the unchanged patch. Separately, reproducibility testing identified archive bytes differing due to tar metadata. The candidate `0f6bf66ba943eb3c9c64ae563c2b23f6970a6d5a` uses the pinned build container for archive creation and has an independent exact-diff ACCEPT plus static checks; its full tests and CI have not run. The SUITE claim is still held by `KimiCode-defect-scan`; an explicit safe-boundary handoff was requested, and no takeover or local test run has occurred.\n+\n+**Qualification status:** No RC4-bound provider or standalone engineering qualification record was found. The latest provider evidence is bound to RC3: ChatGPT and pinned OpenRouter checks passed, but the required live engineering task remains incomplete. The sealed T2 corpus still uses a legacy validator format incompatible with the current evaluator; T2 qualification has not started. Public T2/T3 manifests are metadata only and do not constitute custody acceptance. The public-only custody refresh found no custodian acknowledgement after Issue #1 comment #6378649211, no active custodian claim, and no change to PR #16. No private payload or validator was accessed. T3/T4, long-task and nine-class fault injection, exact-RC provider/standalone qualification, and independent RC acceptance remain incomplete.\n+\n+**Human terminal matrix:** The required five environments are xterm, kitty with keyboard protocol, tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code terminal, and GNOME Terminal, each at 80×24, 40×14, and 200×60. Two screenshots are required per cell by the acceptance worksheet. The latest recorded host setup identifies the connected Ubuntu/GNOME desktop and installed terminal applications, but no human matrix cell has qualifying evidence: 0/15. Automated PTY checks do not satisfy this gate. The matrix must use the exact candidate selected for qualification.\n+\n+**Release disposition:** Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`. RC4 remains published but unaccepted. Stable v1.0.0 publication is authorized and gated by independent exact-RC acceptance. Next: complete PR #194 exact-head checks and integrate it through the approved path; then integrate and qualify the archive-byte reproducibility correction before rerunning RC4 cross-runner comparison. Continue custody, provider, and human terminal work only within their independent ownership and artifact boundaries. No release acceptance or stable publication is claimed.\n+\n+---\n+\n # v1.0.0 release readiness checkpoint\n \n ## Current release convergence status (observed 2026-10-23 13:35 UTC at `1f3c655`)\nbe2cd2f255414f554572c86baa884d9271ff5ea1 2026-10-24 Merge pull request #193 from mikeholownych/v1/defect-mcp-config-persist\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":26869}},"started_at_ms":1792933495319,"completed_at_ms":1792933495320}}
