ect `79b2f4fab6b9584c4e4e3245a5359f009889b7e2`, peeling to source `57b9285c6cead27b2260bf3113b3fc0b847f8169`. Current main descends from that source but contains later changes, including the merged reproducibility fixes in PRs #194 and #196. RC.4 is immutable and does not contain those later changes. A new versioned candidate (next sequence: RC.5) is needed after the remaining source PRs integrate and pass exact-head checks. No stable v1.0.0 release exists; GitHub installer/archive is the approved distribution, and npm publication is inapplicable.\n+\n+**Open source convergence:** PR #200 head `81928bd81d10ec957a3063a0e414aef981c83b20` has independent review ACCEPT; CodeQL passed and Node 22/24 CI was running at the latest check. PR #203 head `ef404986e60a9f53b2d5ea3fca55cf08dada60b3` also has independent review ACCEPT; Node 22…1462 tokens truncated…n. The SUITE claim is still held by `KimiCode-defect-scan`; an explicit safe-boundary handoff was requested, and no takeover or local test run has occurred.\n+\n+**Qualification status:** No RC4-bound provider or standalone engineering qualification record was found. The latest provider evidence is bound to RC3: ChatGPT and pinned OpenRouter checks passed, but the required live engineering task remains incomplete. The sealed T2 corpus still uses a legacy validator format incompatible with the current evaluator; T2 qualification has not started. Public T2/T3 manifests are metadata only and do not constitute custody acceptance. The public-only custody refresh found no custodian acknowledgement after Issue #1 comment #6378649211, no active custodian claim, and no change to PR #16. No private payload or validator was accessed. T3/T4, long-task and nine-class fault injection, exact-RC provider/standalone qualification, and independent RC acceptance remain incomplete.\n+\n+**Human terminal matrix:** The required five environments are xterm, kitty with keyboard protocol, tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code terminal, and GNOME Terminal, each at 80×24, 40×14, and 200×60. Two screenshots are required per cell by the acceptance worksheet. The latest recorded host setup identifies the connected Ubuntu/GNOME desktop and installed terminal applications, but no human matrix cell has qualifying evidence: 0/15. Automated PTY checks do not satisfy this gate. The matrix must use the exact candidate selected for qualification.\n+\n+**Release disposition:** Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`. RC4 remains published but unaccepted. Stable v1.0.0 publication is authorized and gated by independent exact-RC acceptance. Next: complete PR #194 exact-head checks and integrate it through the approved path; then integrate and qualify the archive-byte reproducibility correction before rerunning RC4 cross-runner comparison. Continue custody, provider, and human terminal work only within their independent ownership and artifact boundaries. No release acceptance or stable publication is claimed.\n+\n+---\n+\n # v1.0.0 release readiness checkpoint\n \n ## Current release convergence status (observed 2026-10-23 13:35 UTC at `1f3c655`)\nbe2cd2f255414f554572c86baa884d9271ff5ea1 2026-10-24 Merge pull request #193 from mikeholownych/v1/defect-mcp-config-persist\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17267-b4a8-7073-9d2a-32da76e0ee35","create_time":1792933496.3147054}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
