{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T13:06:27.025Z","ordinal":339152,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17267-b4a8-7073-9d2a-32da76e0ee35","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-a92e31f7-1962-4c72-82c0-29479303f141","process_id":"96905","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md | rg -n -C 3 'DEC-06|model|provider' | head -80 && git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | sed -n '125,160p' && git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | sed -n '68,86p'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md | rg -n -C 3 'DEC-06|model|provider' | head -80 && git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | sed -n '125,160p' && git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md | sed -n '68,86p'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"11-| [DEC-03](#dec-03-team-and-operation-scope-in-v1) | `/team` and `nexus operation` in v1 | Shipped as **experimental**; data-loss fix still a blocker | No |\n12-| [DEC-04](#dec-04-issue-12-open-normative-blockers) | Issue #12 open blockers | EXT-004 implemented; CTX-001 partially implemented; CTX-002 descoped post-v1 | No |\n13-| [DEC-05](#dec-05-v1-evaluation-protocol-and-thresholds) | Evaluation protocol and thresholds | 40 held-out T2 tasks, 5 runs, 2 peers, thresholds below | Needs an external author (see actions) |\n14:| [DEC-06](#dec-06-supported-providers-for-v1) | Supported providers | Local OpenAI-compatible + OpenRouter supported; others experimental until live-verified | No |\n15-| [DEC-07](#dec-07-experimental-surfaces-nexus-eval-tdd-team-roles) | `nexus eval`, `/tdd`, team roles | eval and tdd experimental; eval's workspace mutation fixed; role tool sets enforced | No |\n16-| [DEC-08](#dec-08-version-identity-and-stale-v1x-tags) | Version identity, stale v1.x tags | `package.json` is the source of truth; local v1.x tags deleted (owner action) | No |\n17-| [DEC-09](#dec-09-release-provenance-mechanism) | Release provenance | GitHub artifact attestations | No |\n--\n28-\n29-## DEC-01: Default execution posture\n30-\n31:**Question.** What protects the user by default from model-initiated command execution and network egress? See SEC-01, VER-01, HIST-05 and TUI-07.\n32-\n33-| Option | Description | Tradeoffs |\n34-|---|---|---|\n--\n83-**Chosen protocol (SPEC-10):**\n84-- 40 held-out T2 tasks, at least 20 from external repositories at pinned commits, across JS/TS, Python, Rust and Go, with at least 6 per class (bugfix, feature, refactor, debug).\n85-- 5 runs per task and configuration.\n86:- Peers: Goose and OpenCode, on the same model and budgets.\n87-- 9 T4 fault classes × 5 runs.\n88-- 8 T3 long tasks × 5 runs.\n89-\n--\n109-\n110-**Task authorship.** The owner authorized agent authorship for the T2 tasks on 2026-10-14. A separately-run agent session authors the held-out tasks. It is given only the task schema and the external repositories, with no access to Nexus source, the development set, or tuning history. Its sha256 manifest is committed before the RC freeze. The qualification report must state that the authors were agents, not humans.\n111-\n112:**Inference environment.** All runs go through the homelab-ai gateway, which is the only inference path (owner, 2026-10-14). There is no direct worker access and no extra GPU. Every run, Nexus and peers alike, is serial on one gateway-backed model. Wall time is the critical-path cost (PLAN-10). Live cloud connections (ChatGPT sign-in, OpenRouter) may be used for small-spend checks, but are not used for matched comparisons. One reason: `openrouter/free` routed 3 requests to 3 different models in the 2026-10-14 verify run, which breaks model matching.\n113-\n114-**Rationale.** These figures are the pilot's pre-registered thresholds (eval/README), tightened where the pilot showed weakness: false VERIFIED, crash accounting. The absolute floor prevents \"beat a weak peer\" from passing. Thresholds are fixed **before** the RC run.\n115-\n116:## DEC-06: Supported providers for v1\n117-\n118-| Tier | Providers | Condition |\n119-|---|---|---|\n120-| **Supported** | OpenAI-compatible local servers (llama.cpp server, vLLM, LM Studio, Ollama) | The release notes name the server kinds that pass the standalone matrix (≥ 2 required). Others are listed as \"compatible, not qualified\". |\n121-| **Supported (optional integration)** | homelab-ai gateway | Never required (standalone gate). |\n122:| **Supported** | OpenRouter | Live-verified 2026-10-14 at db1ca55 (`evidence/live/verify_openrouter.json`); re-verify at RC with a **pinned** model (not `openrouter/free`). |\n123:| **Experimental → Supported if live-verified at RC** | OpenAI API key (Responses), Anthropic (Messages), generic compatible cloud | Not connected on the owner's install. They stay experimental unless keys are added and `nexus providers verify` passes at RC. |\n124-| **Experimental (always)** | ChatGPT sign-in (the owner's OpenAI OAuth connection), Copilot sign-in | They use unofficial OAuth flows with terms-of-service and stability risk. Opt-in with a visible warning. ChatGPT sign-in was live-verified on 2026-10-14 (`evidence/live/verify_chatgpt.json`), and a live end-to-end run reached a correct VERIFIED (`evidence/live/run1_chatgpt_bugfix.log`). It is still labelled experimental because the sign-in flow is unofficial. |\n125-\n126-## DEC-07: Experimental surfaces (`nexus eval`, `/tdd`, team roles)\n--\n194-| Option | Description | Assessment |\n195-|---|---|---|\n196-| A | Require a second GPU host running plain servers | Not available. Rejected. |\n197:| B | Qualify standalone only by mocks | Too weak: it never exercises real model behaviour. Rejected as the only evidence. |\n198-| **C (chosen)** | Two-part standalone gate | See below. |\n199-\n200-**Option C, part 1: live gateway-stripped runs (REQ-PRV-106 part a).**\n201-- Nexus runs in a clean HOME with no homelab configuration: no `config.env` gateway entries, no gateway token file, no `X-Task-Class`.\n202:- It talks to `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` on `127.0.0.1`. The proxy forwards to the gateway with the gateway token injected on the proxy side. It strips every gateway extension: `/v1/models` is reduced to `{id, object, owned_by}`, `/v1/tokenize` returns 404, and `X-AIHost-*` response headers and admission headers are removed.\n203:- In a second profile, the proxy rewrites the `/models` and overflow-error shapes into the documented formats of llama.cpp `server`, vLLM and Ollama. That exercises each server kind's discovery and capacity-error path against real model output.\n204-- The standalone T2 subset (≥ 10 tasks) and the T4 subset run in both profiles.\n205-- The proxy only **removes** information. The gateway itself is unchanged, and all workload still flows through it, as the owner requires.\n206-\n207-**Option C, part 2: server-kind conformance (REQ-PRV-106 part b).**\n208:- Response-shape fixtures for llama.cpp, vLLM, LM Studio and Ollama are written from each project's published API documentation, with source references and versions recorded. They cover `/models`, `/props`, `/api/v0/models`, `/api/show`, SSE tool-call deltas, think tags and overflow bodies.\n209-- The fixtures run in CI.\n210:- Optionally, a CPU-only llama.cpp `server` built without AVX (this dev box is a Xeon X5650) with a ≤ 1.5B model is used for a protocol smoke test: one streamed reply, one tool call, one overflow. That is real server code, but task quality is out of scope.\n211-\n212-**Release statement:**\n213:- Release notes say: \"Live-qualified against llama.cpp-served models through a plain OpenAI-compatible interface (gateway extensions removed). vLLM, LM Studio and Ollama: protocol-conformance tested, not live-qualified.\"\n214-- LM Studio stays \"compatible, not live-qualified\" unless a user-run report is added.\n215-\n216-**Tradeoff:** live evidence for server kinds other than llama.cpp is limited to emulated shapes. This is stated plainly rather than over-claimed.\n--\n245-| X1 | ~~`git tag -d v1.1.0 v1.2.0 v1.2.1`~~ **Done by the owner on 2026-10-14.** Verified: `git tag -l` now lists only `v0.1.0-alpha.1` and `v0.1.0-alpha.2`. | DEC-08 | Done |\n246-| X2 | ~~Provide an independent task author~~. **Resolved 2026-10-14 (T2) and 2026-10-18 (T3):** agent authorship authorized and completed for both T2 (`eval/heldout-manifest.json`, sha256 `50895b84…`, 40 tasks) and T3 (`eval/heldout-t3-manifest.json`, sha256 `85fb9caf…`, 8 tasks), each sealed under root-owned `0700` custody. | DEC-05 | Done |\n247-| X3 | ~~Separate standalone host~~. **Withdrawn:** no worker or GPU is available apart from the gateway. Replaced by DEC-16 (stripping proxy plus conformance fixtures). Remaining action: none. Optional: approve a CPU-only llama.cpp container on the dev box for the protocol smoke test. | DEC-16 | — |\n248:| X4 | **Partly resolved 2026-10-14:** the existing ChatGPT sign-in and OpenRouter connections are authorized for small-spend checks; both were live-verified at db1ca55. Optional: add OpenAI API-key or Anthropic keys if those providers should be listed as supported. | DEC-06 | M5 (optional) |\n249-| X5 | Independent reviewer for continuity/compaction acceptance and RC acceptance | REQ-AGT-110, ACCEPTANCE §8 | M5/M6 |\n250-| X6 | Provide a clean Cloudflare account and VM for CON-106; judging is over, so the historical erratum check is no longer applicable | DEC-13 | Post-contest |\n251-| X7 | **Authorized by the owner in the implementation/release handoff, reaffirmed by the 2026-10-18 takeover instruction.** Necessary commits, pushes, PRs, merges, RC tags and final v1.0.0 publication are authorized, conditional on the existing checks and acceptance gates. Release publisher: `codex-api-root`, succeeding rate-limited `claude-code`; no duplicate publisher. See [authorization and handoff](../reviews/evidence/v1/RELEASE-TAKEOVER/authorization-and-handoff.md). | Release | Authorization resolved; execution remains gated |\n### 4.1 Clean-HOME procedure\n\n1. `export HOME=$(mktemp -d)`.\n2. Install the RC with the documented command.\n3. Create `~/.config/nexus/config.env` containing only:\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:<proxy>/v1`\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_MODEL=<id as listed by the proxy>`\n   - `LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY=REDACTED\n\n   No gateway token file, no homelab paths, no `NODE_*` overrides.\n4. Start `node eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs --upstream <gateway> --token-file <operator token> [--emulate <kind>]`. The gateway token stays with the proxy and never reaches the Nexus HOME.\n5. Run `nexus doctor --json` and archive it. It must report the server kind and context source with no `gateway` capability.\n\n### 4.2 Standalone matrix\n\n| Profile | What Nexus sees | Runs | Pass condition |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| P-plain | Bare OpenAI-compatible `/models` and chat. No tokenize, no capacity headers. | Standalone T2 subset (≥ 10 held-out tasks) × 3 runs; T4 classes 1, 3, 4, 7 × 3 | T2 correctness ≥ (gateway-direct T2 correctness on the same tasks − 10 pts). False VERIFIED = 0. T4 truthful = 100%. Context source reported as `client_default` or an operator override, with no error. |\n| P-llamacpp | Emulated llama.cpp `/props` and overflow body | Same tasks × 1 run; plus the forced-overflow case (context limit set to 8k) | Context discovered from `/props`. Overflow gives one compact-and-retry, then success or an actionable error. |\n| P-vllm | Emulated `max_model_len` and vLLM overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `max_model_len` |\n| P-ollama | Emulated `/api/show` and Ollama overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `ollama_show` |\n| Conformance | CI fixtures for llama.cpp, vLLM, LM Studio and Ollama shapes | CI | All pass (ACC-INF-01, -02, -05) |\n\nACC-INF-10 passes only when every row passes. The release notes state the scope in the form required by DEC-16.\n\n### 4.3 Provider matrix (E5)\n\n| Provider | Tier (DEC-06) | Required for v1.0.0 |\n|---|---|---|\n| OpenRouter, pinned model | Supported | `providers verify` PASS, plus one live small task (a §6-style bug fix) reaching a correct outcome |\n| ChatGPT sign-in | Experimental | Verify PASS recorded (already PASS at db1ca55; repeat on the RC) |\n| OpenAI API key, Anthropic | Experimental unless keys are added | If promoted: verify PASS plus one live task. Otherwise NOT RUN, and they are labelled experimental. |\n| Copilot | Experimental | Not required |\n\n## 5. Terminal acceptance (REQ-QUAL-108)\n\n   - `manifest.json`: commit, package sha256, environment, model fingerprint, dates;\n   - raw outputs;\n   - a `SHA256SUMS` file.\n\n   Secrets are redacted before commit.\n5. Any step that cannot run in the available environment is recorded as **NOT RUN** with its reason. A NOT RUN on a blocker gate fails the gate.\n\n## 2. Environments\n\n| ID | Environment | Used for |\n|---|---|---|\n| E1 | GitHub Actions: ubuntu-22.04 and ubuntu-24.04; Node 22 and 24; pinned Rust | Unit, integration and PTY suites; packaging; reproducibility |\n| E2 | Docker clean images: ubuntu:22.04, ubuntu:24.04, debian:12, fedora:40. Each with no Node, then with Node 20, Node 22 and Node 24. Non-root user. | Installer, upgrade, rollback, uninstall, platform failure messages |\n| E3 | Operator dev box: Linux x86-64, real terminals (xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal) | Terminal matrix, live sessions |\n| E4 | Homelab-ai gateway, the **only** inference path (DEC-16): direct, and through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` | Task-quality runs, standalone qualification, T3/T4 |\n| E5 | Cloud, small spend: ChatGPT sign-in (experimental tier) and OpenRouter with a pinned model; OpenAI and Anthropic keys if added | Provider verify; one live task per supported cloud provider |\n\n## 3. Gate checklist (G0–G4: automated acceptance IDs)\n\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":29502}},"started_at_ms":1792933587024,"completed_at_ms":1792933587025}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T13:06:28.687Z","ordinal":339153,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1732b-6ece-71d1-b1da-59144fd5ade7","call_id":"call_07a351238a2a4d14a1c351fdeb4d294a","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.7 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 3230)\nTotal output lines: 129\n\n11-| [DEC-03](#dec-03-team-and-operation-scope-in-v1) | `/team` and `nexus operation` in v1 | Shipped as **experimental**; data-loss fix still a blocker | No |\n12-| [DEC-04](#dec-04-issue-12-open-normative-blockers) | Issue #12 open blockers | EXT-004 implemented; CTX-001 partially implemented; CTX-002 descoped post-v1 | No |\n13-| [DEC-05](#dec-05-v1-evaluation-protocol-and-thresholds) | Evaluation protocol and thresholds | 40 held-out T2 tasks, 5 runs, 2 peers, thresholds below | Needs an external author (see actions) |\n14:| [DEC-06](#dec-06-supported-providers-for-v1) | Supported providers | Local OpenAI-compatible + OpenRouter supported; others experimental until live-verified | No |\n15-| [DEC-07](#dec-07-experimental-surfaces-nexus-eval-tdd-team-roles) | `nexus eval`, `/tdd`, team roles | eval and tdd experimental; eval's workspace mutation fixed; role tool sets enforced | No |\n16-| [DEC-08](#dec-08-version-identity-and-stale-v1x-tags) | Version identity, stale v1.x tags | `package.json` is the source of truth; local v1.x tags deleted (owner action) | No |\n17-| [DEC-09](#dec-09-release-provenance-mechanism) | Release provenance | GitHub artifact attestations | No |\n--\n28-\n29-## DEC-01: Default execution posture\n30-\n31:**Question.** What protects the user by default from model-initiated command execution and network egress? See SEC-01, VER-01, HIST-05 and TUI-07.\n32-\n33-| Option | Description | Tradeoffs |\n34-|---|---|---|\n--\n83-**Chosen protocol (SPEC-10):**\n84-- 40 held-out T2 tasks, at least 20 from external repositories at pinned commits, across JS/TS, Python, Rust and Go, with at least 6 per class (bugfix, feature, refactor, debug).\n85-- 5 runs per task and configuration.\n86:- Peers: Goose and OpenCode, on the same model and budgets.\n87-- 9 T4 fault classes × 5 runs.\n88-- 8 T3 long tasks × 5 runs.\n89-\n--\n109-\n110-**Task authorship.** The owner authorized agent authorship for the T2 tasks on 2026-10-14. A separately-run agent session authors the held-out tasks. It is given only the task schema and the external repositories, with no access to Nexus source, the development set, or tuning history. Its sha256 manifest is committed before the RC freeze. The qualification report must state that the authors were agents, not humans.\n111-\n112:**Inference environment.** All runs go through the homelab-ai gateway, which is the only inference path (owner, 2026-10-14). There is no direct worker access and no extra GPU. Every run, Nexus and peers alike, is serial on one gateway-backed model. Wall time is the critical-path cost (PLAN-10). Live cloud connection…1930 tokens truncated… Same tasks × 1 run; plus the forced-overflow case (context limit set to 8k) | Context discovered from `/props`. Overflow gives one compact-and-retry, then success or an actionable error. |\n| P-vllm | Emulated `max_model_len` and vLLM overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `max_model_len` |\n| P-ollama | Emulated `/api/show` and Ollama overflow body | Same as P-llamacpp | Same, with the context source `ollama_show` |\n| Conformance | CI fixtures for llama.cpp, vLLM, LM Studio and Ollama shapes | CI | All pass (ACC-INF-01, -02, -05) |\n\nACC-INF-10 passes only when every row passes. The release notes state the scope in the form required by DEC-16.\n\n### 4.3 Provider matrix (E5)\n\n| Provider | Tier (DEC-06) | Required for v1.0.0 |\n|---|---|---|\n| OpenRouter, pinned model | Supported | `providers verify` PASS, plus one live small task (a §6-style bug fix) reaching a correct outcome |\n| ChatGPT sign-in | Experimental | Verify PASS recorded (already PASS at db1ca55; repeat on the RC) |\n| OpenAI API key, Anthropic | Experimental unless keys are added | If promoted: verify PASS plus one live task. Otherwise NOT RUN, and they are labelled experimental. |\n| Copilot | Experimental | Not required |\n\n## 5. Terminal acceptance (REQ-QUAL-108)\n\n   - `manifest.json`: commit, package sha256, environment, model fingerprint, dates;\n   - raw outputs;\n   - a `SHA256SUMS` file.\n\n   Secrets are redacted before commit.\n5. Any step that cannot run in the available environment is recorded as **NOT RUN** with its reason. A NOT RUN on a blocker gate fails the gate.\n\n## 2. Environments\n\n| ID | Environment | Used for |\n|---|---|---|\n| E1 | GitHub Actions: ubuntu-22.04 and ubuntu-24.04; Node 22 and 24; pinned Rust | Unit, integration and PTY suites; packaging; reproducibility |\n| E2 | Docker clean images: ubuntu:22.04, ubuntu:24.04, debian:12, fedora:40. Each with no Node, then with Node 20, Node 22 and Node 24. Non-root user. | Installer, upgrade, rollback, uninstall, platform failure messages |\n| E3 | Operator dev box: Linux x86-64, real terminals (xterm, kitty, tmux, VS Code terminal, GNOME Terminal) | Terminal matrix, live sessions |\n| E4 | Homelab-ai gateway, the **only** inference path (DEC-16): direct, and through `eval/standalone/plain_proxy.mjs` | Task-quality runs, standalone qualification, T3/T4 |\n| E5 | Cloud, small spend: ChatGPT sign-in (experimental tier) and OpenRouter with a pinned model; OpenAI and Anthropic keys if added | Provider verify; one live task per supported cloud provider |\n\n## 3. Gate checklist (G0–G4: automated acceptance IDs)\n\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17267-b4a8-7073-9d2a-32da76e0ee35","create_time":1792933588.6869376}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
