{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T13:07:58.542Z","ordinal":339238,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17267-b4a8-7073-9d2a-32da76e0ee35","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-27786a84-6044-4159-b7f7-4cfb6d407611","process_id":"74811","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","/tmp/nexus-rc5-install-check/bin/nexus --help | rg -n 'provider|model|mode|workspace|approval'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"/tmp/nexus-rc5-install-check/bin/nexus --help | rg -n 'provider|model|mode|workspace|approval'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"10:  --approve                                    Require human approval before destructive actions (edits, shell commands)\n11:  -y, --yes                                    Run non-interactively without approval prompts (forces auto mode)\n12:  --mode <mode>                                Execution mode: auto, review, or read-only (default: review; folder trust does not change it)\n15:  -m, --model <name>                           Model name identifier (default: active model in vLLM)\n16:  -w, --workspace <path>                       Workspace directory (default: current directory)\n23:  -t, --temperature <number>                   Model temperature (default: 0.2)\n26:  --context-limit <tokens>                     Context window limit in tokens; below the provider's advertised capacity it is kept, above it the advertised capacity applies (default: advertised capacity, else 65536)\n28:  --sandbox [mode]                             Isolate command execution using bubblewrap (bwrap) or Docker (default: auto)\n31:  --deliverable-file <path>                    Operator-declared workspace-relative product file used for VERIFIED binding (repeatable) (default: [])\n33:  --planner-model <name>                       Deep reasoning model for architecture planning (o3, R1, Sonnet)\n34:  --planner-endpoint <url>                     Dedicated inference endpoint for planner model\n35:  --coder-model <name>                         High-throughput model for surgical code implementation (Qwen 2.5 Coder)\n36:  --coder-endpoint <url>                       Dedicated inference endpoint for coder model\n37:  --provider <id>                              Cloud inference provider: openrouter, openai, anthropic, compatible (default: appliance endpoint)\n38:  --base-url <url>                             Override the provider's base URL (operator-only; required for 'compatible')\n39:  --planner-provider <id>                      Cloud provider for the planner model (requires --planner-model)\n40:  --coder-provider <id>                        Cloud provider for the coder model (requires --coder-model)\n46:  models [options]                             List loaded models from your local LM Studio or vLLM server\n54:  trust [options] [path]                       Trust a workspace so its own .mcp.json servers and plugins are loaded (they run code from the workspace)\n55:  checkpoints [options]                        List saved workspace snapshots and rollback checkpoints\n57:  serve-mcp [options]                          Run Nexus Code as a Model Context Protocol (MCP) server over stdio\n67:  connect [options] <provider>                 Connect a cloud provider: save an API key (verified first) or sign in\n68:  disconnect <provider>                        Remove the credential Nexus saved for a provider (environment and other clients are untouched)\n69:  providers                                    List cloud inference providers, credential status and the selected destinations\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":294444609}},"started_at_ms":1792933678247,"completed_at_ms":1792933678542}}
