{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T13:10:00.055Z","ordinal":339328,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17267-b4a8-7073-9d2a-32da76e0ee35","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-8633099c-794b-44ac-8b2c-ef91576a4c42","process_id":"14154","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git show origin/main:scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md | sed -n '1,220p'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/running_notes.md | sed -n '1,180p'; for f in s1_startup.py s2_approval.py s3_complete.py s4_cancel.py s5_ctrlc.py s6_steer_cancel.py s7_resume.py s8_cancel_tool.py s9_quit_tool.py r1a.notes.txt r1d.py; do echo ===$f===; git show \"origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/$f\" 2>/dev/null | sed -n '1,24p'; done"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git show origin/main:scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md | sed -n '1,220p'; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/running_notes.md | sed -n '1,180p'; for f in s1_startup.py s2_approval.py s3_complete.py s4_cancel.py s5_ctrlc.py s6_steer_cancel.py s7_resume.py s8_cancel_tool.py s9_quit_tool.py r1a.notes.txt r1d.py; do echo ===$f===; git show \"origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/evidence/D_pty/$f\" 2>/dev/null | sed -n '1,24p'; done"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"failed","aggregated_output":"# Manual real-terminal matrix (ACCEPTANCE §5.3, REQ-QUAL-108)\n\nA human runs this procedure against the **installed RC**. Automated PTY suites (§5.1, §5.2) do not replace it.\n\n**Cells:** five terminals, each at 80×24, 40×14 and 200×60, giving 15 cells.\n- xterm\n- kitty, with the kitty keyboard protocol on\n- tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal\n- the VS Code integrated terminal\n- GNOME Terminal\n\n**Gate:** zero FAIL on checks 2, 5 and 6. Any other FAIL needs a written disposition.\n\n## Before you start\n\n1. Install the RC with the documented one-line command. `nexus --version` must print the RC version, and `nexus` must\n   not resolve into a checkout.\n2. Choose a new evidence directory, `OUT=docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/<rc>/terminal`, and use it for every cell.\n3. You need a screenshot tool, and `python3` and `git` on `PATH`. No inference is used: a local mock gateway\n   (`mockgw.py`) answers every request.\n\n## Each cell\n\nOpen the terminal and resize it to the cell's size. For tmux, start tmux inside GNOME Terminal. For kitty, enable the\nkeyboard protocol. Then run:\n\n```sh\nscripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh --rc <rc> --terminal <xterm|kitty|tmux-gnome|vscode|gnome> --size <WxH> --out \"$OUT\"\n```\n\nThe script refuses to start in these cases: the wrong RC, a checkout build, the wrong size, not inside tmux for\n`tmux-gnome`, or a cell already recorded. It creates an isolated HOME and workspace and starts the mock. Then it opens\nthe TUI twice, once normally and once with `NO_COLOR=1`, and prompts you through checks 1–7:\n\n| # | You do | You judge |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | The TUI opens | It renders correctly at this size |\n| 2 | Prompt `approve`. At each approval panel, type continuously, paste 3 lines, then approve with a deliberate key | No decision is made by the stray input, and the deliberate key decides. **Screenshot the panel.** |\n| 3 | Shift+Enter or Alt+Enter while composing | It inserts a newline and does not submit |\n| 4 | Prompt `stream`, then resize while it streams and restore the size | Layout recovers and nothing is garbled or lost |\n| 5 | Prompt `sleep`, then press Esc while `sleep 30` runs | Cancel is acknowledged, and nothing survives |\n| 6 | Press Ctrl-C twice to quit | The terminal is restored: echo on, no stray escape codes. **Screenshot the terminal after exit.** |\n| 7 | Second launch, with `NO_COLOR=1` | The TUI is readable without colour |\n\nThe script also **measures** two things:\n- whether `stty` state after each exit equals the state before it;\n- any process started from the cell's HOME that is still running after exit.\n\nA measured survivor or unavailable systemd-scope measurement fails check 5, and an unrestored terminal fails check 6, whatever you recorded. A zero survivor count is recorded only when the scope's `cgroup.procs` file was readable or systemd confirmed the scope stopped or disappeared. Missing or unreadable scope data while the unit is active is recorded as unavailable and fails the matrix gate. Each cell writes\n`cell-<terminal>-<size>.json` with the RC version, binary path and SHA-256, terminal environment, measurements, your\nresults and notes, screenshot hashes, and the mock request log. A cell is recorded once. To retry, keep the failed\nattempt and use a new evidence directory.\n\n## Gate\n\nThe deterministic systemd-scope measurement fixtures run as part of `npm test` in `cli/`. They cover empty and\npopulated cgroups, stopped and missing units, unavailable or malformed measurements, and the summary gate's response\nto an unavailable measurement.\n\n```sh\n# MANIFEST_SHA: sha256 of MANIFEST.sha256 inside the RC archive, e.g.\n#   tar -xzOf nexus-linux-x86_64-<rc>.tar.gz --wildcards '*/MANIFEST.sha256' | sha256sum\nnode scripts/terminal-acceptance/summarize.mjs \"$OUT\" --rc <rc> --manifest-sha256 \"$MANIFEST_SHA\" [--dispositions dispositions.json]\n```\n\nThe summarizer prints the 15-cell table and writes `matrix-summary.json`. **PASS** requires all of the following:\n- every cell is present (a missing cell is NOT RUN);\n- every attempt names the given RC, and its installed package manifest equals the archive's;\n- checks 2, 5 and 6 have no FAIL;\n- every other FAIL has an entry `\"<cell>:<check>\": \"<fix or documented known limitation>\"` in the dispositions file;\n- every aborted attempt (a `.partial` file, which holds the measurements taken before it was abandoned) has an entry\n  `\"<cell>:partial-<n>\"`.\n\nThe record hashes prove that files are unchanged since recording, not who recorded them. Commit the evidence directory\nto the qualification evidence PR to make it authoritative.\n# Scope D — Terminal experience (nexus-tui live + REPL) — v1.0.0 readiness audit\n\nStatus: IN PROGRESS (written incrementally). Repo HEAD db1ca55. Runtime evidence uses HEAD-built snap binaries\n(`scratchpad/snap/core/target/release/nexus-tui`, `scratchpad/snap/cli/dist`) unless noted; first startup run (s1) used\n`/home/mike/nexus-code/core/target/release/nexus-tui` (built 2026-10-13 17:38, no core/ commits since — INFERENCE: matches HEAD).\nPTY transcripts: `scratchpad/audit/D_pty/` (`*.raw` raw bytes, `*.screens.txt` pyte screen dumps, `*.notes.txt` timelines).\n\n## Running findings (folded into section 3 at the end)\n- s1a: unreachable endpoint (127.0.0.1:9) -> startup screen gives no endpoint health signal; first prompt enters an\n  open-ended \"Inference provider temporarily unavailable (network_error); waiting Ns\" loop (28s+, 7 retries) with no\n  endpoint URL, no fix hint (`harness doctor`, LOCAL_LLM_ENDPOINT, /connect). Esc/Ctrl-C cancels cleanly (\"Cancelled  You\n  stopped the turn during provider wait\"). Continuation lines \"Work is preserved.\" wrap to column 0 (not indented).\n- s2 (TUI --approve, write_file): continuous typing \"yes y y please yy\\ry\\r\" at 120ms gaps across panel appearance,\n  bracketed paste \"y\\ny\\nyes\\n\", unbracketed burst \"yyyyyyyy\\r\\r\\r\", 'y' at 40x14, and a lone 'y' after 2.5s quiet\n  -> NONE decided (file absent); panel switched to \"typing ignored · ←→ approve/deny, pause, enter\". Right + 2.3s +\n  Enter asked \"enter again approves\"; second Enter approved -> file created. PASS (RUNTIME).\n  The pre-panel typed text \"yes y y please yy\" was sent to the model as steering (\"steering · applied\").\n- s2: arrow mapping is spatially inverted: buttons render \"Approve · Approve all later · Deny\" left->right, but\n  Right selects Approve and Left selects Deny (live_state.rs on_approval_key `KeyCode::Left => Denied`). Mitigated by\n  two-step confirm on typed-into panels; letters-mode panel takes one Enter after → (dwell 400ms).\n- s3 (no typing): panel shows \"y Approve  a Approve all later actions  n Deny\"; 'y' after 2.5s approved. Turn end\n  ~5.4s after the approval for a 1-line write (MEASUREMENT). Unicode reply \"完成 ✅ — naïve café 🎉\" rendered correctly\n  at 80x24. Result banner \"! Done · not verified ... → next: /diff or /test\" (good recovery guidance).\n- 40x14: approval hint truncated mid-word (\"…←→ approve/deny, paus\"), footer \"(t…\" — the key instruction is cut.\n- s4a (40x20, NO_COLOR=1): 0 colour SGRs in 867 SGR codes; states carry glyph+word (✓ ◌ ! \"Cancelled\"). Header drops\n  session id; hints truncated with \"…\". Steering during stream -> \"queued for the next step\"; Ctrl-C -> steer \"not\n  applied ... back in the composer\" (good). One run showed \"cancelling…\" for >=11s after Ctrl-C (s4a); 3 reruns\n  (s5/s6/s6n) cancelled in 0.2-2.4s -> intermittent, UNVERIFIED (possible CPU contention from the parallel baseline).\n- s4b: Esc during `run_command \"sleep 20\"` -> tool NOT interrupted; turn ended only when the command finished\n  (Esc->idle 19.5s; \"Cancelled  You stopped the turn during tool settling\"). A hung command cannot be cancelled\n  short of quitting (Ctrl-C x2).\n- r1a (REPL --approve): a lone Enter at \"[Y/n/d/a]\" APPROVED the write (repl.ts:376 `trimmed === \"\"` approves).\n- r1d (REPL --approve): 'y' typed mid-turn (before the prompt existed) + Enter after the prompt appeared -> APPROVED.\n  Typed-ahead partial lines join the approval answer (r1b: answer echoed garbled \" call it greeting.txtwait, actually\").\n- r1b/r1c: non-y answers deny (\"Tool execution cancelled by user.\"); pasted extra lines reported as ignored (good).\n- Launcher: packaged `bin/nexus` = `node lib/cli/dist/index.js` (scripts/package-linux.sh:25-30); no code path in\n  cli/src launches `nexus-tui --live` (grep: none). `nexus` -> readline REPL (index.js:747). Packaged\n  `lib/core/nexus-tui --live` fails: \"sidecar not found at <pkg>/../cli/dist/sidecar.js\" (live.rs:128-131 assumes\n  checkout layout `core/target/<profile>`). USER_MANUAL.md:19 `nexus --approve` and :23 `nexus -r` -> \"error: unknown\n  option\" (RUNTIME). quickstart.md:57 says \"review requested actions\" but default `nexus` is autonomous.\nzsh:1: ==s1_startup.py=== not found\n","exit_code":1,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":30452}},"started_at_ms":1792933800054,"completed_at_ms":1792933800055}}
