{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T13:10:42.336Z","ordinal":339362,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17267-b4a8-7073-9d2a-32da76e0ee35","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-377e7452-af7d-4d82-8da4-c77b2720d0de","process_id":"33614","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","for n in 1 2 3 5 49; do gh issue view \"$n\" --json number,title,state,updatedAt,comments --jq '{number,title,state,updatedAt,lastComments:(.comments|map({createdAt,author:.author.login,body})|.[-2:])}'; done; gh pr list --state open --search 'cross-runner OR reproducibility' --json number,title,headRefName,updatedAt,url; gh run list --workflow repro.yml --limit 6 --json databaseId,headSha,status,conclusion,event,createdAt,url; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md | tail -100"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"for n in 1 2 3 5 49; do gh issue view \"$n\" --json number,title,state,updatedAt,comments --jq '{number,title,state,updatedAt,lastComments:(.comments|map({createdAt,author:.author.login,body})|.[-2:])}'; done; gh pr list --state open --search 'cross-runner OR reproducibility' --json number,title,headRefName,updatedAt,url; gh run list --workflow repro.yml --limit 6 --json databaseId,headSha,status,conclusion,event,createdAt,url; git show origin/main:docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md | tail -100"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"{\"lastComments\":[{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Release convergence update (public metadata only): post-merge CI and CodeQL now pass on current main `4e7297f545538e6422ca3890334a7036f58287ca` (CI run `40156576300`, CodeQL run `40156576296`). RC4 remains the newest prerelease; no stable release or final-candidate qualification has been established. The terminal matrix remains 0/15, T4 has not run, and the reproducibility workflow has not run on an RC. The metadata-only custody request from 2026-10-24 02:16 UTC remains unanswered.\\n\\nPlease reply to that request with the current custodian/owner, status and expected timing for independent custody acceptance, and whether a lossless compatibility path or replacement corpus is planned for the current evaluator contract. Please keep the reply to public metadata; do not post prompts, answers, validators, or protected task content. No held-out payload has been accessed by this implementation lane.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-25T03:55:09Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Follow-up for the current release candidate path (public metadata only): the current evaluator requires the blackbox-v1 task contract, while prior custody records describe the sealed legacy hidden-command corpus. Please confirm the currently assigned custodian, whether the sealed 40-task corpus can be qualified losslessly under the current evaluator or requires a newly versioned corpus, and the expected timing for the required custody acceptance and frozen run metadata. Please do not post task objectives, source payloads, validators, reference solutions, hidden results, or credentials here. No held-out execution has started.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-25T06:51:23Z\"}],\"number\":1,\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"PLAN-10 task 8: finish and seal the held-out T2/T3 corpus\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-25T06:51:23Z\"}\n{\"lastComments\":[{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Status check at `6a16cb6` (claude-code).\\n\\n- **T4 denominator (prior comment):** resolved in ACCEPTANCE.md §6.2. The DEC-05 amendment (PRs #11/#13) keeps **9 fault classes × 5 runs**, including SIGTERM + resume. **Remaining inconsistency:** `docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md` line 34 (task 11) still says \\\"T4 (8×5)\\\". A boundary request to the plan owner is in the claim log; ACCEPTANCE §6.2 is authoritative.\\n- **Prerequisites not yet met:** no RC exists (package `0.1.0-alpha.2`). PR #33 (evaluator confidentiality and hardened-legacy checks) is open with CHANGES-REQUIRED, and held-out runs are prohibited until it is accepted. The qualification host is provisioned and validated on PR #33's branch, but that has not been accepted on integration.\\n- Requirements `--enforce` still fails at `6a16cb6`: 11 rows below threshold, including all of this issue's QUAL rows plus REQ-AGT-002 and REQ-PRV-111.\\n\\nNo M5 run has started.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-18T17:34:27Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"T4 denominator reconciliation (2026-10-22, source check at `main@a4a7edd9a17a0015abdf8135ecf3c1caac05560c`): the inconsistency described in the October 18 note is no longer present in current main. `ACCEPTANCE.md` §6.2 specifies nine fault classes × five runs, including SIGTERM/resume, and PLAN-10 task 11 now says `T4 (9×5)`. The separate run-wall-time table still contains the old `8×5` estimate, but explicitly labels it historical and says it predates the nine-class correction; it is not an execution denominator.\\n\\nThis resolves the planning-text discrepancy only. T4 qualification has not run and remains gated on an accepted installed RC, frozen workload, provider/standalone prerequisites, and the other stated qualification dependencies. No threshold or denominator was changed.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-22T22:47:41Z\"}],\"number\":2,\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"PLAN-10 task 11: complete preregistered M5 qualification runs\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-22T22:47:41Z\"}\n{\"lastComments\":[{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"### Terminal environment preflight (setup only; no qualification cells run)\\n\\nThe connected Ubuntu 26.04 GNOME desktop is reachable and has an active local GNOME/Wayland session. All required terminal applications are installed: xterm XTerm(407), kitty 0.45.0, GNOME Terminal 3.58.0, tmux 3.6, and VS Code 1.143.1. The `nexus` command is not installed on that host yet.\\n\\nThe matrix remains 0/15. Each cell still requires the real interactive checks in ACCEPTANCE.md §5.3 and two screenshots (approval panel and post-exit terminal state). Current public RC4 is not the current source head: its commit is an ancestor of `main` and later source changes exist, so this setup check does not qualify RC4 or any later candidate. Install and run only the exact candidate selected for qualification.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T20:55:35Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"### Terminal host preflight update (2026-10-25; setup only)\\n\\nThe Ubuntu 26.04 GNOME host has all five required terminal applications installed: xterm 407, kitty 0.45.0, GNOME Terminal 3.58.0, tmux 3.6, and VS Code 1.143.1. I also installed GitHub CLI 2.103.2 from GitHub CLI's official signed APT repository after verifying its published key fingerprint; `/usr/bin/gh attestation verify` is available for the candidate installer's provenance check.\\n\\nThis is environment setup only. No current-source RC is installed, no terminal cell has run, and the manual matrix remains 0/15. Each cell still needs the exact candidate identity, interactive checks, and both required screenshots.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-25T05:02:41Z\"}],\"number\":3,\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"PLAN-10 task 12: complete the real-terminal acceptance matrix\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-25T05:02:41Z\"}\n{\"lastComments\":[{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Status check at `6a16cb6` (claude-code): the workflow is integrated. `.github/workflows/repro.yml` plus `scripts/repro-identity.mjs` (PR #20) build on ubuntu-22.04 and 24.04 with fail-closed tag/commit/clean-tree/version identity. It has **not** run on an RC because no RC tag exists yet. REQ-REL-114 is still `RR`, correctly. Next action: once the RC is tagged, the release publisher (codex-api-root) runs repro.yml on the exact RC and attaches the run ID and artifact hashes here.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-18T17:34:28Z\"}],\"number\":5,\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"PLAN-07 PR-7e: prove cross-runner release reproducibility\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-18T17:34:28Z\"}\n{\"lastComments\":[{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only refresh on `mike-dev` (2026-10-21; no directory listing or private payload access): `/home` is `root:root 0755`; `/home/mike` is `mike:mike 0750`; `/home/mike/nexus-heldout-v2` is `root:root 0700`. `getfacl` showed only the base owner/group/other entries on these directories, with no additional ACL grants. The `nexus-eval` account is UID/GID 985 with only its own group; DAC therefore denies it traversal at `/home/mike` and denies non-root access to the store. The implementation account `mike` is also denied by the store's root-only mode.\\n\\nThis is a current filesystem-permission observation and a DAC-based access conclusion. It does not prove the evaluator sandbox's complete runtime boundary, task-process escape resistance, private digest derivation, author-session independence, setup/reference validation, or custodian acceptance. No permissions were changed and no held-out contents were read.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-21T12:22:23Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Release-path reconciliation (2026-10-22; public metadata and source only; no held-out contents accessed):\\n\\n- The issue's PR #33 status is historical. PR #33 is merged into `v1/integration` at `cf06128d035768d82207bf061153301b2c993f94`; that merge is an ancestor of current `main@a4a7edd9a17a0015abdf8135ecf3c1caac05560c`. PR #33's exact-head CI was green on its recorded PR head, but that historical run is not current-head qualification.\\n- PR #140's synthetic host-preflight report merged to `main` at `44ca13d58a262b5f89be459b47aefa50c2d61683`, an ancestor of current main. It records infrastructure fixtures only; it is not private-corpus custody or a held-out run. Current main CI run `39863828016` is still in progress (Node 20/22/24 passed; Linux CLI/package job running).\\n- The current evaluator contract explicitly rejects legacy `hidden.command` validators for qualification. The old held-out manifest therefore remains incompatible with the approved `blackbox-v1` qualification path unless the independent custodian creates and validates a compatible immutable successor. No task has been run.\\n- The latest metadata-only custodian request on issue #1 is from `2026-10-22T22:08:34Z`; no custodian response or accepted handoff is visible as of this update. The release remains gated on custodian-led compatibility/replacement, fresh custody acceptance, and the other independent qualification gates.\\n\\nIssue #49 stays open for these unresolved acceptance dependencies. No thresholds were changed and no private corpus material was accessed.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-22T22:47:13Z\"}],\"number\":49,\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"PLAN-10 PR-10m: accept hardened evaluator boundary (PR #33) and qualification host before held-out runs\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-22T22:47:13Z\"}\n[]\n[{\"conclusion\":\"\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-25T13:01:47Z\",\"databaseId\":40195749685,\"event\":\"workflow_dispatch\",\"headSha\":\"405f5b96e20b988523b99c8907d29b73bcd2a8fd\",\"status\":\"queued\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40195749685\"},{\"conclusion\":\"failure\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T14:46:15Z\",\"databaseId\":40103980794,\"event\":\"workflow_dispatch\",\"headSha\":\"72e769348fe8a978a576627a4802cb6b68ced779\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40103980794\"},{\"conclusion\":\"failure\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T11:58:20Z\",\"databaseId\":40092008160,\"event\":\"workflow_dispatch\",\"headSha\":\"b0240273dc6824c068e6f65719fbbdacf2efb889\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40092008160\"},{\"conclusion\":\"failure\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-23T09:09:56Z\",\"databaseId\":39929864029,\"event\":\"workflow_dispatch\",\"headSha\":\"1b9791f07d301c885fe48f04a796203583ab5a5c\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39929864029\"}]\n- **Supply-chain reproducibility and draft-then-publish release workflow (PRs [#20](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/20), [#21](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/21)):**\n  - `.github/workflows/repro.yml` and `scripts/repro-identity.mjs` (`86bdbe6`, PR #20) enforce fail-closed tag/commit/clean-tree/version identity across independent Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04 builders.\n  - `.github/workflows/release.yml` and `scripts/check-version-only-diff.mjs` (`a7126aa`, PR #21) build RC tags (`vX.Y.Z-rc.N`) as prereleases and build stable tags (`vX.Y.Z`) as **unpublished drafts** (`draft: true`), requiring via the RC's own checker that a stable tag is a single commit directly on its `vX.Y.Z-rc.N` parent changing only synchronized version metadata.\n\n## Historical evidence: Corrected Node 20 full-suite result (2026-10-17 07:40 UTC; superseded for branch status above)\n\n- PR #10 follow-up commit `4439b7e61dd51a60f4674bddbfdd1621386cce53` includes both fixes identified by the exact Node 20 run on `bb8e673`: packaged doctor evidence no longer prints an external launcher target, and `hasExecutedTests()` recognizes Node 20 TAP summaries only when at least one test passed or failed. It includes regression coverage for an external `nexus` symlink, ordinary TAP, all-skipped TAP, zero-test TAP, and cancelled-only TAP. Independent code review accepted these changes. (Subsequently integrated via PR #10 at `2c70d39`.)\n- A complete `npm --prefix cli test` on the corrected exact source tree completed under Node 20.20.2/npm 10.8.2 with **1,104 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped** across 193 suites; shell exit 0; reported duration 1,615,366 ms. The preserved log is `/tmp/nexus-p10g-node20-full-corrected.log`. Build ran before the suite, and the source tree was committed without changes while the test ran, binding the result to `4439b7e`.\n- This full pass supersedes neither the real pre-fix failure on `bb8e673` (1,097 passed, 7 failed) nor its history. The intentionally interrupted pre-correction run remains classified as interrupted. The package leak and parser edge cases were fixed before this corrected run; tests were not skipped or relaxed.\n- At 07:40 UTC, PR #10 checks were run `39014385063` on `4439b7e` and PR #9 checks were run `39012957463` on `6220e14`; superseded runs `39010821988`, `39010709839`, and `39006853703` were cancelled after newer commits replaced their heads.\n\n## Historical evidence: Node 20 full-suite follow-up (2026-10-17 07:13 UTC)\n\n- A complete `npm --prefix cli test` run on exact PR #10 commit `bb8e673637231aa38ab04b6f07a4498a88bdc132`, using Node 20.20.2/npm 10.8.2 and an isolated home, completed with **1,097 passed, 7 failed, 0 skipped**. The preserved log is `/tmp/nexus-p10g-node20-full-bb8e673.log`. The failures include a packaged-doctor evidence disclosure of an external launcher target and valid Node 20 TAP summaries being misread as zero executed tests. This is an actual source-suite failure and supersedes any implication that the full cross-version test set had not yet been exercised locally.\n- A four-file follow-up in the PR #10 worktree avoids exposing external launcher paths in packaged doctor evidence and recognizes Node 20 TAP summaries while rejecting zero-test, all-skipped, and cancelled-only summaries. The cancelled-only edge case was found during independent review and fixed before acceptance; the reviewer accepted the corrected parser/test diff. Build succeeded, the focused four-file selection passed **47/47**, staged `git diff --check` passed, and staged Gitleaks found zero findings.\n- One full-suite attempt on the pre-correction working tree was intentionally interrupted after review found the cancelled-only edge case. It is classified as interrupted, not passed or failed. The prior 1,097/7 result remains historical evidence and is not erased.\n\n## Historical evidence: Release validation update (2026-10-17 06:40 UTC)\n\n- A focused Node 20.20.2 run of `npm --prefix cli test -- test/security_gates.test.ts` against PR #10's pre-fix snapshot reproduced an SBOM test failure: nested `npx` exited with `ENOENT` for the absent `cli/lib` directory after inheriting npm's `npm_config_local_prefix` and `npm_config_prefix`. A prior supplemental command labeled Node 20 was invalid because `node` resolved to Node 24; it is not counted as Node 20 evidence.\n- PR #10 commit `bb8e673637231aa38ab04b6f07a4498a88bdc132` (and `59dc522` on integration) clears the lowercase and uppercase prefix variables only for the nested CycloneDX `npx` call and adds a regression that injects the lowercase values set by `npm --prefix cli`. The focused security-gate suite then passed 10/10 under Node 20.20.2/npm 10.8.2 and 10/10 under Node 24.11.1/npm 11.19.0. `bash -n`, `git diff --check`, and staged Gitleaks also passed. Independent review accepted the scoped fix and confirmed Linux CI compatibility.\n\n## Historical evidence: Review update (2026-10-17 03:10 UTC; pilot packages superseded by `heldout-v2` above)\n\nThis section records the historical inspection at `e1759cae9cf399e2d2586d05bfea3f86b757c412`. The pilot package attempts and their failures remain historical evidence and are not erased; the active sealed held-out corpus is `heldout-v2` (`eval/heldout-manifest.json`, SHA-256 `50895b84…`, PR #16).\n\n- At 03:10 UTC on 2026-10-17, `v1/integration` was `e1759cae9cf399e2d2586d05bfea3f86b757c412` and `v1/candidate-1` was `6151a231e9179c109cfbe8cff87e0a4148587b6a`.\n- Independent inspection of pilot candidate v17 verified manifest digest `ce44dd2066dc4dec6c5e1f56021e3b442aa293510cbf9f217cf2c2e2256d83fe`, all 227 listed file hashes/sizes, no unlisted package files, 40 parseable tasks, 20 repository/20 fixture tasks, and 80/80 validator-command digest coverage. That author-exposed set was not independently held out or accepted and was retired as development/pilot material when `heldout-v2` was commissioned.\n- Independent inspection of Node 24.11.1 supplement v2 verified its manifest digest (`fc8fe753272bdd2b66e17e84f6f910b1aa4230b4f9284f022e09eff0df0afd7c`), payload `SUPPLEMENTARY_VALIDATION.json` digest (`aec9651dac09d38867201d0c37163fb25213222f912114bfbda49f50e096ce36`), and binding to v17. Its three specified tasks passed the recorded base-failure/reference-pass checks.\n- A separate harmless synthetic canary reproduction against the pre-PR-#10 `runIsolated()` boundary confirmed a material hidden-oracle integrity defect at `e1759ca`: candidate-like code executed by a checker could read and overwrite a hidden file copied into the same writable `/workspace`; its canary appeared in captured output and would be persisted in `hidden.log`. No host escape was demonstrated, and no held-out payload or model candidate was used in that reproduction. (Subsequently remediated at the source level by `blackbox-v1` oracle separation in PR #10 `2c70d39`, workspace history isolation in PR #18 `96aeef2`, and kernel resource isolation in PR #19 `91406bd`.)\n\n## Historical evidence: Security and T2 update (2026-10-17)\n\n- PR [#10](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/10), initial commit `aa2cd6228303b850f1406de94c5c9ee044ff9bf5` (merged at `2c70d39`), added the `blackbox-v1` oracle boundary and regression coverage.\n- The earlier corpus author supplied pilot overlay v18 at `/tmp/nexus-v1-heldout-author/DEC-05-v1-blackbox-dev-v18` (`SHA256SUMS.json` digest `e830c82c60a7767d4d235cc53764d8298abadc2d22107a5e6ee7ed3664509dd4`), with seven fixture tasks migrated and 33 unmigrated. That overlay remains unsealed historical pilot material and is superseded by the sealed 40-task external-repository corpus `heldout-v2` (`eval/heldout-manifest.json`, PR #16).\n- On historical integration `e1759ca`, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs` reported 121 rows (106 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open), and `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` reported all versioned components at `0.1.0-alpha.2`.\n\n## Historical evidence: Earlier state checkpoint (2026-10-17 02:51 UTC)\n\n- At 02:51 UTC on 2026-10-17, `v1/integration` was at `8c9994596144c5674d9be8e011ad1feb4109ffb4` and `v1/candidate-1` was at `6151a231e9179c109cfbe8cff87e0a4148587b6a`.\n- A confirmed CI dependency defect was fixed at `642ba37`: the contest-contract job builds the CLI after installing dependencies and before running demo tests, because `cli/dist` is generated and untracked. The prior run at `10fe416` failed when `demo/lib/real-agent-runner.mjs` could not import `cli/dist/client.js`; that failure remains historical evidence.\n- `rust-toolchain.toml` is tracked and pins Rust `1.95.0` with `rustfmt` and `clippy`.\n- `REQ-DX-106` is satisfied on the integration branch: GitHub milestone [v1.0.0](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/milestone/1) has seven open plan-group issues ([#1–#7](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/issues/1)).\n- The earlier v12 (`82886448799cb9c63d28a8f5f28b940229b981a51982c49bad80b7f7d2c73092`), v15 (`6f78983cc860a4ed616f5aa5375b8d3fec5b7335ea6bac47a448924dc91af06d`), and v16 T2 pilot packages and their failed Docker validation attempts remain historical evidence only.\n\n## Historical evidence at `6151a23`\n\n- At that historical inspection, `v1/integration` and `v1/candidate-1` identified the same commit (`6151a231e9179c109cfbe8cff87e0a4148587b6a`).\n- `make build` completed successfully in an isolated candidate worktree. The produced TUI and CLI entrypoint hashes were respectively `ca20da9214db8dcb130cfa35f25f2e76f9caad63dcf3dfbefe49132fcaa9e52f` and `8da0ccf909d5432de22d62459168f21a22b4360607cbf47259338cc144758f42`.\n- After the build, isolated `make test` passed: Rust 281/281; CLI 1087/1087 across 193 suites; zero failures and zero skipped. Runtime was Node 24.11.1. `scripts/security_gates.sh` passed its npm audit (zero high/critical), Rust advisory/license, credential-scan, diff-hygiene and documentation checks. Output is retained outside the repository at `/tmp/nexus-v1-make-test-built-6151.log` (SHA-256 `b72e0e15819985fc48f39998d2adc5ce90e9dd125519784c25a2a2b4d2db9521`).\n- The earlier unbuilt `make test` failed (Rust 281 passed; CLI 1060/1087 passed, 27 failed, zero skipped) because required generated build outputs were absent. It is preserved at `/tmp/nexus-v1-make-test-6151.log` (SHA-256 `7c4a364daedc3b26bd6b0392f6e0466c581c33ae5ef9d04c11348129e0abbb31`) and is superseded only for the source-suite result by the correctly ordered build-then-test run.\n- Automated PTY acceptance tests are included in the passing CLI suite. This is not human interaction in each required terminal emulator.\n- The source suite includes the T1 evaluator smoke and two-fault T4 smoke. These do not establish the full T2, T3, T4 qualification thresholds.\n\n## Requirements below their required gate (reconciled at `a7126aa`)\n\n| ID | Current state | Remaining behavior or evidence | Dependency | Owner role | Exact next action |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `REQ-AGT-002` | partial | Zero false `VERIFIED` across the frozen qualification workloads; source regression tests pass (`1,152/1,152` at `a7126aa`) but no held-out evaluation exists. | T2/T3/T4 RC runs | Qualification operator | Run the preregistered acceptance set on an installed RC and retain per-run evidence; fix and repeat any false `VERIFIED`. |\n| `REQ-AGT-004` | tested (depth 0; work-unit mechanism landed in PR-4b) | `AGT-02a` archive→task→session commit ordering is applied to durable work units by PR-4b (`agent.ts:3339-3402`, `operation_runner.ts:566`, `durable_continuity.test.ts:359`, `dispositions.md` M2); work-unit pressure-forced compaction + SIGKILL crash-boundary test is in flight under `PLAN-04 PR-4g`, and live long-task `ACC-CONT-10` remains pending RC qualification. | `PLAN-04 PR-4g` (`ACC-CONT-03` SIGKILL), `ACC-CONT-10` on installed RC | Continuity implementer, independent reviewer, and qualification operator | Land and independently review `PLAN-04 PR-4g` (M1/M3/L5), then execute `ACC-CONT-10` on the installed RC during M5. |\n| `REQ-AGT-010` | partial (RR; v1 subset independently accepted at `f68b5bc`) | `ACC-TRUST-04` v1 subset (workspace skills/knowledge trust gating and source/trust annotations in `workspace_trust.test.ts`, 5/5 pass) is source-tested and independently accepted (PR #17 `f68b5bc`); `DEC-04` defers the full `CTX-001` provenance graph and `CTX-002` to post-v1. | Installed-RC verification; post-v1 deferral recorded | Requirement owner | Preserve the `DEC-04` v1 subset / post-v1 boundary in release notes and verify no regression on the installed RC. |\n| `REQ-AGT-111` | open (post-v1 shared-loop refactor; v1 behavior still required) | `PLAN-04` defers the full shared step implementation, while v1 requires documented main/subagent divergences and `measureAdmission` in the subagent loop. Calls exist in both loops, and divergence documentation is tracked under `PLAN-04`. | `PLAN-04` task 6 and source evidence | Continuity implementer, then requirement owner | Verify both `measureAdmission` calls satisfy strict-counting behavior and ensure main/subagent divergence documentation is reconciled in the ledger. |\n| `REQ-PRV-003` | implemented | Standalone behavior has scripted tests but no qualifying live standalone evidence (HIST-08). | Installed RC; standalone matrix | Provider qualification operator | Run `ACCEPTANCE.md` §4 for supported server profiles and archive sanitized receipts. |\n| `REQ-REL-005` | partial (RR) | Candidate source security gates passed on `a7126aa` (run `39108774170`); exact-RC artifact/security evidence is pending RC tag construction. `security_gates.sh` requires `cargo-deny` or `cargo-audit` and fails closed when neither is installed (`ACC-SUP-04`). | Exact RC and `ACC-SUP-05` release CI matrix | Release engineering | On the frozen RC tag, run and archive the release workflow security evidence. |\n| `REQ-REL-106` | open (post-v1; manual path defined for v1) | `SPEC-06` marks self-uninstall/prune post-v1 and retains the quickstart manual uninstall as the v1 path. The ledger's open status is a roadmap deferral, not a v1 implementation blocker. | Post-v1 scope; release documentation | Release/documentation owner | Preserve the documented manual uninstall path for v1 and record this item as explicitly deferred in the final release ledger. |\n| `REQ-AGT-118` | tested (source level; `DEC-17` exceptions preserved) | Conflict resolved by `DEC-17` (PR #11 `f771a3c`): the `≥ 1` token-per-CJK/Hangul-character admission-safety floor takes precedence over the `≤ 1.5×` band, which applies to corpora not dominated by the floor; Chinese (`2.00×`) and Hangul (`1.67×`) floor exceptions remain recorded. Source tests (`tokens.test.ts` 3/3) and independent review records (PRs #12, #14, #15) are integrated. | Installed-RC qualification | Qualification operator | Retain the `DEC-17` exception record; source-level `tested` status does not substitute for installed-RC product qualification. |\n| `REQ-AGT-110` | open | Independent continuity/compaction/truncation acceptance under `ACCEPTANCE.md` §8, including an independent long task with two compactions and kill/resume. | Installed RC and reviewer who did not implement the work | Owner-supplied independent reviewer | After RC freeze, execute the reviewer procedure and archive a per-area verdict; this cannot be self-signed. |\n| `REQ-PER-107` | implemented (post-v1 optional item) | `SPEC-08` marks parent-directory fsync post-v1 and optional. Source evidence exists; this is not a v1 gate under the accepted spec. | Post-v1 scope | Persistence implementer and requirement owner | Keep recorded as optional post-v1 scope. |\n| `REQ-PRV-111` | partial | RC-pinned live provider verification is incomplete. Historical OpenRouter/ChatGPT evidence is not RC evidence; OpenRouter must use a pinned model. OpenAI API-key and Anthropic paths have no configured authorization. | Installed RC; available provider authorization | Provider qualification operator | On the RC, run `providers verify` for OpenRouter with a pinned model and complete one live small §6-style bug-fix task with a correct outcome. Repeat ChatGPT sign-in verification and retain PASS on the RC; keep ChatGPT, OpenAI API-key, and Anthropic experimental unless separately verified. |\n| `REQ-REL-114` | open (workflow enforced at `86bdbe6`; RC run pending) | `.github/workflows/repro.yml` and `scripts/repro-identity.mjs` (PR #20 `86bdbe6`) enforce fail-closed tag/commit/clean-tree/toolchain/artifact identity across Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04 builders, covered by `repro_identity.test.ts`. Live execution on an actual RC tag remains pending RC construction. | Final RC tag and `.github/workflows/repro.yml` run | Release engineering | Dispatch `repro.yml` against the exact `v1.0.0-rc.1` tag/commit and archive both runner manifests and comparison evidence. |\n| `REQ-QUAL-101` | tested (corpus sealed at `f776903`; live T2 run pending) | The 40-task external-repository T2 corpus (`heldout-v2`) is sealed and committed in `eval/heldout-manifest.json` (SHA-256 `50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b`, PR #16 `f776903`, custody record `ce3f590`). Independent metadata review (`codex-lead`) accepted the public manifest structure/digest; private payload validation (40/40, 2 rounds each) and author-isolation audits are custodian-recorded with store permissions `0700`/`0500`. | Qualification-host provisioning, frozen resource config, installed RC, peer calibration | Custodian and qualification operator | Keep `/home/mike/nexus-heldout-v2` restricted from implementation agents; complete qualification-host provisioning and execute the 5-run T2 matrix on the installed RC. |\n| `REQ-QUAL-107` | open | No accepted live standalone/proxy matrix or RC-pinned provider verification. | RC, qualifying held-out subset, provider access, serial gateway window | Qualification operator | Execute `ACCEPTANCE.md` §4 through the approved stripped proxy and collect E5 provider verification receipts on the installed RC. |\n| `REQ-QUAL-102` | tested as harness control | Missing fingerprint and mismatched comparison settings are rejected by tests; no live matched model/configuration record exists. | Frozen RC, identified model/server, task corpus | Qualification operator | Before each comparison, record and verify exact RC, weights hash, server build, sampling, context/output limits, allowlisted environment and equal task budgets in every run manifest. |\n| `REQ-QUAL-103` | tested as harness control | Five-run pair validation and peer configuration forwarding are tested; no live matched T2 results exist. | Sealed T2 set, RC, peers on same model | Qualification operator | Run five serial repetitions for each task/configuration for Nexus, Goose and OpenCode; retain original and replacement records and paired score inputs. |\n| `REQ-QUAL-104` | tested as scorer control | The separate metrics and scorer are tested; threshold outcomes and zero-false-`VERIFIED` have not been measured on qualification workloads. | Completed T2/T3/T4 evidence | Qualification operator | Score every preregistered metric separately and apply the fixed thresholds and confidence intervals; any false `VERIFIED` fails the hard gate. |\n| `REQ-QUAL-105` | tested as injector/smoke (`DEC-05` 9-class count resolved) | `DEC-05` amendment (`f771a3c`) and `ACCEPTANCE.md` §6.2 (`77102c5`) resolve the scenario count to **9 fault classes × 5 runs** (retaining SIGTERM + `run --resume`). Injector and two-fault smoke pass in CI; full 9×5 RC evidence is pending M5 execution. | Installed RC and gateway window | Qualification operator | Execute and score all 9 fault classes × 5 runs against the installed RC. |\n| `REQ-QUAL-106` | tested as harness/isolation controls (live M5 audit pending) | `blackbox-v1` oracle separation (`2c70d39`, PR #10), ancestor-only repository workspace staging (`96aeef2`, PR #18), and delegated cgroup v2 CPU/memory/pids/tmpfs-storage enforcement with `cgroup.kill` cleanup (`91406bd`, PR #19) are integrated, independently reviewed, and CI-tested (`1,152/1,152`). Live qualification-host provisioning and full-run inclusion/exclusion audit remain pending M5 execution. | Qualification-host provisioning (`nexus-eval` user, dedicated tmpfs mount, frozen `config.resources`), installed RC, completed M5 | Evaluator/host operator and independent reviewer | Provision the qualification host and freeze `config.resources`; run M5 with unreadable hidden tests and enforced cgroup/tmpfs bounds; archive every inclusion, exclusion, and replacement reason for independent review. |\n| `REQ-QUAL-108` | partial | Automated PTY suite passes on `a7126aa`; the human matrix is absent for xterm, kitty (keyboard protocol enabled), tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code terminal and GNOME Terminal at 80×24, 40×14 and 200×60. | Human terminal access and RC install | Human acceptance operator | Execute the `ACCEPTANCE.md` §5.3 manual matrix on the installed RC across all required terminal×size cells and archive screenshots and verdicts. |\n| `REQ-QUAL-109` | open | No T3 evidence for 8 tasks × 5 runs, each ≥60 steps with ≥2 compactions and steering; thresholds are false-absence 0 and steering ≥95%. | Frozen T3 workload, RC, gateway capacity | Qualification operator | Freeze/register T3 tasks before execution, then run all repetitions and score using the accepted rules. |\n\nAt `a7126aa`, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs` passes in report mode: **121 rows; 107 tested, 5 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open**. In `--enforce` mode (the G6 release gate), the checker remains fail-closed until the remaining blocker and release-required rows above reach their required post-qualification states.\n\n## Gate reconciliation (at `a7126aa`)\n\n| Gate | Evidence at `a7126aa` | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| G0 clean-clone/isolation | CI run `39108774170` passed across Node 20/22/24 and Ubuntu 22.04 with isolated HOME/cgroups/bubblewrap. | Source gate green on `v1/integration`; repeat on exact pre-tag commit on `main`. |\n| G1 safety | Full source suite (`1,152/1,152` CLI, `281/281` Rust, 0 skipped) and `scripts/security_gates.sh` pass in CI run `39108774170`. | Source gate green; artifact-bound checks run at Stage 3 after RC construction. |\n| G2 package | `linux-x86_64` job in run `39108774170` passed double-build byte comparison, CycloneDX SBOM validation, `smoke-package.sh`, and `installer-smoke.sh`; `repro.yml` (`86bdbe6`) and draft-then-publish `release.yml` (`a7126aa`) are integrated. | Source/CI packaging green; Stage 2/3 workflow-built RC archive and cross-runner `repro.yml` dispatch pending RC tag. |\n| G3 continuity/inference/verification/eval | Source suite, T1 self-test, T4 smoke, `blackbox-v1` oracle isolation, repo history isolation, cgroup v2 resource contract, and sealed 40-task T2 manifest (`50895b84…`) are integrated. `PLAN-04 PR-4g` (continuity M1/M3/L5) and qualification-host provisioning (`PLAN-10 QUAL-HOST` / `PR-10j`) are in flight. | Partial; live T2/T3/full T4 and standalone/provider matrices pending Stage 4 installed-RC execution. |\n| G4 persistence | Source persistence and retention tests pass in CI (`39108774170`). | Source gate green; independent RC acceptance (§8) pending Stage 4. |\n\n## Release and qualification sequence (`ACCEPTANCE.md` §1.1)\n\n1. **Close remaining source & host prerequisites on `v1/integration`:** Land and independently review `PLAN-04 PR-4g` (Continuity M1/M3/L5), `PLAN-10 PR-10j` (dedicated-tmpfs storage preflight & canary), and `PLAN-10 QUAL-HOST` (qualification-host provisioning bundle and frozen resource profile); update the stale `ACCEPTANCE.md` §1.1 sentence now that PR #21 (`a7126aa`) implements draft-then-publish for stable tags.\n2. **Stage 1 — Pre-RC source gates & integration to `main`:** Merge `v1/integration` to `main` (PR #8) once all pre-RC source checks pass, synchronize version metadata to `1.0.0-rc.1` (`scripts/sync-version.mjs`), add `docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.1.md`, and verify green source CI on `main`.\n3. **Stage 2 — RC artifact construction:** Tag `v1.0.0-rc.1` on the verified `main` commit and build/publish the prerelease RC candidate via `.github/workflows/release.yml`, recording the workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and provenance attestation.\n4. **Stage 3 — RC artifact gates:** Run `ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08` and dispatch `.github/workflows/repro.yml` (`REQ-REL-114`) against the exact `v1.0.0-rc.1` tag and commit.\n5. **Stage 4 — Installed-RC qualification:** Install the workflow-produced `v1.0.0-rc.1` package via the documented installer and execute `ACCEPTANCE.md` §§4–8 (standalone/provider matrix, CI/scripted/manual terminal matrix, T2 40×5 held-out comparison, T4 9×5 fault matrix, T3 8×5 long-task matrix, install matrix, SPEC-09 §3.2 docs checklist, and §8 independent acceptance). Archive all evidence under `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/v1.0.0-rc.1/`.\n6. **Stage 5 — G6 decision, version-only stable promotion, draft verification, and publication:** After G6 passes on the accepted RC, create the version-only `v1.0.0` commit directly on the accepted RC commit (enforced by `scripts/check-version-only-diff.mjs` in `release.yml`), run source CI, tag `v1.0.0` to build the unpublished draft release, complete Stage 5 stable artifact/install/attestation checks, record the signed G6 and Stage 5 disposition, and publish the draft release (`gh release edit v1.0.0 --draft=false`).\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":5,"nanos":127661559}},"started_at_ms":1792933837207,"completed_at_ms":1792933842335}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T13:10:43.242Z","ordinal":339363,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1732f-512a-7441-8da9-f55c8e227d40","call_id":"call_dfd03c760a664f9abbb94b77a380d036","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 7.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 8906)\nTotal output lines: 107\n\n{\"lastComments\":[{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Release convergence update (public metadata only): post-merge CI and CodeQL now pass on current main `4e7297f545538e6422ca3890334a7036f58287ca` (CI run `40156576300`, CodeQL run `40156576296`). RC4 remains the newest prerelease; no stable release or final-candidate qualification has been established. The terminal matrix remains 0/15, T4 has not run, and the reproducibility workflow has not run on an RC. The metadata-only custody request from 2026-10-24 02:16 UTC remains unanswered.\\n\\nPlease reply to that request with the current custodian/owner, status and expected timing for independent custody acceptance, and whether a lossless compatibility path or replacement corpus is planned for the current evaluator contract. Please keep the reply to public metadata; do not post prompts, answers, validators, or protected task content. No held-out payload has been accessed by this implementation lane.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-25T03:55:09Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Follow-up for the current release candidate path (public metadata only): the current evaluator requires the blackbox-v1 task contract, while prior custody records describe the sealed legacy hidden-command corpus. Please confirm the currently assigned custodian, whether the sealed 40-task corpus can be qualified losslessly under the current evaluator or requires a newly versioned corpus, and the expected timing for the required custody acceptance and frozen run metadata. Please do not post task objectives, source payloads, validators, reference solutions, hidden results, or credentials here. No held-out execution has started.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-25T06:51:23Z\"}],\"number\":1,\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"PLAN-10 task 8: finish and seal the held-out T2/T3 corpus\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-25T06:51:23Z\"}\n{\"lastComments\":[{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Status check at `6a16cb6` (claude-code).\\n\\n- **T4 denominator (prior comment):** resolved in ACCEPTANCE.md §6.2. The DEC-05 amendment (PRs #11/#13) keeps **9 fault classes × 5 runs**, including SIGTERM + resume. **Remaining inconsistency:** `docs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-10-v1-qualification-and-evaluation.md` line 34 (task 11) still says \\\"T4 (8×5)\\\". A boundary request to the plan owner is in the claim log; ACCEPTANCE §6.2 is authoritative.\\n- **Prerequisites not yet met:** no RC exists (package `0.1.0-alpha.2`). PR #33 (evaluator confidentiality and hardened-legacy checks) is open with CHANGES-REQUIRED, and held-out runs are prohibited until it is accepted. The qualification host is provisioned and validated on PR #33's branch, but that has not been accepted on integration.\\n- Requirements `--enforce` still fails at `6a16cb6`: 11 rows below threshold, including all of this issue's QUAL rows plus REQ-AGT-002 and REQ-PRV-111.\\n\\nNo M5 run has started.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-18T17:34:27Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"T4 denominator reconciliation (2026-10-22, source check at `main@a4a7edd9a17a0015abdf8135ecf3c1caac05560c`): the inconsistency described in the October 18 note is no longer present in current main. `ACCEPTANCE.md` §6.2 specifies nine fault classes × five runs, including SIGTERM/resume, and PLAN-10 task 11 now says `T4 (9×5)`. The separate run-wall-time table still contains the old `8×5` estimate, but explicitly labels it historical and says it predates the nine-class correction; it is not an execution denominator.\\n\\nThis resolves the planning-text discrepancy only. T4 qualification has not run and remains gated on an accepted installed RC, frozen workload, provider/standalone prerequisites, and the other stated qualification dependencies. No threshold or denominator was changed.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-22T22:47:41Z\"}],\"number\":2,\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"PLAN-10 task 11: complete preregistered M5 qualification runs\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-22T22:47:41Z\"}\n{\"lastComments\":[{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"### Terminal environment preflight (setup only; no qualification cells run)\\n\\nThe connected Ubuntu 26.04 GNOME desktop is reachable and has an active local GNOME/Wayland session. All required terminal applications are installed: xterm XTerm(407), kitty 0.45.0, GNOME Terminal 3.58.0, tmux 3.6, and VS Code 1.143.1. The `nexus` command is not installed on that host yet.\\n\\nThe matrix remains 0/15. Each cell still requires the real interactive checks in ACCEPTANCE.md §5.3 and two screenshots (approval panel and post-exit terminal state). Current public RC4 is not the current source head: its commit is an ancestor of `main` and later source changes exist, so this setup check does not qualify RC4 or any later candidate. Install and run only the exact candidate selected for qualification.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T20:55:35Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"### Terminal host preflight update (2026-10-25; setup only)\\n\\nThe Ubuntu 26.04 GNOME host has all five required terminal applications installed: xterm 407, kitty 0.45.0, GNOME Terminal 3.58.0, tmux 3.6, and VS Code 1.143.1. I also installed GitHub CLI 2.103.2 from GitHub CLI's official signed APT repository after verifying its published key fingerprint; `/usr/bin/gh attestation verify` is available for the candidate installer's provenance check.\\n\\nThis is environment setup only. No current-source RC is installed, no terminal cell has run, and the manual matrix remains 0/15. Each cell still needs the exact candidate identity, interactive checks, and both required screenshots.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-25T05:02:41Z\"}],\"number\":3,\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"PLAN-10 task 12: complete the real-terminal acceptance matrix\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-25T05:02:41Z\"}\n{\"lastComments\":[{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Status check at `6a16cb6` (claude-code): the workflow is integrated. `.github/workflows/repro.yml` plus `scripts/repro-identity.mjs` (PR #20) build on ubuntu-22.04 and 24.04 with fail-closed tag/commit/clean-tree/version identity. It has **not** run on an RC because no RC tag exists yet. REQ-REL-114 is still `RR`, correctly. Next action: once the RC is tagged, the release publisher (codex-api-root) runs repro.yml on the exact RC and attaches the run ID and artifact hashes here.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-18T17:34:28Z\"}],\"number\":5,\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"PLAN-07 PR-7e: prove cross-runner release reproducibility\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-18T17:34:28Z\"}\n{\"lastComments\":[{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Metadata-only refresh on `mike-dev` (2026-10-21; no directory listing or private payload access): `/home` is `root:root 0755`; `/home/mike` is `mike:mike 0750`; `/home/mike/nexus-heldout-v2` is `root:root 0700`. `getfacl` showed only the base owner/group/other entries on these directories, with no additional ACL grants. The `nexus-eval` account is UID/GID 985 with only its own group; DAC therefore denies it traversal at `/home/mike` and denies non-root access to the store. The implementation account `mike` is also denied by the store's root-only mode.\\n\\nThis is a current filesystem-permission observation and a DAC-based access conclusion. It does not prove the evaluator sandbox's complete runtime boundary, task-process escape resistance, private digest derivation, author-session independence, setup/reference validation, or custodian acceptance. No permissions were changed and no held-out contents were read.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-21T12:22:23Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Release-path reconciliation (2026-10-22; public metadata and source only; no held-out contents accessed):\\n\\n- The issue's PR #33 status is historical. PR #33 is merged into `v1/integration` at `cf06128d035768d82207bf061153301b2c993f94`; that merge is an ancestor of current `main@a4a7edd9a17a0015abdf8135ecf3c1caac05560c`. PR #33's exact-head CI was green on its recorded PR head, but that historical run is not current-head qualification.\\n- PR #140's synthetic host-preflight report merged to `main` at `44ca13d58a262b5f89be459b47aefa50c2d61683`, an ancestor of current main. It records infrastructure fixtures only; it is not private-corpus custody or a held-out run. Current main CI run `39863828016` is still in progress (Node 20/22/24 passed; Linux CLI/package job running).\\n- The current evaluator contract explicitly rejects legacy `hidden.command` validators for qualification. The old held-out manifest therefore remains incompatible with the approved `blackbox-v1` qualification path unless the independent custodian creates and validates a compatible immutable successor. No task has been run.\\n- The latest metadata-only custodian request on issue #1 is from `2026-10-22T22:08:34Z`; no custodian response or accepted handoff is visible as of this update. The release remains gated on custodian-led compatibility/replacement, fresh custody acceptance, and the other independent qualification gates.\\n\\nIssue #49 stays open for these unresolved acceptance dependencies. No thresholds were changed and no private corpus material was accessed.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-22T22:47:13Z\"}],\"number\":49,\"state\":\"OPEN\",\"title\":\"PLAN-10 PR-10m: accept hardened evaluator boundary (PR #33) and qualification host before held-out runs\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-22T22:47:13Z\"}\n[]\n[{\"conclusion\":\"\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-25T13:01:47Z\",\"databaseId\":40195749685,\"event\":\"workflow_dispatch\",\"headSha\":\"405f5b96e20b988523b99c8907d29b73bcd2a8fd\",\"status\":\"queued\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40195749685\"},{\"conclusion\":\"failure\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T14:46:15Z\",\"databaseId\":40103980794,\"event\":\"workflow_dispatch\",\"headSha\":\"72e769348fe8a978a576627a4802cb6b68ced779\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40103980794\"},{\"conclusion\":\"failure\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-24T11:58:20Z\",\"databaseId\":40092008160,\"event\":\"workflow_dispatch\",\"headSha\":\"b0240273dc6824c068e6f65719fbbdacf2efb889\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40092008160\"},{\"conclusion\":\"failure\",\"created…3906 tokens truncated…v1 and optional. Source evidence exists; this is not a v1 gate under the accepted spec. | Post-v1 scope | Persistence implementer and requirement owner | Keep recorded as optional post-v1 scope. |\n| `REQ-PRV-111` | partial | RC-pinned live provider verification is incomplete. Historical OpenRouter/ChatGPT evidence is not RC evidence; OpenRouter must use a pinned model. OpenAI API-key and Anthropic paths have no configured authorization. | Installed RC; available provider authorization | Provider qualification operator | On the RC, run `providers verify` for OpenRouter with a pinned model and complete one live small §6-style bug-fix task with a correct outcome. Repeat ChatGPT sign-in verification and retain PASS on the RC; keep ChatGPT, OpenAI API-key, and Anthropic experimental unless separately verified. |\n| `REQ-REL-114` | open (workflow enforced at `86bdbe6`; RC run pending) | `.github/workflows/repro.yml` and `scripts/repro-identity.mjs` (PR #20 `86bdbe6`) enforce fail-closed tag/commit/clean-tree/toolchain/artifact identity across Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04 builders, covered by `repro_identity.test.ts`. Live execution on an actual RC tag remains pending RC construction. | Final RC tag and `.github/workflows/repro.yml` run | Release engineering | Dispatch `repro.yml` against the exact `v1.0.0-rc.1` tag/commit and archive both runner manifests and comparison evidence. |\n| `REQ-QUAL-101` | tested (corpus sealed at `f776903`; live T2 run pending) | The 40-task external-repository T2 corpus (`heldout-v2`) is sealed and committed in `eval/heldout-manifest.json` (SHA-256 `50895b84a604fbfd45ed82e29cbef4ba795d7fffbe6611af23bfbc9851f3e89b`, PR #16 `f776903`, custody record `ce3f590`). Independent metadata review (`codex-lead`) accepted the public manifest structure/digest; private payload validation (40/40, 2 rounds each) and author-isolation audits are custodian-recorded with store permissions `0700`/`0500`. | Qualification-host provisioning, frozen resource config, installed RC, peer calibration | Custodian and qualification operator | Keep `/home/mike/nexus-heldout-v2` restricted from implementation agents; complete qualification-host provisioning and execute the 5-run T2 matrix on the installed RC. |\n| `REQ-QUAL-107` | open | No accepted live standalone/proxy matrix or RC-pinned provider verification. | RC, qualifying held-out subset, provider access, serial gateway window | Qualification operator | Execute `ACCEPTANCE.md` §4 through the approved stripped proxy and collect E5 provider verification receipts on the installed RC. |\n| `REQ-QUAL-102` | tested as harness control | Missing fingerprint and mismatched comparison settings are rejected by tests; no live matched model/configuration record exists. | Frozen RC, identified model/server, task corpus | Qualification operator | Before each comparison, record and verify exact RC, weights hash, server build, sampling, context/output limits, allowlisted environment and equal task budgets in every run manifest. |\n| `REQ-QUAL-103` | tested as harness control | Five-run pair validation and peer configuration forwarding are tested; no live matched T2 results exist. | Sealed T2 set, RC, peers on same model | Qualification operator | Run five serial repetitions for each task/configuration for Nexus, Goose and OpenCode; retain original and replacement records and paired score inputs. |\n| `REQ-QUAL-104` | tested as scorer control | The separate metrics and scorer are tested; threshold outcomes and zero-false-`VERIFIED` have not been measured on qualification workloads. | Completed T2/T3/T4 evidence | Qualification operator | Score every preregistered metric separately and apply the fixed thresholds and confidence intervals; any false `VERIFIED` fails the hard gate. |\n| `REQ-QUAL-105` | tested as injector/smoke (`DEC-05` 9-class count resolved) | `DEC-05` amendment (`f771a3c`) and `ACCEPTANCE.md` §6.2 (`77102c5`) resolve the scenario count to **9 fault classes × 5 runs** (retaining SIGTERM + `run --resume`). Injector and two-fault smoke pass in CI; full 9×5 RC evidence is pending M5 execution. | Installed RC and gateway window | Qualification operator | Execute and score all 9 fault classes × 5 runs against the installed RC. |\n| `REQ-QUAL-106` | tested as harness/isolation controls (live M5 audit pending) | `blackbox-v1` oracle separation (`2c70d39`, PR #10), ancestor-only repository workspace staging (`96aeef2`, PR #18), and delegated cgroup v2 CPU/memory/pids/tmpfs-storage enforcement with `cgroup.kill` cleanup (`91406bd`, PR #19) are integrated, independently reviewed, and CI-tested (`1,152/1,152`). Live qualification-host provisioning and full-run inclusion/exclusion audit remain pending M5 execution. | Qualification-host provisioning (`nexus-eval` user, dedicated tmpfs mount, frozen `config.resources`), installed RC, completed M5 | Evaluator/host operator and independent reviewer | Provision the qualification host and freeze `config.resources`; run M5 with unreadable hidden tests and enforced cgroup/tmpfs bounds; archive every inclusion, exclusion, and replacement reason for independent review. |\n| `REQ-QUAL-108` | partial | Automated PTY suite passes on `a7126aa`; the human matrix is absent for xterm, kitty (keyboard protocol enabled), tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code terminal and GNOME Terminal at 80×24, 40×14 and 200×60. | Human terminal access and RC install | Human acceptance operator | Execute the `ACCEPTANCE.md` §5.3 manual matrix on the installed RC across all required terminal×size cells and archive screenshots and verdicts. |\n| `REQ-QUAL-109` | open | No T3 evidence for 8 tasks × 5 runs, each ≥60 steps with ≥2 compactions and steering; thresholds are false-absence 0 and steering ≥95%. | Frozen T3 workload, RC, gateway capacity | Qualification operator | Freeze/register T3 tasks before execution, then run all repetitions and score using the accepted rules. |\n\nAt `a7126aa`, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs` passes in report mode: **121 rows; 107 tested, 5 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open**. In `--enforce` mode (the G6 release gate), the checker remains fail-closed until the remaining blocker and release-required rows above reach their required post-qualification states.\n\n## Gate reconciliation (at `a7126aa`)\n\n| Gate | Evidence at `a7126aa` | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| G0 clean-clone/isolation | CI run `39108774170` passed across Node 20/22/24 and Ubuntu 22.04 with isolated HOME/cgroups/bubblewrap. | Source gate green on `v1/integration`; repeat on exact pre-tag commit on `main`. |\n| G1 safety | Full source suite (`1,152/1,152` CLI, `281/281` Rust, 0 skipped) and `scripts/security_gates.sh` pass in CI run `39108774170`. | Source gate green; artifact-bound checks run at Stage 3 after RC construction. |\n| G2 package | `linux-x86_64` job in run `39108774170` passed double-build byte comparison, CycloneDX SBOM validation, `smoke-package.sh`, and `installer-smoke.sh`; `repro.yml` (`86bdbe6`) and draft-then-publish `release.yml` (`a7126aa`) are integrated. | Source/CI packaging green; Stage 2/3 workflow-built RC archive and cross-runner `repro.yml` dispatch pending RC tag. |\n| G3 continuity/inference/verification/eval | Source suite, T1 self-test, T4 smoke, `blackbox-v1` oracle isolation, repo history isolation, cgroup v2 resource contract, and sealed 40-task T2 manifest (`50895b84…`) are integrated. `PLAN-04 PR-4g` (continuity M1/M3/L5) and qualification-host provisioning (`PLAN-10 QUAL-HOST` / `PR-10j`) are in flight. | Partial; live T2/T3/full T4 and standalone/provider matrices pending Stage 4 installed-RC execution. |\n| G4 persistence | Source persistence and retention tests pass in CI (`39108774170`). | Source gate green; independent RC acceptance (§8) pending Stage 4. |\n\n## Release and qualification sequence (`ACCEPTANCE.md` §1.1)\n\n1. **Close remaining source & host prerequisites on `v1/integration`:** Land and independently review `PLAN-04 PR-4g` (Continuity M1/M3/L5), `PLAN-10 PR-10j` (dedicated-tmpfs storage preflight & canary), and `PLAN-10 QUAL-HOST` (qualification-host provisioning bundle and frozen resource profile); update the stale `ACCEPTANCE.md` §1.1 sentence now that PR #21 (`a7126aa`) implements draft-then-publish for stable tags.\n2. **Stage 1 — Pre-RC source gates & integration to `main`:** Merge `v1/integration` to `main` (PR #8) once all pre-RC source checks pass, synchronize version metadata to `1.0.0-rc.1` (`scripts/sync-version.mjs`), add `docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.1.md`, and verify green source CI on `main`.\n3. **Stage 2 — RC artifact construction:** Tag `v1.0.0-rc.1` on the verified `main` commit and build/publish the prerelease RC candidate via `.github/workflows/release.yml`, recording the workflow run, tag commit, artifact digests, and provenance attestation.\n4. **Stage 3 — RC artifact gates:** Run `ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08` and dispatch `.github/workflows/repro.yml` (`REQ-REL-114`) against the exact `v1.0.0-rc.1` tag and commit.\n5. **Stage 4 — Installed-RC qualification:** Install the workflow-produced `v1.0.0-rc.1` package via the documented installer and execute `ACCEPTANCE.md` §§4–8 (standalone/provider matrix, CI/scripted/manual terminal matrix, T2 40×5 held-out comparison, T4 9×5 fault matrix, T3 8×5 long-task matrix, install matrix, SPEC-09 §3.2 docs checklist, and §8 independent acceptance). Archive all evidence under `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/v1.0.0-rc.1/`.\n6. **Stage 5 — G6 decision, version-only stable promotion, draft verification, and publication:** After G6 passes on the accepted RC, create the version-only `v1.0.0` commit directly on the accepted RC commit (enforced by `scripts/check-version-only-diff.mjs` in `release.yml`), run source CI, tag `v1.0.0` to build the unpublished draft release, complete Stage 5 stable artifact/install/attestation checks, record the signed G6 and Stage 5 disposition, and publish the draft release (`gh release edit v1.0.0 --draft=false`).\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17267-b4a8-7073-9d2a-32da76e0ee35","create_time":1792933843.242323}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
