{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T13:14:05.444Z","ordinal":339542,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a17332-6704-70a1-a30f-01beccb98842","call_id":"call_40e11f25b0df48778b95488d21740f9b","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/current_main_rc_path_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT.** The root, CLI, lockfile, and Cargo versions are synchronized at `1.0.0-rc.5`. The release workflow requires a matching tag, synchronized versions, a tag on `main`, and a matching release note before producing artifacts. The PR #215 clarification accurately describes evaluator-harness changes and does not claim product qualification or acceptance; the notes keep RC5 qualification pending.\\n\\nRead-only review; no tests were run.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/pr207_independent_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** — candidate `fb36b03c2ad9a22f4e94139accccee1d2f137ae3` versus current `main` at `016bbc332d694b32072f6346e7f3127fb98b691f`.\\n\\nThe six-file security patch is unchanged. Its diff SHA-256 is `55b0230bcdb125cecc263c83afbb83dc9bc54cab24ca557209a92f57d503de7a`.\\n\\nThe reported 18-file diff against stale base `19b30a4` includes 12 files changed on current `main` since that base; they add no candidate-only changes versus current `main`. Refreshing the PR base to `016bbc3` will make its displayed scope clear. `git diff --check` is clean. I did not run tests.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/t4_runner_independent_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"ACCEPT — after the child’s `close` event, `kill()` now only attempts cgroup cleanup and cannot signal a potentially reused PID or create lingering timers. Before `close`, immediate and repeated cgroup cleanup behavior is preserved. The diff check was clean; I did not run tests.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17267-b4a8-7073-9d2a-32da76e0ee35","create_time":1792934045.4444776}},