{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T13:23:02.331Z","ordinal":339943,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_060b64278a9dfb15016ade02afbc1481a09accbb0f1e899bd8","status":"completed","call_id":"call_a408e725262845d4921f2479d8d79d11","name":"exec","input":"const r=await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"cat > /tmp/nexus-rc5-issue3-update.md <<'EOF'\\n### RC5 terminal matrix preparation (2026-10-25; no cells run)\\n\\nThe exact candidate is public as `v1.0.0-rc.5`, source commit `405f5b96e20b988523b99c8907d29b73bcd2a8fd`, with published archive SHA-256 `b15c45f6ac7684ce8752b45432df30d77b3ecd4cc7c4ab9ee1afc8670eea8c19`. The official installer and provenance were verified on the authenticated engineering host.\\n\\nThe connected Ubuntu 26.04/GNOME desktop has all five required terminals installed. The RC5 installer check there stopped before creating files because `gh auth status` reports no GitHub login; the version-scoped install prefix is absent. After signing in with GitHub CLI on that desktop, use the documented RC5 installer with prefix `$HOME/.local/rc5-qual-405f5`, verify `nexus --version` is `1.0.0-rc.5 (405f5b96e20b)`, and use that installed binary for the matrix.\\n\\nThe matrix remains **0/15**. Run `scripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh` once for each of the five terminals (`xterm`, `kitty`, `tmux-gnome`, `vscode`, `gnome`) at 80×24, 40×14, and 200×60. Each cell needs the interactive checks and two distinct screenshots (approval panel and post-exit terminal). Automated PTY checks do not count as these operator results. The existing script records installed binary identity, package manifest, per-check verdicts, screenshot hashes, mock request log, terminal restoration, and process-scope cleanup measurements.\\n\\nAcceptance is still in progress; no terminal cell is claimed complete by this setup update.\\nEOF\\ncat > /tmp/nexus-rc5-issue5-update.md <<'EOF'\\n### RC5 exact-tag reproducibility run (2026-10-25)\\n\\nDispatched `.github/workflows/repro.yml` as run [40195749685](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40195749685) against published tag `v1.0.0-rc.5` at `405f5b96e20b988523b99c8907d29b73bcd2a8fd`.\\n\\nBoth independent builder jobs (`ubuntu-22.04` and `ubuntu-24.04`) completed successfully. Their identities agree on the exact source, tag object, lockfiles, pinned toolchain, reviewed packaging script and six reproducibility artifact hashes. Both produced the published archive SHA-256 `b15c45f6ac7684ce8752b45432df30d77b3ecd4cc7c4ab9ee1afc8670eea8c19`. The repository's exact comparator, run locally over the workflow-uploaded identity records, returned `REQ-REL-114 / ACC-SUP-08 PASS`.\\n\\nThe workflow's own `compare` job is still queued. Until that job reaches a terminal result, `REQ-REL-114` remains pending in the enforced ledger; this issue update does not claim the formal gate is complete.\\nEOF\\ngh issue comment 3 --body-file /tmp/nexus-rc5-issue3-update.md && gh issue comment 5 --body-file /tmp/nexus-rc5-issue5-update.md\",workdir:\"/home/mike/nexus-code\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:700});\ntext(r.output);\ntext(\"exit=\"+r.exit_code);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17267-b4a8-7073-9d2a-32da76e0ee35","create_time":1792934575.8535686}}}
