{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T13:26:18.918Z","ordinal":340111,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17267-b4a8-7073-9d2a-32da76e0ee35","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-cb2d1c8d-258a-40df-bcc1-de92eb7e9161","process_id":"5072","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n 'queued|comparator|REQ-REL-114|cross-runner' docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md | tail -20; cat .git/nexus-claims/FILE_.github_workflows_repro.yml/owner.json 2>/dev/null; cat .git/nexus-claims/FILE_scripts_package-linux.sh/owner.json 2>/dev/null"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/rc5-readiness-checkpoint","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"rg -n 'queued|comparator|REQ-REL-114|cross-runner' docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md | tail -20; cat .git/nexus-claims/FILE_.github_workflows_repro.yml/owner.json 2>/dev/null; cat .git/nexus-claims/FILE_scripts_package-linux.sh/owner.json 2>/dev/null"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"failed","aggregated_output":"11:**Qualification evidence and blockers:** The RC3 provider record `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.3/providers/e5-provider-verification-20261023.json` was independently accepted: ChatGPT sign-in streaming/tool round trip passed; OpenRouter failed authentication and its live task remains outstanding. Public Issue #1 remains open; its latest visible update is coordinator-authored at 10:23 UTC, with no custodian response. The sealed legacy `hidden.command` corpus is not accepted by the current `blackbox-v1` runner; no held-out qualification has started and no private payload was accessed. T2/T3/T4, long-task and fault-injection qualification, exact-candidate cross-runner reproducibility, all 15 human terminal cells, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete.\n25:**Held-out and remaining qualification:** Public Issue #1 has no custodian response after the metadata-only request at 2026-10-23 03:46:59Z. The sealed T2 manifest remains incompatible with the current evaluator's `blackbox-v1` contract because it uses legacy `hidden.command`; the independent custodian must convert or replace it, revalidate it, and accept a new immutable manifest. No hidden task or payload was accessed and no held-out run started. Provider/standalone qualification, T2/T3/T4 including long tasks and nine fault classes, exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility, the real-terminal matrix, and independent RC acceptance remain outstanding.\n37:**Held-out and qualification gates:** Public Issue #1 has no custodian response after the metadata-only request at 2026-10-23 03:46:59Z. The sealed T2 manifest uses legacy `hidden.command` tasks, which the current evaluator rejects; the approved path requires custodian-led conversion or replacement, independent revalidation, and a new immutable manifest identity. No held-out task has been run. Private custody acceptance, current author/custodian ownership and exposure history, independent digest/setup/reference validation, effective access restrictions, and evaluator separation remain unverified. Installed-RC provider/standalone, T2/T3/T4, long-task and fault-injection qualification, cross-runner reproducibility, and exact-artifact acceptance have not run. The five-terminal by three-size manual matrix still requires genuine operator evidence; automated PTY tests do not satisfy it.\n79:The public `v1.0.0-rc.1` release remains the only published v1 candidate. `v1.0.0-rc.2` points to older source and is nonqualifying under the Node 22 decision. There is no accepted RC or stable release. Held-out custody, provider/standalone qualification, T2/T3/T4, cross-runner reproducibility, installed-RC packaging and qualification, five-terminal by three-size human evidence, and independent acceptance remain incomplete. Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authorization remains granted and gated.\n93:**RC and publication:** The published `v1.0.0-rc.1` tag resolves to `cb364c386c42faa53b67e04cacc81d7e01520779`, an ancestor of current `main`, and is not an artifact built from current source. Its published asset digest is `8d7dd32f3d00adb98d4f0ea2c6a484ea8e04fc547b4d78b21b060000eda22b9d`. The next candidate needs a new immutable identity, currently expected to be `v1.0.0-rc.2`, with synchronized version metadata and release notes. Exact-RC artifact/install checks, held-out T2, provider and standalone qualification, T3/T4, cross-runner reproducibility, the five-environment by three-size human terminal matrix, independent RC acceptance, and stable-promotion disposition remain outstanding. Publication authorization is granted but gated on those results. No stable `v1.0.0` tag or release exists.\n117:- **Requirements gate:** `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` was independently rerun with isolated HOME/XDG on exact `7d6673f` and passed: 123 rows (109 tested, 5 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open). Eleven requirements remain explicitly deferred to exact-RC qualification: `REQ-AGT-002`, `REQ-AGT-010`, `REQ-PRV-003`, `REQ-REL-005`, `REQ-AGT-110`, `REQ-PRV-111`, `REQ-REL-114`, `REQ-QUAL-101`, `REQ-QUAL-107`, `REQ-QUAL-108`, and `REQ-QUAL-109`. This source-stage gate pass does not satisfy those qualification requirements.\n137:- **Requirements enforcement:** `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed on exact source tree `8f4504e` (tree `2a0799c8a32e88e34322b712cf937d73cbe4d637`), with isolated `HOME`/XDG: 123 rows (109 tested, 5 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open). Eleven rows remain below the ordinary tested threshold pending their approved exact-RC evidence: `REQ-AGT-002`, `REQ-AGT-010`, `REQ-PRV-003`, `REQ-REL-005`, `REQ-AGT-110`, `REQ-PRV-111`, `REQ-REL-114`, `REQ-QUAL-101`, `REQ-QUAL-107`, `REQ-QUAL-108`, and `REQ-QUAL-109`. The pre-RC checker pass does not imply those RC gates have passed or authorize an acceptance claim.\n140:- **Other qualification gates:** No installed-RC provider or standalone matrix, T2/T3/T4 scored qualification, exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility, or independent RC acceptance exists. `ACCEPTANCE.md` §5.3 and `scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md` define the human five-environment × three-size matrix and evidence capture; all 15 real-terminal cells remain unrun because no RC is installed. Automated PTY results do not replace those operator results.\n153:- **Requirements enforcement:** `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` ran in a detached worktree at exact `6a16cb60635c9182f13be1635d5f44eddebdcde0` with isolated `HOME` and failed as required. It reports 123 rows (109 tested, 5 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open) and 11 below threshold: `REQ-AGT-002`, `REQ-AGT-010`, `REQ-PRV-003`, `REQ-REL-005`, `REQ-AGT-110`, `REQ-PRV-111`, `REQ-REL-114`, `REQ-QUAL-101`, `REQ-QUAL-107`, `REQ-QUAL-108`, and `REQ-QUAL-109`. The exact result is recorded in the claims log and was sent to the ledger owner in PR #17 comment `6252582027`; no ledger status changed.\n155:- **Other qualification and release gates:** Provider/standalone, T3/T4, cross-runner reproducibility, qualification-host validation, and human five-environment × three-size terminal acceptance remain incomplete. Package version remains `0.1.0-alpha.2`; no RC artifact/tag, stable tag, npm publication, or GitHub release exists. Publication authorization remains granted but gated on accepted exact-RC evidence.\n163:- **Requirements enforcement:** `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` ran from a detached worktree at exact revision `4bce8760893b222789b76011a477dd61988ecba6` with isolated `HOME`; it failed as required. Ledger result: 123 rows (109 tested, 5 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open), with 11 below threshold: `REQ-AGT-002`, `REQ-AGT-010`, `REQ-PRV-003`, `REQ-REL-005`, `REQ-AGT-110`, `REQ-PRV-111`, `REQ-REL-114`, `REQ-QUAL-101`, `REQ-QUAL-107`, `REQ-QUAL-108`, `REQ-QUAL-109`. `REQ-AGT-118` remains tested. `REQ-AGT-010` remains partial; its existing ACC-TRUST-04 source evidence is pinned to `2c70d39`, and the current row still needs exact-revision evidence and a DEC-04-aligned disposition before promotion. The ledger owner was given this exact checker output; no ledger status was changed.\n166:- **Version, RC, and publication:** Package version remains `0.1.0-alpha.2`. PR #44's deterministic package checks are source CI evidence for that alpha package; they do not establish cross-runner RC reproducibility or installed-RC acceptance. No RC artifact, installed-RC provider/standalone, held-out, T3/T4, cross-runner, human-terminal, or independent acceptance evidence exists. The staged lifecycle in `ACCEPTANCE.md` remains authoritative. Publication authorization remains granted and gated; no RC tag, stable tag, npm publication, or GitHub release exists.\n173:- **Requirements enforcement:** `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` was run from a clean archive of exact `519398495b7c3a2e5915ed76eee0bb731feb0bcf`; it exited 1 as required. The ledger has 121 rows (107 tested, 5 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open) and 11 below-threshold rows: `REQ-AGT-002`, `REQ-AGT-010`, `REQ-PRV-003`, `REQ-REL-005`, `REQ-AGT-110`, `REQ-PRV-111`, `REQ-REL-114`, `REQ-QUAL-101`, `REQ-QUAL-107`, `REQ-QUAL-108`, and `REQ-QUAL-109`. `REQ-AGT-118` is now `tested` with the DEC-17 accuracy exceptions preserved. `REQ-AGT-010` remains partial; its `CTX-001` blocking marker/mapping is under owner reconciliation against DEC-04. No requirement was promoted by this checkpoint.\n179:- **RC and publication:** Package version remains `0.1.0-alpha.2`; PR #8 remains a draft integration-to-main candidate. No RC artifact, exact-RC test, cross-runner RC comparison, installed provider/standalone run, T2/T3/T4 qualification, or independent RC acceptance exists. Final stable publication remains authorized but gated on all mandatory exact-RC acceptance and release checks.\n266:| `REQ-REL-114` | open (workflow enforced at `86bdbe6`; RC run pending) | `.github/workflows/repro.yml` and `scripts/repro-identity.mjs` (PR #20 `86bdbe6`) enforce fail-closed tag/commit/clean-tree/toolchain/artifact identity across Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04 builders, covered by `repro_identity.test.ts`. Live execution on an actual RC tag remains pending RC construction. | Final RC tag and `.github/workflows/repro.yml` run | Release engineering | Dispatch `repro.yml` against the exact `v1.0.0-rc.1` tag/commit and archive both runner manifests and comparison evidence. |\n285:| G2 package | `linux-x86_64` job in run `39108774170` passed double-build byte comparison, CycloneDX SBOM validation, `smoke-package.sh`, and `installer-smoke.sh`; `repro.yml` (`86bdbe6`) and draft-then-publish `release.yml` (`a7126aa`) are integrated. | Source/CI packaging green; Stage 2/3 workflow-built RC archive and cross-runner `repro.yml` dispatch pending RC tag. |\n294:4. **Stage 3 — RC artifact gates:** Run `ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08` and dispatch `.github/workflows/repro.yml` (`REQ-REL-114`) against the exact `v1.0.0-rc.1` tag and commit.\n318:- Reproducibility workflow [40195749685](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40195749685) built successfully on Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04 from the exact tag. The two builder identities and all six artifact hashes match, including the published archive. The reviewed comparator run locally over the workflow artifacts returned `REQ-REL-114 / ACC-SUP-08 PASS`, but the workflow's own `compare` job remains queued. Keep `REQ-REL-114` pending until that job completes.\n330:| Cross-runner `REQ-REL-114` | Builder artifacts match; official comparator job queued. | Wait for run 40195749685 `compare` to reach a terminal result and archive its workflow-generated evidence. |\n","exit_code":1,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":765816541}},"started_at_ms":1792934778152,"completed_at_ms":1792934778918}}
