{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T13:26:48.250Z","ordinal":340128,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17267-b4a8-7073-9d2a-32da76e0ee35","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-812ebfb0-d8c1-483c-86eb-99a5e681927d","process_id":"53855","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/rc5-readiness-checkpoint status --short --branch && git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/rc5-readiness-checkpoint log -1 --oneline && rg -n \"40195749685|REQ-REL-114|cross-runner|reproducib\" /home/mike/nexus-wt/rc5-readiness-checkpoint/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md && cat /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/FILE_.github_workflows_repro.yml/owner.json && cat /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/FILE_scripts_package-linux.sh/owner.json"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/rc5-readiness-checkpoint status --short --branch && git -C /home/mike/nexus-wt/rc5-readiness-checkpoint log -1 --oneline && rg -n \"40195749685|REQ-REL-114|cross-runner|reproducib\" /home/mike/nexus-wt/rc5-readiness-checkpoint/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md && cat /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/FILE_.github_workflows_repro.yml/owner.json && cat /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/FILE_scripts_package-linux.sh/owner.json"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"## v1/rc5-readiness-checkpoint...origin/v1/rc5-readiness-checkpoint\n31a7ba9 docs(release): add exact RC5 qualification checkpoint\n5:**Authoritative source and source gates:** `origin/main` is `1f3c655971ade086f55347926db16cf2ecd52d1f`, merging PR #161's pinned Linux builder/reproducibility changes. Exact-main CI [39957281380](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39957281380) completed successfully: Node 22, Node 24, and Linux x86-64 jobs all passed, including the full CLI suite, security gates, requirements check, reproducible package builds, SBOM validation, package smoke, and installer smoke. Exact-main CodeQL [39957281390](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39957281390) also passed. On a clean detached checkout of this exact SHA with isolated HOME/XDG, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed: 123 rows (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open), with 12 explicit exact-RC qualification deferrals. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` reports all components at `1.0.0-rc.3`. These are source-gate results; the CI package is validation output, not a new published RC.\n11:**Qualification evidence and blockers:** The RC3 provider record `docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification/rc.3/providers/e5-provider-verification-20261023.json` was independently accepted: ChatGPT sign-in streaming/tool round trip passed; OpenRouter failed authentication and its live task remains outstanding. Public Issue #1 remains open; its latest visible update is coordinator-authored at 10:23 UTC, with no custodian response. The sealed legacy `hidden.command` corpus is not accepted by the current `blackbox-v1` runner; no held-out qualification has started and no private payload was accessed. T2/T3/T4, long-task and fault-injection qualification, exact-candidate cross-runner reproducibility, all 15 human terminal cells, and independent exact-RC acceptance remain incomplete.\n19:**Exact source gates:** `origin/main` and the signed `v1.0.0-rc.3` tag resolve to source commit `1b9791f07d301c885fe48f04a796203583ab5a5c`. Exact-main CI [39923089278](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39923089278) and CodeQL [39923089363](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39923089363) completed successfully on that commit. CI passed Node 22, Node 24, Linux CLI tests, security gates, requirements checks, two-build package reproducibility, SBOM validation, package smoke, and installer smoke. `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check --tag v1.0.0-rc.3` and `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed at the same source; the latter reports 123 rows (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open), with 12 explicit exact-RC qualification deferrals. This is source-gate evidence, not product acceptance.\n25:**Held-out and remaining qualification:** Public Issue #1 has no custodian response after the metadata-only request at 2026-10-23 03:46:59Z. The sealed T2 manifest remains incompatible with the current evaluator's `blackbox-v1` contract because it uses legacy `hidden.command`; the independent custodian must convert or replace it, revalidate it, and accept a new immutable manifest. No hidden task or payload was accessed and no held-out run started. Provider/standalone qualification, T2/T3/T4 including long tasks and nine fault classes, exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility, the real-terminal matrix, and independent RC acceptance remain outstanding.\n33:**Source gates:** PR #159 (`a81f79df35a76207751ffd8a86640baafca98eeb`) merged as `1b9791f`. Its exact-head Node 22, Node 24, Linux package/reproducibility/install-smoke, and CodeQL checks passed; independent source review accepted the change. The focused Doctor schema-2 empty-history regression passed 1/1 with isolated HOME. At exact post-merge source `1b9791f`, `node scripts/sync-version.mjs --check` passes with all components at `1.0.0-rc.3`; `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passes with 123 rows (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open) and 12 explicit exact-RC qualification deferrals. Post-merge CI run [39923089278](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39923089278) and CodeQL run [39923089363](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39923089363) are running on the exact merge commit; do not claim post-merge CI complete until both terminate successfully.\n35:**Checkpoint failure:** `/home/mike/.local/bin/nexus` resolves to the installed `v1.0.0-rc.1` package and reports `1.0.0-rc.1 (cb364c386c42)`. That immutable package lacks checkpoint choices, so the reported failure before turn start is reproducible by version identity and will persist on RC1. The fix is integrated in PR #147 (TUI/sidecar) and PR #153 (legacy REPL): before starting a turn, Nexus asks the operator whether to use read-only mode, continue in the configured mode without a rollback checkpoint, create the checkpoint with the sensitive-content risk acknowledged, cancel, or enter a different instruction. Both PRs passed exact-head checks, and the subsequent exact-main CI on `dac465d` passed. No replacement package has been installed. The public release page still has RC1 only; RC2 has a tag but no published release, and RC3 has neither tag nor release.\n37:**Held-out and qualification gates:** Public Issue #1 has no custodian response after the metadata-only request at 2026-10-23 03:46:59Z. The sealed T2 manifest uses legacy `hidden.command` tasks, which the current evaluator rejects; the approved path requires custodian-led conversion or replacement, independent revalidation, and a new immutable manifest identity. No held-out task has been run. Private custody acceptance, current author/custodian ownership and exposure history, independent digest/setup/reference validation, effective access restrictions, and evaluator separation remain unverified. Installed-RC provider/standalone, T2/T3/T4, long-task and fault-injection qualification, cross-runner reproducibility, and exact-artifact acceptance have not run. The five-terminal by three-size manual matrix still requires genuine operator evidence; automated PTY tests do not satisfy it.\n43:**Authoritative release source:** `origin/main` is `1a484c38518688005e9434b18c889c77b408e145`, the PR #155 merge commit. PRs #153, #154, and #155 are merged. PR #153 integrated the checkpoint-choice flow; PR #154 refreshed readiness and the terminal worksheet; PR #155 fixed the remaining doctor integrity-scan timeout by batching metadata checks. PR #155 exact-head CI `39893335185`, CodeQL `39893335167`, and independent review passed on head `76b34f1d18d766b06011176a85679e7c3434ba30`. Current-main CI run [39896372677](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39896372677) completed successfully on exact `1a484c38518688005e9434b18c889c77b408e145`: Node 24 at 03:56:55Z, Node 22 at 03:57:48Z, and Linux x86-64 packaging/reproducibility/package-smoke/installer-smoke at 04:11:34Z. Its Linux job validated identical package archives, checksums, notices, SBOM and installer across two builds. Current-main CodeQL run [39896372726](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/39896372726) completed successfully at 03:43:55Z on that same SHA. CI’s Linux package used existing `1.0.0-rc.2` version metadata; it is source CI evidence, not an immutable RC3 artifact or qualification.\n47:**Node runtime floor:** The accepted user decision is Node `>=22`. PR #150 integrates that floor in package engines, installer checks, CLI diagnostics and upgrade behavior, CI/release/reproducibility configuration, tests, and current release documentation. Superseded PRs #137 and #146 were closed after their intended policy changes were verified in current main; their older branch evidence is not current qualification evidence.\n55:**Qualification and release disposition:** Public Issue #1 remains open; the latest custodian metadata request has no response in the available checkpoint, so T2 qualification has not started and no held-out payload was accessed. Installed-RC E2, standalone/provider, T2/T3/T4, exact-RC reproducibility, human five-terminal by three-size acceptance ([terminal matrix worksheet](TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md)), and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding. Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authorization remains granted and gated. No RC is accepted and no stable v1.0.0 release is claimed.\n59:**Authoritative release source:** `origin/main` was `fa16045a6351ce61763bc3fcc93b562c50849285`, the merge of PR #152. PR #152 carried the readiness checkpoint refresh and terminal worksheet wording separating the §5.3 disposition gate from `ACC-TUI-MANUAL`; its exact head `deaf56fdb074df3f5cd3b62d50f811a2f14ca101` passed Node 22, Node 24, and Linux x86-64 package/repro/install-smoke CI in run `39881805268`; CodeQL `39881805274` passed. The independent reviewer accepted that exact head. Post-merge CI run `39885102002` passed Node 22, Node 24, and Linux x86-64 packaging/reproducibility/smoke/install; post-merge CodeQL `39885101945` passed. These checks are bound to exact main `fa16045`. Retained post-merge check summary: [CI and CodeQL result](../reviews/evidence/v1/plan10-readiness-post152/post-merge-ci-main-fa16045.txt).\n61:**Node runtime floor:** The accepted user decision is Node `>=22`. PR #150 integrates that floor in package engines, installer checks, CLI diagnostics and upgrade behavior, CI/release/reproducibility configuration, tests, and current release documentation. Superseded PRs #137 and #146 were closed after their intended policy changes were verified in current main; their older branch evidence is not current qualification evidence.\n69:**Qualification and release disposition:** Public Issue #1 remains open, with no custodian response to the latest metadata-only compatibility request posted at 22:08 UTC; T2 qualification has not started and no held-out payload was accessed. Installed-RC E2, standalone/provider, T3/T4, exact-RC reproducibility, human five-terminal by three-size acceptance ([terminal matrix worksheet](TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md)), and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding. Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authorization remains granted and gated. No RC is accepted and no stable v1.0.0 release is claimed.\n79:The public `v1.0.0-rc.1` release remains the only published v1 candidate. `v1.0.0-rc.2` points to older source and is nonqualifying under the Node 22 decision. There is no accepted RC or stable release. Held-out custody, provider/standalone qualification, T2/T3/T4, cross-runner reproducibility, installed-RC packaging and qualification, five-terminal by three-size human evidence, and independent acceptance remain incomplete. Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authorization remains granted and gated.\n89:**Requirements and acceptance:** I reran `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` at 09:34 UTC from a clean detached worktree at exact source `44ca13d58a262b5f89be459b47aefa50c2d61683`, with isolated HOME/XDG; it exited 0 and reported 123 rows (109 tested, 5 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open), with 11 requirements explicitly mapped to exact-RC qualification in `ACCEPTANCE.md` §1.1. The checker output is reproducible from that source revision. This is a source-stage gate only; it does not establish RC qualification or acceptance. Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance remains `IN_PROGRESS`.\n93:**RC and publication:** The published `v1.0.0-rc.1` tag resolves to `cb364c386c42faa53b67e04cacc81d7e01520779`, an ancestor of current `main`, and is not an artifact built from current source. Its published asset digest is `8d7dd32f3d00adb98d4f0ea2c6a484ea8e04fc547b4d78b21b060000eda22b9d`. The next candidate needs a new immutable identity, currently expected to be `v1.0.0-rc.2`, with synchronized version metadata and release notes. Exact-RC artifact/install checks, held-out T2, provider and standalone qualification, T3/T4, cross-runner reproducibility, the five-environment by three-size human terminal matrix, independent RC acceptance, and stable-promotion disposition remain outstanding. Publication authorization is granted but gated on those results. No stable `v1.0.0` tag or release exists.\n117:- **Requirements gate:** `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` was independently rerun with isolated HOME/XDG on exact `7d6673f` and passed: 123 rows (109 tested, 5 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open). Eleven requirements remain explicitly deferred to exact-RC qualification: `REQ-AGT-002`, `REQ-AGT-010`, `REQ-PRV-003`, `REQ-REL-005`, `REQ-AGT-110`, `REQ-PRV-111`, `REQ-REL-114`, `REQ-QUAL-101`, `REQ-QUAL-107`, `REQ-QUAL-108`, and `REQ-QUAL-109`. This source-stage gate pass does not satisfy those qualification requirements.\n119:- **Qualification and release:** PR #102 contributes synthetic host-preflight evidence only. Private held-out custody/schema compatibility, T2/T3/T4 qualification, live provider and standalone checks, exact-RC reproducibility, the five-environment by three-size human terminal matrix, and independent RC acceptance remain outstanding. No RC has been constructed, installed, or accepted.\n137:- **Requirements enforcement:** `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` passed on exact source tree `8f4504e` (tree `2a0799c8a32e88e34322b712cf937d73cbe4d637`), with isolated `HOME`/XDG: 123 rows (109 tested, 5 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open). Eleven rows remain below the ordinary tested threshold pending their approved exact-RC evidence: `REQ-AGT-002`, `REQ-AGT-010`, `REQ-PRV-003`, `REQ-REL-005`, `REQ-AGT-110`, `REQ-PRV-111`, `REQ-REL-114`, `REQ-QUAL-101`, `REQ-QUAL-107`, `REQ-QUAL-108`, and `REQ-QUAL-109`. The pre-RC checker pass does not imply those RC gates have passed or authorize an acceptance claim.\n140:- **Other qualification gates:** No installed-RC provider or standalone matrix, T2/T3/T4 scored qualification, exact-RC cross-runner reproducibility, or independent RC acceptance exists. `ACCEPTANCE.md` §5.3 and `scripts/terminal-acceptance/README.md` define the human five-environment × three-size matrix and evidence capture; all 15 real-terminal cells remain unrun because no RC is installed. Automated PTY results do not replace those operator results.\n153:- **Requirements enforcement:** `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` ran in a detached worktree at exact `6a16cb60635c91