{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T13:27:35.045Z","ordinal":340187,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17267-b4a8-7073-9d2a-32da76e0ee35","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-5c1ba5d2-e327-4195-9f9c-2520673eb16f","process_id":"39852","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh issue view 5 --json url,title,comments --jq '.comments[-5:][] | {id,createdAt,body}'; git diff --check 405f5b96e20b988523b99c8907d29b73bcd2a8fd; git diff --stat; git diff -- docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md; git status --short"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/rc5-readiness-checkpoint","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh issue view 5 --json url,title,comments --jq '.comments[-5:][] | {id,createdAt,body}'; git diff --check 405f5b96e20b988523b99c8907d29b73bcd2a8fd; git diff --stat; git diff -- docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md; git status --short"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"{\"body\":\"Status check at `6a16cb6` (claude-code): the workflow is integrated. `.github/workflows/repro.yml` plus `scripts/repro-identity.mjs` (PR #20) build on ubuntu-22.04 and 24.04 with fail-closed tag/commit/clean-tree/version identity. It has **not** run on an RC because no RC tag exists yet. REQ-REL-114 is still `RR`, correctly. Next action: once the RC is tagged, the release publisher (codex-api-root) runs repro.yml on the exact RC and attaches the run ID and artifact hashes here.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-18T17:34:28Z\",\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABdLTlOw\"}\n{\"body\":\"### RC5 exact-tag reproducibility run (2026-10-25)\\n\\nDispatched `.github/workflows/repro.yml` as run [40195749685](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40195749685) against published tag `v1.0.0-rc.5` at `405f5b96e20b988523b99c8907d29b73bcd2a8fd`.\\n\\nBoth independent builder jobs (`ubuntu-22.04` and `ubuntu-24.04`) completed successfully. Their identities agree on the exact source, tag object, lockfiles, pinned toolchain, reviewed packaging script and six reproducibility artifact hashes. Both produced the published archive SHA-256 `b15c45f6ac7684ce8752b45432df30d77b3ecd4cc7c4ab9ee1afc8670eea8c19`. The repository's exact comparator, run locally over the workflow-uploaded identity records, returned `REQ-REL-114 / ACC-SUP-08 PASS`.\\n\\nThe workflow's own `compare` job is still queued. Until that job reaches a terminal result, `REQ-REL-114` remains pending in the enforced ledger; this issue update does not claim the formal gate is complete.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-25T13:23:05Z\",\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABfVycuQ\"}\n docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md | 4 ++--\n 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)\ndiff --git a/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md b/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\nindex 1d1faac..0629e32 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\n+++ b/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\n@@ -315,7 +315,7 @@ At `a7126aa`, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs` passes in report mode: **121\n \n - On the exact installed RC5 package, OpenRouter pinned model `nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free` and ChatGPT sign-in model `gpt-6-luna` each passed streamed completion and tool-call/result verification. No workspace content was involved. OpenRouter's required live small engineering task remains pending; the disposable synthetic task has a failing baseline and waits for the operator's folder-trust choice. Nexus remains in its default `review` approval mode; folder trust does not change approvals.\n - The installed-package startup PTY smoke reached the Nexus prompt under isolated HOME. This does not satisfy the §5.2 scripted PTY set or the §5.3 human matrix. An attempted legacy §5.2 driver was invalid: its checkout-layout paths and wait condition do not match the current RC startup/trust prompt; its mock gateway recorded zero requests. No product pass/fail was inferred.\n-- Reproducibility workflow [40195749685](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40195749685) built successfully on Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04 from the exact tag. The two builder identities and all six artifact hashes match, including the published archive. The reviewed comparator run locally over the workflow artifacts returned `REQ-REL-114 / ACC-SUP-08 PASS`, but the workflow's own `compare` job remains queued. Keep `REQ-REL-114` pending until that job completes.\n+- Reproducibility workflow [40195749685](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40195749685) built successfully on Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04 from the exact tag, but its official `compare` job **failed**. Both runner builds match each other and the published archive on the six recorded artifact hashes; the full comparison also checks the SBOM and found `metadata.tools` records npm `10.9.9` in the published RC versus npm `10.9.4` in both rebuilds. A local comparison of only the runner identity artifacts passed but did not establish `REQ-REL-114 / ACC-SUP-08`; the official result is authoritative. `REQ-REL-114` remains open until the toolchain is aligned, the release/rebuild evidence is regenerated as needed, and a new exact-RC comparison passes.\n \n ### Remaining qualification gates\n \n@@ -327,7 +327,7 @@ At `a7126aa`, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs` passes in report mode: **121\n | T4 and long-task T3 | Not run. T4 remains nine fault classes × five runs; T3 remains eight tasks × five runs. | Freeze approved workload/configurations and prerequisites, then run exact RC serially with independent scoring. |\n | Scripted installed-RC PTY (§5.2) | Not established; legacy driver invocation was invalid. | Use an RC-compatible driver or otherwise execute all listed scenarios against the installed package and mock gateway, with measured outcomes. |\n | Human terminal matrix (§5.3) | 0/15. No screenshots or per-cell operator verdicts. | Install exact RC on the desktop after GitHub CLI authentication; complete all five terminals × three sizes with two distinct screenshots per cell. |\n-| Cross-runner `REQ-REL-114` | Builder artifacts match; official comparator job queued. | Wait for run 40195749685 `compare` to reach a terminal result and archive its workflow-generated evidence. |\n+| Cross-runner `REQ-REL-114` | **Failed** on RC5: run 40195749685 `compare` reports npm-version metadata mismatch (published 10.9.9; both rebuilds 10.9.4). Builder archives match, but the SBOM does not. | Align and pin release/rebuild toolchains; independently review and integrate the fix; create the next correctly versioned RC only after pre-RC gates; rerun exact-artifact cross-runner comparison and retain its generated evidence. |\n | Independent RC acceptance | Not performed. | Independent reviewer evaluates the exact candidate and all mandatory evidence after qualification gates pass. |\n | Stable v1.0.0 | Not created or published. | Follow the version-only stable promotion and publish only after accepted RC, G6, final artifact/install checks and release evidence are complete. |\n \n M docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":311240686}},"started_at_ms":1792934853734,"completed_at_ms":1792934855045}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T13:27:35.962Z","ordinal":340188,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1733e-c51a-7710-9575-3b2a896195b1","call_id":"call_759b1f38f6c647659e92597a7cb93f6d","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.3 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"body\":\"Status check at `6a16cb6` (claude-code): the workflow is integrated. `.github/workflows/repro.yml` plus `scripts/repro-identity.mjs` (PR #20) build on ubuntu-22.04 and 24.04 with fail-closed tag/commit/clean-tree/version identity. It has **not** run on an RC because no RC tag exists yet. REQ-REL-114 is still `RR`, correctly. Next action: once the RC is tagged, the release publisher (codex-api-root) runs repro.yml on the exact RC and attaches the run ID and artifact hashes here.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-18T17:34:28Z\",\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABdLTlOw\"}\n{\"body\":\"### RC5 exact-tag reproducibility run (2026-10-25)\\n\\nDispatched `.github/workflows/repro.yml` as run [40195749685](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40195749685) against published tag `v1.0.0-rc.5` at `405f5b96e20b988523b99c8907d29b73bcd2a8fd`.\\n\\nBoth independent builder jobs (`ubuntu-22.04` and `ubuntu-24.04`) completed successfully. Their identities agree on the exact source, tag object, lockfiles, pinned toolchain, reviewed packaging script and six reproducibility artifact hashes. Both produced the published archive SHA-256 `b15c45f6ac7684ce8752b45432df30d77b3ecd4cc7c4ab9ee1afc8670eea8c19`. The repository's exact comparator, run locally over the workflow-uploaded identity records, returned `REQ-REL-114 / ACC-SUP-08 PASS`.\\n\\nThe workflow's own `compare` job is still queued. Until that job reaches a terminal result, `REQ-REL-114` remains pending in the enforced ledger; this issue update does not claim the formal gate is complete.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-25T13:23:05Z\",\"id\":\"IC_kwDOVGxXKc8AAAABfVycuQ\"}\n docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md | 4 ++--\n 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)\ndiff --git a/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md b/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\nindex 1d1faac..0629e32 100644\n--- a/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\n+++ b/docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\n@@ -315,7 +315,7 @@ At `a7126aa`, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs` passes in report mode: **121\n \n - On the exact installed RC5 package, OpenRouter pinned model `nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b:free` and ChatGPT sign-in model `gpt-6-luna` each passed streamed completion and tool-call/result verification. No workspace content was involved. OpenRouter's required live small engineering task remains pending; the disposable synthetic task has a failing baseline and waits for the operator's folder-trust choice. Nexus remains in its default `review` approval mode; folder trust does not change approvals.\n - The installed-package startup PTY smoke reached the Nexus prompt under isolated HOME. This does not satisfy the §5.2 scripted PTY set or the §5.3 human matrix. An attempted legacy §5.2 driver was invalid: its checkout-layout paths and wait condition do not match the current RC startup/trust prompt; its mock gateway recorded zero requests. No product pass/fail was inferred.\n-- Reproducibility workflow [40195749685](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40195749685) built successfully on Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04 from the exact tag. The two builder identities and all six artifact hashes match, including the published archive. The reviewed comparator run locally over the workflow artifacts returned `REQ-REL-114 / ACC-SUP-08 PASS`, but the workflow's own `compare` job remains queued. Keep `REQ-REL-114` pending until that job completes.\n+- Reproducibility workflow [40195749685](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40195749685) built successfully on Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04 from the exact tag, but its official `compare` job **failed**. Both runner builds match each other and the published archive on the six recorded artifact hashes; the full comparison also checks the SBOM and found `metadata.tools` records npm `10.9.9` in the published RC versus npm `10.9.4` in both rebuilds. A local comparison of only the runner identity artifacts passed but did not establish `REQ-REL-114 / ACC-SUP-08`; the official result is authoritative. `REQ-REL-114` remains open until the toolchain is aligned, the release/rebuild evidence is regenerated as needed, and a new exact-RC comparison passes.\n \n ### Remaining qualification gates\n \n@@ -327,7 +327,7 @@ At `a7126aa`, `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs` passes in report mode: **121\n | T4 and long-task T3 | Not run. T4 remains nine fault classes × five runs; T3 remains eight tasks × five runs. | Freeze approved workload/configurations and prerequisites, then run exact RC serially with independent scoring. |\n | Scripted installed-RC PTY (§5.2) | Not established; legacy driver invocation was invalid. | Use an RC-compatible driver or otherwise execute all listed scenarios against the installed package and mock gateway, with measured outcomes. |\n | Human terminal matrix (§5.3) | 0/15. No screenshots or per-cell operator verdicts. | Install exact RC on the desktop after GitHub CLI authentication; complete all five terminals × three sizes with two distinct screenshots per cell. |\n-| Cross-runner `REQ-REL-114` | Builder artifacts match; official comparator job queued. | Wait for run 40195749685 `compare` to reach a terminal result and archive its workflow-generated evidence. |\n+| Cross-runner `REQ-REL-114` | **Failed** on RC5: run 40195749685 `compare` reports npm-version metadata mismatch (published 10.9.9; both rebuilds 10.9.4). Builder archives match, but the SBOM does not. | Align and pin release/rebuild toolchains; independently review and integrate the fix; create the next correctly versioned RC only after pre-RC gates; rerun exact-artifact cross-runner comparison and retain its generated evidence. |\n | Independent RC acceptance | Not performed. | Independent reviewer evaluates the exact candidate and all mandatory evidence after qualification gates pass. |\n | Stable v1.0.0 | Not created or published. | Follow the version-only stable promotion and publish only after accepted RC, G6, final artifact/install checks and release evidence are complete. |\n \n M docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17267-b4a8-7073-9d2a-32da76e0ee35","create_time":1792934855.9625535}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
