{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T13:27:54.990Z","ordinal":340199,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_060b64278a9dfb15016ade03d8399c81a0bca17959e5395212","status":"completed","call_id":"call_bdb5a899500948e78821e25ef2d0750b","name":"exec","input":"const r = await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"gh pr edit 232 --body $'## Summary\\\\n\\\\nAppend one exact-revision RC5 qualification checkpoint to `docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md`. Historical checkpoints remain unchanged. The new section distinguishes verified source and artifact gates from partial E2, the formal cross-runner comparison failure, unrun qualification, and the human terminal/custody dependencies.\\\\n\\\\n## Candidate and evidence\\\\n\\\\n- Base: `405f5b96e20b988523b99c8907d29b73bcd2a8fd`\\\\n- Candidate: `cc41123a0e7bfafafa07ddcdeaba810144bce71a`\\\\n- `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce`: PASS on the clean candidate; exact-RC qualification rows remain deferred.\\\\n- `git diff --check`: PASS.\\\\n- Cross-runner workflow `40195749685` failed its official compare: published SBOM npm 10.9.9 versus rebuilt SBOM npm 10.9.4. `REQ-REL-114` remains open.\\\\n- No product source, requirements thresholds, test expectations, or acceptance criteria changed.\\\\n- Acceptance remains IN_PROGRESS; no accepted RC or stable release is claimed.'; gh issue comment 5 --body $'Correction to my earlier update: the official `compare` job in run [40195749685](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40195749685) has now completed **failure**. Both rebuilt runner artifacts match each other, and the release archive hash matches RC5, but the formal comparison checks the SBOM too: the published RC SBOM reports npm `10.9.9`, while both rebuild SBOMs report npm `10.9.4`. The prior local identity-record comparison did not cover this SBOM mismatch and is not acceptance evidence. `REQ-REL-114 / ACC-SUP-08` remains open. PR #233 is aligning the release and repro toolchains; after independent revie