{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T13:28:00.804Z","ordinal":340201,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17267-b4a8-7073-9d2a-32da76e0ee35","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-39ea74cd-3425-4f02-8ff3-e18fde18bc4b","process_id":"51008","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh pr edit 232 --body $'## Summary\\n\\nAppend one exact-revision RC5 qualification checkpoint to `docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md`. Historical checkpoints remain unchanged. The new section distinguishes verified source and artifact gates from partial E2, the formal cross-runner comparison failure, unrun qualification, and the human terminal/custody dependencies.\\n\\n## Candidate and evidence\\n\\n- Base: `405f5b96e20b988523b99c8907d29b73bcd2a8fd`\\n- Candidate: `cc41123a0e7bfafafa07ddcdeaba810144bce71a`\\n- `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce`: PASS on the clean candidate; exact-RC qualification rows remain deferred.\\n- `git diff --check`: PASS.\\n- Cross-runner workflow `40195749685` failed its official compare: published SBOM npm 10.9.9 versus rebuilt SBOM npm 10.9.4. `REQ-REL-114` remains open.\\n- No product source, requirements thresholds, test expectations, or acceptance criteria changed.\\n- Acceptance remains IN_PROGRESS; no accepted RC or stable release is claimed.'; gh issue comment 5 --body $'Correction to my earlier update: the official `compare` job in run [40195749685](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40195749685) has now completed **failure**. Both rebuilt runner artifacts match each other, and the release archive hash matches RC5, but the formal comparison checks the SBOM too: the published RC SBOM reports npm `10.9.9`, while both rebuild SBOMs report npm `10.9.4`. The prior local identity-record comparison did not cover this SBOM mismatch and is not acceptance evidence. `REQ-REL-114 / ACC-SUP-08` remains open. PR #233 is aligning the release and repro toolchains; after independent review and integration, the corrected lifecycle requires a newly versioned RC and a passing exact-tag comparison.'; gh pr view 233 --json state,headRefOid,mergeStateStatus,statusCheckRollup,url; gh pr view 232 --json body,headRefOid"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/rc5-readiness-checkpoint","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh pr edit 232 --body $'## Summary\\n\\nAppend one exact-revision RC5 qualification checkpoint to `docs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md`. Historical checkpoints remain unchanged. The new section distinguishes verified source and artifact gates from partial E2, the formal cross-runner comparison failure, unrun qualification, and the human terminal/custody dependencies.\\n\\n## Candidate and evidence\\n\\n- Base: `405f5b96e20b988523b99c8907d29b73bcd2a8fd`\\n- Candidate: `cc41123a0e7bfafafa07ddcdeaba810144bce71a`\\n- `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce`: PASS on the clean candidate; exact-RC qualification rows remain deferred.\\n- `git diff --check`: PASS.\\n- Cross-runner workflow `40195749685` failed its official compare: published SBOM npm 10.9.9 versus rebuilt SBOM npm 10.9.4. `REQ-REL-114` remains open.\\n- No product source, requirements thresholds, test expectations, or acceptance criteria changed.\\n- Acceptance remains IN_PROGRESS; no accepted RC or stable release is claimed.'; gh issue comment 5 --body $'Correction to my earlier update: the official `compare` job in run [40195749685](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40195749685) has now completed **failure**. Both rebuilt runner artifacts match each other, and the release archive hash matches RC5, but the formal comparison checks the SBOM too: the published RC SBOM reports npm `10.9.9`, while both rebuild SBOMs report npm `10.9.4`. The prior local identity-record comparison did not cover this SBOM mismatch and is not acceptance evidence. `REQ-REL-114 / ACC-SUP-08` remains open. PR #233 is aligning the release and repro toolchains; after independent review