{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T13:29:27.846Z","ordinal":340288,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a17340-7a26-7c02-bd07-94a2ca56fee0","author":"/root/plan05_readonly_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/plan05_readonly_review\nPayload:\n**ACCEPT** — PR #233 exact HEAD `2af50a532eddddb6071a6f0c5d61b15279499973`, base `405f5b96e20b988523b99c8907d29b73bcd2a8fd`. Diff SHA-256: `3db86f5917a29f47851ac3f12461528a9c5de8b9f5bfdbdfce480c6717848a59`.\n\nBoth workflows pin Node 22.22.1 and assert npm 10.9.4 before the package build that generates the SBOM. That Node release bundles npm 10.9.4, and the pin satisfies the project’s `node >=22` engine requirement. I found no conflicting `packageManager` declaration. Release and repro therefore use the same checked npm version for `npm sbom`, reducing SBOM drift between the published artifact and rebuild. ([Node.js v22.22.1 archive](https://nodejs.org/en/download/archive/v22.22.1))\n\nSource review only; I did not run tests."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17267-b4a8-7073-9d2a-32da76e0ee35","create_time":1792934967.8466766}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":16964}}
