{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T13:30:26.652Z","ordinal":340346,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17267-b4a8-7073-9d2a-32da76e0ee35","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-3f5d25bd-b7e2-491a-a1cf-c51ef68ccba4","process_id":"11418","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '188,215p' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md; ssh -o BatchMode=yes mike@10.0.8.3 'loginctl list-sessions --no-legend; loginctl seat-status seat0 2>/dev/null | head -n 15; pgrep -a gnome-shell || true; ls -d /run/user/* 2>/dev/null | head -n 10'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/rc5-readiness-checkpoint","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"sed -n '188,215p' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md; ssh -o BatchMode=yes mike@10.0.8.3 'loginctl list-sessions --no-legend; loginctl seat-status seat0 2>/dev/null | head -n 15; pgrep -a gnome-shell || true; ls -d /run/user/* 2>/dev/null | head -n 10'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"| r1a / r1d REPL approvals | DENIED for a lone Enter and for a typed-ahead `y`. |\n\n### 5.3 Manual real-terminal matrix (E3)\n\nTerminals: xterm, kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on), tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code integrated terminal, GNOME Terminal. Sizes: 80×24, 40×14, 200×60.\n\nFor each terminal × size, check:\n\n1. Launch `nexus` (the TUI appears).\n2. Approval panel. Type continuously across it. Paste 3 lines. Approve with a deliberate key.\n3. Shift+Enter or Alt+Enter multiline.\n4. Resize during streaming.\n5. Esc during `sleep 30` (no survivors).\n6. Ctrl-C twice (clean terminal restore: echo on, no stray escape codes).\n7. NO_COLOR.\n\nRecord PASS/FAIL per cell, with a screenshot of the approval panel and the post-exit terminal state.\n\n**Gate:** zero FAIL on checks 2, 5 and 6, which are safety checks. Other FAILs need a written disposition (fix, or a documented known limitation).\n\n## 6. Task-quality qualification (REQ-QUAL-101 to REQ-QUAL-106, REQ-QUAL-109)\n\nEnvironment: E4 (gateway direct), serial runs, with matched model fingerprint, budgets and env (REQ-QUAL-102).\n\n### 6.1 T2 held-out (ACC-QUAL-T2)\n\n- 40 sealed tasks. The manifest is committed before RC1, and authorship is recorded (agent-authored, DEC-05).\n- 5 runs × {Nexus RC, Goose, OpenCode}.\n  2 1000 mike seat0 6528   user    tty2 yes 10h ago\n  3 1000 mike -     6597   manager -    no  -\n313 1000 mike -     109744 user    -    no  -\n 45 1000 mike -     56109  user    -    no  -\n521 1000 mike -     138891 user    -    no  -\n 95 1000 mike -     62707  user    -    no  -\n 96 1000 mike -     62880  user    -    no  -\nseat0\nSessions: *2\n Devices: n/a\n         ├─/sys/devices/pci0000:00/0000:00:02.0/drm/card1\n         │ [MASTER] drm:card1\n         │ ├─/sys/devices/pci0000:00/0000:00:02.0/drm/card1/card1-DP-1\n         │ │ [MASTER] drm:card1-DP-1\n         │ ├─/sys/devices/pci0000:00/0000:00:02.0/drm/card1/card1-DP-2\n         │ │ [MASTER] drm:card1-DP-2\n         │ ├─/sys/devices/pci0000:00/0000:00:02.0/drm/card1/card1-HDMI-A-1\n         │ │ [MASTER] drm:card1-HDMI-A-1\n         │ └─/sys/devices/pci0000:00/0000:00:02.0/drm/card1/card1-HDMI-A-2\n         │   [MASTER] drm:card1-HDMI-A-2\n         ├─/sys/devices/pci0000:00/0000:00:02.0/drm/renderD128\n         │ drm:renderD128\n6916 /usr/bin/gnome-shell --mode=ubuntu\n6974 /usr/libexec/gnome-shell-calendar-server\n/run/user/1000\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":399538097}},"started_at_ms":1792935025251,"completed_at_ms":1792935026651}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T13:30:27.953Z","ordinal":340347,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a17341-64f0-7f71-b7ca-f3ec643179ac","call_id":"call_3eb37a805bbc47f69217f1b9bb242f22","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.8 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"| r1a / r1d REPL approvals | DENIED for a lone Enter and for a typed-ahead `y`. |\n\n### 5.3 Manual real-terminal matrix (E3)\n\nTerminals: xterm, kitty (kitty keyboard protocol on), tmux 3.x inside GNOME Terminal, VS Code integrated terminal, GNOME Terminal. Sizes: 80×24, 40×14, 200×60.\n\nFor each terminal × size, check:\n\n1. Launch `nexus` (the TUI appears).\n2. Approval panel. Type continuously across it. Paste 3 lines. Approve with a deliberate key.\n3. Shift+Enter or Alt+Enter multiline.\n4. Resize during streaming.\n5. Esc during `sleep 30` (no survivors).\n6. Ctrl-C twice (clean terminal restore: echo on, no stray escape codes).\n7. NO_COLOR.\n\nRecord PASS/FAIL per cell, with a screenshot of the approval panel and the post-exit terminal state.\n\n**Gate:** zero FAIL on checks 2, 5 and 6, which are safety checks. Other FAILs need a written disposition (fix, or a documented known limitation).\n\n## 6. Task-quality qualification (REQ-QUAL-101 to REQ-QUAL-106, REQ-QUAL-109)\n\nEnvironment: E4 (gateway direct), serial runs, with matched model fingerprint, budgets and env (REQ-QUAL-102).\n\n### 6.1 T2 held-out (ACC-QUAL-T2)\n\n- 40 sealed tasks. The manifest is committed before RC1, and authorship is recorded (agent-authored, DEC-05).\n- 5 runs × {Nexus RC, Goose, OpenCode}.\n  2 1000 mike seat0 6528   user    tty2 yes 10h ago\n  3 1000 mike -     6597   manager -    no  -\n313 1000 mike -     109744 user    -    no  -\n 45 1000 mike -     56109  user    -    no  -\n521 1000 mike -     138891 user    -    no  -\n 95 1000 mike -     62707  user    -    no  -\n 96 1000 mike -     62880  user    -    no  -\nseat0\nSessions: *2\n Devices: n/a\n         ├─/sys/devices/pci0000:00/0000:00:02.0/drm/card1\n         │ [MASTER] drm:card1\n         │ ├─/sys/devices/pci0000:00/0000:00:02.0/drm/card1/card1-DP-1\n         │ │ [MASTER] drm:card1-DP-1\n         │ ├─/sys/devices/pci0000:00/0000:00:02.0/drm/card1/card1-DP-2\n         │ │ [MASTER] drm:card1-DP-2\n         │ ├─/sys/devices/pci0000:00/0000:00:02.0/drm/card1/card1-HDMI-A-1\n         │ │ [MASTER] drm:card1-HDMI-A-1\n         │ └─/sys/devices/pci0000:00/0000:00:02.0/drm/card1/card1-HDMI-A-2\n         │   [MASTER] drm:card1-HDMI-A-2\n         ├─/sys/devices/pci0000:00/0000:00:02.0/drm/renderD128\n         │ drm:renderD128\n6916 /usr/bin/gnome-shell --mode=ubuntu\n6974 /usr/libexec/gnome-shell-calendar-server\n/run/user/1000\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17267-b4a8-7073-9d2a-32da76e0ee35","create_time":1792935027.9528475}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
