CCEPTANCE.md:322:| CON-A3 | On a clean VM, `install.sh --fresh` followed by `post-install-qualify.py` passes. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:204:- A complete `npm --prefix cli test` on the corrected exact source tree completed under Node 20.20.2/npm 10.8.2 with **1,104 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped** across 193 suites; shell exit 0; reported duration 1,615,366 ms. The preserved log is `/tmp/nexus-p10g-node20-full-corrected.log`. Build ran before the suite, and the source tree was committed without changes while the test ran, binding the result to `4439b7e`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:210:- A complete `npm --prefix cli test` run on exact PR #10 commit `bb8e673637231aa38ab04b6f07a4498a88bdc132`, using Node 20.20.2/npm 10.8.2 and an isolated home, completed with **1,097 passed, 7 failed, 0 skipped**. The preserved log is `/tmp/nexus-p10g-node20-full-bb8e673.log`. The failures include a packaged-doctor evidence disclosure of an external launcher target and valid Node 20 TAP summaries being misread as zero executed tests. This is an actual source-suite failure and supersedes any implication that the full cross-version test set had not yet been exercised locally.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:216:- A focused Node 20.20.2 run of `npm --prefix cli test -- test/security_gates.test.ts` against PR #10's pre-fix snapshot reproduced an SBOM test failure: nested `npx` exited with `ENOENT` for the absent `cli/lib` directory after inheriting npm's `npm_config_local_prefix` and `npm_config_prefix`. A prior supplemental command labeled Node 20 was invalid because `node` resolved to Node 24; it is not counted as Node 20 evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:217:- PR #10 commit `bb8e673637231aa38ab04b6f07a4498a88bdc132` (and `59dc522` on integration) clears the lowercase and uppercase prefix variables only for the nested CycloneDX `npx` call and adds a regression that injects the lowercase values set by `npm --prefix cli`. The focused security-gate suite then passed 10/10 under Node 20.20.2/npm 10.8.2 and 10/10 under Node 24.11.1/npm 11.19.0. `bash -n`, `git diff --check`, and staged Gitleaks also passed. Independent review accepted the scoped fix and confirmed Linux CI compatibility.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:312:- Ubuntu/GNOME is reachable and has all five required terminal applications, but `gh auth status` there reports no GitHub login. The RC5 installer stopped before creating files; the version-scoped desktop install prefix is absent. The manual terminal matrix is **0/15**.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:318:- Reproducibility workflow [40195749685](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40195749685) built successfully on Ubuntu 22.04 and 24.04 from the exact tag, but its official `compare` job **failed**. The comparator's earlier archive and compatibility checks passed; it then found that `metadata.tools` records npm `10.9.9` in the published RC SBOM versus npm `10.9.4` in both rebuild SBOMs. Because it stopped at that mismatch, the later `install.sh` comparison was not reached. A local comparison of only the runner identity artifacts passed but did not establish `REQ-REL-114 / ACC-SUP-08`; the official result is authoritative. `REQ-REL-114` remains open until the toolchain is aligned, the release/rebuild evidence is regenerated as needed, and a new exact-RC comparison passes.\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:74:| `harness.sh`, `install.sh`, `scripts/package-linux.sh`, `.github/workflows/*` | 05, 06, 07, 09, C1 | Claim required. Workflow edits are separate commits. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:22:| Build entry points | `make build` (cargo release + `tsc`), `make test` (cargo test + `npm --prefix cli test` + `scripts/security_gates.sh`), `scripts/package-linux.sh`, `scripts/smoke-package.sh`, `scripts/installer-smoke.sh`. CI: `.github/workflows/ci.yml` (contest contract job + `linux-x86_64`), `release.yml` (tag-triggered). A dead `.gitlab-ci.yml` also exists. | SRC |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:144:| Distribution and CI: `install.sh, harness.sh, Makefile, package.json` ×2, lockfiles, `scripts/*`, workflows, `.gitlab-ci.yml`, `LICENSE`, `doctor.ts` | 20 | Full read + installer runs (6 scratch HOMEs + docker) + CI log | E_distribution | Lockfiles audited by tool, not by line |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:273:| REL-08 | S3 | RR | Installer | `install.sh:21-24` | RT | Opaque no-version failure | REQ-REL-105 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:275:| REL-10 | S3 | RR | Reinstall | `install.sh:48-49` | RT | Cannot repair | REQ-REL-105 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:276:| REL-11 | S4 | RR | Tag validation | `install.sh:26` | RT | Loose regex | REQ-REL-105 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:277:| REL-12 | S4 | RR | Installer UX | `install.sh:32-33` | RT | Noisy output | REQ-REL-105 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:72:| REQ-REL-11 | D3/R11 | Versioned install, upgrade, rollback; LICENSE/SECURITY/CHANGELOG | TOP_TIER D3/D4 | install.sh + GitHub prereleases v0.1.0-alpha.1/.2 with SHA256SUMS; LICENSE present; **no SECURITY.md, no CHANGELOG, no rollback procedure, no signing/provenance** | N |\ndocs/v1.0.0/evidence/F_requirements_history.md:254:Spot-checks: grep in cli/src/{plugins,mcp,agent,tools,security,tester,parser,worktree,client,index,sandbox}.ts, cli/src/core/{capabilities,egress,candidate}.ts, core/src/{file_ops,search}.rs, scripts/{security_gates,generate_sbom}.sh, install.sh, .github/workflows/*.yml\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:76:| REQ-REL-001 | quickstart | Installer: non-root; SHA-256 verified; no shell-rc edits; refuses a foreign `nexus`; atomic symlink swap; failure leaves HOME untouched. | `install.sh` | RT (E §4); TEST installer-smoke | tested | N | — | ACC-PKG-05 | K | SPEC-06 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:78:| REQ-REL-003 | DEVELOPMENT.md; DEC-12 | Supported platform: Linux x86-64, glibc ≥ 2.35, Node ≥ 22. Clear failure messages elsewhere. | `install.sh`, doctor, upgrade preflight | Runtime/workflow source candidate `7c46a6d52095588f48579d9a96c5b2d526bdb3d9` passed PR #150 exact CI run `39866110578` (Node 22, Node 24, and `linux