{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T13:39:39.716Z","ordinal":340739,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17267-b4a8-7073-9d2a-32da76e0ee35","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-ebb7d559-bf84-4be9-b658-a35af6630dbe","process_id":"80373","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '250,330p' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md; rg -n 'upgrade|rollback|uninstall|lifecycle|E2|minimum runtime' eval scripts docs/v1.0.0 | head -n 100; find /home/mike/nexus-wt/rc5-postmerge-405f5b9/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification -maxdepth 4 -type f | rg '/e2|E2|install' | head -n 50"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/rc5-readiness-checkpoint","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '250,330p' docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md","name":"ACCEPTANCE.md","path":"docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'upgrade|rollback|uninstall|lifecycle|E2|minimum runtime' eval scripts docs/v1.0.0","query":"upgrade|rollback|uninstall|lifecycle|E2|minimum runtime","path":"eval"},{"type":"list_files","cmd":"find /home/mike/nexus-wt/rc5-postmerge-405f5b9/docs/reviews/evidence/v1-qualification -maxdepth 4 -type f","path":"v1-qualification"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg '/e2|E2|install'","query":"/e2|E2|install","path":null}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"\n### 6.4 Thresholds (DEC-05; all must hold)\n\n| Metric | Gate |\n|---|---|\n| False VERIFIED (T2 + T3 + T4) | **= 0** |\n| T2 pooled hidden-test correctness | ≥ 60% and ≥ best matched peer − 10 pts |\n| T2 per class (bugfix, feature, refactor, debug) | ≥ 40% |\n| Crash rate (all Nexus runs) | ≤ 2% |\n| Regression rate | ≤ 5% |\n| T4 truthful outcome | = 100% |\n| T4 hang beyond budget + 5 min | = 0 |\n| T3 false-absence | = 0 |\n| T3 false-presence | = 0 |\n| T3 steering honoured | ≥ 95% |\n| Operator interventions in `run` mode | = 0 |\n\nThe scorer output `verdict.md` lists each metric with its Wilson 95% interval, along with the infrastructure reruns and the excluded contaminated runs.\n\n## 7. Install, upgrade, rollback, uninstall (ACC-PLAT; E2)\n\n| Case | Command | Pass condition |\n|---|---|---|\n| Fresh install, each image with Node ≥ 22 | Documented one-line command with `NEXUS_VERSION=<rc>`, then the no-version command after v1.0.0 is published | Installed. `nexus --version` equals the RC. `nexus doctor` shows no version warning and an empty stderr. |\n| No Node / Node 20 | Same | Clear prerequisite message before download or state change. HOME untouched. |\n| Upgrade alpha.2 → RC | Same, with the tag | Symlink swapped. Old version retained. User state intact. |\n| Rollback RC → alpha.2 | Same, with the old tag | Works. |\n| Repair | Delete a file in the version dir, then reinstall | Repaired (REQ-REL-105). Same-version reinstall preserves working files if package fails verification. |\n| Uninstall (documented manual) | Commands from the quickstart | Only Nexus-owned paths removed. `~/.config/nexus` and `~/.nexus` retained. |\n| Checksum tamper | installer-smoke | Refused. The existing install is unchanged. |\n| Attestation | `gh attestation verify <tarball> -R mikeholownych/nexus-code` | PASS |\n| Upgrade self-test failure | `nexus upgrade` (broken candidate package) | Refused. Staging verified before switch; if post-switch verification fails, launcher atomically rolls back to previous target and journal records `rolled_back`. |\n| Upgrade crash recovery | `nexus upgrade --recover` | Idempotent recovery. Cleans incomplete staging, restores unverified launcher symlink, verifies functional installation. |\n| Backup restore | `nexus upgrade --restore-backup <state-backup-directory>` | Snapshot of configuration and complete durable state restored from a recognized private backup directory (`backup.json`, `state/`, optional `config/`), with strict 0600 file / 0700 directory modes. A canonical `config.env.bak.*` path restores configuration only. Arbitrary files and tar archives are rejected. Run it through the stable `nexus` launcher; close existing legacy clients, then keep version-pinned legacy binaries and direct old entry points offline until the durable restore journal is cleared. |\n| Incompatible downgrade | `nexus upgrade --version <v> --allow-downgrade` (incompatible state schema) | Refused fail-closed with actionable state schema explanation. Existing installation unchanged. |\n\n## 8. Independent acceptance (REQ-AGT-110, ACC-CONT-10)\n\nThe reviewer is supplied by the owner (X5) and did not implement the work under review.\n\nThe reviewer receives:\n\n- the RC package;\n- this file;\n- the REQUIREMENTS ledger;\n- SPEC-04;\n- read access to the evidence directory.\n\nThe reviewer performs:\n\n1. An independent re-run of a sample. At minimum:\n   - ACC-SAFE-01, 03, 09;\n   - ACC-PROC-02;\n   - ACC-TRUST-01, 02;\n   - ACC-CONT-01, 03;\n   - ACC-VER-01, 03;\n   - ACC-PKG-01;\n   - 5 random T2 tasks;\n   - 2 T4 classes.\n2. One live long task (≥ 60 steps, ≥ 2 compactions) on the RC through the gateway, including one kill and resume.\n3. A review of the scorer verdict and of contamination handling.\n\n**Output:** `docs/reviews/<date>-v1-rc-independent-acceptance.md` with an ACCEPT, ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS, or REJECT verdict per area. \"Accept with defects\" needs an owner disposition for every defect, and for a blocker area the only acceptable disposition is a fix.\n\n## 9. Contest (separate product; not a client gate)\n\nThe contest submission is complete and judging has concluded. No contest freeze applies (DEC-13 status amendment); post-contest hardening is tracked separately from client v1.0.0 acceptance and is accepted by:\n\n| ID | Check |\n|---|---|\n| CON-A1 | Ordinary maintained package/experiment checks build `agent-collab-worker`. `worker.config.json` has the configured name, and the bundle contains the `/work-state` handler. Do not restore the retired `cloudflare-contest-contract` status check. |\n| CON-A2 | Broker negative tests: caller-supplied env paths and URLs are ignored. A host outside `*.artifacts.cloudflare.net` is refused. |\n| CON-A3 | On a clean VM, `install.sh --fresh` followed by `post-install-qualify.py` passes. |\n| CON-A4 | `sudo -l` for the demo user shows only fixed argv. `sudo setpriv --reuid=0 id` is denied. |\n| CON-A5 | One clean-account `--mode cloudflare --agents real` run, with a committed, redacted run record. |\n| CON-A6 | The video source commits are tagged and published, or the docs state that they are unpublished. |\n\n## 10. Release decision (G6)\n\nG6 passes only when every item below holds. It authorizes a version-only stable commit from the accepted RC source, followed by its source checks, stable tag, and unpublished draft candidate; it does not authorize making stable assets publicly available. RC tags are candidate construction inputs governed by §1.1; an RC tag or its successful build does not satisfy this release decision.\n\ndocs/v1.0.0/README.md:36:| 12 | In-place CLI and TUI upgrade | [SPEC-12](specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md) | [PLAN-12](plans/PLAN-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md) | M2 | REL-115 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/README.md:44:2. **M1 is the critical path.** Work through PLAN-01, PLAN-02, PLAN-03 and PLAN-11 PR-11a/b in the PR slices listed. Each plan names its safe change boundary, code locations, tests and rollback.\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:61:| `evidence/E_distribution.md` | Distribution and doctor | 6 scratch-HOME installs; docker `ubuntu:22.04` (no node, node 12); upgrade and rollback; doctor and repair runs; CI log |\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:100:- **Unreviewed regions** are listed in AUDIT §4: file_ops.rs:400-575, MCP remote transports, browser.ts and lsp.ts at depth, the rendering modules line by line, and `PHASE2S_SECURITY_AND_DATA_REVIEW.md`. These are open qualification gaps.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:155:- Automatic GC runs at most daily. The first run after upgrade needs acknowledgement, or `NEXUS_GC=auto`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:27:| **M2 Product parity and supply chain** (parallel with M1 after PLAN-01 PR-1b) | PLAN-06 (unified launcher with the TUI as the packaged default, doc commands, doctor, installer); PLAN-07 (notices, SBOM, provenance, CI matrix, `cli/dist` untracked, SECURITY.md, CHANGELOG); PLAN-12 (CLI and TUI upgrade engine) | The installed product equals the tested product. Compliant release assets. In-place upgrade safely verifies and swaps releases. | **G2**: ACC-PKG-01..09, ACC-SUP-01..07, ACC-UPG-01..06 | 8–14 ed |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:73:| **Post-v1** | REQUIREMENTS §5: single step loop, full context provenance, knowledge freshness, `/tdd` and `nexus eval` fixes, cgroups, macOS/arm64, self-uninstall, and others |\nscripts/installer-smoke.sh:170:# Distinct from the version under test, whatever it is, so the upgrade path is always exercised.\nscripts/installer-smoke.sh:171:UPGRADE_VERSION=\"$VERSION-upgrade-smoke\"\nscripts/installer-smoke.sh:172:mkdir -p \"$TMP/release/download/$UPGRADE_VERSION\" \"$TMP/upgrade-unpack\"\nscripts/installer-smoke.sh:173:tar -xzf \"$ARCHIVE\" -C \"$TMP/upgrade-unpack\"\nscripts/installer-smoke.sh:174:printf '%s\\n' \"$UPGRADE_VERSION\" > \"$TMP/upgrade-unpack/nexus/VERSION\"\nscripts/installer-smoke.sh:175:node - \"$TMP/upgrade-unpack/nexus\" \"$UPGRADE_VERSION\" <<'NODE'\nscripts/installer-smoke.sh:191:(cd \"$TMP/upgrade-unpack/nexus\" && find . -type f ! -name MANIFEST.sha256 | LC_ALL=C sort | xargs sha256sum > MANIFEST.sha256)\nscripts/installer-smoke.sh:193:tar -C \"$TMP/upgrade-unpack\" -czf \"$TMP/release/download/$UPGRADE_VERSION/$UPGRADE_ARCHIVE\" nexus\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:20:## 1.1 Release-candidate lifecycle and evidence identity\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:80:| E2 | Docker clean images: ubuntu:22.04, ubuntu:24.04, debian:12, fedora:40. Each with no Node, then with Node 20, Node 22 and Node 24. Non-root user. | Installer, upgrade, rollback, uninstall, platform failure messages |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:87:Every ACC ID below is defined in the linked spec. The plan for each spec names the test that implements it. Run each check at the lifecycle stage dictated by its acceptance method in §1.1: source-applicable checks before the RC tag; checks requiring the RC archive, attestation, release, or installed package after RC construction; environment-specific checks in their declared environment. Bind every result to the exact source commit and, when artifact-dependent, the RC package digest. A source test or local build does not replace an artifact-bound check, and no G0–G4 ID is complete until all of its applicable checks pass.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:116:| ACC-PLAT | E2 matrix, §7 | All rows pass. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:172:- new: `process_lifecycle_e2e`\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:269:## 7. Install, upgrade, rollback, uninstall (ACC-PLAT; E2)\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:281:| Upgrade self-test failure | `nexus upgrade` (broken candidate package) | Refused. Staging verified before switch; if post-switch verification fails, launcher atomically rolls back to previous target and journal records `rolled_back`. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:282:| Upgrade crash recovery | `nexus upgrade --recover` | Idempotent recovery. Cleans incomplete staging, restores unverified launcher symlink, verifies functional installation. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:283:| Backup restore | `nexus upgrade --restore-backup <state-backup-directory>` | Snapshot of configuration and complete durable state restored from a recognized private backup directory (`backup.json`, `state/`, optional `config/`), with strict 0600 file / 0700 directory modes. A canonical `config.env.bak.*` path restores configuration only. Arbitrary files and tar archives are rejected. Run it through the stable `nexus` launcher; close existing legacy clients, then keep version-pinned legacy binaries and direct old entry points offline until the durable restore journal is cleared. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:284:| Incompatible downgrade | `nexus upgrade --version <v> --allow-downgrade` (incompatible state schema) | Refused fail-closed with actionable state schema explanation. Existing installation unchanged. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:341:  The version 1 record contains `sourceCommit` (full commit ID), `rcTag` (for example `v1.0.0-rc.1`), `artifactSha256`, `artifactProvenance` (`sourceCommit`, `artifactSha256`, and a hashed provenance report), `independentAcceptance` (`disposition`, `reviewer`, `implementers`, zero `blockingDefects`, and a hashed report reference), and one `requirements` entry for every B/RR row. For `ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS`, include each non-blocking defect with its owner disposition; unresolved or blocking defects fail. Each requirement entry records its status and one or more hashed evidence files covering the exact criteria required by the ledger and the §1.1 qualification-only map. Every criterion evidence file must be a JSON object with top-level `sourceCommit`, `rcTag`, and `artifactSha256` values exactly matching the validated qualification record, current RC source commit, and installed RC artifact. A digest-valid report copied from another source revision, RC tag, or artifact is rejected. A B row recorded as `tested` also needs a non-empty `qualificationNotApplicable.reason` and a `qualificationNotApplicable.decision` matching the approved per-requirement exception table and a matching applicability declaration in DECISIONS.md; an unrelated or record-supplied decision is rejected. Evidence paths must be relative regular files under the evidence root, with no symlinks. Missing, unknown, stale, mismatched, or incomplete evidence fails the gate. The checker requires a clean worktree, rejects `--ledger` overrides, enforces source-ledger thresholds outside the explicit §1.1 lifecycle rows, and requires the exact-RC record itself to meet the normal status threshold for every row. It never mutates the source ledger or relaxes a requirement's B/RR record threshold. The checker validates source/tag/artifact identity bindings and evidence hashes; it does not authenticate the reviewer or prove that the artifact was built from the source commit. The approved release workflow must independently verify build provenance/attestation, and the designated custodian and independent reviewer must verify their respective approvals and custody evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:63:| REQ-AGT-009 | EXEC-001..004, CAND-001..004 | One task lifecycle. Effects bound to a verified root. Validation bound to an immutable candidate. Merge requires receipt and identity equality. | `core/spine.ts`, `core/candidate.ts`, `worktree.ts:278-310` | TEST; HIST spot-check holds (F §4 #8) | tested | P (WP01/WP04 reviews) | — | existing suites | K | — |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:78:| REQ-REL-003 | DEVELOPMENT.md; DEC-12 | Supported platform: Linux x86-64, glibc ≥ 2.35, Node ≥ 22. Clear failure messages elsewhere. | `install.sh`, doctor, upgrade preflight | Runtime/workflow source candidate `7c46a6d52095588f48579d9a96c5b2d526bdb3d9` passed PR #150 exact CI run `39866110578` (Node 22, Node 24, and `linux-x86_64`) and CodeQL `39866110533`; focused `node_floor.test.ts` passed 6/6 on Node 24. Installed-RC platform qualification E2 remains pending. | partial | N | Installed-RC platform qualification E2 remains pending. | ACC-PLAT | RR | SPEC-07 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:79:| REQ-REL-004 | quickstart | Upgrade and rollback by re-running the installer with a tag. Manual uninstall keeps user data. | `install.sh` | RT (alpha.1→2→1) | tested | N | Reinstall does not repair (REL-10) | ACC-PKG-05 | K | SPEC-06 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:89:| Issue #12 (122 IDs, `PHASE2_RECONCILED_REQUIREMENTS.md`) | OPEN; 104 DEMONSTRATED | ≥ 10 DEMONSTRATED rows were later contradicted (HIST-02). More found here: EXEC-009, EXEC-011, UI-004. | **Superseded** by this ledger. The matrices are historical. Requirements still in force are carried in §2.1 and §3. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:127:| REQ-AGT-109 | EXEC-009 (carried) | Cancel kills in-flight tool process groups within 5 s. | safety | `runner.rs`, `tools.ts`, `agent.ts` | TEST (ACC-PROC-01, ACC-PROC-04; `cli/test/process_lifecycle.test.ts`, `core::runner::tests::cancel_ends_the_command_group`) | tested | ACC-PROC-01, ACC-PROC-04 | **B** | TUI-01, SEC-07 | SPEC-02 / PLAN-02 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:128:| REQ-SEC-106 | SUBP-004/005 (carried) | No task-owned process survives client exit, crash, SIGTERM or SIGHUP. Services are registered. | safety | `main.rs`, `runner.rs` | TEST (ACC-PROC-02, ACC-PROC-03; `cli/test/process_lifecycle.test.ts`, `core/tests/rpc_shutdown.rs`, `core::runner::tests::background_processes_left_by_a_command_are_ended`) | tested | ACC-PROC-02, ACC-PROC-03 | **B** | SEC-07, TUI-01 | SPEC-02 / PLAN-02 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:191:| REQ-REL-106 | Audit | `nexus self uninstall`/`prune`. | convenience | — | — | open | — | P (docs RR, already met) | REL-10 | SPEC-06 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:204:| REQ-REL-115 | Scope addition | CLI (`nexus upgrade`) and TUI (`/upgrade`) compare installed version with releases and safely upgrade to latest stable or pinned version. | user maintenance / lifecycle | `cli/src/upgrade.ts`, `cli/src/slash/session_commands.ts` | TEST (ACC-UPG-01 to ACC-UPG-06; test:cli/test/upgrade.test.ts::\"successfully performs an end-to-end upgrade with atomic symlink swap and verification\", test:cli/test/upgrade_cli.test.ts::\"returns exit code 1 when update is available in --check mode\", test:cli/test/upgrade_tui.test.ts::\"exercises deliberate approval interaction when executing /upgrade in TUI\") | tested | ACC-UPG-01 to ACC-UPG-06 | **B** | REL-14 | SPEC-12 / PLAN-12 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:205:| REQ-REL-116 | Scope addition | Machine-readable compatibility metadata, download origin & archive extraction safety, pre-migration backups, downgrade state protection, durable provenance, crash recovery, and runtime verification. | installation integrity & lifecycle | `cli/src/upgrade.ts`, `cli/src/compatibility.ts`, `cli/src/tar_safety.ts`, `cli/src/upgrade_journal.ts`, `docs/UPGRADE_SECURITY.md` | TEST (ACC-UPG-07 to ACC-UPG-14; test:cli/test/upgrade_safety.test.ts::\"rejects malicious tar archive with path traversal\", test:cli/test/upgrade_safety.test.ts::\"creates protected config and state backups with 0600 file and 0700 dir permissions\", test:cli/test/upgrade_acceptance.test.ts::\"upgrades from previous release v0.1.0-alpha.2 to v1.0.0 preserving state, configuration and permissions\", test:cli/test/upgrade_acceptance.test.ts::\"refuses downgrade when target release has incompatible state schema version\") | tested | ACC-UPG-07 to ACC-UPG-14 | **B** | REL-15 | SPEC-12 / PLAN-12 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:263:- REQ-REL-106 (self uninstall).\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:111:| M5 | **Serial on `GATEWAY`.** The eval runner, the stripped-proxy runs and the independent reviewer's live task each take the `GATEWAY` claim. The terminal matrix (E3) and the install matrix (E2) can run in parallel with gateway runs. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-08-persistence-hygiene.md:58:## Migration and rollback\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:9:**RC3, checkpoint choice, and Doctor:** RC3 remains the latest published prerelease, tagged at `1b9791f07d301c885fe48f04a796203583ab5a5c`; its archive digest and provenance are recorded in the snapshot below. The operator's `Sensitive content prevents durable persistence to checkpoint` failure occurred on immutable RC1, which predates the interactive choice flow. RC3 source contains the five choices: read-only, continue in the configured mode without a rollback checkpoint, create a checkpoint with the sensitivity risk acknowledged, cancel, or re-enter the instruction. Current RC3 source also scans saved-state metadata asynchronously in bounded batches, accepts schema-2 task `messageLog` records, and treats a configured model absent from `/models` as unverified rather than unavailable; a `--deep` inference probe can verify it. The interrupted-write temporary file reported by Doctor is a separate real warning and is not automatically repaired. These source checks and existing tests do not substitute for exercising the exact installed candidate on the operator's own state.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:23:**Installed-candidate and checkpoint-choice observation:** The published installer completed with `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1` and installed RC3 under `/home/mike/.local/lib/nexus/v1.0.0-rc.3`; installer provenance records the exact archive digest and source revision. `/home/mike/.local/bin/nexus --version` reports `1.0.0-rc.3 (1b9791f07d30)`. The previous RC1 directory remains installed at `/home/mike/.local/lib/nexus/v1.0.0-rc.1` for rollback. The coordinator reported an automated PTY probe of the installed default TUI using a synthetic Git workspace, fake credential-shaped canary, and unreachable loopback endpoint. The reported probe displayed the five choices and selected cancel before inference. Its transcript/capture was not retained in the release evidence tree, so this observation is unarchived and was not independently verified in the readiness review. It is diagnostic context only: it does not establish the checkpoint-choice gate, the five-environment by three-size human terminal matrix, or provider/task qualification.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:35:**Checkpoint failure:** `/home/mike/.local/bin/nexus` resolves to the installed `v1.0.0-rc.1` package and reports `1.0.0-rc.1 (cb364c386c42)`. That immutable package lacks checkpoint choices, so the reported failure before turn start is reproducible by version identity and will persist on RC1. The fix is integrated in PR #147 (TUI/sidecar) and PR #153 (legacy REPL): before starting a turn, Nexus asks the operator whether to use read-only mode, continue in the configured mode without a rollback checkpoint, create the checkpoint with the sensitive-content risk acknowledged, cancel, or enter a different instruction. Both PRs passed exact-head checks, and the subsequent exact-main CI on `dac465d` passed. No replacement package has been installed. The public release page still has RC1 only; RC2 has a tag but no published release, and RC3 has neither tag nor release.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:47:**Node runtime floor:** The accepted user decision is Node `>=22`. PR #150 integrates that floor in package engines, installer checks, CLI diagnostics and upgrade behavior, CI/release/reproducibility configuration, tests, and current release documentation. Superseded PRs #137 and #146 were closed after their intended policy changes were verified in current main; their older branch evidence is not current qualification evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:49:**Checkpoint failure and remediation:** The operator reports every launch attempt on installed RC1 fails before the turn starts with `Sensitive content prevents durable persistence to checkpoint`. This is confirmed as an RC1 limitation: immutable RC1 source predates the checkpoint-choice flow. PR #153 integrates that flow in current main, offering read-only, continue without a rollback checkpoint, create the checkpoint despite sensitive content, cancel, or re-enter the instruction. This is source-integrated behavior only; the installed candidate must exercise the prompt and selected actions before acceptance. RC1 and RC2 remain unchanged and do not contain this behavior.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:55:**Qualification and release disposition:** Public Issue #1 remains open; the latest custodian metadata request has no response in the available checkpoint, so T2 qualification has not started and no held-out payload was accessed. Installed-RC E2, standalone/provider, T2/T3/T4, exact-RC reproducibility, human five-terminal by three-size acceptance ([terminal matrix worksheet](TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md)), and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding. Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authorization remains granted and gated. No RC is accepted and no stable v1.0.0 release is claimed.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:61:**Node runtime floor:** The accepted user decision is Node `>=22`. PR #150 integrates that floor in package engines, installer checks, CLI diagnostics and upgrade behavior, CI/release/reproducibility configuration, tests, and current release documentation. Superseded PRs #137 and #146 were closed after their intended policy changes were verified in current main; their older branch evidence is not current qualification evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:65:**Checkpoint failure and remediation:** The operator reports that every attempt to start Nexus RC1 fails with `Sensitive content prevents durable persistence to checkpoint`. This is consistent with RC1's exact source predating PR #147's checkpoint-choice flow. PR #147 is integrated in current main and its exact-head CI and CodeQL passed; the interactive TUI now offers read-only, continue without a rollback checkpoint, create the checkpoint anyway with a sensitivity warning, cancel, or re-enter the instruction. RC1 and RC2 are immutable and do not contain this behavior. The next candidate must include the fix, and the installed candidate must be exercised to verify the choices before any acceptance claim.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:69:**Qualification and release disposition:** Public Issue #1 remains open, with no custodian response to the latest metadata-only compatibility request posted at 22:08 UTC; T2 qualification has not started and no held-out payload was accessed. Installed-RC E2, standalone/provider, T3/T4, exact-RC reproducibility, human five-terminal by three-size acceptance ([terminal matrix worksheet](TERMINAL-MATRIX-WORKSHEET.md)), and independent exact-RC acceptance remain outstanding. Campaign status is `NEXUS_V1_CONVERGENCE_ACTIVE`; acceptance is `IN_PROGRESS`; publication authorization remains granted and gated. No RC is accepted and no stable v1.0.0 release is claimed.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:141:- **Version, RC, and publication:** Root and CLI package versions remain `0.1.0-alpha.2`. GitHub currently lists only alpha pre-releases `v0.1.0-alpha.1` and `v0.1.0-alpha.2`; no `v1.0.0-rc.N` artifact/tag or stable v1.0.0 tag, npm package, or GitHub release exists. Follow the staged lifecycle in `ACCEPTANCE.md`: pre-RC source gates, RC construction, artifact-bound RC gates, installed-RC qualification and independent G6 acceptance, then stable promotion/publication and post-publication verification.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:166:- **Version, RC, and publication:** Package version remains `0.1.0-alpha.2`. PR #44's deterministic package checks are source CI evidence for that alpha package; they do not establish cross-runner RC reproducibility or installed-RC acceptance. No RC artifact, installed-RC provider/standalone, held-out, T3/T4, cross-runner, human-terminal, or independent acceptance evidence exists. The staged lifecycle in `ACCEPTANCE.md` remains authoritative. Publication authorization remains granted and gated; no RC tag, stable tag, npm publication, or GitHub release exists.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:192:- **Governance, tokenizer, and acceptance lifecycle reconciliations (PRs [#11](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/11)–[#15](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/15), [#17](https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/17)):**\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:196:  - `ACCEPTANCE.md` §1.1 (`77102c5`, PR #13) defines the five-stage RC lifecycle binding source gates, workflow-built RC artifact construction, RC artifact gates (`ACC-SUP-01/02/03/06/08`), installed-RC qualification, and version-only stable promotion.\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:261:| `REQ-REL-106` | open (post-v1; manual path defined for v1) | `SPEC-06` marks self-uninstall/prune post-v1 and retains the quickstart manual uninstall as the v1 path. The ledger's open status is a roadmap deferral, not a v1 implementation blocker. | Post-v1 scope; release documentation | Release/documentation owner | Preserve the documented manual uninstall path for v1 and record this item as explicitly deferred in the final release ledger. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/READINESS.md:311:- E2 is **partial**: all eight fresh-install/minimum-runtime cells and eight expected negative preflight cells passed across the prepared Ubuntu 22.04/24.04, Debian 12 and Fedora 40 images. One Ubuntu 22.04 / Node 22 lifecycle cell passed alpha.2 upgrade, repair, rollback and uninstall. The remaining lifecycle cases are not complete. Current-source evaluator host preflight passed 10/10 using synthetic markers only; this is not held-out custody or qualification evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-06-packaged-product-parity.md:57:10. **REQ-REL-106 (POST-V1, docs RELEASE-REQUIRED).** `nexus self uninstall` / `nexus self prune`. For v1 the manual uninstall in quickstart remains the documented path.\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-02-process-ownership-and-bounds.md:49:- **TS:** a `process_lifecycle_e2e.test.ts` PTY test that ports `evidence/D_pty/s8_cancel_tool.py` and `s9_quit_tool.py`. After each scenario it asserts there are no survivors, using `ps -eo pid,ppid,args` filtered by a unique sleep duration token.\neval/host/README.md:21:- `rollback.sh` removes them. It keeps `/opt/nexus-qual` unless you pass `--purge-runtime`, and it leaves `acl` installed.\neval/host/README.md:27:# undo: sudo bash eval/host/rollback.sh\neval/host/README.md:30:`eval/host/container-test/run.sh` exercises provision and rollback as root in a disposable privileged container:\neval/host/README.md:31:fresh and repeated runs, rollback, refusal of a foreign account, sudoers file or symlinked root (with no changes),\neval/host/README.md:32:recovery from an interrupted run, and rollback leaving a re-created account alone. Every line must read PASS.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-08-persistence-hygiene.md:55:   - A future-schema file gives \"created by a newer Nexus (schema N); upgrade\".\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-08-persistence-hygiene.md:76:- The first automatic GC after upgrade is preceded by a one-time notice with the dry-run size. It runs only after the user acknowledges it, or with `NEXUS_GC=auto`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-08-persistence-hygiene.md:85:| ACC-PER-04 | A truncated session JSON gives an explicit corrupt message and a quarantined file. A `schemaVersion: 99` file gives the upgrade message. An ambiguous prefix is refused. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-C1-contest-submission-track.md:17:- Broker and Worker unit tests pass, including demo-transport 8/8, token-response revoke cases, the credential lifecycle and the work-state contract.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-C1-contest-submission-track.md:29:| CON-005 | S2 | The committed bundle fails its own checksum on `demo-transport.mjs`, and the installer is upgrade-only. | RUNTIME |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-C1-contest-submission-track.md:31:| CON-007 to CON-014 | S3/S4 | Containment, token lifecycle, dev-dependency audit, the agent-collab-worker typecheck, Worker auth, doc staleness, information exposure and static demo strings. | See the evidence file |\neval/host/provision.sh:8:# ledger and then confirmed, so an interrupted run can be resumed or rolled back; rollback.sh removes only resources the\neval/host/provision.sh:49:flock -n 9 || { echo \"another provision or rollback is running\" >&2; exit 1; }\neval/host/provision.sh:162:[[ \"$live\" == \"tmpfs $storage_bytes $op_uid 711\" ]] || { echo \"mounted $workspace_root is '$live', not 'tmpfs $storage_bytes $op_uid 711'; run rollback.sh, then provision again\" >&2; exit 1; }\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:1:# SPEC-12: CLI and TUI upgrade commands\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:6:| Release class | **BLOCKER**: in-product safe upgrade mechanism for CLI and TUI; required before RC freeze. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:8:| Findings | UPG-01 (no supported in-product upgrade path without manual curl-pipe script execution) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:9:| Plan | [PLAN-12](../plans/PLAN-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:14:Nexus currently requires operators to re-run the external `install.sh` script via `curl -fsSL ... | sh` to upgrade or downgrade installed binaries. There is no CLI command (`nexus upgrade`) and no TUI slash command (`/upgrade`) to:\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:17:3. Inspect upgrade, downgrade, or reinstallation changes non-destructively (`--check`).\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:18:4. Perform an atomic, verified, checksummed upgrade directly from the terminal or TUI with deliberate operator confirmation.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:24:1. **REQ-REL-115 (CLI and TUI upgrade).**\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:25:   - Provide `nexus upgrade` and `/upgrade` slash command backed by a shared release-resolution and upgrade engine.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:26:   - Support `nexus upgrade --check` and `nexus upgrade --check --version <v>` to non-destructively compare installed and published versions, exiting 0 (up to date), 1 (update available), or 2 (operational error).\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:27:   - Support `nexus upgrade` (defaulting to latest published stable release, excluding drafts and prereleases) and `nexus upgrade --version <version>` (targeting exact pinned release, allowing prereleases only when explicitly requested).\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:28:   - Support structured JSON output via `--json` across check and upgrade operations.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:32:   - In the TUI, `/upgrade` must use the established deliberate approval interaction (`Overlay::Approval`), ensuring ordinary typing, queued input, pasted input, or accidental bare Enter cannot authorize an installation change.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:35:   - Prevent concurrent upgrade attempts via atomic lockfile.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:37:   - Protect running TUI processes: never terminate active sessions unsafely or overwrite loaded components; report when restart is required and verify the upgraded version upon fresh launch without claiming the current process has changed version in-flight.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:43:   - Create 0600-permission pre-migration configuration and state backups; refuse state-incompatible downgrades fail-closed; support distinct `--rollback-binary` and `--restore-backup <path>`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:45:   - Maintain transaction journal (`.upgrade-journal.json`); provide idempotent crash recovery (`--recover` and automatic check on startup).\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:53:The upgrade capability is implemented in `cli/src/upgrade.ts` as a pure, testable engine with interfaces for release lookup, provenance detection, artifact retrieval, integrity verification, and atomic switching.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:57:                      │  CLI: nexus upgrade [...]  │\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:62:│ TUI: /upgrade [...]     ├──►│    Upgrade Engine         ├──►│ GitHub Releases API       │\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:63:│ (deliberate approval)   │   │    (cli/src/upgrade.ts)   │   │ & SHA256SUMS asset        │\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:79:- Downgrades: When `target < installed`, the upgrade engine flags the action as `downgrade` and requires explicit authorization (`--allow-downgrade` or explicit confirmation).\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:88:  - Concurrency: Flocked or exclusive lockfile `$PREFIX/lib/nexus/.upgrade.lock`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:103:- `/upgrade` routes through `cli/src/slash/router.ts` to `session_commands.ts`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:108:  - Action (upgrade, downgrade, reinstall).\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:117:| ACC-UPG-01 | `nexus upgrade --check` | Compares installed version with latest published stable release. Exits 0 if already current, 1 if update available, 2 on operational error. Does not modify filesystem. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:118:| ACC-UPG-02 | `nexus upgrade --check --version <v>` | Compares installed version with exact specified version. Exits 0 if matching/newer, 1 if update available, 2 on error/missing release. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:119:| ACC-UPG-03 | `nexus upgrade` (CLI install) | Resolves latest stable release; prompts for confirmation in interactive mode; requires `--yes` in noninteractive mode; exits with code 0 on success, 1 if declined, 2 on failure. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:121:| ACC-UPG-05 | `/upgrade` slash command in TUI | Supports `--check`, `--version`, and install modes. Uses deliberate TUI approval modal (`Overlay::Approval`). Preserves session state and explains restart requirement. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:125:| ACC-UPG-09 | Migration & Downgrade Protection | Creates 0600-permission pre-migration backups, refuses state-incompatible downgrades fail-closed, supports distinct `--rollback-binary` and `--restore-backup <path>`. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:127:| ACC-UPG-11 | Upgrade Journal & Crash Recovery | Maintains `.upgrade-journal.json`, recovers interrupted upgrades idempotently via `--recover` and automatic check on startup. |\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":737555519}},"started_at_ms":1792935578977,"completed_at_ms":1792935579716}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T13:39:41.186Z","ordinal":340740,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a17349-d601-73e3-934b-8496e54ce69c","call_id":"call_fa0628ac70de4a4aa246296f05f0d17a","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.3 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 9042)\nTotal output lines: 181\n\n\n### 6.4 Thresholds (DEC-05; all must hold)\n\n| Metric | Gate |\n|---|---|\n| False VERIFIED (T2 + T3 + T4) | **= 0** |\n| T2 pooled hidden-test correctness | ≥ 60% and ≥ best matched peer − 10 pts |\n| T2 per class (bugfix, feature, refactor, debug) | ≥ 40% |\n| Crash rate (all Nexus runs) | ≤ 2% |\n| Regression rate | ≤ 5% |\n| T4 truthful outcome | = 100% |\n| T4 hang beyond budget + 5 min | = 0 |\n| T3 false-absence | = 0 |\n| T3 false-presence | = 0 |\n| T3 steering honoured | ≥ 95% |\n| Operator interventions in `run` mode | = 0 |\n\nThe scorer output `verdict.md` lists each metric with its Wilson 95% interval, along with the infrastructure reruns and the excluded contaminated runs.\n\n## 7. Install, upgrade, rollback, uninstall (ACC-PLAT; E2)\n\n| Case | Command | Pass condition |\n|---|---|---|\n| Fresh install, each image with Node ≥ 22 | Documented one-line command with `NEXUS_VERSION=<rc>`, then the no-version command after v1.0.0 is published | Installed. `nexus --version` equals the RC. `nexus doctor` shows no version warning and an empty stderr. |\n| No Node / Node 20 | Same | Clear prerequisite message before download or state change. HOME untouched. |\n| Upgrade alpha.2 → RC | Same, with the tag | Symlink swapped. Old version retained. User state intact. |\n| Rollback RC → alpha.2 | Same, with the old tag | Works. |\n| Repair | Delete a file in the version dir, then reinstall | Repaired (REQ-REL-105). Same-version reinstall preserves working files if package fails verification. |\n| Uninstall (documented manual) | Commands from the quickstart | Only Nexus-owned paths removed. `~/.config/nexus` and `~/.nexus` retained. |\n| Checksum tamper | installer-smoke | Refused. The existing install is unchanged. |\n| Attestation | `gh attestation verify <tarball> -R mikeholownych/nexus-code` | PASS |\n| Upgrade self-test failure | `nexus upgrade` (broken candidate package) | Refused. Staging verified before switch; if post-switch verification fails, launcher atomically rolls back to previous target and journal records `rolled_back`. |\n| Upgrade crash recovery | `nexus upgrade --recover` | Idempotent recovery. Cleans incomplete staging, restores unverified launcher symlink, verifies functional installation. |\n| Backup restore | `nexus upgrade --restore-backup <state-backup-directory>` | Snapshot of configuration and complete durable state restored from a recognized private backup directory (`backup.json`, `state/`, optional `config/`), with strict 0600 file / 0700 directory modes. A canonical `config.env.bak.*` path restores configuration only. Arbitrary files and tar archives are rejected. Run it through the stable `nexus` launcher; close existing legacy clients, then keep version-pinned legacy binaries and direct old entry points offline until the durable restore journal is cleared. |\n| Incompatible downgrade | `nexus upgrade --version <v> --allow-downgrade` (incompatible state schema) | Refused fail-closed with actionable state schema explanation. Existing installation unchanged. |\n\n## 8. Independent acceptance (REQ-AGT-110, ACC-CONT-10)\n\nThe reviewer is supplied by the owner (X5) and did not implement the work under review.\n\nThe reviewer receives:\n\n- the RC package;\n- this file;\n- the REQUIREMENTS ledger;\n- SPEC-04;\n- read access to the evidence directory.\n\nThe reviewer performs:\n\n1. An independent re-run of a sample. At minimum:\n   - ACC-SAFE-01, 03, 09;\n   - ACC-PROC-02;\n   - ACC-TRUST-01, 02;\n   - ACC-CONT-01, 03;\n   - ACC-VER-01, 03;\n   - ACC-PKG-01;\n   - 5 random T2 tasks;\n   - 2 T4 classes.\n2. One live long task (≥ 60 steps, ≥ 2 compactions) on the RC through the gateway, including one kill and resume.\n3. A review of the scorer verdict and of contamination handling.\n\n**Output:** `docs/reviews/<date>-v1-rc-independent-acceptance.md` with an ACCEPT, ACCEPT WITH DEFECTS, or REJECT verdict per area. \"Accept with defects\" needs an owner disposition for every defect, and for a blocker area the only acceptable disposition is a fix.\n\n## 9. Contest (separate product; not a client gate)\n\nThe contest submission is complete and judging has concluded. No contest freeze applies (DEC-13 status amendment); post-contest hardening is tracked separately from client v1.0.0 acceptance and is accepted by:\n\n| ID | Check |\n|---|---|\n| CON-A1 | Ordinary maintained package/experiment checks build `agent-collab-worker`. `worker.config.json` has the configured name, and the bundle contains the `/work-state` handler. Do not restore the retired `cloudflare-contest-contract` status check. |\n| CON-A2 | Broker negative tests: caller-supplied env paths and URLs are ignored. A host outside `*.artifacts.cloudflare.net` is refused. |\n| CON-A3 | On a clean VM, `install.sh --fresh` followed by `post-install-qualify.py` passes. |\n| CON-A4 | `sudo -l` for the demo user shows only fixed argv. `sudo setpriv --reuid=0 id` is denied. |\n| CON-A5 | One clean-account `--mode cloudflare --agents real` run, with a committed, redacted run record. |\n| CON-A6 | The video source commits are tagged and published, or the docs state that they are unpublished. |\n\n## 10. Release decision (G6)\n\nG6 passes only when every item below holds. It authorizes a version-only stable commit from the accepted RC source, followed by its source checks, stable tag, and unpublished draft candidate; it does not authorize making stable assets publicly available. RC tags are candidate construction inputs governed by §1.1; an RC tag or its successful build does not satisfy this release decision.\n\ndocs/v1.0.0/README.md:36:| 12 | In-place CLI and TUI upgrade | [SPEC-12](specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md) | [PLAN-12](plans/PLAN-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md) | M2 | REL-115 |\ndocs/v1.0.0/README.md:44:2. **M1 is the critical path.** Work through PLAN-01, PLAN-02, PLAN-03 and PLAN-11 PR-11a/b in the PR slices listed. Each plan names its safe change boundary, code locations, tests and rollback.\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:61:| `evidence/E_distribution.md` | Distribution and doctor | 6 scratch-HOME installs; docker `ubuntu:22.04` (no node, node 12); upgrade and rollback; doctor and repair runs; CI log |\ndocs/v1.0.0/EVIDENCE.md:100:- **Unreviewed regions** are listed in AUDIT §4: file_ops.rs:400-575, MCP remote transports, browser.ts and lsp.ts at depth, the rendering modules line by line, and `PHASE2S_SECURITY_AND_DATA_REVIEW.md`. These are open qualification gaps.\ndocs/v1.0.0/DECISIONS.md:155:- Automatic GC runs at most daily. The first run after upgrade needs acknowledgement, or `NEXUS_GC=auto`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:27:| **M2 Product parity and supply chain** (parallel with M1 after PLAN-01 PR-1b) | PLAN-06 (unified launcher with the TUI as the packaged default, doc commands, doctor, installer); PLAN-07 (notices, SBOM, provenance, CI matrix, `cli/dist` untracked, SECURITY.md, CHANGELOG); PLAN-12 (CLI and TUI upgrade engine) | The installed product equals the tested product. Compliant release assets. In-place upgrade safely verifies and swaps releases. | **G2**: ACC-PKG-01..09, ACC-SUP-01..07, ACC-UPG-01..06 | 8–14 ed |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:73:| **Post-v1** | REQUIREMENTS §5: single step loop, full context provenance, knowledge freshness, `/tdd` and `nexus eval` fixes, cgroups, macOS/arm64, self-uninstall, and others |\nscripts/installer-smoke.sh:170:# Distinct from the version under test, whatever it is, so the upgrade path is always exercised.\nscripts/installer-smoke.sh:171:UPGRADE_VERSION=\"$VERSION-upgrade-smoke\"\nscripts/installer-smoke.sh:172:mkdir -p \"$TMP/release/download/$UPGRADE_VERSION\" \"$TMP/upgrade-unpack\"\nscripts/installer-smoke.sh:173:tar -xzf \"$ARCHIVE\" -C \"$TMP/upgrade-unpack\"\nscripts/installer-smoke.sh:174:printf '%s\\n' \"$UPGRADE_VERSION\" > \"$TMP/upgrade-unpack/nexus/VERSION\"\nscripts/installer-smoke.sh:175:node - \"$TMP/upgrade-unpack/nexus\" \"$UPGRADE_VERSION\" <<'NODE'\nscripts/installer-smoke.sh:191:(cd \"$TMP/upgrade-unpack/nexus\" && find . -type f ! -name MANIFEST.sha256 | LC_ALL=C sort | xargs sha256sum > MANIFEST.sha256)\nscripts/installer-smoke.sh:193:tar -C \"$TMP/upgrade-unpack\" -czf \"$TMP/release/download/$UPGRADE_VERSION/$UPGRADE_ARCHIVE\" nexus\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:20:## 1.1 Release-candidate lifecycle and evidence identity\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:80:| E2 | Docker clean images: ubuntu:22.04, ubuntu:24.04, debian:12, fedora:40. Each with no Node, then with Node 20, Node 22 and Node 24. Non-root user. | Installer, upgrade, rollback, uninstall, platform failure messages |\ndocs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md:87:Every ACC ID below is defined in the linked spec. The plan for each spec names the test that implements it. Run each check at the lifecycle stage dictated by its acceptance method in §1.1: source-applicable checks before the RC tag; checks requiring the RC archive, attestation, release, or installed package after RC construction; environment-specific checks in their declared environment. Bind every result to the exact source commit and, when artifact-dependent, the RC package dige…4542 tokens truncated…held-out custody or qualification evidence.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-06-packaged-product-parity.md:57:10. **REQ-REL-106 (POST-V1, docs RELEASE-REQUIRED).** `nexus self uninstall` / `nexus self prune`. For v1 the manual uninstall in quickstart remains the documented path.\ndocs/v1.0.0/plans/PLAN-02-process-ownership-and-bounds.md:49:- **TS:** a `process_lifecycle_e2e.test.ts` PTY test that ports `evidence/D_pty/s8_cancel_tool.py` and `s9_quit_tool.py`. After each scenario it asserts there are no survivors, using `ps -eo pid,ppid,args` filtered by a unique sleep duration token.\neval/host/README.md:21:- `rollback.sh` removes them. It keeps `/opt/nexus-qual` unless you pass `--purge-runtime`, and it leaves `acl` installed.\neval/host/README.md:27:# undo: sudo bash eval/host/rollback.sh\neval/host/README.md:30:`eval/host/container-test/run.sh` exercises provision and rollback as root in a disposable privileged container:\neval/host/README.md:31:fresh and repeated runs, rollback, refusal of a foreign account, sudoers file or symlinked root (with no changes),\neval/host/README.md:32:recovery from an interrupted run, and rollback leaving a re-created account alone. Every line must read PASS.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-08-persistence-hygiene.md:55:   - A future-schema file gives \"created by a newer Nexus (schema N); upgrade\".\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-08-persistence-hygiene.md:76:- The first automatic GC after upgrade is preceded by a one-time notice with the dry-run size. It runs only after the user acknowledges it, or with `NEXUS_GC=auto`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-08-persistence-hygiene.md:85:| ACC-PER-04 | A truncated session JSON gives an explicit corrupt message and a quarantined file. A `schemaVersion: 99` file gives the upgrade message. An ambiguous prefix is refused. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-C1-contest-submission-track.md:17:- Broker and Worker unit tests pass, including demo-transport 8/8, token-response revoke cases, the credential lifecycle and the work-state contract.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-C1-contest-submission-track.md:29:| CON-005 | S2 | The committed bundle fails its own checksum on `demo-transport.mjs`, and the installer is upgrade-only. | RUNTIME |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-C1-contest-submission-track.md:31:| CON-007 to CON-014 | S3/S4 | Containment, token lifecycle, dev-dependency audit, the agent-collab-worker typecheck, Worker auth, doc staleness, information exposure and static demo strings. | See the evidence file |\neval/host/provision.sh:8:# ledger and then confirmed, so an interrupted run can be resumed or rolled back; rollback.sh removes only resources the\neval/host/provision.sh:49:flock -n 9 || { echo \"another provision or rollback is running\" >&2; exit 1; }\neval/host/provision.sh:162:[[ \"$live\" == \"tmpfs $storage_bytes $op_uid 711\" ]] || { echo \"mounted $workspace_root is '$live', not 'tmpfs $storage_bytes $op_uid 711'; run rollback.sh, then provision again\" >&2; exit 1; }\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:1:# SPEC-12: CLI and TUI upgrade commands\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:6:| Release class | **BLOCKER**: in-product safe upgrade mechanism for CLI and TUI; required before RC freeze. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:8:| Findings | UPG-01 (no supported in-product upgrade path without manual curl-pipe script execution) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:9:| Plan | [PLAN-12](../plans/PLAN-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md) |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:14:Nexus currently requires operators to re-run the external `install.sh` script via `curl -fsSL ... | sh` to upgrade or downgrade installed binaries. There is no CLI command (`nexus upgrade`) and no TUI slash command (`/upgrade`) to:\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:17:3. Inspect upgrade, downgrade, or reinstallation changes non-destructively (`--check`).\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:18:4. Perform an atomic, verified, checksummed upgrade directly from the terminal or TUI with deliberate operator confirmation.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:24:1. **REQ-REL-115 (CLI and TUI upgrade).**\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:25:   - Provide `nexus upgrade` and `/upgrade` slash command backed by a shared release-resolution and upgrade engine.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:26:   - Support `nexus upgrade --check` and `nexus upgrade --check --version <v>` to non-destructively compare installed and published versions, exiting 0 (up to date), 1 (update available), or 2 (operational error).\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:27:   - Support `nexus upgrade` (defaulting to latest published stable release, excluding drafts and prereleases) and `nexus upgrade --version <version>` (targeting exact pinned release, allowing prereleases only when explicitly requested).\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:28:   - Support structured JSON output via `--json` across check and upgrade operations.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:32:   - In the TUI, `/upgrade` must use the established deliberate approval interaction (`Overlay::Approval`), ensuring ordinary typing, queued input, pasted input, or accidental bare Enter cannot authorize an installation change.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:35:   - Prevent concurrent upgrade attempts via atomic lockfile.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:37:   - Protect running TUI processes: never terminate active sessions unsafely or overwrite loaded components; report when restart is required and verify the upgraded version upon fresh launch without claiming the current process has changed version in-flight.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:43:   - Create 0600-permission pre-migration configuration and state backups; refuse state-incompatible downgrades fail-closed; support distinct `--rollback-binary` and `--restore-backup <path>`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:45:   - Maintain transaction journal (`.upgrade-journal.json`); provide idempotent crash recovery (`--recover` and automatic check on startup).\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:53:The upgrade capability is implemented in `cli/src/upgrade.ts` as a pure, testable engine with interfaces for release lookup, provenance detection, artifact retrieval, integrity verification, and atomic switching.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:57:                      │  CLI: nexus upgrade [...]  │\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:62:│ TUI: /upgrade [...]     ├──►│    Upgrade Engine         ├──►│ GitHub Releases API       │\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:63:│ (deliberate approval)   │   │    (cli/src/upgrade.ts)   │   │ & SHA256SUMS asset        │\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:79:- Downgrades: When `target < installed`, the upgrade engine flags the action as `downgrade` and requires explicit authorization (`--allow-downgrade` or explicit confirmation).\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:88:  - Concurrency: Flocked or exclusive lockfile `$PREFIX/lib/nexus/.upgrade.lock`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:103:- `/upgrade` routes through `cli/src/slash/router.ts` to `session_commands.ts`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:108:  - Action (upgrade, downgrade, reinstall).\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:117:| ACC-UPG-01 | `nexus upgrade --check` | Compares installed version with latest published stable release. Exits 0 if already current, 1 if update available, 2 on operational error. Does not modify filesystem. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:118:| ACC-UPG-02 | `nexus upgrade --check --version <v>` | Compares installed version with exact specified version. Exits 0 if matching/newer, 1 if update available, 2 on error/missing release. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:119:| ACC-UPG-03 | `nexus upgrade` (CLI install) | Resolves latest stable release; prompts for confirmation in interactive mode; requires `--yes` in noninteractive mode; exits with code 0 on success, 1 if declined, 2 on failure. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:121:| ACC-UPG-05 | `/upgrade` slash command in TUI | Supports `--check`, `--version`, and install modes. Uses deliberate TUI approval modal (`Overlay::Approval`). Preserves session state and explains restart requirement. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:125:| ACC-UPG-09 | Migration & Downgrade Protection | Creates 0600-permission pre-migration backups, refuses state-incompatible downgrades fail-closed, supports distinct `--rollback-binary` and `--restore-backup <path>`. |\ndocs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:127:| ACC-UPG-11 | Upgrade Journal & Crash Recovery | Maintains `.upgrade-journal.json`, recovers interrupted upgrades idempotently via `--recover` and automatic check on startup. |\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17267-b4a8-7073-9d2a-32da76e0ee35","create_time":1792935581.1858122}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
