{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T13:57:02.176Z","ordinal":341165,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a17359-b860-7ed2-8842-12efb52ec34f","call_id":"call_3f75363504fd4042a7d6810dbce45e8d","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/current_main_rc_path_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"PR #232 remains open at the reviewed head. I did not merge it. GitHub rejected the approval because the connected account is the PR author, so another reviewer must record the formal approval.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/plan05_readonly_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** — PR #233 exact HEAD `2af50a532eddddb6071a6f0c5d61b15279499973`, base `405f5b96e20b988523b99c8907d29b73bcd2a8fd`. Diff SHA-256: `3db86f5917a29f47851ac3f12461528a9c5de8b9f5bfdbdfce480c6717848a59`.\\n\\nBoth workflows pin Node 22.22.1 and assert npm 10.9.4 before the package build that generates the SBOM. That Node release bundles npm 10.9.4, and the pin satisfies the project’s `node >=22` engine requirement. I found no conflicting `packageManager` declaration. Release and repro therefore use the same checked npm version for `npm sbom`, reducing SBOM drift between the published artifact and rebuild. ([Node.js v22.22.1 archive](https://nodejs.org/en/download/archive/v22.22.1))\\n\\nSource review only; I did not run tests.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/t4_runner_independent_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"ACCEPT — after the child’s `close` event, `kill()` now only attempts cgroup cleanup and cannot signal a potentially reused PID or create lingering timers. Before `close`, immediate and repeated cgroup cleanup behavior is preserved. The diff check was clean; I did not run tests.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17359-3515-7cd3-8706-e6bd2e3432cb","create_time":1792936622.1761937}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
