{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T13:59:56.545Z","ordinal":341233,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_060b64278a9dfb15016ade0b5acb8881a0a6c23d94fab1749b","status":"completed","call_id":"call_edf2322a294d4751af01429f8d0d0c40","name":"exec","input":"const r=await Promise.allSettled([\n tools.exec_command({cmd:\"gh issue view 3 --json body,comments | jq -r '.body, .comments[-3:][]?.body' | tail -120\",workdir:\"/home/mike/nexus-code\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:1600}),\n tools.exec_command({cmd:\"gh pr checks 232\",workdir:\"/home/mike/nexus-code\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:800}),\n tools.exec_command({cmd:\"gh run view 40197651928 --json jobs | jq -r '.jobs[]|[.name,.status,([.steps[]|select(.status==\\\"in_progress\\\")|.name]|join(\\\"; \\\"))]|@tsv'; gh run view 40197810800 --json jobs | jq -r '.jobs[]|[.name,.status,([.steps[]|select(.status==\\\"in_progress\\\")|.name]|join(\\\"; \\\"))]|@tsv'\",workdir:\"/home/mike/nexus-code\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:500})\n]);\nfor(const x of r) text(x.status===\"fulfilled\"?x.value.output:x.reason);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17359-3515-7cd3-8706-e6bd2e3432cb","create_time":1792936794.7974677}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T13:59:56.630Z","ordinal":341234,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17359-3515-7cd3-8706-e6bd2e3432cb","session_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","root_turn_id":"01a17359-3515-7cd3-8706-e6bd2e3432cb","response_id":"resp_060b64278a9dfb15016ade0b56d46081a0873edc3ba8667d14","usage":{"input_tokens":101410,"cached_input_tokens":100736,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":640,"reasoning_output_tokens":371,"total_tokens":102050},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":1363650,"cached_input_tokens":1350272,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":4424,"reasoning_output_tokens":2198,"total_tokens":1368074},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":6229889031,"cached_input_tokens":6163282560,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":17756697,"reasoning_output_tokens":10251609,"total_tokens":6247645728}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T13:59:58.039Z","ordinal":341235,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17359-3515-7cd3-8706-e6bd2e3432cb","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-cfe5f55e-51c1-431b-9a36-40d0d8f6676e","process_id":"46426","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh issue view 3 --json body,comments | jq -r '.body, .comments[-3:][]?.body' | tail -120"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh issue view 3 --json body,comments | jq -r '.body, .comments[-3:][]?.body' | tail -120"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"## Scope\nComplete the manual E3 matrix on actual supported terminals; automated PTY tests are not a substitute for human interaction evidence.\n\n## Acceptance\n- Exercise the exact terminal × size matrix and required approval, typing/paste, cancellation, cleanup, resize, steering, and recovery cases from ACCEPTANCE.md §5.3.\n- Record terminal/emulator, PTY, OS, launcher/build/package identity, scenario result, and required screenshots/evidence.\n- Preserve failures and classify unavailable terminal environments as NOT RUN; do not silently substitute another terminal.\n- Update REQ-QUAL-108 only when its manual evidence is complete.\n\nReference: `docs/v1.0.0/ACCEPTANCE.md` §5.3 and PLAN-10 task 12.\n### RC5 terminal matrix preparation (2026-10-25; no cells run)\n\nThe exact candidate is public as `v1.0.0-rc.5`, source commit `405f5b96e20b988523b99c8907d29b73bcd2a8fd`, with published archive SHA-256 `b15c45f6ac7684ce8752b45432df30d77b3ecd4cc7c4ab9ee1afc8670eea8c19`. The official installer and provenance were verified on the authenticated engineering host.\n\nThe connected Ubuntu 26.04/GNOME desktop has all five required terminals installed. The RC5 installer check there stopped before creating files because `gh auth status` reports no GitHub login; the version-scoped install prefix is absent. After signing in with GitHub CLI on that desktop, use the documented RC5 installer with prefix `$HOME/.local/rc5-qual-405f5`, verify `nexus --version` is `1.0.0-rc.5 (405f5b96e20b)`, and use that installed binary for the matrix.\n\nThe matrix remains **0/15**. Run `scripts/terminal-acceptance/run-cell.sh` once for each of the five terminals (`xterm`, `kitty`, `tmux-gnome`, `vscode`, `gnome`) at 80×24, 40×14, and 200×60. Each cell needs the interactive checks and two distinct screenshots (approval panel and post-exit terminal). Automated PTY checks do not count as these operator results. The existing script records installed binary identity, package manifest, per-check verdicts, screenshot hashes, mock request log, terminal restoration, and process-scope cleanup measurements.\n\nAcceptance is still in progress; no terminal cell is claimed complete by this setup update.\n\n### RC5 installer verification follow-up (2026-10-25; no cells run)\n\nOn the connected Ubuntu 26.04/GNOME desktop, the public RC5 archive downloads successfully and its SHA-256 matches the published `SHA256SUMS` entry (`b15c45f6ac7684ce8752b45432df30d77b3ecd4cc7c4ab9ee1afc8670eea8c19`). The installer’s required provenance verification remains unavailable because GitHub CLI is not signed in on that host (`gh attestation verify` requests `gh auth login`). I did not set `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=0` or create an installation. The version-scoped prefix remains absent; the terminal matrix is still 0/15.\n\nTo proceed with the official installer and preserve the provenance gate, sign in on that desktop using GitHub CLI, then rerun the documented installer command from the prior update.\n### Candidate selection correction (2026-10-25)\n\nRC5 has now failed its official cross-runner comparison because the published SBOM and rebuild SBOMs record different npm versions. Do not treat terminal runs on RC5 as v1.0.0 acceptance evidence. Keep the matrix at **0/15** and retain the existing worksheet/setup notes; after the toolchain fix is integrated and the successor RC is built and published, install that exact successor with provenance verification and bind every cell and screenshot to its identity and digest.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":391120003}},"started_at_ms":1792936797648,"completed_at_ms":1792936798039}}
