{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T14:09:49.838Z","ordinal":341539,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_060b64278a9dfb15016ade0dac913481a0910ddcc8bcc8031b","status":"completed","call_id":"call_062de0fbaaaa49b7bc993e5f25cdc495","name":"exec","input":"const r=await tools.exec_command({cmd:\"sed -n '1,55p' docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md; rg -n 'nexus-claims|owner.json|claim.*atomic' scripts docs/v1.0.0 .github | head -80; rg -n \\\"Checkpoint could not verify protected Git state\\\" cli/src/checkpoint.ts\",workdir:\"/home/mike/nexus-wt/rc5-readiness-checkpoint\",yield_time_ms:10000,max_output_tokens:1400});\ntext(r.output);\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17359-3515-7cd3-8706-e6bd2e3432cb","create_time":1792937388.569911}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T14:09:49.989Z","ordinal":341540,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17359-3515-7cd3-8706-e6bd2e3432cb","session_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","root_turn_id":"01a17359-3515-7cd3-8706-e6bd2e3432cb","response_id":"resp_060b64278a9dfb15016ade0da9b76481a0b2ce9e4d066fb35b","usage":{"input_tokens":133661,"cached_input_tokens":132224,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":391,"reasoning_output_tokens":262,"total_tokens":134052},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":5946580,"cached_input_tokens":5897600,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":18445,"reasoning_output_tokens":9936,"total_tokens":5965025},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":6234471961,"cached_input_tokens":6167829888,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":17770718,"reasoning_output_tokens":10259347,"total_tokens":6252242679}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T14:09:52.182Z","ordinal":341541,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17359-3515-7cd3-8706-e6bd2e3432cb","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-9db839f0-1b22-4dda-a99b-6ed860e8540c","process_id":"15296","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1,55p' docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md; rg -n 'nexus-claims|owner.json|claim.*atomic' scripts docs/v1.0.0 .github | head -80; rg -n \"Checkpoint could not verify protected Git state\" cli/src/checkpoint.ts"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/rc5-readiness-checkpoint","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,55p' docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md","name":"CONCURRENCY.md","path":"docs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'nexus-claims|owner.json|claim.*atomic' scripts docs/v1.0.0 .github","query":"nexus-claims|owner.json|claim.*atomic","path":"scripts"},{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'Checkpoint could not verify protected Git state' cli/src/checkpoint.ts","query":"Checkpoint could not verify protected Git state","path":"checkpoint.ts"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"# Running multiple agents on this plan without collisions\n\nThese rules apply to every agent (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Nexus itself, or a human) that implements any part of this package at the same time as another. The repository's root `AGENTS.md` points here. The rules come from incidents recorded in `tasks/lessons.md`:\n\n- a concurrent agent overwrote newer evidence;\n- full test suites were contaminated by edits made mid-run;\n- `pkill -f` killed the agent's own shell;\n- HEAD moved during a pause.\n\nThey also follow from audit finding PER-03: the test suite writes into the real `~/.nexus`.\n\n## 1. Unit of work: one claimed PR slice per agent\n\n- The unit of concurrent work is **one PR slice** from a plan, for example `PLAN-01/PR-1a`. Every slice lists its tasks and its safe change boundary in its plan.\n- An agent works on exactly one claimed slice at a time.\n- An agent must not edit files outside its slice's boundary. The exceptions are the ledger rows and the shared files covered by §4. If the work needs a file outside the boundary, the agent stops and records a **boundary request** (§6). It does not edit the file.\n\n## 2. Claiming a slice (atomic and machine-local)\n\nClaims live in the repository's shared git directory. They are visible to every worktree, and they are never committed.\n\n```sh\nCLAIMS=\"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims\"\nmkdir -p \"$CLAIMS\"\nSLICE=\"PLAN-01_PR-1a\"\nif mkdir \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\" 2>/dev/null; then          # mkdir is atomic: exactly one agent wins\n  printf '{\"agent\":\"%s\",\"branch\":\"%s\",\"since\":\"%s\",\"pid\":%s}\\n' \\\n    \"$AGENT_NAME\" \"v1/plan-01-pr-1a\" \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ)\" \"$$\" > \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\"\nelse\n  echo \"claimed by: $(cat \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\")\"; exit 1\nfi\n```\n\n- **Release** the claim by deleting its directory (`rm -r \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\"`) after the slice merges or is abandoned. Write one line about the outcome to `$CLAIMS/../nexus-claims.log`.\n- **Hot-file claims** use the same mechanism with the name `FILE_<path with / replaced by _>`, for example `FILE_cli_src_agent.ts`. See §4.\n- **Stale claims.** A claim older than 24 h whose PID is gone may be broken, but only by the owner, or by an agent that first records the broken claim in the log.\n- If the MCP Agent Mail server is available, its file reservations (`file_reservation_paths`) may be used as well. The git-common-dir claim stays authoritative, because every agent can see it without extra tooling.\n\n## 3. Isolation: worktree, branch, HOME, ports, processes\n\n| Resource | Rule |\n|---|---|\n| Source | One `git worktree` per claimed slice: `git worktree add ../nexus-wt/<slice> -b v1/<plan>-<slice> origin/main`. Never edit `~/nexus-code` itself. It is the owner's checkout, and `/usr/local/bin/nexus` runs from it. |\n| Branch | `v1/plan-NN-pr-Nx`. One branch per slice. Never commit to `main` directly. |\n| HOME and state | Until PLAN-08 PR-8a lands, every test, build and probe run sets `HOME=$(mktemp -d)` and `XDG_CONFIG_HOME=\"$HOME/.config\"`. After PR-8a, the test setup enforces this, but scripts and probes outside `npm test` must still set it. **Never** run anything that writes to the real `~/.nexus` or `~/.config/nexus`. |\n| Test runs | Full suites run on a **snapshot copy** of the worktree (`git worktree add` at the commit under test, or `git archive`), never on the tree being edited. `tsx` reads `src/` live. |\n| Builds | Each worktree builds into its own `core/target`, and `cli/dist` is per worktree. To share the Rust build cache, set `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` per worktree, never to one shared directory. |\n| Ports | Mock servers bind `127.0.0.1:0` (an ephemeral port) and publish the chosen port to a file. Fixed ports are forbidden. |\n| Processes | Kill only PIDs you started, taken from `$!` or `ps -eo pid,args \\| grep -v grep`. **Never `pkill -f` or `killall`.** Long background jobs are stopped through the agent's own task controls. |\n| Full test suites | The PTY and provider tests are timing-sensitive. Take the claim `SUITE` before running a full suite (`make test`, or `npm test` over all files). While anyone holds `SUITE`, nobody runs other suites or targeted test files on the same machine. Concurrent load caused a false failure on 2026-10-15: `cloud_providers` saw an extra provider request after a load-induced timeout. Release the claim when the run ends. |\n| Inference | There is one inference host (DEC-16). Any run that uses the gateway takes the claim `GATEWAY` first. That includes eval runs, live checks and stripped-proxy runs. One gateway run at a time, which keeps eval timings valid and prevents overload. Small cloud checks (E5) take `CLOUD` to avoid duplicate spend. |\n| Credentials | Agents never read or copy `~/.config/nexus/credentials.json`, `config.env` values, or gateway tokens. The stripped proxy reads the token file itself. |\n\n## 4. Hot files: serialise, do not merge blindly\n\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:18:## 2. Claiming a slice (atomic and machine-local)\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:23:CLAIMS=\"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims\"\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:26:if mkdir \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\" 2>/dev/null; then          # mkdir is atomic: exactly one agent wins\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:28:    \"$AGENT_NAME\" \"v1/plan-01-pr-1a\" \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ)\" \"$$\" > \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\"\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:30:  echo \"claimed by: $(cat \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\")\"; exit 1\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:34:- **Release** the claim by deleting its directory (`rm -r \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\"`) after the slice merges or is abandoned. Write one line about the outcome to `$CLAIMS/../nexus-claims.log`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:95:| Claims | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/` | Who owns which slice or file right now |\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:96:| Claim log | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims.log` (append-only, one line per event) | Claim, release, broken claim, boundary request |\n159:        throw new Error(\"Checkpoint could not verify protected Git state; no checkpoint was written\");\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":161033523}},"started_at_ms":1792937391020,"completed_at_ms":1792937392181}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T14:09:53.382Z","ordinal":341542,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a17365-7ce5-74e3-b829-f04a8b0b2311","call_id":"call_062de0fbaaaa49b7bc993e5f25cdc495","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.5 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 1506)\nTotal output lines: 64\n\n# Running multiple agents on this plan without collisions\n\nThese rules apply to every agent (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Nexus itself, or a human) that implements any part of this package at the same time as another. The repository's root `AGENTS.md` points here. The rules come from incidents recorded in `tasks/lessons.md`:\n\n- a concurrent agent overwrote newer evidence;\n- full test suites were contaminated by edits made mid-run;\n- `pkill -f` killed the agent's own shell;\n- HEAD moved during a pause.\n\nThey also follow from audit finding PER-03: the test suite writes into the real `~/.nexus`.\n\n## 1. Unit of work: one claimed PR slice per agent\n\n- The unit of concurrent work is **one PR slice** from a plan, for example `PLAN-01/PR-1a`. Every slice lists its tasks and its safe change boundary in its plan.\n- An agent works on exactly one claimed slice at a time.\n- An agent must not edit files outside its slice's boundary. The exceptions are the ledger rows and the shared files covered by §4. If the work needs a file outside the boundary, the agent stops and records a **boundary request** (§6). It does not edit the file.\n\n## 2. Claiming a slice (atomic and machine-local)\n\nClaims live in the repository's shared git directory. They are visible to every worktree, and they are never committed.\n\n```sh\nCLAIMS=\"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims\"\nmkdir -p \"$CLAIMS\"\nSLICE=\"PLAN-01_PR-1a\"\nif mkdir \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\" 2>/dev/null; then          # mkdir is atomic: exactly one agent wins\n  printf '{\"agent\":\"%s\",\"branch\":\"%s\",\"since\":\"%s\",\"pid\":%s}\\n' \\\n    \"$AGENT_NAME\" \"v1/plan-01-pr-1a\" \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ)\" \"$$\" > \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\"\nelse\n  echo \"claimed by: $(cat \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\")\"; exit 1\nfi\n```\n\n- **Release** the claim by deleting its directory (`rm -r \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\"`) after the slice merges or is abandoned. Write one line about the outcome to `$CLAIMS/../nexus-claims.log`.\n- **Hot-file claims** use the same mechanism with the name `FILE_<path with / replaced by _>`, for example `FILE_cli_src_agent.ts`. See §4.\n- **Stale claims.** A claim older than 24 h whose PID is gone may be broken, but only by the owner, or by an agent that first records the broken claim in the log.\n- If the MCP Agent Mail server is available, its file reservations (`file_reservation_paths`) may be used as well. The git-common-dir claim stays authoritative, because every agent can see it without extra tooling.\n\n## 3. Isolation: worktree, branch, HOME, ports, processes\n\n| Resource | Rule |\n|---|---|\n| Source | One `git worktree` per claimed slice: `git worktree add ../nexus-wt/<slice> -b v1/<plan>-<slice> origin/main`. Never edit `~/nexus-code` itself. It is the owner's checkout, and `/usr/local/bin/nexus` runs from it. |\n| Branch | `v1/plan-NN-pr-Nx`. One br…106 tokens truncated…hot copy** of the worktree (`git worktree add` at the commit under test, or `git archive`), never on the tree being edited. `tsx` reads `src/` live. |\n| Builds | Each worktree builds into its own `core/target`, and `cli/dist` is per worktree. To share the Rust build cache, set `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` per worktree, never to one shared directory. |\n| Ports | Mock servers bind `127.0.0.1:0` (an ephemeral port) and publish the chosen port to a file. Fixed ports are forbidden. |\n| Processes | Kill only PIDs you started, taken from `$!` or `ps -eo pid,args \\| grep -v grep`. **Never `pkill -f` or `killall`.** Long background jobs are stopped through the agent's own task controls. |\n| Full test suites | The PTY and provider tests are timing-sensitive. Take the claim `SUITE` before running a full suite (`make test`, or `npm test` over all files). While anyone holds `SUITE`, nobody runs other suites or targeted test files on the same machine. Concurrent load caused a false failure on 2026-10-15: `cloud_providers` saw an extra provider request after a load-induced timeout. Release the claim when the run ends. |\n| Inference | There is one inference host (DEC-16). Any run that uses the gateway takes the claim `GATEWAY` first. That includes eval runs, live checks and stripped-proxy runs. One gateway run at a time, which keeps eval timings valid and prevents overload. Small cloud checks (E5) take `CLOUD` to avoid duplicate spend. |\n| Credentials | Agents never read or copy `~/.config/nexus/credentials.json`, `config.env` values, or gateway tokens. The stripped proxy reads the token file itself. |\n\n## 4. Hot files: serialise, do not merge blindly\n\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:18:## 2. Claiming a slice (atomic and machine-local)\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:23:CLAIMS=\"$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims\"\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:26:if mkdir \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\" 2>/dev/null; then          # mkdir is atomic: exactly one agent wins\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:28:    \"$AGENT_NAME\" \"v1/plan-01-pr-1a\" \"$(date -u +%FT%TZ)\" \"$$\" > \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\"\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:30:  echo \"claimed by: $(cat \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE/owner.json\")\"; exit 1\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:34:- **Release** the claim by deleting its directory (`rm -r \"$CLAIMS/$SLICE\"`) after the slice merges or is abandoned. Write one line about the outcome to `$CLAIMS/../nexus-claims.log`.\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:95:| Claims | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims/` | Who owns which slice or file right now |\ndocs/v1.0.0/CONCURRENCY.md:96:| Claim log | `$(git rev-parse --git-common-dir)/nexus-claims.log` (append-only, one line per event) | Claim, release, broken claim, boundary request |\n159:        throw new Error(\"Checkpoint could not verify protected Git state; no checkpoint was written\");\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17359-3515-7cd3-8706-e6bd2e3432cb","create_time":1792937393.3819194}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
