{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T14:19:10.553Z","ordinal":341969,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a1736d-fd59-7223-9ec6-6af4cfbde0e7","author":"/root/plan05_readonly_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/plan05_readonly_review\nPayload:\n**CHANGES_REQUIRED** — base/HEAD `b29f40b7b7a2d9c09f92e9111713633b1f5810d5`; uncommitted diff SHA-256 `6a09683e3dfeb00f949271b700c54c4643caf2ca6336208bb2bdf4998f13faab`.\n\nThe failed-checkpoint flow correctly pauses before starting the turn, preserves fail-closed checkpoint creation, and offers all five choices. The 40×14 regression also checks that the failure reason and choices fit.\n\nOne disclosure gap remains: for a generic checkpoint failure, [live_view.rs](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-protected-git/core/src/bin/nexus_tui/live_view.rs:242) strips the choice enumeration and displays only the failure reason, while option 3 is labeled “Create checkpoint anyway.” It omits that retrying allows sensitive persistence. The sidecar message does include that warning at [sidecar.ts](/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-protected-git/cli/src/sidecar.ts:558), but the TUI hides it. Keep a concise sensitive-persistence warning visible in this modal and assert it at 40×14. I did not edit files or run tests."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17359-3515-7cd3-8706-e6bd2e3432cb","create_time":1792937950.5531983}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":17028}}
