{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T14:19:52.315Z","ordinal":342002,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1736e-a07b-7052-bff8-9bd029280aaf","call_id":"call_4ab800fadaf54d65a20dd2d9ce777f11","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 1.3 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"[\"mcp__mcp_search__get_observations: Step 3: Fetch selected useful details for the IDs chosen after reviewing the index and timeline. Any shortening is marked. Params: ids (required), orderBy, limit, project (worker) or projectId (server). This tool is part of plugin `claude-mem`.\\n\\nexec tool declaration:\\n```ts\\ndeclare const tools: { mcp__mcp_search__get_observations(args: {\\n  // Array of selected observation IDs to fetch (string IDs in server runtime)\\n  ids: Array<number | string>;\\n  // Server project ID; defaults to the configured server project\\n  projectId?: string;\\n  [key: string]: unknown;\\n}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };\\n```\",\"mcp__mcp_search__search: Smart search (default), step 1: search memory for an index with IDs. Review it, use timeline for context, then get_observations only for selected IDs. Params: query, limit, project, platformSource, type, obs_type, dateStart, dateEnd, offset, orderBy. This tool is part of plugin `claude-mem`.\\n\\nexec tool declaration:\\n```ts\\ndeclare const tools: { mcp__mcp_search__search(args: {\\n  // End date filter (ISO)\\n  dateEnd?: string;\\n  // Start date filter (ISO)\\n  dateStart?: string;\\n  // Max results (default 20)\\n  limit?: number;\\n  // Filter observations by their type (e.g. bugfix, feature). Comma-separated for multiple.\\n  obs_type?: string;\\n  // Pagination offset\\n  offset?: number;\\n  // Sort order: dat\",\"mcp__mcp_search__timeline: Step 2: Get context around results. Params: anchor (observation ID) OR query (finds anchor automatically), depth_before, depth_after, project. This tool is part of plugin `claude-mem`.\\n\\nexec tool declaration:\\n```ts\\ndeclare const tools: { mcp__mcp_search__timeline(args: {\\n  // Observation ID to center the timeline around (string ID in server runtime)\\n  anchor?: number | string;\\n  // Items after anchor (default 3)\\n  depth_after?: number;\\n  // Items before anchor (default 3)\\n  depth_before?: number;\\n  // Worker project name\\n  project?: string;\\n  // Server project ID; defaults to the configured server project\\n  projectId?: string;\\n  // Query to find anchor automatically\\n  query?: string;\\n  [key:\",\"mcp__mcp_search__work_state_read: Read this project's to-do lists and working state written with work_state_write: every open item, or one list, with done and dropped items when includeClosed is true. Params: list, includeClosed. This tool is part of plugin `claude-mem`.\\n\\nexec tool declaration:\\n```ts\\ndeclare const tools: { mcp__mcp_search__work_state_read(args: {\\n  // Also show done and dropped items and closed lists\\n  includeClosed?: boolean;\\n  // Read only this list\\n  list?: string;\\n}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };\\n```\"]"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"- nexus-v1-release: pr133_ci=Node20/22/24 and CodeQL passed exact head; Linux packaging run 39665020828 active, pr133_head=6f522952bb50d956f259068b0a34151f614c956a, next=Wait exact PR #233 CI. If all pass, integrate through protected PR path, verify post-merge gates, prepare and publish a new RC because RC5 is immutable, then rerun cross-runner exact artifact reproduction., current_main=main advanced to ae69fe03b935006ccda12b7a28f49f610d064617, merge of PR #215. PR #215 exact CI40182316462 and CodeQL40182316289 passed; independent review ACCEPT exact c8d374a. Post-merge CI40184831801 and CodeQL40184831809 are in progress., sbom=PR134 merged as 049880f; exact PR CI39679493728 all4 SUCCESS, CodeQL39679493753 SUCCESS, focused SBOM closure tests 10/10 PASS, independent ACCEPT; post-merge main gates pass, active_claims=Release publishe