{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T14:36:15.455Z","ordinal":342666,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a1737d-a0df-7041-b537-4419981c248c","author":"/root/current_main_rc_path_audit","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/current_main_rc_path_audit\nPayload:\n**CHANGES_REQUIRED**\n\n- `install.sh:21` uses `${NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION:-auto}`, which treats an explicitly empty value as `auto`. But [SPEC-12:95](/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md:95) says other values are rejected, and the upgrade command rejects an empty value. Distinguish unset from empty in the installer and add a blank-value smoke case so malformed configuration fails closed.\n\nThe automatic fallback notices are visible in both installer and upgrade flows. Explicit `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=0` remains silent. The changes are compatible with the GitHub-installer-only release target; they do not add npm publishing behavior."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17359-3515-7cd3-8706-e6bd2e3432cb","create_time":1792938975.4552174}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":17062}}
