{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T14:36:15.464Z","ordinal":342668,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a1737d-a0e7-7353-8d8e-bfd0603f4655","author":"/root/t4_runner_independent_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/t4_runner_independent_review\nPayload:\nACCEPT for PR #234’s version synchronization and RC6 sequencing. The root, CLI, and Rust package versions are all `1.0.0-rc.6`, including their lockfile entries. The release note correctly describes RC6 as an unaccepted candidate whose qualification must use workflow-produced artifacts.\n\n**It is not ready to merge or tag yet:** PR #234 is open and blocked, has no reviews, and its Linux packaging check is still running. After exact-head checks and independent review, merge through the approved path; then require stable-main checks and completion of authorized critical fixes before tagging RC6. No tests, tags, or publication were performed."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17359-3515-7cd3-8706-e6bd2e3432cb","create_time":1792938975.463887}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":17063}}
