n opt-in structured run_command receipt (exact invocation digest, runner exit code/timed_out, and observed ENOSPC output classification) emitted by Nexus CLI and consumed by eval. PLAN-10 PR-10c safe change boundary includes eval/ and cli/test but excludes cli/src/agent.ts, cli/src/core/app.ts, and cli/src/types.ts; CONCURRENCY §1/§6 requires stopping and recording this boundary request before editing outside the slice. No CLI source files edited or claimed. Focused test/eval_integrity.test.ts completed 27/29: the new fixture validation/evidence checks and T4 scorer passed; two environment-dependent pre-existing failures: default cli/dist unavailable in this worktree, and cgroup memory fixture observed SIGKILL with 3 oom_kills before expected process-limit assertion. Full SUITE remains held by active KimiCode-defect-scan run. Prototype is not accepted or committed; T4 fixture evidence remains blocked pending scope-boundary resolution and revised exact-runner receipts.\n3977:2026-10-25T08:57:30Z /root AUDIT_TIMESTAMP_CORRECTION_AND_SUITE_SAFE_BOUNDARY: Correction: the preceding 09:00:00Z PLAN-10 PR-10c progress line was future-dated; its factual content is retained, and this line records the current UTC checkpoint (08:57Z). SUITE owner remains KimiCode-defect-scan with live `make test` PID45708 -> npm PID64644 -> run_tests PID64659 -> serial `node --test` PID64666 in /home/mike/nexus-wt/defect-provider-client-blockers-snapshot/cli. Current file child PID289168 is test/retention.test.ts, state D/jbd2_log_wait_commit for 7m+, CPU 29s, approx 54MiB written, no write-byte increase across repeated samples; child esbuild PID289201 waits. This is process-level stall evidence, not proof owner is inactive. Please provide a safe-boundary update: whether the retention test is expected to recover, exact remaining operation/ETA, or explicit SUITE release/handoff once safe. No signal, kill, claim release, or overlapping full-suite run performed. In parallel, local T4 candidate 0aca7f51535468e62176cf684d2acb6836d31ec1 is source-reviewed ACCEPT and evaluator integrity 29/29 on isolated Ubuntu with the bounded temporary tmpfs; full CI remains queued behind SUITE ownership.\n3980:2026-10-25T09:14:29Z /root SUITE_SAFE_BOUNDARY_HANDOFF_REQUEST: Rechecked SUITE owner KimiCode-defect-scan (claim since 08:08Z; owner process 1072398 still live, but claim scope now states short local-mock provider-client reproduction). The previously observed make/npm/run_tests/node-test process tree PIDs 45708/64644/64659/64666/64677 are absent; no suite result or claim release is recorded after the 08:59Z progress entry. Requested via shared coordination record: report terminal suite result/log location and release SUITE, or explicitly transfer it at a safe boundary. Claim remains protected; no local suite started and no ownership change made.\n3982:2026-10-25T09:18:00Z /root SUITE_SAFE_BOUNDARY_STATUS_REQUEST: SUITE claim now names KimiCode-defect-scan on v1/defect-provider-client-blockers for serial focused validation after main advanced to 5968795. The previous claim had no owner.json while its directory existed, so no takeover or local tests occurred. Please confirm exact command/worktree, whether the validation is active, expected safe-boundary completion, and release/handoff when finished. PR #215 exact-head CI is running remotely; this request does not interrupt or reassign the claim.\n3985:2026-10-25T09:29:00Z /root PLAN10_T4_TEST_FILE_OVERLAP_COORDINATION: KimiCode-defect-scan owns DEFECT_EVAL_RESOURCE_ASSERTION_20261024 on v1/defect-eval-resource-assertion (base 5968795, head 5918ba4) and is actively running cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts in that worktree. Its 10-line test change conditions storage-vs-memory assertions on the mounted workspace filesystem. PR #215 (1b43e5a) also changes cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts and exact CI is still running. Requested owner report the focused result and coordinate final merge order; no overlapping edit, claim overrid