{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T14:49:37.343Z","ordinal":343220,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17359-3515-7cd3-8706-e6bd2e3432cb","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-230bc81c-3cec-4247-8d24-7725781b6901","process_id":"17692","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh pr view 237 --json headRefOid,comments --jq '{headRefOid,comments:[.comments[-1]|{author:.author.login,body:.body,createdAt:.createdAt}]}'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-protected-git","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh pr view 237 --json headRefOid,comments --jq '{headRefOid,comments:[.comments[-1]|{author:.author.login,body:.body,createdAt:.createdAt}]}'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"{\"comments\":[{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Independent read-only review of exact head `37549f153ceccc7b8ccf5739b10590145b610f46` found two terminal injection paths still outside this PR's sanitizer. `cli/src/agent.ts:5356-5363` writes streamed model tokens directly with `process.stdout.write(token)`, so OSC/CSI sequences in a response (including hostile workspace/tool content echoed by the model) still reach the terminal. `cli/src/agent.ts:6112-6117` prints the user-controlled task prompt raw before inference. Please sanitize both at their output boundaries, audit adjacent direct output of untrusted workspace/model fields, and add regression tests for actual streamed tokens and prompt rendering. The PR's current sanitizer does not close these paths.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-25T14:49:09Z\"}],\"headRefOid\":\"37549f153ceccc7b8ccf5739b10590145b610f46\"}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":795091725}},"started_at_ms":1792939775547,"completed_at_ms":1792939777342}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T14:49:37.362Z","ordinal":343221,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17359-3515-7cd3-8706-e6bd2e3432cb","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-8d32838b-b87b-4607-9a3b-354ba7879c98","process_id":"38879","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh pr view 236 --json comments,reviews --jq '{reviews:[.reviews[]|{author:.author.login,state:.state,submittedAt:.submittedAt,body:.body}], comments:[.comments[-1]|{author:.author.login,body:.body,createdAt:.createdAt}]}'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-protected-git","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh pr view 236 --json comments,reviews --jq '{reviews:[.reviews[]|{author:.author.login,state:.state,submittedAt:.submittedAt,body:.body}], comments:[.comments[-1]|{author:.author.login,body:.body,createdAt:.createdAt}]}'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"{\"comments\":[{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Independent static review at current head `7b96408297959c0a6dcd1119ecc8f5770b8d150a`: the sensitive-persistence warning regression is corrected, but one release-blocking authority-reporting issue remains. In `cli/src/sidecar.ts`, the `without_checkpoint` branch clears `checkpointReadOnlyFallback` without calling `emitSessionState()` before `runTurn`. After an earlier read-only fallback, the TUI therefore continues to display read-only while the agent has already recovered configured review/auto authority. Please emit session state immediately after restoring the fallback flag, before the turn starts, and add a two-turn regression that checks both the immediate `session.state` event and restored tool authority. Tests were not run by this reviewer.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-25T14:49:26Z\"}],\"reviews\":[{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Independent review of exact head `7b96408297959c0a6dcd1119ecc8f5770b8d150a` against base `b29f40b7b7a2d9c09f92e9111713633b1f5810d5`. ACCEPT. The exact three-file diff matches the reviewed checkpoint-failure flow: checkpoint errors pause the turn, the 40x14 TUI keeps the reason, sensitive-persistence warning, and all five choices visible, and choosing sensitive retry emits a notice that the turn stays paused until success or another choice. Diff SHA-256: `faa620d34101319b4401cd22a8e6bbadd3f3ff38a3fd78236292325b495521c8`. Source review only; I did not run tests. This does not establish release acceptance.\",\"state\":\"COMMENTED\",\"submittedAt\":\"2026-10-25T14:47:16Z\"}]}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":553549230}},"started_at_ms":1792939775808,"completed_at_ms":1792939777362}}
