{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T14:52:25.244Z","ordinal":343384,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a1738c-6d1c-7e71-ad87-2da7fefdfc20","call_id":"call_faeebbecfff54af7931c399432c56929","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"mcp__codex_app__create_thread\nTools provided by the Codex app.\n\nCreate a separate task only when the user explicitly asks for a new task. The prompt appears as a user-visible message in the new task. Write clear, cohesive, human-readable prose. Use project for repository work, projectless for work without a repository, or chatgp\nmcp__codex_app__fork_thread\nTools provided by the Codex app.\n\nFork a Codex task, including a local Work task. Omit threadId to fork the calling Codex or local Work task. From a ChatGPT-backed cloud Work conversation, provide an explicit Codex threadId; this tool cannot fork ChatGPT conversations, even when they use a local exe\nmcp__codex_app__handoff_thread\nTools provided by the Codex app.\n\nMove another Codex thread and its associated git state between its checkout and Codex worktree on its current host. Running threads are interrupted before handoff. Omit destinationHostId for this current-host toggle. The calling thread cannot move itself, and cloud \nmcp__codex_app__send_message_to_thread\nTools provided by the Codex app.\n\nSend a follow-up prompt to an existing thread or chat only when the user explicitly authorizes messaging that task. Typed or spoken authorization counts. Authorization must come directly from the human user, either in this sending chat or via other trusted evidence."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17359-3515-7cd3-8706-e6bd2e3432cb","create_time":1792939945.2442217}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
