home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/archived/FILE_READINESS-node22-58df-20261022T222908Z\n/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/archived/FILE_cli_src_upgrade.ts.root-stale-2026-10-21T22:43:19Z.json\n/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/archived/FILE_core_src_runner.rs-merged-20261023T214913Z\n/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/archived/FILE_core_src_runner.rs-previous-claim-20261023T205749Z\n/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/archived/GATEWAY-E5-rc3-openrouter-complete-20261023T221357Z\n/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/archived/REDACTED.json\n/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/archived/PR171-merged-file-claims-20261023T220041Z\n/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/archived/SUITE-codex-root-PR173-20261023T205942Z\n/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/archived/SUITE-codex-root-PR173-review-followup-20261023T210222Z\n/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/archived/SUITE-node22-58df-20261022T222908Z\n/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/archived/SUITE-node22-build58-20261022T223017Z\n/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/archived/SUITE-root-node22-readiness-6of6-20261022T223534Z.json\n/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/archived/pr89-claude-code-20261020T220408Z\n/home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/archived/pr89-claude-egress-test-20261020T221728Z\n3914:2026-10-25T06:15:30Z RC5_NOTES_RECONCILED_LOCAL: Rebased existing RC5 notes branch onto exact main016bbc3. Added five summary bullets covering merged PR203-206 and208-211, including mandatory-by-default install provenance verification and explicit opt-out. Excluded PR207 because it remains open/unmerged. Commit8b7c09c; docs diff-check PASS; exact current diff SHA256 d737494a1d518a5108c307171fc3caf38ef82e5c836727fc7156a4f822264086. Earlier independent ACCEPT does not cover this new delta; fresh review pending. Docs-only, no tests. No push/tag/PR action. RC4 remains latest; custody and installed qualification/human acceptance gates remain blocked.\n3934:2026-10-25T06:52:00Z /root RELEASE_CHECKPOINT: Remote main remains 016bbc332d694b32072f6346e7f3127fb98b691f. PR207 exact head fb36b03: current diff resolves to six reviewed files; Node22/24 checks in progress, CodeQL and JS/TS pass; merge blocked pending checks/review. PR212 exact head 8b7c09c based on current main: Node22/24, CodeQL and JS/TS pass; Linux packaging in progress. KimiCode defect scan remains live (PID1072398, suite runner PID2726168, fifth READONLY_ADMISSION snapshot make test PID3792957/npm test PID3799744); no overlapping local suite started. Public metadata-only custodian follow-up posted to Issue #1 comment 6394571756 asking current owner, blackbox-v1 compatibility/replacement status, custody acceptance/run metadata timing; no protected payload requested or accessed. Latest public release remains v1.0.0-rc.4; no stable release or accepted RC.\n3937:2026-10-25T06:56:30Z /root VERIFIED_WAIT_PROGRESS: Kimi's READONLY_ADMISSION snapshot is still live and advanced from the PTY acceptance test to TUI surface test. Current chain is npm test3799744 -> Node runner3799780 -> tui_surface_driver3946767 -> nexus-tui3946768 -> sidecar3946771. The sequence is making progress; no interruption/restart or overlapping suite. PR207/212 checks remain nonterminal as last polled; custodian response has not changed.\n3940:2026-10-25T07:04:00Z /root LIVE_GATE_RECHECK: PR207 exact headfb36b03 Node22/24 still IN_PROGRESS (CodeQL and JS/TS SUCCESS); PR212 exact head8b7c09c Node22/24/CodeQL/JS-TS SUCCESS with Linux packaging job still IN_PROGRESS. GitHub says detailed logs unavailable until each job completes. The serialized Kimi suite process tree is absent; Kimi session1072398 remains active and SUITE claim still names KimiCode-defect-scan. Result/release safe-boundary request remains unanswered. Issue1 has no custodian reply after comment6394571756. No tests started by /root.\n3952:2026-10-25T07:24:54Z /root RC5_CONVERGENCE_RECHECK: Refreshed origin/main remains exact 05994a40c6e13bdaad9348fe62751220f7f53099; shared checkout remains dirty on local main db1ca55 and untouched. Exact main requirements gate was run in a clean detached worktree with isolated HOME: `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` exit 0, 123 rows (108 tested, 6 partial, 2 implemented, 7 open), 12 mapped to exact-RC qualification. Main CI40171717813: Node24 SUCCESS, Node22 running `npm --prefix cli test`; CodeQL40171717805 SUCCESS. PR213 exact head7a5d4dcc3d35c68caf8a93a3bdeb2d7141101153 remains based on 016bbc3; CodeQL and JS/TS SUCCESS, Node22/24 full suites still running; merge state BLOCKED. No refresh/push/merge while exact tests active. Kimi SUITE claim now names branch v1/defect-readonly-mode-admission since 07:16Z; active test process 4034329 and descendants in its dedicated worktree; no competing test started. Issue #1 has no custodian response after coordinator metadata request 6394571756; no protected payload accessed or qualification started. GitHub still lists only RC4 as newest prerelease; tags stop at v1.0.0-rc.4. Folder trust/default approval is already separated in current main and RC5 notes: unset mode defaults to review; no source change needed. Acceptance IN_PROGRESS; RC5 not yet tagged.\n3956:2026-10-25T07:35:00Z /root CLAIM PLAN-10_PR-10c: Claimed PLAN-10 PR-10c and hot files eval/run.mjs, eval/score.mjs, eval/validate.mjs, cli/test/eval_integrity.test.ts, eval/README.md at exact origin/main 05994a40c6e13bdaad9348fe62751220f7f53099. Scope is T4 coverage gap: currently only six model-proxy faults are represented/scored; implement bounded synthetic fixture and runner handling for the hanging-command, full-disk, and SIGTERM-resume classes, plus per-class scoring/evidence. No held-out task access, no live inference, no threshold changes. Worktree /home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4 on v1/plan-10-pr10c-t4-qualification. SUITE remains owned by Kimi; no tests until explicit release.\n3959:2026-10-25T08:42:00Z /root T4_SCORER_SYNTHETIC_CHECK: Exact eval/score.mjs content SHA-256 6bc38f96dbf3fe5ca165a4a5654671a1c9b84fba60dd424187272976556bc301 was copied to separate host ubuntu-desktop (Node v22.22.1), run against synthetic JSONL only, then removed. All assertions passed: nine classes/45 T4 records PASS; six-class partial set FAIL; wrong source for sigterm_resume yields invalidEvents=1 and FAIL; T2 injected-fault metadata contributes zero qualification runs. No Nexus process, model, held-out task, or qualification run. This does not replace the pending repository test suite or implementation of T4 runner faults.\n3963:2026-10-25T09:02:00Z /root T4_TARGETED_TESTS_REMOTE: Separate host ubuntu-desktop, Node22.22.1. Snapshot source base 05994a40c6e13bdaad9348fe62751220f7f53099 plus exact 3-file working diff. T4 scoring test `test/eval_integrity.test.ts` pattern `T4 scoring requires all nine classes and five injected runs per class`: 1/1 PASS. `test/eval_harness.test.ts` pattern `T4 smoke:`: 2/2 PASS. Fresh HOME/XDG used and removed. Harness core sourced from successful exact-main CI40171717813 package artifact 12591611369; tarball SHA256 d1b201295de970e88283e297cbef93c486e13c230e3e5a5befe5a0dc46922527, harness-core SHA256 1f42db93163d50daf2cd2816db9c0e9adb674a4733c93def40d0ce57f4d8e320 verified identical after transfer. Host test workspace remains isolated under /home/mike/nexus-t4-validation-work/snapshot; no shared checkout changes, held-out data, or inference. These are targeted source tests only, not T4 qualification.\n3964:2026-10-25T09:08:00Z /root T4_SCORER_AND_SMOKE_TESTS_PASS: The T4 scorer integrity case passed 1/1 and the two T4 smoke cases passed 2/2 on ubuntu-desktop using a snapshot of exact base 05994a4 plus only this claimed slice diff. Source test runner used a fresh isolated HOME/XDG and the exact-main CI package harness-core; no inference or held-out data. An initial attempt under /tmp was correctly refused by the harness protected-runtime-root policy and is recorded as an environment-path setup failure; relocating the disposable snapshot under /home/mike allowed the tests to run. Local Kimi SUITE remains active; no local tests were started.\n3966:2026-10-25T08:11:59Z codex-root PLAN-10_PR-10c progress: added cgroup-supervisor FD control channel for graceful SIGTERM delivery to every payload pid with bounded forced cleanup; added host fixture proving handler writes its state marker before supervisor cleanup; run-agent signals only after first model response and restarts Nexus with --resume; scorer rejects runner-fault labels lacking runner evidence; task validation accepts sigterm_resume only on T4; corrected memory enforcement fixture to allocate tmpfs-backed pages (instead of output-limited tail). Separate ubuntu-desktop targeted checks: T4 scoring + task validation + graceful signal 3/3 PASS; T4 proxy smoke 2/2 PASS. Broader resource-contract check confirmed memory OOM and process-count enforcement, then failed at workspace-storage assertion because this host uses shared /dev/shm rather than required dedicated size-capped tmpfs; recorded as environment prerequisite, not pass. No held-out tasks/inference. Exact source base 05994a40c6e13bdaad9348fe62751220f7f53099; independent review pending.\n3967:2026-10-25T09:12:00Z /root PLAN-10_PR-10c_FOLLOWUP_FIXES: Addressed independent T4 review findings in claimed worktree /home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4, branch v1/plan-10-pr10c-t4-qualification, exact base 05994a40c6e13bdaad9348fe62751220f7f53099. Scorer now requires delivered SIGTERM during an active inference turn, first process exit by SIGTERM, resume exit 0, and resulting turn COMPLETED; runner records these observations rather than unconditional resumed=true. Supervisor defers cgroup cleanup/escalation until SIGTERM grace elapses even when main child exits, allowing descendants to flush. Added regressions for missing resume evidence/inactive signal and descendant flush. On ubuntu-desktop isolated snapshot with fresh HOME/XDG: T4 scorer+supervisor focused patterns 2/2 PASS; T4 smoke patterns 2/2 PASS; diff-check PASS. No inference, held-out task, or full suite. Independent read-only re-review requested; no commit/PR until disposition.\n3968:2026-10-25T09:18:00Z /root PLAN-10_PR-10c_WRAPPER_SIGNAL_FIX: Follow-up independent review identified that child.close observes the systemd-run wrapper, while the contained supervisor reports the actual payload signal. Replaced scorer input with payloadExitSignal sourced from containment.final.signal; recorded supervisorWrapperExitSignal separately for diagnosis. Added regression rejecting wrapper-only SIGTERM. Exact branch base remains 05994a40c6e13bdaad9348fe62751220f7f53099; diff-check clean. Ubuntu desktop isolated HOME/XDG targeted T4 scorer and descendant-grace cases PASS 2/2 after correction. Fresh independent read-only re-review requested; no commit/PR, qualification, inference, or held-out access.\n3969:2026-10-25T08:29:25Z /root PLAN10_PR10c_T4_FIXTURE_EVIDENCE: Expanded claimed T4 runner slice in /home/mike/nexus-wt/plan10-pr10c-t4 from base 05994a40c6e13bdaad9348fe62751220f7f53099. Added eval/t4_fixtures.mjs to validate public task metadata and derive hanging-test/full-disk evidence only from a matching exact Nexus run_command transcript, observed timeout/ENOSPC result, and outer cgroup cleanup with zero survivors; full-disk storage cap must match the configured resource contract. Wired evidence into run records/scorer and documented schema; added synthetic integrity and validation regressions. Node syntax checks and diff-check pass. No behavioral tests run because KimiCode-defect-scan currently owns SUITE and is actively running make test in defect-provider-client-blockers-snapshot. Fresh read-only independent review requested from t4_runner_independent_review. No qualification, inference, held-out access, push, or PR.\n3972:2026-10-25T09:20:00Z /root PLAN10_PR10c_BOUNDARY_APPROVED: Approved narrow boundary extension after reviewer showed TaskExecutionResult omits tool messages and