{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T14:57:58.007Z","ordinal":343692,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a17391-80f7-7a50-ac41-51337a4f3c30","call_id":"call_07336a59e9624ba2b286e6352c030867","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/current_main_rc_path_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**CHANGES_REQUIRED**\\n\\n- Model output still bypasses the sanitizer: [agent.ts:5356-5363](/home/mike/nexus-code/cli/src/agent.ts:5356) writes streamed model tokens directly to stdout. A response containing OSC or CSI sequences can still control the terminal without passing through `TerminalUI.safeTerminal`.\\n- [agent.ts:6112-6117](/home/mike/nexus-code/cli/src/agent.ts:6112) also prints the user-supplied task prompt directly. A prompt containing terminal controls can inject sequences before inference begins.\\n\\nSanitize both output paths and add coverage for streamed model output and prompt rendering. The new `TerminalUI` boundary covers its listed methods, but it does not close these direct-write paths.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/plan05_readonly_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"**ACCEPT** — PR #236 exact HEAD `58597d6b10648633ce451e799bec57e8c9988f86`, base `b29f40b7b7a2d9c09f92e9111713633b1f5810d5`; diff SHA-256 `012e247608dccc1e44c93ce049ef6deb48a3fe155a1d981f71f4b899117448ad`.\\n\\nThe sidecar restores the approval mode and emits updated session state synchronously before setting the turn ready to proceed. The two-turn regression verifies that the next model call sees `auto`, that the state event precedes the write-tool start, and that the write completes. Source review only; I did not run tests.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/t4_runner_independent_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Submitted the formal `COMMENT` review on PR #234, anchored to `403d6de657542a50cdbcfe714751870835505888`. It records the independent ACCEPT for the version-sync and sequencing content,