{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T14:59:09.943Z","ordinal":343764,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a17392-99f7-7942-871f-379f45c7bb4f","author":"/root/plan05_readonly_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/plan05_readonly_review\nPayload:\n**ACCEPT** — reviewed PR #236 at exact head `364577620caf1756c984699acf2a1608514d492f` against base `3a4dbf1d0aca3d1689799cb703a40cf8f3bcc3ab`. Diff SHA-256: `21d494e084fc41595fe07d0350c4406453a54a189b31f5a492fd5bc0eed17f76`.\n\nGeneric checkpoint failures offer `retry` but exclude `allow_sensitive`; sensitivity-blocked failures offer `allow_sensitive` but exclude `retry` ([sidecar.ts](/home/mike/nexus-code/cli/src/sidecar.ts:559), [sidecar.ts](/home/mike/nexus-code/cli/src/sidecar.ts:702)). The TUI displays and maps those options consistently ([live_view.rs](/home/mike/nexus-code/core/src/bin/nexus_tui/live_view.rs:229), [live_state.rs](/home/mike/nexus-code/core/src/bin/nexus_tui/live_state.rs:1620)). The regression verifies an unavailable sensitive-consent choice is rejected, leaves the turn paused, and a normal retry does not opt into sensitive persistence ([sidecar.test.ts](/home/mike/nexus-code/cli/test/sidecar.test.ts:565)).\n\nAfter explicit sensitive-persistence consent, a later generic retry preserves that already-granted setting, as its notice says. I did not run tests."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17359-3515-7cd3-8706-e6bd2e3432cb","create_time":1792940349.9431298}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":17100}}
