{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T15:01:24.336Z","ordinal":343897,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17359-3515-7cd3-8706-e6bd2e3432cb","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-d182d556-8b2f-48fb-a390-dbd1a2b4c817","process_id":"43743","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","rg -n 'STAGNATION_DETECTED|stagnation|unchanged workspace|recovery note|unchanged result' /home/mike/nexus-code/cli/src /home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-protected-git/cli/src /home/mike/nexus-code/docs | head -120"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"search","cmd":"rg -n 'STAGNATION_DETECTED|stagnation|unchanged workspace|recovery note|unchanged result' /home/mike/nexus-code/cli/src /home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-protected-git/cli/src /home/mike/nexus-code/docs","query":"STAGNATION_DETECTED|stagnation|unchanged workspace|recovery note|unchanged result","path":"cli"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/USER_MANUAL.md:166:of progress (`--stagnation-steps`, default 12 consecutive steps without progress, or a repeated action on an unchanged\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/USER_MANUAL.md:167:workspace after two recovery notes), an actionable failure, or a limit **you** set (`--max-total-steps`,\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY.md:22:| no progress for `--stagnation-steps` consecutive steps (default 12) | `STAGNATION_DETECTED` |\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY.md:23:| the same action gives the same result on an unchanged workspace after two recovery notes | `STAGNATION_DETECTED` |\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY.md:87:  a recovery note; after two notes the turn stops with the loop cited.\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY.md:90:- **Polling**: an external command (`run_command`, network tools) returning the same result on an unchanged workspace\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY.md:93:  changes ends the turn through the stagnation threshold.\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY.md:101:  unchanged workspace.\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY.md:103:The stagnation threshold (12) counts consecutive steps without progress. Any progressing step resets it, so it does\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY.md:115:- recovery notes and backoff waits;\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY.md:250:| Turn loop: state identity per step, backoff, recovery notes, stops | `cli/src/agent.ts` `runTurn`, `workspaceStateIdentity`, `runSubagent` |\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY.md:270:two occurrences of a loop could lose the first one; the stagnation threshold still bounds that case.\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/research/context-engineering/DISPOSITION-2026-10-04.md:17:| Evidence-based stagnation detection | Retain as candidate |\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/research/context-engineering/DOGFOOD-CONTEXT-FORENSICS.md:141:3. Nexus had no signal for the stagnant 18-step loop other than the step count: the same refusal text appeared three times with no change in evidence. (OBSERVED.) Crush's repeated-interaction detector would have fired on identical (tool, args, output) signatures within a 10-step window; the *model's* narrow variations (different echo strings) would have evaded a naive version, which is an argument for evidence-based, not text-based, stagnation signals.\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/reviews/NEXUS_APPLICATION_MATURITY_REVIEW_2026-10-12.md:65:The provider assessment records token usage as estimated in some paths and no cost/spending controls. Session export explains that prompt totals sum input tokens for every request and repeated context retransmission drives cumulative usage (`cli/src/session_export.ts:86–88`). This makes accounting clarity and resource bounds important even where continuation/stagnation budgets exist.\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/research/context-engineering/CONTEXT-ENGINEERING-VALIDATION-PLAN.md:44:| H9 | Context management distinguishes progress from stagnation better than a step counter | on labelled traces (recorded stagnant 18-step loop; synthetic slow-progress traces) the evidence-based detector has precision <0.9 or recall <0.9, or is not better than count-only | 1 |\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-04-continuity-and-durable-work.md:17:- state-aware stagnation detection;\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-04-continuity-and-durable-work.md:40:- c. `ExecutionTracker.fresh()` runs every turn, so loop and stagnation history resets on every resume.\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-04-continuity-and-durable-work.md:54:| AGT-09 | Once state identity is \"unknown\" (more than 1.5 s on a large repo, `agent.ts:2026-2047`), ≥12 consecutive successful writes count as no progress, which gives a false STAGNATION_DETECTED (INFERENCE). |\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-04-continuity-and-durable-work.md:66:3. **REQ-AGT-103.** Durable work units persist execution tracking (loops, stagnation, cumulative steps) and their change baseline across resume.\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-04-continuity-and-durable-work.md:147:| ACC-CONT-04 | Resume a unit after two identical loops. A third repetition triggers the recovery note, not a fresh count. |\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-04-continuity-and-durable-work.md:152:| ACC-CONT-09 | Unknown state identity + 14 distinct writes gives no STAGNATION_DETECTED. 13 identical writes do stagnate. |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-protected-git/cli/src/sidecar.ts:500:            : `The agent repeated ${toolName(detail)} with an unchanged result: Nexus told it to change approach (${n} of ${max}).`;\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-protected-git/cli/src/sidecar.ts:1065:    .option(\"--stagnation-steps <number>\", \"Continuation: stop after this many steps without progress (default 12)\")\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/research/context-engineering/PRIOR-ART-CONTEXT-MANAGEMENT.md:32:- **Loop detection** (`loop_detection.go`): SHA-256 over (tool name, input, **output**) per step; stop if any signature occurs **>5 times in a window of 10 steps**. A stagnation signal based on *interaction identity*, not on step count.\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/research/context-engineering/PRIOR-ART-CONTEXT-MANAGEMENT.md:76:4. **Interaction-signature stagnation detector** (Crush) — informs H9; its naive form is text-fragile.\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/reviews/2026-10-13-compaction-continuity-acceptance.md:69:| Persist repetition, stagnation, failed approaches, interventions, progress evidence across compaction, follow-up and restart | `ExecutionTracking` in the ledger, persisted with task state and session | unit \"ledger carries tracking\"; integration follow-up and restart tests; live run 3 tracking dump | Met | — |\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/reviews/2026-10-13-compaction-continuity-acceptance.md:72:| Continue while progressing; stop on completion, cancel, no progress or failure; cosmetic changes are not progress | `evaluateStep` (new state / new info / new ledger state / operator input). Plan edits, identical rewrites, reverts and timestamps excluded. | unit \"progress\"; \"rewriting identical content … stagnation\" | Met | An agent can still manufacture \"new information\" by running new trivial commands; the stagnation threshold does not catch that |\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/reviews/2026-10-13-compaction-continuity-acceptance.md:73:| Use existing recovery policies; explain thresholds | Repetition threshold 3 (existing), `maxRecoveries` 2 (existing), stagnation 12 (existing), backoff 1–30 s; explained in docs | `docs/COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY.md` | Met | — |\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/reviews/2026-10-13-compaction-continuity-acceptance.md:74:| Bounded storage without hiding a loop | Recurring records are never evicted first; 16-hex seen-sets with eviction counts; recurrence after eviction still counted | unit \"bounded storage does not hide a loop\" | Met | A loop whose period exceeds 4,096 distinct observations could lose its first occurrence (stagnation still bounds it) |\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/reviews/2026-10-13-compaction-continuity-acceptance.md:83:| Polling and transient failures separate; justified backoff | `poll` verdict for external unchanged success; transient classifier; 1–30 s doubling backoff | \"unchanged poll waits with backoff\"; live run 3 interventions (run_tests waits) | Met | Polls end only through the stagnation threshold (about 4 min of backoff at the defaults) |\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/reviews/2026-10-13-compaction-continuity-acceptance.md:145:| 1 | earlier build of this branch (identity not captured) | 24,576 (operator) | `STAGNATION_DETECTED` at step 4 | **Defect found:** compaction truncated unseen file outputs, the model re-read them, and the re-reads were stopped as a loop. Fixed as re-acquisition. Also found: re-count per step when the operator limit was below capacity (fixed). |\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/v1.0.0/ROADMAP.md:28:| **M3 Continuity and inference** | PLAN-04 (resume, durable work units, accounting, error path, stagnation, team semantics); PLAN-05 code tasks (server-kind discovery, compact-and-retry, error bounds, timeouts, parser robustness, receipts, startup probe, decoupling, CA); PLAN-11 PR-11c..e; PLAN-10 harness tasks 1–7, 9, 10, 13 | Resume and compaction never lose state. Standalone sizing works. Eval harness ready. | **G3**: ACC-CONT-01..09, ACC-INF-01..09, ACC-VER-05..09, eval self-tests | 15–25 ed |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-protected-git/cli/src/config.ts:361:    stagnationSteps: Math.floor(positive(options.stagnationSteps, effectiveSetting(\"NEXUS_STAGNATION_STEPS\"), DEFAULT_CONTINUATION.stagnationSteps)),\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/reviews/NEXUS_CONTEXT_CONVERGENCE_REMEDIATION_2026-10-09.md:261:| Continuation | on by default (300 steps, 120 min, stagnation 12), completion nudges for open requirements | empty-reply continuation, closing notice | empty reply first, then nudges; notices count against `maxTotalSteps` |\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/reviews/NEXUS_CONTEXT_CONVERGENCE_REMEDIATION_2026-10-09.md:268:pinned to the established budget (`-s 120 --max-total-steps 120 --max-turn-minutes 420`); stagnation detection is\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/reviews/NEXUS_CONTEXT_CONVERGENCE_REMEDIATION_2026-10-09.md:381:- the stagnation recovery note becoming the last user message.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-protected-git/cli/src/doctor.ts:282:  { key: \"NEXUS_STAGNATION_STEPS\", flag: \"stagnationSteps\", field: (c) => (c.continuation ? String(c.continuation.stagnationSteps) : \"continuation off\"), fallback: \"12\" },\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-protected-git/cli/src/team.ts:26:/** Role turns segment at 15 steps (durable checkpoint boundary; continues until completion, stagnation or cancel unless --no-continuation is set). */\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:55:| REQ-AGT-001 | COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY §A; operator directive | No default cumulative step or time ceiling. Turns end on completion, cancel, demonstrated stagnation, actionable failure or an operator-set budget. Resource-safety valves (provider iterations, 10k scheduler transitions, 5 compaction attempts) are allowed and labelled. | `types.ts:127-133`; `agent.ts:4379-4445` | TEST + SRC (A §5) | tested | N | — | ACC-CONT-04, ACC-QUAL-T3 | K | SPEC-04 |\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:57:| REQ-AGT-003 | COMPACTION §B | State-aware repetition and stagnation (action/outcome/state identity; polls vs loops; compaction re-acquisition is not repetition). | `execution_tracking.ts` | TEST (ACC-CONT-09; test:cli/test/execution_tracking.test.ts) | tested | N | — | ACC-CONT-09 | K | SPEC-04 |\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/v1.0.0/REQUIREMENTS.md:162:| REQ-AGT-108 | Audit | No false stagnation when state identity is unknown. | workflow | `execution_tracking.ts` | TEST (ACC-CONT-09; test:cli/test/execution_tracking.test.ts) | tested | ACC-CONT-09 | RR | AGT-09 | SPEC-04 / PLAN-04 |\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/research/context-engineering/TURN-SPECIFIC-CONTEXT-ENGINEERING-HYPOTHESIS.md:39:| **A1** | **Bounded ingestion + evidence refs + dedup (simplest viable alternative)** | every tool result capped at ingestion (≈2–4k tokens projection); full raw stored durably under `evidence://<id>` (spill file/blob, redacted by the existing classifier); the transcript holds the projection + ref; identical results (same tool/args/output hash) replaced by a back-reference; an explicit `recall(ref, range|query)` tool; **pinned objective + operator constraints message that survives any view change**; stagnation detector on (tool, args, output-hash) | OpenCode truncate+spill, Crush spill+loop detector |\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/research/context-engineering/TURN-SPECIFIC-CONTEXT-ENGINEERING-HYPOTHESIS.md:134:## 9. Step limit and stagnation (H9)\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/research/context-engineering/TURN-SPECIFIC-CONTEXT-ENGINEERING-HYPOTHESIS.md:136:A hard step limit stays as an emergency breaker. A better primary signal is *evidence-based stagnation*: N consecutive steps with (a) no new evidence hash,\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/research/context-engineering/TURN-SPECIFIC-CONTEXT-ENGINEERING-HYPOTHESIS.md:138:(c)+(a) were true for 18 steps. Whether a step-count-free policy distinguishes slow legitimate progress from stagnation is the test.\n/home/mike/nexus-code/cli/src/sidecar.ts:453:            : `The agent repeated ${toolName(detail)} with an unchanged result: Nexus told it to change approach (${n} of ${max}).`;\n/home/mike/nexus-code/cli/src/sidecar.ts:911:    .option(\"--stagnation-steps <number>\", \"Continuation: stop after this many steps without progress (default 12)\")\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/research/context-engineering/DECISION-MEMO.md:22:**A1+E**: cap each tool result at ingestion with the raw stored durably behind a ref (through the existing redaction classifier), exact-duplicate back-references keyed by (tool,args,output-hash,repo fingerprint), a `recall(ref)` tool, view-level eviction of old results to ref stubs (store untouched), a pinned objective/constraint message, and an interaction-signature stagnation detector. Deterministic; no planner, no embeddings, no LLM summarisation.\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/research/context-engineering/CURRENT-NEXUS-CONTEXT-ARCHITECTURE.md:99:No deduplication or supersession anywhere. REPRODUCED in the dogfood session: `git_status` result returned twice (2,067 tokens each, exact duplicates), the oracle refusal text three times, repeated `echo` outputs; 2,336 est. tokens of exact-duplicate messages (the tail-of-run duplicates only; earlier equivalent-but-not-identical results such as re-reads are not counted). Three `task_completed` attempts met the same unchanged verifier failure (messages 33/43/47), followed by an attempt to \"bypass the verification\" with `echo`; Nexus has no loop/stagnation detector, only the step count.\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/reviews/NEXUS_MATURITY_FIXES_2026-10-11_REQUEST.md:24:Find every step-limit configuration and termination path. Remove the fixed 30-step cutoff as an unconditional task-ending rule; merely raising the number is insufficient. Preserve the unresolved objective, original requirements, plan, completed work, verification state, and next action across continuation and compaction. Continue automatically while making progress, without requiring “continue” from the user. Retain configurable resource budgets, cancellation, bounded recovery, and stagnation detection with clear termination reasons. Demonstrate a task exceeding 30 steps and a stuck task stopping boundedly.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-protected-git/cli/src/agent.ts:185:   * or `recovery` (it repeated an action with an unchanged result). `n` of `max` such prompts this turn.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-protected-git/cli/src/agent.ts:3468:          tracker.stagnation(tracker.data.cumulativeSteps, \"compaction_thrash\", \"pressure compaction found nothing to remove; further compaction waits until a request would not fit\");\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-protected-git/cli/src/agent.ts:3502:      tracker.stagnation(tracker.data.cumulativeSteps, \"compaction_thrash\", `${tracker.data.lowYieldCompactions} consecutive pressure compactions each freed under 5% of the window; further compaction waits until a request would not fit`);\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-protected-git/cli/src/agent.ts:5145:        if (budget && tracker.data.stepsWithoutProgress >= budget.stagnationSteps) {\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-protected-git/cli/src/agent.ts:5146:          stopReason = \"STAGNATION_DETECTED\";\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-protected-git/cli/src/agent.ts:5150:          tracker.stagnation(tracker.data.cumulativeSteps, \"no_progress\", stopDetail);\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-protected-git/cli/src/agent.ts:5206:          tracker.intervention(cumulativeStep, \"backoff\", `waited ${wait} ms before re-running ${prior.action} (${prior.outcomeClass === \"transient_failure\" ? \"transient failure\" : \"unchanged result\"} ×${prior.count} on an unchanged workspace)`);\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-protected-git/cli/src/agent.ts:5224:            tracker.stagnation(cumulativeStep, \"context_thrash\", `${verdict.record.action} re-read ${verdict.record.reacquired} times after compaction removed its output; the context window does not hold the working set`);\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-protected-git/cli/src/agent.ts:5232:            tracker.stagnation(cumulativeStep, \"repetition_state_unknown\", `${verdict.record.action} ×${verdict.record.count}: ${this.stateIdentityUncertainty ?? \"workspace state unknown\"}`);\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-protected-git/cli/src/agent.ts:5239:                `[Nexus] ${name} returned the same result ${verdict.record.count} times on an unchanged workspace` +\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-protected-git/cli/src/agent.ts:5247:          tracker.stagnation(cumulativeStep, \"repetition\", `${verdict.record.action} ×${count} with the same result on an unchanged workspace -> ${verdict.record.outcome.slice(0, 160)}`);\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-protected-git/cli/src/agent.ts:5255:              `[Nexus recovery ${recoveries}/${budget.maxRecoveries}] You have called ${name} with the same arguments ${count} times on an unchanged workspace and received the same result each time. ` +\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-protected-git/cli/src/agent.ts:5259:            stopReason = \"STAGNATION_DETECTED\";\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-protected-git/cli/src/agent.ts:5260:            stopDetail = `repeated ${name} ${count} times with an unchanged result on an unchanged workspace after ${budget.maxRecoveries} recovery notes`;\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-protected-git/cli/src/agent.ts:5261:            tracker.stagnation(cumulativeStep, \"repetition_stop\", stopDetail);\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-protected-git/cli/src/agent.ts:6099:      else if (turn.reason === \"STAGNATION_DETECTED\") nextAction = \"Review the repeated action and give the agent new direction (steer or a narrower request).\";\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-protected-git/cli/src/agent.ts:6208:   * and stops on its report, on the same repetition and stagnation rules as a turn, or when the parent's turn is\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-protected-git/cli/src/agent.ts:6210:   * stagnation and cancellation are reported as not completed. Durable autonomous work (/team, nexus operation) does\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-protected-git/cli/src/agent.ts:6229:    const stagnationSteps = this.config.continuation?.stagnationSteps ?? DEFAULT_CONTINUATION.stagnationSteps;\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-protected-git/cli/src/agent.ts:6242:      if (tracker.data.stepsWithoutProgress >= stagnationSteps) {\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-protected-git/cli/src/agent.ts:6350:            return { completed: false, summary: finalSummary, reason: `repeated ${toolName} ${verdict.record.count} times with an unchanged result on an unchanged workspace` };\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-protected-git/cli/src/agent.ts:6353:          note = `[Nexus recovery ${recoveries}/${maxRecoveries}] You have called ${toolName} with the same arguments ${verdict.record.count} times on an unchanged workspace and received the same result each time. Use the result you have or change approach; if you cannot proceed, report what you found.`;\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/releases/v0.1.0-alpha.2.md:16:- **State-aware repetition.** A repeated action is judged against the workspace state it ran on: an unchanged failing command on an unchanged workspace is a loop; polling backs off instead; plan edits are not progress. Tracking is persisted per objective and survives compaction, follow-up turns and restart.\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/v1.0.0/evidence/A2_verification.md:59:| VER-08 | S2 | `--tdd` / `/tdd` | synthesizer.ts:239-326; agent.ts:5236-5255 | SOURCE + INFERENCE. `runAutonomousTdd` never calls `verifyRedPhase` or `verifyGreenPhase`, ignores every `agent.run` result, and contains dead code (266-272). Success is only a full-suite exit 0, with no check that tests executed. Each `agent.run` calls `resetConversation()` (AGT-01), so GREEN starts with no memory of the RED test. The RED prompt asks the model to call `task_completed` with a deliberately failing test, but the completion oracle runs the discovered verifier, which fails → completion refused (INFERENCE). The success summary claims \"RED -> GREEN -> REFACTOR verified\". | The TDD mode advertises a protocol it does not enforce. RED turns likely end in NOT_ESTABLISHED or stagnation. | RELEASE-REQUIRED: enforce the phases (run the repro target and require fail, then pass), carry the conversation between phases, exempt the RED phase from the completion oracle; or mark the mode experimental. Add an e2e test with a mock model. |\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-protected-git/cli/src/core/turn.ts:44:  | \"STAGNATION_DETECTED\"\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-protected-git/cli/src/core/turn.ts:295:    /** Demonstrated loops: the same action and result on an unchanged workspace, at least REPEAT_THRESHOLD times. */\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-protected-git/cli/src/core/turn.ts:421:    if (t.reason === \"STAGNATION_DETECTED\") {\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-protected-git/cli/src/core/turn.ts:422:      return { heading: \"STOPPED - NO PROGRESS\", line: `execution=LIMIT_REACHED outcome=NOT_ESTABLISHED (STAGNATION_DETECTED${t.detail ? `: ${t.detail}` : \"\"}; ${t.steps.used} steps${segments})` };\n/home/mike/nexus-code/cli/src/config.ts:205:    stagnationSteps: Math.floor(positive(options.stagnationSteps, process.env.NEXUS_STAGNATION_STEPS, DEFAULT_CONTINUATION.stagnationSteps)),\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-protected-git/cli/src/types.ts:138:   * Consecutive steps without observed progress before the turn stops (STAGNATION_DETECTED). A repeated-state\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-protected-git/cli/src/types.ts:141:  stagnationSteps: number;\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-protected-git/cli/src/types.ts:151:  stagnationSteps: 12,\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-protected-git/cli/src/index.ts:297:  .option(\"--stagnation-steps <number>\", \"Continuation: stop after this many steps without progress (default 12)\")\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-protected-git/cli/src/index.ts:334:  .option(\"--stagnation-steps <number>\", \"Continuation: stop after this many steps without progress (default 12)\")\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-protected-git/cli/src/index.ts:375:  .option(\"--stagnation-steps <number>\", \"Continuation: stop after this many steps without progress (default 12)\")\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-protected-git/cli/src/core/operation_runner.ts:835:      // A continued unit stops only on a budget or on stagnation; say which, so the operator's choice is informed.\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-protected-git/cli/src/core/operation_runner.ts:837:        turn.reason === \"STAGNATION_DETECTED\"\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-protected-git/cli/src/core/operation_runner.ts:845:        reason: turn.reason === \"STAGNATION_DETECTED\" || turn.reason === \"TIME_BUDGET_EXHAUSTED\" ? `${turn.reason}: ${why}` : `step limit ${turn.steps.max} reached`,\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-protected-git/cli/src/core/execution_tracking.ts:107:  stagnation: TrackingEvent[];\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-protected-git/cli/src/core/execution_tracking.ts:128:    stagnation: [],\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-protected-git/cli/src/core/execution_tracking.ts:294:  /** Recurrence of an external action's unchanged result, or of a transient failure: waits, not a loop. */\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-protected-git/cli/src/core/execution_tracking.ts:448:  stagnation(step: number, kind: string, detail: string): void {\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-protected-git/cli/src/core/execution_tracking.ts:449:    this.event(this.data.stagnation, MAX_EVENTS, step, kind, detail);\n/home/mike/nexus-wt/checkpoint-protected-git/cli/src/core/objective.ts:592:      out.push(\"Repeated without progress on an unchanged workspace (do not repeat these; change approach):\");\n/home/mike/nexus-code/cli/src/core/turn.ts:43:  | \"STAGNATION_DETECTED\"\n/home/mike/nexus-code/cli/src/core/turn.ts:289:    /** Demonstrated loops: the same action and result on an unchanged workspace, at least REPEAT_THRESHOLD times. */\n/home/mike/nexus-code/cli/src/core/turn.ts:415:    if (t.reason === \"STAGNATION_DETECTED\") {\n/home/mike/nexus-code/cli/src/core/turn.ts:416:      return { heading: \"STOPPED - NO PROGRESS\", line: `execution=LIMIT_REACHED outcome=NOT_ESTABLISHED (STAGNATION_DETECTED${t.detail ? `: ${t.detail}` : \"\"}; ${t.steps.used} steps${segments})` };\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:45:- **No default step ceiling.** Turns end on completion, cancel, stagnation or failure.\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:251:| AGT-09 | S3 | RR | Large repos | `agent.ts:2026-2047` | INF | False stagnation | REQ-AGT-108 |\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/v1.0.0/AUDIT.md:353:- **No artificial step ceiling.** Evidence-based stagnation detection. Bounded provider recovery with a well-typed failure taxonomy. Evidence: A §5, B §5.\n/home/mike/nexus-code/cli/src/types.ts:117:   * Consecutive steps without observed progress before the turn stops (STAGNATION_DETECTED). A repeated-state\n/home/mike/nexus-code/cli/src/types.ts:120:  stagnationSteps: number;\n/home/mike/nexus-code/cli/src/types.ts:130:  stagnationSteps: 12,\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:31:- Stop conditions: `task_completed` success, FINAL_TEXT (after up to `maxCompletionNudges`=2 nudges while requirements are open), cancellation (AbortController; in-flight tool awaited), inference failure after recovery, context admission refusal (BLOCKED), persistence failure, stagnation (`stagnationSteps`=12 consecutive no-progress steps, or a repeated loop after `maxRecoveries`=2 notes), operator step/time budgets (default +Infinity, types.ts:127-133), `--no-continuation` (maxSteps, default 30, as a hard LIMIT_REACHED).\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:45:| AGT-02 | S2 | `/team`, `nexus operation run/resume` (work units) | agent.ts:3081 (`durableUnit = this.depth === 0`), 3127, 1136-1139, 4389, 1489-1501; operation_runner.ts:559 | SOURCE + DOC-CLAIM. Work units run as `new AutonomousAgent(config, 1)` and ARE durable (resumed via `recoverFromTaskState`), but every depth-gated rule treats depth 1 as a non-durable in-turn subagent: (a) compaction is applied in memory only — no archive append, no checkpoint, never `PERSISTENCE_FAILED`; the next `persistProgress` then writes the compacted conversation and a `committedCompactions` id that has no archive lines, so originals are lost and `read_archive` cannot return them after resume (contradicts COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY.md:145-160 \"Every compaction ... is committed in a fixed order\"); (b) no objective ledger: no requirement gating, no steering, `update_requirements`/`read_objective` not offered; (c) `ExecutionTracker.fresh()` per turn, so loop/stagnation history and cumulative steps reset at every resume/retry; (d) no change baseline / independence judgement (`captureChangeBaseline` depth 0 only, 4034) so discovered-verifier passes are at best REGRESSION_FREE. `runningAsSubagent` already distinguishes the two cases (5003). | Long team/operation units lose compaction originals and convergence history across resume; doc claims overstate durability. | Gate on `runningAsSubagent` (non-durable) instead of `depth`; add a work-unit compaction+resume test asserting archive lines exist. |\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:50:| AGT-07 | S3 | Team step bound (doc vs code) | team.ts:26-27,91; EXECUTION_CONVERGENCE.md:117-118; config.ts:189-205 | SOURCE + DOC-CLAIM. Doc says units are \"capped at 15 steps\". With default continuation (`maxTotalSteps=+Inf`) 15 is only a segment size; units run until completion/stagnation/cancel. Under `--no-continuation` it becomes a hard LIMIT_REACHED. Not an arbitrary ceiling in the default path (good), but doc is wrong and `ROLE_MAX_STEPS` comment (\"step bound the team has always used\") misleads. | Operators misjudge cost/duration of team runs. | Fix doc/comment. |\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:52:| AGT-09 | S3 | Stagnation false positive on large repos | agent.ts:2026-2047 (1.5 s budget), execution_tracking.ts observe()/evaluateStep() | INFERENCE. Once state identity exceeds 1.5 s it is \"unknown\" for the rest of the turn; then mutate-kind calls are never `informative` and \"new state\" cannot be shown, so a run of ≥12 steps that only write/edit files (e.g. generating many files) counts as no progress → `STAGNATION_DETECTED`. | Productive long edit sequences stopped on big monorepos. | Treat successful mutations with distinct args as progress when state is unknown; add test. |\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:94:| Large-repo stagnation false positive (AGT-09) | In a repo where `computeCandidateIdentitySync` > 1.5 s (or stub `workspaceStateIdentity` to \"unknown\"), script 14 consecutive distinct `write_file` steps; expect no STAGNATION_DETECTED. |\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:107:| AGT-R3 | Work units keep execution tracking (loops, stagnation, cumulative steps) across resume. | failure/convergence (AGT-02c) | RELEASE-REQUIRED | Resume a unit after 2 identical loops; third repetition triggers recovery note, not a fresh count. |\n/home/mike/nexus-code/cli/src/core/operation_runner.ts:691:      // A continued unit stops only on a budget or on stagnation; say which, so the operator's choice is informed.\n/home/mike/nexus-code/cli/src/core/operation_runner.ts:693:        turn.reason === \"STAGNATION_DETECTED\"\n/home/mike/nexus-code/cli/src/core/operation_runner.ts:701:        reason: turn.reason === \"STAGNATION_DETECTED\" || turn.reason === \"TIME_BUDGET_EXHAUSTED\" ? `${turn.reason}: ${why}` : `step limit ${turn.steps.max} reached`,\n/home/mike/nexus-code/cli/src/agent.ts:176:   * or `recovery` (it repeated an action with an unchanged result). `n` of `max` such prompts this turn.\n/home/mike/nexus-code/cli/src/agent.ts:3091:          tracker.stagnation(tracker.data.cumulativeSteps, \"compaction_thrash\", \"pressure compaction found nothing to remove; further compaction waits until a request would not fit\");\n/home/mike/nexus-code/cli/src/agent.ts:3125:      tracker.stagnation(tracker.data.cumulativeSteps, \"compaction_thrash\", `${tracker.data.lowYieldCompactions} consecutive pressure compactions each freed under 5% of the window; further compaction waits until a request would not fit`);\n/home/mike/nexus-code/cli/src/agent.ts:4416:        if (budget && tracker.data.stepsWithoutProgress >= budget.stagnationSteps) {\n/home/mike/nexus-code/cli/src/agent.ts:4417:          stopReason = \"STAGNATION_DETECTED\";\n/home/mike/nexus-code/cli/src/agent.ts:4421:          tracker.stagnation(tracker.data.cumulativeSteps, \"no_progress\", stopDetail);\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":26767}},"started_at_ms":1792940484335,"completed_at_ms":1792940484335}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T15:01:25.840Z","ordinal":343898,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a17394-accf-7ea3-bdb6-b00f05d2f317","call_id":"call_d847a5eb0942410d9af8736b08de3e8e","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.6 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Warning: truncated output (original token count: 7769)\nTotal output lines: 120\n\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/USER_MANUAL.md:166:of progress (`--stagnation-steps`, default 12 consecutive steps without progress, or a repeated action on an unchanged\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/USER_MANUAL.md:167:workspace after two recovery notes), an actionable failure, or a limit **you** set (`--max-total-steps`,\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY.md:22:| no progress for `--stagnation-steps` consecutive steps (default 12) | `STAGNATION_DETECTED` |\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY.md:23:| the same action gives the same result on an unchanged workspace after two recovery notes | `STAGNATION_DETECTED` |\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY.md:87:  a recovery note; after two notes the turn stops with the loop cited.\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY.md:90:- **Polling**: an external command (`run_command`, network tools) returning the same result on an unchanged workspace\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY.md:93:  changes ends the turn through the stagnation threshold.\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY.md:101:  unchanged workspace.\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY.md:103:The stagnation threshold (12) counts consecutive steps without progress. Any progressing step resets it, so it does\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY.md:115:- recovery notes and backoff waits;\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY.md:250:| Turn loop: state identity per step, backoff, recovery notes, stops | `cli/src/agent.ts` `runTurn`, `workspaceStateIdentity`, `runSubagent` |\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/COMPACTION_AND_CONTINUITY.md:270:two occurrences of a loop could lose the first one; the stagnation threshold still bounds that case.\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/research/context-engineering/DISPOSITION-2026-10-04.md:17:| Evidence-based stagnation detection | Retain as candidate |\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/research/context-engineering/DOGFOOD-CONTEXT-FORENSICS.md:141:3. Nexus had no signal for the stagnant 18-step loop other than the step count: the same refusal text appeared three times with no change in evidence. (OBSERVED.) Crush's repeated-interaction detector would have fired on identical (tool, args, output) signatures within a 10-step window; the *model's* narrow variations (different echo strings) would have evaded a naive version, which is an argument for evidence-based, not text-based, stagnation signals.\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/reviews/NEXUS_APPLICATION_MATURITY_REVIEW_2026-10-12.md:65:The provider assessment records token usage as estimated in some paths and no cost/spending controls. Session export explains that prompt totals sum input tokens for every request and repeated context retransmission drives cumulative usage (`cli/src/session_export.ts:86–88`). This makes accounting clarity and resource bounds important even where continuation/stagnation budgets exist.\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/research/contex…6269 tokens truncated…n arbitrary ceiling in the default path (good), but doc is wrong and `ROLE_MAX_STEPS` comment (\"step bound the team has always used\") misleads. | Operators misjudge cost/duration of team runs. | Fix doc/comment. |\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:52:| AGT-09 | S3 | Stagnation false positive on large repos | agent.ts:2026-2047 (1.5 s budget), execution_tracking.ts observe()/evaluateStep() | INFERENCE. Once state identity exceeds 1.5 s it is \"unknown\" for the rest of the turn; then mutate-kind calls are never `informative` and \"new state\" cannot be shown, so a run of ≥12 steps that only write/edit files (e.g. generating many files) counts as no progress → `STAGNATION_DETECTED`. | Productive long edit sequences stopped on big monorepos. | Treat successful mutations with distinct args as progress when state is unknown; add test. |\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:94:| Large-repo stagnation false positive (AGT-09) | In a repo where `computeCandidateIdentitySync` > 1.5 s (or stub `workspaceStateIdentity` to \"unknown\"), script 14 consecutive distinct `write_file` steps; expect no STAGNATION_DETECTED. |\n/home/mike/nexus-code/docs/v1.0.0/evidence/A_core_agent.md:107:| AGT-R3 | Work units keep execution tracking (loops, stagnation, cumulative steps) across resume. | failure/convergence (AGT-02c) | RELEASE-REQUIRED | Resume a unit after 2 identical loops; third repetition triggers recovery note, not a fresh count. |\n/home/mike/nexus-code/cli/src/core/operation_runner.ts:691:      // A continued unit stops only on a budget or on stagnation; say which, so the operator's choice is informed.\n/home/mike/nexus-code/cli/src/core/operation_runner.ts:693:        turn.reason === \"STAGNATION_DETECTED\"\n/home/mike/nexus-code/cli/src/core/operation_runner.ts:701:        reason: turn.reason === \"STAGNATION_DETECTED\" || turn.reason === \"TIME_BUDGET_EXHAUSTED\" ? `${turn.reason}: ${why}` : `step limit ${turn.steps.max} reached`,\n/home/mike/nexus-code/cli/src/agent.ts:176:   * or `recovery` (it repeated an action with an unchanged result). `n` of `max` such prompts this turn.\n/home/mike/nexus-code/cli/src/agent.ts:3091:          tracker.stagnation(tracker.data.cumulativeSteps, \"compaction_thrash\", \"pressure compaction found nothing to remove; further compaction waits until a request would not fit\");\n/home/mike/nexus-code/cli/src/agent.ts:3125:      tracker.stagnation(tracker.data.cumulativeSteps, \"compaction_thrash\", `${tracker.data.lowYieldCompactions} consecutive pressure compactions each freed under 5% of the window; further compaction waits until a request would not fit`);\n/home/mike/nexus-code/cli/src/agent.ts:4416:        if (budget && tracker.data.stepsWithoutProgress >= budget.stagnationSteps) {\n/home/mike/nexus-code/cli/src/agent.ts:4417:          stopReason = \"STAGNATION_DETECTED\";\n/home/mike/nexus-code/cli/src/agent.ts:4421:          tracker.stagnation(tracker.data.cumulativeSteps, \"no_progress\", stopDetail);\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17359-3515-7cd3-8706-e6bd2e3432cb","create_time":1792940485.8399296}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
