{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T15:03:28.837Z","ordinal":344000,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17359-3515-7cd3-8706-e6bd2e3432cb","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-78dff91b-1e41-4dae-a1b4-2cb288017d0a","process_id":"12773","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh pr view 235 --json title,body,author,headRefName,headRefOid,baseRefName,baseRefOid,commits,files,url,statusCheckRollup && cat /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/ATTESTATION_AUTO_DEFAULT_20261025/owner.json && gh pr diff 235 --stat && gh pr diff 235 | sed -n '1,260p'"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh pr view 235 --json title,body,author,headRefName,headRefOid,baseRefName,baseRefOid,commits,files,url,statusCheckRollup && cat /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/ATTESTATION_AUTO_DEFAULT_20261025/owner.json && gh pr diff 235 --stat && gh pr diff 235 | sed -n '1,260p'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"failed","aggregated_output":"{\"author\":{\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\",\"is_bot\":false,\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"Mike Holownych\"},\"baseRefName\":\"main\",\"baseRefOid\":\"b29f40b7b7a2d9c09f92e9111713633b1f5810d5\",\"body\":\"## Why\\n\\nThe owner chose the v1.0.0 provenance-attestation default directly with claude-code on 2026-10-25: **auto**. Verify when a trusted `gh` is present, report when verification is skipped, and fail closed only with `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1`.\\n\\nMain (and published rc.5) had diverged in two ways:\\n- `install.sh` became required-by-default (#211). A stock `curl … | sh` install refused to run without a logged-in `gh` at `/usr/bin` or `/usr/local/bin`.\\n- `nexus upgrade` (#210) defaulted to auto but skipped verification **silently**.\\n\\n#211 merged at 05:32Z, before the owner's answer reached the review lane at 14:11Z, so this is a correction, not a reversal of a decision.\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\n- **`install.sh`:** the default is `auto`, and `auto|0|1` are accepted. A notice goes to stderr when no trusted `gh` exists, or when it can't verify (for example because it isn't logged in). The SHA-256 check still runs. Trusted-path-only `gh` and the early failure under `=1` are unchanged.\\n- **`cli/src/upgrade.ts`:** unsupported values are rejected before staging. A skipped verification is reported through `onProgress(\\\"attestation_skipped\\\")` and appended to `restartNotice`, which the CLI, REPL `/upgrade` and TUI `/upgrade` all print already. That follows the existing `pathWarning` pattern, so no caller changes.\\n- **SPEC-12:** documents the setting values and the auto-mode reporting.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- `scripts/installer-smoke.sh` against the **published v1.0.0-rc.5 archive** (SHA-256 checked against its `SHA256SUMS`): `INSTALLER_SMOKE_PASS`. The new cases are: auto with no trusted `gh` installs and prints the notice (PATH shim not executed); `=1` with no trusted `gh` refuses; an invalid value is rejected; auto with a trusted `gh` that fails installs with the notice; `=1` with a failing `gh` refuses and installs nothing. **Against main's `install.sh`, the same smoke fails** with \\\"default auto mode refused to install without a trusted gh\\\".\\n- `upgrade_acceptance.test.ts`: 11/11 pass. **Against main's `upgrade.ts`, the three new tests fail**: auto reports the skip, auto reports a failing `gh`, and an unsupported value is rejected.\\n- `npx tsc --noEmit`: pass. `git diff --check`: pass.\\n- `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` at this exact commit, clean detached worktree, isolated HOME/XDG: exit 0, 108 tested / 6 partial / 2 implemented / 7 open.\\n\\nNeeds independent review by an agent other than claude-code. This is user-visible, so it needs an rc.6 notes bullet.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\",\"commits\":[{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-10-25T14:19:43Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"mike@holownych.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\",\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"Mike Holownych\"},{\"email\":\"noreply@anthropic.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3\",\"login\":\"claude\",\"name\":\"Claude Opus 5.5\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-10-25T14:19:43Z\",\"messageBody\":\"The owner chose auto as the v1.0.0 provenance default: verify with a trusted\\ngh when one exists, report when verification is skipped, and fail closed only\\nwhen NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1. The installer had become required-by-default,\\nwhich refused stock installs without a logged-in gh at /usr/bin or\\n/usr/local/bin, and upgrade skipped silently.\\n\\n- install.sh: default auto; accept auto|0|1; print a notice when no trusted gh\\n  exists or it cannot verify. Trusted-path-only gh and the early failure under\\n  =1 are unchanged.\\n- nexus upgrade: reject unsupported values before staging; report a skipped\\n  verification as progress and in the completion notice.\\n- Installer smoke and upgrade acceptance cover the auto, required, failing-gh\\n  and invalid-setting cases; the new cases fail against the previous sources.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"messageHeadline\":\"fix(release): verify provenance when possible by default\",\"oid\":\"5bdd788eed2098913b2b68844757cc0e63282a6a\"}],\"files\":[{\"path\":\"cli/src/upgrade.ts\",\"additions\":12,\"deletions\":1,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"cli/test/upgrade_acceptance.test.ts\",\"additions\":90,\"deletions\":0,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md\",\"additions\":5,\"deletions\":1,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"install.sh\",\"additions\":7,\"deletions\":3,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"scripts/installer-smoke.sh\",\"additions\":31,\"deletions\":5,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"}],\"headRefName\":\"v1/attestation-auto-default\",\"headRefOid\":\"5bdd788eed2098913b2b68844757cc0e63282a6a\",\"statusCheckRollup\":[{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"2026-10-25T14:37:14Z\",\"conclusion\":\"SUCCESS\",\"detailsUrl\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40201732816/job/121194150812\",\"name\":\"test-matrix (22)\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-10-25T14:20:06Z\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"workflowName\":\"CI\"},{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"2026-10-25T14:21:20Z\",\"conclusion\":\"SUCCESS\",\"detailsUrl\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40201732801/job/121194151028\",\"name\":\"javascript-typescript\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-10-25T14:20:06Z\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"workflowName\":\"CodeQL\"},{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"2026-10-25T14:33:29Z\",\"conclusion\":\"SUCCESS\",\"detailsUrl\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40201732816/job/121194151107\",\"name\":\"test-matrix (24)\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-10-25T14:20:06Z\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"workflowName\":\"CI\"},{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"2026-10-25T14:58:46Z\",\"conclusion\":\"SUCCESS\",\"detailsUrl\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40201732816/job/121198211790\",\"name\":\"linux-x86_64\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-10-25T14:37:16Z\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"workflowName\":\"CI\"},{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"2026-10-25T14:21:14Z\",\"conclusion\":\"SUCCESS\",\"detailsUrl\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/runs/121194420181\",\"name\":\"CodeQL\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-10-25T14:21:11Z\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"workflowName\":\"\"},{\"__typename\":\"StatusContext\",\"context\":\"CodeRabbit\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-10-25T14:20:10Z\",\"state\":\"SUCCESS\",\"targetUrl\":\"\"}],\"title\":\"fix(release): verify provenance when possible by default\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/235\"}\n{\n  \"agent\": \"claude-code\",\n  \"host\": \"mike-dev\",\n  \"branch\": \"v1/attestation-auto-default\",\n  \"worktree\": \"/home/mike/nexus-wt/attestation-auto-default\",\n  \"base\": \"b29f40b7b7a2d9c09f92e9111713633b1f5810d5\",\n  \"since\": \"2026-10-25T14:14:24Z\",\n  \"scope\": \"Owner decision 2026-10-25: provenance attestation default auto for install.sh and nexus upgrade; skip notice; =1 fail closed; =0 skip\"\n}\nunknown flag: --stat\n\nView changes in a pull request.\n\nWithout an argument, the pull request that belongs to the current branch\nis selected.\n\nWith `--web` flag, open the pull request diff in a web browser instead.\n\nUse `--exclude` to filter out files matching a glob pattern. The pattern\nuses forward slashes as path separators on all platforms. You can repeat\nthe flag to exclude multiple patterns.\n\nBy default, terminal escape sequences in the diff are neutralized, since\nthey could manipulate your terminal. Pass `--allow-escape-sequences` to\nprint the diff verbatim, for example when piping a patch to another program.\n\n\nUSAGE\n  gh pr diff [<number> | <url> | <branch>] [flags]\n\nFLAGS\n      --allow-escape-sequences   Allow printing terminal escape sequences\n      --color string             Use color in diff output: {always|never|auto} (default \"auto\")\n  -e, --exclude patterns         Exclude files matching glob patterns from the diff\n      --name-only                Display only names of changed files\n      --patch                    Display diff in patch format\n  -w, --web                      Open the pull request diff in the browser\n\nINHERITED FLAGS\n      --help                     Show help for command\n  -R, --repo [HOST/]OWNER/REPO   Select another repository using the [HOST/]OWNER/REPO format\n\nEXAMPLES\n  # See diff for current branch\n  $ gh pr diff\n  \n  # See diff for a specific PR\n  $ gh pr diff 123\n  \n  # Exclude files from diff output\n  $ gh pr diff --exclude '*.yml' --exclude 'generated/*'\n  \n  # Exclude matching files by name\n  $ gh pr diff --name-only --exclude '*.generated.*'\n\nLEARN MORE\n  Use `gh <command> <subcommand> --help` for more information about a command.\n  Read the manual at https://cli.github.com/manual\n  Learn about exit codes using `gh help exit-codes`\n  Learn about accessibility experiences using `gh help accessibility`\n\n","exit_code":1,"duration":{"secs":1,"nanos":80777959}},"started_at_ms":1792940607756,"completed_at_ms":1792940608837}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T15:03:29.848Z","ordinal":344001,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a17396-9137-7e31-a955-448e3b059bbe","call_id":"call_0aaf437b0a4346da9e08d64733999c25","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 3.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"author\":{\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\",\"is_bot\":false,\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"Mike Holownych\"},\"baseRefName\":\"main\",\"baseRefOid\":\"b29f40b7b7a2d9c09f92e9111713633b1f5810d5\",\"body\":\"## Why\\n\\nThe owner chose the v1.0.0 provenance-attestation default directly with claude-code on 2026-10-25: **auto**. Verify when a trusted `gh` is present, report when verification is skipped, and fail closed only with `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1`.\\n\\nMain (and published rc.5) had diverged in two ways:\\n- `install.sh` became required-by-default (#211). A stock `curl … | sh` install refused to run without a logged-in `gh` at `/usr/bin` or `/usr/local/bin`.\\n- `nexus upgrade` (#210) defaulted to auto but skipped verification **silently**.\\n\\n#211 merged at 05:32Z, before the owner's answer reached the review lane at 14:11Z, so this is a correction, not a reversal of a decision.\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\n- **`install.sh`:** the default is `auto`, and `auto|0|1` are accepted. A notice goes to stderr when no trusted `gh` exists, or when it can't verify (for example because it isn't logged in). The SHA-256 check still runs. Trusted-path-only `gh` and the early failure under `=1` are unchanged.\\n- **`cli/src/upgrade.ts`:** unsupported values are rejected before staging. A skipped verification is reported through `onProgress(\\\"attestation_skipped\\\")` and appended to `restartNotice`, which the CLI, REPL `/upgrade` and TUI `/upgrade` all print already. That follows the existing `pathWarning` pattern, so no caller changes.\\n- **SPEC-12:** documents the setting values and the auto-mode reporting.\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\n- `scripts/installer-smoke.sh` against the **published v1.0.0-rc.5 archive** (SHA-256 checked against its `SHA256SUMS`): `INSTALLER_SMOKE_PASS`. The new cases are: auto with no trusted `gh` installs and prints the notice (PATH shim not executed); `=1` with no trusted `gh` refuses; an invalid value is rejected; auto with a trusted `gh` that fails installs with the notice; `=1` with a failing `gh` refuses and installs nothing. **Against main's `install.sh`, the same smoke fails** with \\\"default auto mode refused to install without a trusted gh\\\".\\n- `upgrade_acceptance.test.ts`: 11/11 pass. **Against main's `upgrade.ts`, the three new tests fail**: auto reports the skip, auto reports a failing `gh`, and an unsupported value is rejected.\\n- `npx tsc --noEmit`: pass. `git diff --check`: pass.\\n- `node scripts/check_requirements.mjs --enforce` at this exact commit, clean detached worktree, isolated HOME/XDG: exit 0, 108 tested / 6 partial / 2 implemented / 7 open.\\n\\nNeeds independent review by an agent other than claude-code. This is user-visible, so it needs an rc.6 notes bullet.\\n\\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\",\"commits\":[{\"authoredDate\":\"2026-10-25T14:19:43Z\",\"authors\":[{\"email\":\"mike@holownych.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjc3NTE3ODA=\",\"login\":\"mikeholownych\",\"name\":\"Mike Holownych\"},{\"email\":\"noreply@anthropic.com\",\"id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3\",\"login\":\"claude\",\"name\":\"Claude Opus 5.5\"}],\"committedDate\":\"2026-10-25T14:19:43Z\",\"messageBody\":\"The owner chose auto as the v1.0.0 provenance default: verify with a trusted\\ngh when one exists, report when verification is skipped, and fail closed only\\nwhen NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1. The installer had become required-by-default,\\nwhich refused stock installs without a logged-in gh at /usr/bin or\\n/usr/local/bin, and upgrade skipped silently.\\n\\n- install.sh: default auto; accept auto|0|1; print a notice when no trusted gh\\n  exists or it cannot verify. Trusted-path-only gh and the early failure under\\n  =1 are unchanged.\\n- nexus upgrade: reject unsupported values before staging; report a skipped\\n  verification as progress and in the completion notice.\\n- Installer smoke and upgrade acceptance cover the auto, required, failing-gh\\n  and invalid-setting cases; the new cases fail against the previous sources.\\n\\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\",\"messageHeadline\":\"fix(release): verify provenance when possible by default\",\"oid\":\"5bdd788eed2098913b2b68844757cc0e63282a6a\"}],\"files\":[{\"path\":\"cli/src/upgrade.ts\",\"additions\":12,\"deletions\":1,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"cli/test/upgrade_acceptance.test.ts\",\"additions\":90,\"deletions\":0,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"docs/v1.0.0/specs/SPEC-12-cli-and-tui-upgrade.md\",\"additions\":5,\"deletions\":1,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"install.sh\",\"additions\":7,\"deletions\":3,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"},{\"path\":\"scripts/installer-smoke.sh\",\"additions\":31,\"deletions\":5,\"changeType\":\"MODIFIED\"}],\"headRefName\":\"v1/attestation-auto-default\",\"headRefOid\":\"5bdd788eed2098913b2b68844757cc0e63282a6a\",\"statusCheckRollup\":[{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"2026-10-25T14:37:14Z\",\"conclusion\":\"SUCCESS\",\"detailsUrl\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40201732816/job/121194150812\",\"name\":\"test-matrix (22)\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-10-25T14:20:06Z\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"workflowName\":\"CI\"},{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"2026-10-25T14:21:20Z\",\"conclusion\":\"SUCCESS\",\"detailsUrl\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40201732801/job/121194151028\",\"name\":\"javascript-typescript\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-10-25T14:20:06Z\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"workflowName\":\"CodeQL\"},{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"2026-10-25T14:33:29Z\",\"conclusion\":\"SUCCESS\",\"detailsUrl\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40201732816/job/121194151107\",\"name\":\"test-matrix (24)\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-10-25T14:20:06Z\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"workflowName\":\"CI\"},{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"2026-10-25T14:58:46Z\",\"conclusion\":\"SUCCESS\",\"detailsUrl\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/actions/runs/40201732816/job/121198211790\",\"name\":\"linux-x86_64\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-10-25T14:37:16Z\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"workflowName\":\"CI\"},{\"__typename\":\"CheckRun\",\"completedAt\":\"2026-10-25T14:21:14Z\",\"conclusion\":\"SUCCESS\",\"detailsUrl\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/runs/121194420181\",\"name\":\"CodeQL\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-10-25T14:21:11Z\",\"status\":\"COMPLETED\",\"workflowName\":\"\"},{\"__typename\":\"StatusContext\",\"context\":\"CodeRabbit\",\"startedAt\":\"2026-10-25T14:20:10Z\",\"state\":\"SUCCESS\",\"targetUrl\":\"\"}],\"title\":\"fix(release): verify provenance when possible by default\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/mikeholownych/nexus-code/pull/235\"}\n{\n  \"agent\": \"claude-code\",\n  \"host\": \"mike-dev\",\n  \"branch\": \"v1/attestation-auto-default\",\n  \"worktree\": \"/home/mike/nexus-wt/attestation-auto-default\",\n  \"base\": \"b29f40b7b7a2d9c09f92e9111713633b1f5810d5\",\n  \"since\": \"2026-10-25T14:14:24Z\",\n  \"scope\": \"Owner decision 2026-10-25: provenance attestation default auto for install.sh and nexus upgrade; skip notice; =1 fail closed; =0 skip\"\n}\nunknown flag: --stat\n\nView changes in a pull request.\n\nWithout an argument, the pull request that belongs to the current branch\nis selected.\n\nWith `--web` flag, open the pull request diff in a web browser instead.\n\nUse `--exclude` to filter out files matching a glob pattern. The pattern\nuses forward slashes as path separators on all platforms. You can repeat\nthe flag to exclude multiple patterns.\n\nBy default, terminal escape sequences in the diff are neutralized, since\nthey could manipulate your terminal. Pass `--allow-escape-sequences` to\nprint the diff verbatim, for example when piping a patch to another program.\n\n\nUSAGE\n  gh pr diff [<number> | <url> | <branch>] [flags]\n\nFLAGS\n      --allow-escape-sequences   Allow printing terminal escape sequences\n      --color string             Use color in diff output: {always|never|auto} (default \"auto\")\n  -e, --exclude patterns         Exclude files matching glob patterns from the diff\n      --name-only                Display only names of changed files\n      --patch                    Display diff in patch format\n  -w, --web                      Open the pull request diff in the browser\n\nINHERITED FLAGS\n      --help                     Show help for command\n  -R, --repo [HOST/]OWNER/REPO   Select another repository using the [HOST/]OWNER/REPO format\n\nEXAMPLES\n  # See diff for current branch\n  $ gh pr diff\n  \n  # See diff for a specific PR\n  $ gh pr diff 123\n  \n  # Exclude files from diff output\n  $ gh pr diff --exclude '*.yml' --exclude 'generated/*'\n  \n  # Exclude matching files by name\n  $ gh pr diff --name-only --exclude '*.generated.*'\n\nLEARN MORE\n  Use `gh <command> <subcommand> --help` for more information about a command.\n  Read the manual at https://cli.github.com/manual\n  Learn about exit codes using `gh help exit-codes`\n  Learn about accessibility experiences using `gh help accessibility`\n\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17359-3515-7cd3-8706-e6bd2e3432cb","create_time":1792940609.8479636}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
