{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T15:04:12.303Z","ordinal":344051,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a17397-370f-7980-8903-cf9464cba596","call_id":"call_355b7acfc5544c59b6c7344e8b88b932","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.7 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"## Summary\n\n- Pause the turn when checkpoint creation fails and show user-controlled options: read-only, continue without rollback checkpoint, retry with sensitive persistence allowed, cancel, or re-enter the instruction.\n- Keep checkpoint creation fail-closed; do not start the turn until a checkpoint succeeds or the user explicitly selects another path.\n- Preserve the failure reason and show a sensitive-persistence warning in the TUI, including at 40x14.\n- Make the retry notice clear that the turn remains paused until the retry succeeds or the user chooses another option.\n\n## Validation\n\n- TypeScript compiler: PASS (`tsc --noEmit`).\n- Rust compile: PASS (`cargo check --bin nexus-tui`).\n- `git diff --check`: PASS.\n- Focused regression tests: PENDING; the shared SUITE claim is held by KimiCode-defect-scan. A safe-boundary request is recorded in the claims log. No tests were run under conflicting ownership.\n- Independent source review: ACCEPT (plan05_readonly_review).\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Base: `b29f40b7b7a2d9c09f92e9111713633b1f5810d5`\n- Commit: `75450b4`\n- Acceptance: IN_PROGRESS; this PR does not establish RC or release acceptance.\n\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17359-3515-7cd3-8706-e6bd2e3432cb","create_time":1792940652.3031883}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
