{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T15:05:08.974Z","ordinal":344097,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a17398-146e-7410-aa2f-e2445856138a","author":"/root/plan05_readonly_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/plan05_readonly_review\nPayload:\n**CHANGES_REQUIRED** for head `5bdd788eed2098913b2b68844757cc0e63282a6a`, compared with requested base `3a4dbf1d0aca3d1689799cb703a40cf8f3bcc3ab` (diff SHA-256 `c6becc051290553f0af522d49f09bf20840d26fef7e5a3bed124f857949f21a7`).\n\nThe empty-value mismatch is real: [`install.sh`](/home/mike/nexus-code/install.sh:21) uses `${NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION:-auto}`, so an explicitly empty value becomes `auto`. [`upgrade.ts`](/home/mike/nexus-code/cli/src/upgrade.ts:917) uses `?? \"auto\"`, preserving the empty string, which the following allowlist rejects. The spec says values other than `auto`, `1`, and `0` are rejected. Either make both paths treat empty as unset, or reject it consistently; add an empty-value case to installer and upgrade tests.\n\nOne base caveat: GitHub currently reports PR #235 targeting `b29f40b7b7a2d9c09f92e9111713633b1f5810d5`; this candidate is a single commit on that parent, not rebased onto the requested `3a4dbf1…` base. My review covers the attestation behavior, but exact-current-base checks need a refreshed candidate. No tests were run."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17359-3515-7cd3-8706-e6bd2e3432cb","create_time":1792940708.974513}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"user_input_order":17119}}
