{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T15:05:16.739Z","ordinal":344106,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_060b64278a9dfb15016ade1aac39bc81a0949364193ecbcdf5","status":"completed","call_id":"call_ef7bdb46894a45da91e2b6f635b7adaa","name":"exec","input":"const a = ALL_TOOLS.filter(x=>x.name.includes(\"mcp_agent_mail\") && /register_agent|list_agents|send_message|find_agent|resource/.test(x.name)); text(a.map(x=>x.name+\"\\n\"+x.description.slice(0,1000)).join(\"\\n---\\n\"));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17359-3515-7cd3-8706-e6bd2e3432cb","create_time":1792940716.2274125}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T15:05:16.874Z","ordinal":344107,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17359-3515-7cd3-8706-e6bd2e3432cb","session_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","root_turn_id":"01a17359-3515-7cd3-8706-e6bd2e3432cb","response_id":"resp_060b64278a9dfb15016ade1aa8339081a0898581ff2a0f389a","usage":{"input_tokens":143156,"cached_input_tokens":132992,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":438,"reasoning_output_tokens":362,"total_tokens":143594},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":50505233,"cached_input_tokens":49911680,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":167508,"reasoning_output_tokens":97199,"total_tokens":50672741},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":6279030614,"cached_input_tokens":6211843968,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":17919781,"reasoning_output_tokens":10346610,"total_tokens":6296950395}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T15:05:16.877Z","ordinal":344108,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a17398-334d-79e3-84d9-642bab2dbc2a","call_id":"call_ef7bdb46894a45da91e2b6f635b7adaa","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.0 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"mcp__mcp_agent_mail__deregister_agent\nYou are the MCP Agent Mail coordination server. Provide message routing, coordination tooling, and project context to cooperating agents. Outputs are JSON by default; pass format='toon' (or set MCP_AGENT_MAIL_OUTPUT_FORMAT=toon) to receive {format:'toon', data:'<TOON>'}.\n\nRemove an agent from a project. Marks the agent as inactive and removes it from the active roster. Messages from/to the agent are preserved for audit but the agent can no longer send or receive new messages.\n\nexec tool declaration:\n```ts\ndeclare const tools: { mcp__mcp_agent_mail__deregister_agent(args: { agent_name: string; project_key: string; registration_token?: string | null; }): Promise<CallToolResult<{ [key: string]: unknown; }>>; };\n```\n---\nmcp__mcp_agent_mail__register_agent\nYou are the MCP Agent Mail coordination server. Provide message routing, coordination tooling, and project context to cooperating agents. Outputs are JSON by default; pass format='toon' (or set MCP_AGENT_MAIL_OUTPUT_FORMAT=toon) to receive {format:'toon', data:'<TOON>'}.\n\nCreate or update an agent identity within a project and persist its profile to Git.\n\nWhen to use\n-----------\n- At the start of a coding session by any automated agent.\n- To update an existing agent's program/model/task metadata and bump last_active.\n\nSemantics\n---------\n- If `name` is omitted, a random adjective+noun name is auto-generated.\n- Reusing the same `name` updates the profile (program/model/task) and\n  refreshes `last_active_ts`.\n- A `profile.json` file is written under `agents/<Name>/` in the project archive.\n\nAgent Identity\n---------------\nTwo naming modes are supported:\n1. **Explicit identity** — pass a stable ID like ``alpha-one``, ``cc-0``,\n   or ``worker_42``.  Must match ``[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]{0,\n---\nmcp__mcp_agent_mail__send_message\nYou are the MCP Agent Mail coordination server. Provide message routing, coordination tooling, and project context to cooperating agents. Outputs are JSON by default; pass format='toon' (or set MCP_AGENT_MAIL_OUTPUT_FORMAT=toon) to receive {format:'toon', data:'<TOON>'}.\n\nSend a Markdown message to one or more recipients and persist canonical and mailbox copies to Git.\n\nDiscovery\n---------\nTo discover available agent names for recipients, use: resource://agents/{project_key}\nAgent names are NOT the same as program names or user names.\n\nWhat this does\n--------------\n- Stores message (and recipients) in the database; updates sender's activity\n- Writes a canonical `.md` under `messages/YYYY/MM/`\n- Writes sender outbox and per-recipient inbox copies\n- Optionally converts referenced images to WebP and embeds small images inline\n- Supports explicit attachments via `attachment_paths` in addition to inline references\n\nParameters\n----------\nproject_key : str\n    Project identifier (same used wi"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17359-3515-7cd3-8706-e6bd2e3432cb","create_time":1792940716.8775039}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
