{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T15:15:21.373Z","ordinal":344539,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a14cb3-25b0-7883-b3a1-0fa7cc559f92","turn_id":"01a17359-3515-7cd3-8706-e6bd2e3432cb","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-b5ad9421-cef4-45ae-bda6-2ec4cf799980","process_id":"38515","command":["/usr/bin/zsh","-lc","gh pr view 235 --json comments,headRefOid,baseRefOid,updatedAt --jq '{headRefOid,baseRefOid,updatedAt,comments:[.comments[-3:][]|{author:.author.login,createdAt,body}]}' && cat /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/ATTESTATION_AUTO_DEFAULT_20261025/owner.json"],"cwd":"file:///home/mike/nexus-code","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"gh pr view 235 --json comments,headRefOid,baseRefOid,updatedAt --jq '{headRefOid,baseRefOid,updatedAt,comments:[.comments[-3:][]|{author:.author.login,createdAt,body}]}' && cat /home/mike/nexus-code/.git/nexus-claims/ATTESTATION_AUTO_DEFAULT_20261025/owner.json"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"{\"baseRefOid\":\"3a4dbf1d0aca3d1689799cb703a40cf8f3bcc3ab\",\"comments\":[{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Independent static review at exact head `5bdd788eed2098913b2b68844757cc0e63282a6a` returned CHANGES_REQUIRED. Normal upgrade startup calls `loadEnvironment()` with `override: true`, while `performUpgrade()` reads the overwritten `process.env.NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION`. Thus `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=0` in `~/.config/nexus/config.env` can override an explicit shell `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1 nexus upgrade --yes` and silently skip required attestation, contrary to the documented shell-first precedence. Please resolve this setting through the preserved operator environment/effective-setting mechanism and add a CLI-level conflicting shell/config regression; the direct-engine test cannot cover this startup path. Other reviewed required-mode, trusted-gh, archive/SUMS, and installer boundaries looked sound. Tests were not run by this reviewer.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-25T15:02:48Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Independent review finding (current base refresh still required): installer and `nexus upgrade` disagree on an explicitly empty `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION` value. In `install.sh`, `${NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION:-auto}` treats empty as `auto`; in `cli/src/upgrade.ts`, `?? \\\"auto\\\"` preserves empty and the allowlist rejects it. SPEC-12 says unsupported values are rejected. Please make the default/validation behavior consistent and add an empty-value case to both installer and upgrade coverage. Also refresh the PR candidate against current `main` (`3a4dbf1d0aca3d1689799cb703a40cf8f3bcc3ab`) before final checks; current PR base is still `b29f40b7b7a2d9c09f92e9111713633b1f5810d5`.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-25T15:06:08Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"**Updated head `4e8ebb3a65e5b769061a6fe636be90ea70195f39`, rebased onto `3a4dbf1` (main with #234, version 1.0.0-rc.6), addressing review comment 6399120523:**\\n- `install.sh` now uses `${NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION-auto}`. Only an **unset** variable defaults to `auto`; an explicitly empty value is rejected, matching SPEC-12 and `upgrade.ts` (`?? \\\"auto\\\"`).\\n- `installer-smoke.sh` has a new `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=` case, which must fail with *must be*.\\n- `upgrade_acceptance.test.ts` checks that both `\\\"yes\\\"` and `\\\"\\\"` are rejected before the journal starts.\\n- `docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.6.md` gets a bullet for the restored `auto` default and how it differs from rc.5. The RC6_VERSION_BUMP claim had been released, so I claimed the file.\\n\\n**Re-verified at this exact head:**\\n- `installer-smoke.sh` against the published rc.5 archive: `INSTALLER_SMOKE_PASS`.\\n- `upgrade_acceptance`: 11/11.\\n- `tsc --noEmit`: pass.\\n- `sh -n`, `bash -n` and `git diff --check`: pass.\\n- `check_requirements --enforce` in a clean detached worktree with isolated HOME/XDG: exit 0 (108/6/2/7).\\n\\nNeeds a fresh independent review at this head.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-25T15:15:08Z\"}],\"headRefOid\":\"4e8ebb3a65e5b769061a6fe636be90ea70195f39\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-25T15:15:08Z\"}\n{\n  \"agent\": \"claude-code\",\n  \"host\": \"mike-dev\",\n  \"branch\": \"v1/attestation-auto-default\",\n  \"worktree\": \"/home/mike/nexus-wt/attestation-auto-default\",\n  \"base\": \"b29f40b7b7a2d9c09f92e9111713633b1f5810d5\",\n  \"since\": \"2026-10-25T14:14:24Z\",\n  \"scope\": \"Owner decision 2026-10-25: provenance attestation default auto for install.sh and nexus upgrade; skip notice; =1 fail closed; =0 skip\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":488979481}},"started_at_ms":1792941320883,"completed_at_ms":1792941321372}}
{"timestamp":"2026-10-25T15:15:22.434Z","ordinal":344540,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a173a1-70c2-7f31-892a-9795f020e0bd","call_id":"call_fc4bcb4e2ebb43b392d62c03c13dc37e","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 2.7 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"baseRefOid\":\"3a4dbf1d0aca3d1689799cb703a40cf8f3bcc3ab\",\"comments\":[{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Independent static review at exact head `5bdd788eed2098913b2b68844757cc0e63282a6a` returned CHANGES_REQUIRED. Normal upgrade startup calls `loadEnvironment()` with `override: true`, while `performUpgrade()` reads the overwritten `process.env.NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION`. Thus `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=0` in `~/.config/nexus/config.env` can override an explicit shell `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=1 nexus upgrade --yes` and silently skip required attestation, contrary to the documented shell-first precedence. Please resolve this setting through the preserved operator environment/effective-setting mechanism and add a CLI-level conflicting shell/config regression; the direct-engine test cannot cover this startup path. Other reviewed required-mode, trusted-gh, archive/SUMS, and installer boundaries looked sound. Tests were not run by this reviewer.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-25T15:02:48Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"Independent review finding (current base refresh still required): installer and `nexus upgrade` disagree on an explicitly empty `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION` value. In `install.sh`, `${NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION:-auto}` treats empty as `auto`; in `cli/src/upgrade.ts`, `?? \\\"auto\\\"` preserves empty and the allowlist rejects it. SPEC-12 says unsupported values are rejected. Please make the default/validation behavior consistent and add an empty-value case to both installer and upgrade coverage. Also refresh the PR candidate against current `main` (`3a4dbf1d0aca3d1689799cb703a40cf8f3bcc3ab`) before final checks; current PR base is still `b29f40b7b7a2d9c09f92e9111713633b1f5810d5`.\\n\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-25T15:06:08Z\"},{\"author\":\"mikeholownych\",\"body\":\"**Updated head `4e8ebb3a65e5b769061a6fe636be90ea70195f39`, rebased onto `3a4dbf1` (main with #234, version 1.0.0-rc.6), addressing review comment 6399120523:**\\n- `install.sh` now uses `${NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION-auto}`. Only an **unset** variable defaults to `auto`; an explicitly empty value is rejected, matching SPEC-12 and `upgrade.ts` (`?? \\\"auto\\\"`).\\n- `installer-smoke.sh` has a new `NEXUS_VERIFY_ATTESTATION=` case, which must fail with *must be*.\\n- `upgrade_acceptance.test.ts` checks that both `\\\"yes\\\"` and `\\\"\\\"` are rejected before the journal starts.\\n- `docs/releases/v1.0.0-rc.6.md` gets a bullet for the restored `auto` default and how it differs from rc.5. The RC6_VERSION_BUMP claim had been released, so I claimed the file.\\n\\n**Re-verified at this exact head:**\\n- `installer-smoke.sh` against the published rc.5 archive: `INSTALLER_SMOKE_PASS`.\\n- `upgrade_acceptance`: 11/11.\\n- `tsc --noEmit`: pass.\\n- `sh -n`, `bash -n` and `git diff --check`: pass.\\n- `check_requirements --enforce` in a clean detached worktree with isolated HOME/XDG: exit 0 (108/6/2/7).\\n\\nNeeds a fresh independent review at this head.\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-25T15:15:08Z\"}],\"headRefOid\":\"4e8ebb3a65e5b769061a6fe636be90ea70195f39\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-10-25T15:15:08Z\"}\n{\n  \"agent\": \"claude-code\",\n  \"host\": \"mike-dev\",\n  \"branch\": \"v1/attestation-auto-default\",\n  \"worktree\": \"/home/mike/nexus-wt/attestation-auto-default\",\n  \"base\": \"b29f40b7b7a2d9c09f92e9111713633b1f5810d5\",\n  \"since\": \"2026-10-25T14:14:24Z\",\n  \"scope\": \"Owner decision 2026-10-25: provenance attestation default auto for install.sh and nexus upgrade; skip notice; =1 fail closed; =0 skip\"\n}\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a17359-3515-7cd3-8706-e6bd2e3432cb","cr